window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1601,"title":"Chapter 1601: Complete Bloodline","paragraphs":["The moment the word left Max’s lips, the black flames erupted with terrifying hunger.","What had begun as fire around his body instantly surged outward in every direction, racing across the colossal corpse like a living tide. Streams of dark flame climbed the ribs, wrapped around the spine, poured through the hollow skull, and descended into every crack and crevice of the ancient remains.","Within moments, the entirety of the gigantic black dragon corpse was engulfed.","The flames did not burn like ordinary fire. They consumed essence. They devoured origin.","They fed upon the ancient draconic power hidden within the bones that had endured countless ages.","The whole Dragon Death Valley began to tremble.","Violent currents of draconic aura rushed toward the corpse from every direction, drawn into the black inferno as though returning to their source. Crimson storms formed in the sky. The earth cracked further. Countless beasts across the core region howled in fear and instinctive submission.","At the center of it all stood Max.","Both his hands remained buried within the remains while torrents of energy surged into him through the connection.","His veins glowed.","His bones vibrated.","His bloodline roared like a waking sovereign beast.","The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline was changing.","Before this moment, it had already been extraordinary, granting immense physical power, draconic affinity, and the ability to condense Draconic Essences. But now it was devouring the essence of a true black dragon, a being whose corpse still ruled an entire forbidden zone after death.","That nourishment was beyond ordinary fortune.","It was a heaven-defying opportunity.","Inside Max’s body, the bloodline began to evolve rapidly.","Its aura grew deeper, heavier, and far more ancient. The draconic dominance it released became purer than before, no longer resembling a descendant bloodline but something closer to an original sovereign lineage.","Each pulse of his heart released waves of pressure strong enough to distort the air around him.","His scales darkened into a richer shade of black, polished like divine metal. Fine patterns resembling ancient dragon runes appeared across them, each one carrying traces of chaotic power.","The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline had broken through its final limitations.","It reached the highest stage possible.","Peak bloodline perfection. No further refinement remained.","At that level, Max’s bloodline no longer merely inherited the strength of black dragons.","It stood among them.","The devouring continued for hours.","The mountain-like skeleton gradually dimmed as the ancient essence hidden within it was stripped away layer by layer. Bones that had resisted time for ages began turning gray. Their terrifying aura weakened. The pressure dominating the valley steadily collapsed.","Meanwhile, Max’s body transformed continuously.","Draconic Essences condensed within him at a terrifying pace, one after another, forming like stars in an endless night sky.","His Dragon Scales multiplied and strengthened, spreading denser layers of defense and power throughout his physique.","The number rose without pause.","Three thousand.","Four thousand.","Then finally—","Five thousand.","When the last trace of essence was devoured, the colossal corpse that had once shaken Orion lost all brilliance and crumbled into lifeless dust.","The black flames returned to Max and sank into his body.","Silence descended across the core region.","Max slowly withdrew his hands and stood upright. A terrifying aura spread from him naturally.","Within his body now rested 5000 Draconic Essences.","Across his physique existed 5000 Dragon Scales, each scale carrying immense durability and monstrous strength.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline had ascended to its supreme stage.","Max opened his eyes. For a brief instant, a phantom black dragon seemed to awaken behind him and gaze upon the world.","Then it vanished.","Max clenched his fist, feeling the unimaginable force coursing through every part of his body.","The greatest treasure of Dragon Death Valley had become his nourishment.","As the final traces of power settled within his body, Max stood motionless amidst the dust of the fallen corpse.","Deep inside his body, the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline pulsed with a majestic rhythm.","It no longer felt incomplete.","It no longer felt like a fragmentary inheritance passed down through diluted generations.","It had become whole.","At that exact moment, a familiar translucent screen of light appeared before Max.","The system had responded.","Golden symbols formed rapidly before transforming into clear words.","----","[Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline has fully evolved.]","– Current Status: [Complete Bloodline]","– Bloodline Rank: [Supreme]","[You have inherited the complete source lineage of the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline.]","[All previous limitations removed.]","----","Max’s eyes sharpened as more lines appeared.","----","Bloodline Abilities Unlocked:","1. Dragon Scales Transformation","Cover the body in supreme black dragon scales, greatly increasing defense, physical strength, regeneration, and resistance to elemental and law-based attacks.","2. Draconification","Partially awaken the primal black dragon state. Gain draconic claws, horns, tail, enhanced senses, savage battle instincts, flight capability, and explosive combat power.","3. True Dragon Transformation","Manifest the complete body of a primordial black dragon. Gain overwhelming draconic might, immense size, sky-ruling mobility, destructive breath attacks, terrifying suppression aura, and a body capable of crushing mountains.","----","The screen flickered once more before displaying a final line.","[You are now the true inheritor of the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline.]","Max stared at the words in silence.","Even for him, the final ability caused a ripple in his heart.","True Dragon Transformation.","That was no mere enhancement technique.","That was the power to become a genuine black dragon.","A slow smile formed on his face.","He could already feel it sleeping within his blood, vast and ancient, waiting for the moment he chose to awaken it.","Max clenched his fist as black power surged through his veins like a roaring sea.","\"Let me try this new ability first,\" he said with clear anticipation.","Even with everything he had experienced, the chance to transform into a true dragon stirred something primal within him. It was not merely another technique or battle art. This was the awakening of a bloodline taken to its absolute peak.","Without hesitation, Max activated True Dragon Transformation.","The moment the command was made, his body erupted with boundless draconic power."]},{"number":1602,"title":"Chapter 1602: Across the Multiverse!","paragraphs":["A violent storm of black energy exploded outward from him, sweeping across the core region like a hurricane. The ground split apart in all directions. Mountains around Dragon Death Valley trembled. The air itself screamed under the pressure of the awakening force.","Max’s body began to grow.","His bones expanded with thunderous cracking sounds. Muscles surged. Flesh transformed. Countless layers of dark scales spread rapidly across his form, each scale polished like divine obsidian and engraved with faint runic patterns that shimmered with chaotic light.","His arms lengthened into colossal forelimbs ending in claws sharp enough to rend steel mountains apart.","His legs thickened into pillars of overwhelming might.","A long, massive tail emerged behind him, striking the earth once and causing shockwaves to ripple through the valley.","His neck extended upward as his human features vanished completely, replaced by the noble and terrifying visage of a true dragon. Two majestic horns curved backward from his skull like crowns forged by nature itself. His eyes opened next, vast golden-black pupils glowing with sovereign authority.","Wings burst from his back.","They were enormous, layered with black scales and lined with blade-like bones, large enough to eclipse entire ridges when fully spread.","In only moments, where Max had once stood, there now towered a monstrous black dragon of breathtaking scale.","He was immense beyond reason.","His body stretched across the broken lands of the core region like a living mountain range. Each breath he exhaled stirred violent winds. His mere presence caused weaker beasts across Orion to collapse in terror.","Yet despite the monstrous power radiating from him, there was majesty in his form.","He did not resemble a beast born of madness.","He looked like an ancient ruler of dragons.","A sovereign creature worthy of fear and reverence.","Max slowly raised his enormous head toward the heavens. Power gathered within his chest, ancient and thunderous.","Then he roared.","\"ROOAAAARRRR!\"","The sound that erupted from him was not merely noise.","It was domination given voice.","It tore through Dragon Death Valley first, shattering cliffs, dispersing clouds, and sending every beast in the region fleeing in panic. Then it spread across the whole of Orion like a world-ending wave.","Cities shook.","Forests bent.","Seas churned.","Cultivators everywhere froze as their hearts trembled under the dragon roar.","\"What’s going on?!\" Rose and Lucia found themselves trembled as the heard the roar of the dragon. For a moment they were horrified wondering what was going on in the core region of the Dragon Death Valley that they could hear the roar of a dragon.","Just as they were wondering, the roar didn’t stop there.","The roar surged beyond Orion itself, crossing the void of space and echoing into the surrounding planets of the same star realm.","On distant worlds, powerful experts abruptly opened their eyes in shock. Ancient beasts lowered their heads instinctively. Hidden elders emerged from seclusion with grave expressions.","All of them felt the same thing.","A supreme draconic existence had awakened.","Back on Orion, Max remained suspended above Dragon Death Valley in his colossal dragon form, wings spread wide enough to shadow the land beneath him.","His golden-black eyes looked down upon the world.","And for that brief moment, he truly resembled a dragon emperor returned from ancient times.","----","Far beyond the universe that housed the Limitless Expanse Divine Realm, beyond countless layers of void and the reach of ordinary cosmic laws, another universe existed.","It was a realm ancient beyond measure, one whose stars burned with draconic fire and whose heavens were ruled by bloodlines older than many worlds themselves.","At the heart of that universe stood a colossal palace suspended above an endless sea of clouds.","The palace was vast enough to rival continents. Pillars carved from black-gold crystal rose into the heavens, each wrapped by statues of coiling dragons. Rivers of molten light flowed through open channels in the floor, while immense braziers burned with eternal flame that gave off no smoke. Every inch of the structure radiated nobility, dominance, and terrifying age.","Within its grand central hall, many figures were seated in ordered rows.","They were humanoid in shape, yet clearly not human.","Each possessed bodies covered in scales of varying colors and lusters. Some bore crimson scales like flowing magma. Others carried silver hides that reflected starlight. Some were dark as abyssal steel, while others shimmered with violet or emerald tones. Horns curved from their heads, tails rested behind their thrones, and their eyes held slit pupils filled with instinctive superiority.","Their forms resembled Max’s Dragon Scales Transformation, but far more complete and natural. Where Max still carried traces of a human foundation, these beings appeared born from dragon blood itself. Their muscles, bones, and presence were all aligned more closely with dragons than mortals.","They were discussing matters of territories, bloodline inheritances, border conflicts, and cosmic resources, their voices deep and powerful enough to shake lesser realms.","At the far end of the hall stood the highest throne.","It towered above all others, forged from ancient golden metal and shaped from the skeleton of some long-forgotten beast king. Upon it sat a single figure.","His body was entirely covered in radiant golden dragon scales that shone with supreme authority. Even seated casually, he gave the impression of a mountain overlooking insects. One arm rested on the throne’s armrest while his chin leaned lazily against one hand.","His eyes were half closed, as though nothing in the meeting before him truly interested him.","Yet no one dared mistake that relaxed posture for weakness.","The pressure unconsciously leaking from him was enough to make the air itself kneel.","He was the unquestioned ruler of this hall.","As one elder was speaking about the allocation of draconic veins across several star sectors, the golden-scaled figure suddenly opened one eye.","At the same moment, every being in the hall stiffened.","A roar had reached them.","It crossed dimensions.","It crossed universes.","It carried savage majesty, pure dragon authority, and the unmistakable resonance of a true dragon awakening.","The sound was distant and faint by the time it arrived, yet the hall fell into instant silence.","Several dragon-scaled elders rose from their seats in shock.","\"A true dragon roar?\"","\"Impossible. No lineage branch in our universe has reported such an awakening.\"","\"That sound came from beyond our cosmic boundaries.\"","\"It carries black dragon authority... Could it be from another universe?\"","Many voices overlapped with disbelief.","The golden-scaled figure on the throne straightened slowly, all laziness vanishing from his posture.","His slit pupils narrowed.","For the first time in ages, interest appeared in his eyes.","\"A true black dragon roar?\" he said quietly, his eyebrows furrowed.","His voice alone caused the entire hall to tremble.","He then leaned forward, gaze fixed toward a direction no one else could comprehend, as if seeing through layers of universes.","\"How could a true black dragon appear now?\"","The other dragon beings lowered their heads instinctively, sensing that something significant had just happened."]},{"number":1603,"title":"Chapter 1603: All Knowing Book!","paragraphs":["The golden-scaled figure remained seated upon his towering throne, yet his eyes had grown far sharper than before.","The faint echo of the black dragon roar still lingered in the hall like an omen.","Silence ruled the chamber. None of the dragon-scaled beings dared speak carelessly while their ruler was thinking.","At last, the golden-scaled figure slowly raised his head.","His gaze swept across the hall, and the pressure released from that simple movement caused the air to grow heavy.","\"Go,\" he ordered in a calm voice that carried unquestionable authority. \"Find the universe from which that true black dragon roar came.\"","The moment his words fell, the entire hall erupted into motion.","The seated elders rose instantly.","War generals wrapped in crimson scales stepped forward with fierce expressions. Silver-scaled strategists opened ancient maps formed from floating light. Several figures tore open spatial rifts on the spot, preparing to cross cosmic boundaries.","Others issued commands through dragon runes that flew into the heavens like meteors, summoning fleets, scouts, and bloodline seekers from distant territories.","No one questioned the order.","No one hesitated.","Within moments, the once orderly grand hall had become the center of a vast mobilization spanning universes.","Yet through all of it, the golden-scaled figure remained seated.","He watched the chaos below with quiet amusement.","Then, when no one was close enough to hear, he muttered softly to himself.","\"Little brother... has your descendant finally appeared?\"","For the first time in ages, a genuine smile appeared on his face.","It was not warm.","It was the smile of someone who had waited through endless years for the return of an opportunity too great to miss.","\"Good... very good.\"","His fingers tapped lightly against the armrest of the throne.","\"We have waited for a very long time.\"","His golden eyes looked beyond the palace walls, beyond the stars of his universe, beyond the countless realities between him and the source of that roar.","Then his expression gradually turned cold and majestic.","\"It is time,\" he said quietly, \"to begin the greatest war the multiverse has ever seen.\"","The hall trembled.","The stars outside dimmed for a brief instant.","Somewhere across endless universes, ancient forces that had slumbered for eras were about to awaken.","Within the Limitless Expanse Divine Realm, far beyond the countless star realms known to ordinary cultivators, there existed a floating island suspended in the endless void.","From a distance, it appeared no larger than a small landmass drifting silently through space. Its shape was simple, almost unremarkable, and many who saw it from afar would dismiss it as nothing more than an isolated celestial fragment.","But appearances meant nothing there.","Its true size could not be measured from outside.","Its boundaries were hidden by ancient spatial laws so profound that only those who had entered it personally could comprehend its vastness. Within that concealed world were oceans, mountains, ancient cities, sacred lands, and skies large enough to contain stars of their own.","This was one of the most mysterious places in the Limitless Expanse Divine Realm.","At that moment, four figures sat together in a serene pavilion overlooking an endless sea of clouds. A table of white jade rested between them, and fragrant tea steamed gently in crystal cups.","The four figures looked almost human, yet no mortal could mistake them for such.","Each carried an indescribable aura of divinity. Their presence seemed intertwined with natural law itself. Merely sitting there, they gave the impression of beings who stood above heaven and earth, as though gods had chosen human forms for convenience.","They were the Four Primarchs of the Primordial Race.","Ancient rulers.","Living pillars of one of the oldest races in existence.","They had gathered not for politics or conflict, but for quiet tea and discussion.","Then the roar came.","A deep, majestic dragon roar echoed across the floating island, crossing distance, law, and dimensional barriers as though none of them existed. The tea within their cups rippled violently. Clouds below scattered. Even the island’s defensive formations trembled faintly in response.","All four Primarchs stopped what they were doing.","They slowly lifted their gazes and looked toward one another.","The first Primarch let out a long sigh.","\"The roar of a true black dragon...\" he said softly. \"I never believed I would hear that sound again in this lifetime.\"","The second Primarch’s expression grew grave.","\"As much as we dislike admitting it, we all know what this signifies.\"","His eyes darkened with memory.","\"The All Knowing Book recorded it clearly. Whenever the roar of a true black dragon echoes throughout the multiverse, great change follows. Not change of some small forces, but change on the scale of civilizations.\"","He set down his cup carefully.","\"The last time this roar was heard, the bloodline of the true black dragon went extinct. Kazreth invaded our universe with the devil legions. The Spirit Race and Dragon Race entered total war. Entire star realms were burned away.\"","His voice lowered.","\"And in the end, the race that benefited the most from that chaos was the Angel Race.\"","Silence settled heavily.","Then he continued.","\"Now the roar has sounded again.\"","He looked toward the dark heavens beyond the island.","\"I do not know if we will survive what is coming. The last war was already brutal enough to drown eras in blood. Yet I have a feeling the next one will make that conflict look like children fighting in dust.\"","The third Primarch, a woman whose eyes carried endless wisdom, spoke next.","\"The All Knowing Book has never been wrong.\"","Her tone was calm, but there was steel beneath it.","\"We should begin preparing now. Disorder will spread through the multiverse soon enough.\"","She paused briefly.","\"It is fortunate that the Cosmic Ascension Conference will be held soon. Many geniuses will emerge from it.\"","Then her expression dimmed slightly.","\"I only do not know whether those geniuses will have enough time to mature before the storm reaches them.\"","The three Primarchs fell silent.","Then the last Primarch finally spoke.","Unlike the others, he had not shown fear or concern since the roar began. His expression remained steady, almost detached, as if he had accepted this truth long ago.","\"This is inevitable,\" he said.","His voice was calm, yet it carried immense weight.","\"War has never been an accident in the history of existence. It is the result of accumulation. Grudges pile upon grudges. Ambition grows in silence. Fear breeds weapons. Desire breeds alliances. Power creates imbalance, and imbalance always seeks correction through blood.\"","He slowly rose to his feet.","\"The black dragon’s roar did not create what is coming. It merely announced that the hidden fires are ready to surface.\"","The wind around the pavilion began to stir.","\"Every race has prepared in secret. Every ancient enemy remembers old hatred. Every ambitious ruler dreams of ruling the ashes after the slaughter.\"","His gaze swept across the endless heavens.","\"The multiverse has been too quiet for too long.\"","The other Primarchs listened in silence.","Then the last Primarch spoke one final time.","\"When the first blade is drawn, countless others will follow. Worlds will burn. Bloodlines will vanish. New heroes will rise, and old monsters will awaken.\"","He looked toward the direction from which the dragon roar had come.","\"And whether we welcome it or not...\"","\"The next great war has already begun.\""]},{"number":1604,"title":"Chapter 1604: Cracks on Dragon Egg?!","paragraphs":["\"ROOOAAARRR!\"","After the overwhelming roar burst from Max’s dragon form and shook Orion along with the surrounding star realms, he soared through the skies of Dragon Death Valley for several minutes.","In his true dragon body, movement felt entirely different from anything he had experienced before. The winds bent around him as if welcoming their ruler. Each beat of his massive wings sent storms rolling across the heavens. Mountains beneath him looked small, and the clouds were scattered wherever he passed.","For a brief time, Max simply enjoyed the sensation.","Strength.","Freedom.","Dominance.","Flying in the body of a true black dragon awakened instincts buried deep within his bloodline, and even someone as experienced as Max could not deny the exhilaration of it.","Then, just as he was circling high above the valley, a scene from his clone caused him to halt midair.","His enormous wings slowed.","Golden-black eyes narrowed.","\"The black dragon egg has started hatching?\" Max muttered in clear surprise.","That egg had remained dormant for countless years. Even after being brought into his possession and nourished within the Dimension of Spirit, it had shown little more than faint life fluctuations.","Yet now it was finally awakening.","Max’s thoughts moved quickly.","Could his own transformation into a true black dragon have triggered something?","Could the roar, the bloodline resonance, or the ancient draconic aura he had devoured have stimulated the sleeping life within the egg?","He did not know for certain.","Still, a grin spread across his dragon face.","\"Hehe... this is good.\"","His eyes gleamed with anticipation.","\"I might soon have a true black dragon as my companion.\"","----","Inside the Dimension of Spirit, all attention was focused on a single object.","The black dragon egg.","Max’s clone stood nearby with a serious expression, while Lily, Blob, Tian, and many spirits had gathered around it in a wide circle. Even the usually playful spirits had become unusually quiet, sensing that something extraordinary was about to happen.","The egg rested upon a nest of spiritual crystals and dragon essence stones that had long been prepared for it. Its shell was dark as midnight, marked with natural patterns that resembled scales forged from ancient metal.","At first, it only trembled lightly.","Then it shook again.","A faint cracking sound echoed through the space.","Everyone’s eyes widened.","A thin line appeared across the shell, glowing briefly from within before spreading wider.","Another crack followed.","Then another.","The life aura hidden inside the egg, once weak and distant, was now rising steadily with every passing second.","Blob bounced excitedly in circles.","\"It is hatching! It is really hatching!\"","Lily’s expression softened with rare excitement, while Tian folded his arms and stared closely, unwilling to miss a single detail.","The shell continued to fracture.","Tiny fragments broke away and fell to the ground, revealing flashes of darkness moving inside.","Then, slowly but steadily, the top portion of the egg split apart.","A small claw pushed through first.","It was tiny compared to Max’s monstrous dragon form, but perfectly shaped, covered in glossy black scales that shimmered faintly under the spiritual light.","Soon after, a small head forced its way out.","Two little curved horns rested atop its skull. Bright golden eyes blinked repeatedly in confusion as the newborn creature looked around at the many figures surrounding it.","The tiny dragon let out a soft, hoarse sound.","\"Rrrr...\"","Then with clumsy determination, it wriggled free from the shell and stumbled onto the nest.","A small black dragon had been born.","Its wings were still folded tightly to its sides, its tail swayed awkwardly, and it looked more adorable than fearsome at the moment. Yet the purity of the aura around it made everyone understand the truth instantly.","This was no ordinary hatchling.","This was a genuine true black dragon.","The little creature tilted its head, sniffed the air, then looked directly toward Max’s clone.","Its eyes brightened.","Without hesitation, it waddled forward with tiny unsteady steps and pounced onto him.","Blob burst into laughter.","Lily covered her mouth to hide a smile.","Even Tian’s stern expression cracked slightly.","The newborn dragon curled itself comfortably against Max’s clone and closed its eyes as if it had already chosen its family.","And somewhere far away, the true Max, still in dragon form above Dragon Death Valley, could not help but laugh when he sensed it.","\"Haha, nice,\" Max muttered with satisfaction.","The connection with his clone allowed him to experience everything happening inside the Dimension of Spirit while continuing his own actions elsewhere. He could remain in Dragon Death Valley, continue cultivating, and at the same time share moments with Lily and the others.","\"Having a clone is truly a blessing,\" he said with a grin. \"I can be with Lily and everyone there while still handling my own matters here.\"","At that very moment, within the Dimension of Spirit, his clone was fully occupied with the newly hatched dragon.","The little black dragon was overflowing with energy.","It had only just broken free from its shell, yet it was already darting around the area with surprising speed. Its tiny wings beat rapidly as it circled above everyone’s heads, sometimes wobbling in the air before correcting itself at the last second. Every now and then it would let out proud little growls as though convinced it was already a mighty ruler of the skies.","\"Little dragon, stop flying around and come here!\" Max’s clone called out with laughter.","The hatchling ignored him completely.","Instead, it swooped low over Blob’s head, causing the spirit to bounce wildly in alarm, then climbed upward again in a crooked spiral.","\"I want to play with him too!\" Lily said as she kept running behind the little dragon.","Eventually, after another few circles, the tiny dragon landed clumsily on Max’s clone’s shoulder. It adjusted its footing with exaggerated seriousness before folding its wings and lifting its chin proudly.","Max’s clone reached up and gently rubbed the little creature beneath the jaw.","\"You really are lively,\" he said. Then his expression turned thoughtful. \"Tell me, little one... what should we call you? What is your name?\""]},{"number":1605,"title":"Chapter 1605: Vormir","paragraphs":["The newborn dragon blinked twice.","Then, in a clear and youthful voice, it answered without hesitation.","\"My name is Vormir.\"","Silence fell instantly.","Max’s clone froze.","His hand remained suspended in midair as he stared at the tiny dragon in utter disbelief.","\"You... can talk?\"","The shock that hit him was genuine.","He had expected the hatchling to chirp, roar, or perhaps communicate through instinctive feelings. Never had he imagined that a creature born only moments ago would casually speak perfect words.","Even more unbelievable was the second part.","It already had a name.","Not a name given by others.","Its own name.","Max’s clone felt truly shaken.","\"What kind of race hatches already knowing how to speak and introducing themselves?\" he muttered.","The little dragon, Vormir, puffed out his chest proudly as though the reaction was entirely appropriate.","Tian then stepped forward with his usual calm demeanor.","\"There is no need to be so surprised,\" he said. \"Dragons are among the oldest races in existence. Their origins trace back to ages when many current bloodlines had not yet been born.\"","He looked at the hatchling with rare respect.","\"Unlike ordinary creatures, true dragons inherit ancient knowledge through their bloodline. The moment they hatch, many instincts are already awakened. Speech is natural to them, and so is the awareness of their own names.\"","Max’s clone frowned in amazement. \"They are born knowing their names?\"","Tian nodded.","\"A dragon’s name is not chosen randomly. It is tied to lineage, soul resonance, and blood memory. In a sense, the name awakens together with the dragon.\"","Max looked at Vormir with renewed curiosity.","\"That sounds unfair,\" he said softly. \"Some children learn to speak after years, and he came out of the egg already introducing himself.\"","Blob bounced in agreement.","\"And flying too!\"","Vormir gave a smug little snort, clearly pleased by the attention.","Then he leaped from Max’s clone’s shoulder, flapped his wings, and began circling everyone again as if showing off even harder now that his greatness had been acknowledged.","Max’s clone stared upward before laughing helplessly.","\"So not only can you talk...\"","He shook his head.","\"You are arrogant from birth as well.\"","The little dragon roared proudly in response, though the sound came out more adorable than fearsome.","Max smiled when he witnessed everything through the shared perception of his clone.","Watching the little dragon boast, fly in circles, and treat the entire Dimension of Spirit as though it already belonged to him brought genuine amusement to Max. Even from far away, the hatchling’s lively nature was impossible to ignore.","Then an idea suddenly came to him.","With a thought, he opened a connection to the Dimension of Spirit and summoned the little dragon to his side.","A flash of light appeared in the skies above Dragon Death Valley.","The next moment, Vormir emerged in midair, flapping his tiny wings wildly in surprise as he struggled to steady himself.","He looked around in confusion.","The familiar surroundings of the Dimension of Spirit had vanished. Lily, Blob, Tian, and the others were nowhere to be seen. In their place was an endless sky, violent winds, and the vast lands of Orion spread far below.","Then his gaze shifted.","And froze.","Beside him hovered an enormous black dragon whose body stretched like a moving mountain through the heavens. Scales darker than night covered its colossal form. Vast wings stirred storms with every motion. Golden-black eyes shone with sovereign majesty.","Vormir’s little mouth fell open.","Then excitement exploded across his face.","\"Big Brother Max!\" he cried in his youthful voice. \"Are you also a dragon?!\"","Without the slightest fear, the hatchling immediately began circling around Max’s gigantic dragon body, inspecting him from every angle with amazement.","He flew past the great horns, around the massive wings, under the long neck, and around the tail, letting out impressed little sounds the entire time.","Max was briefly surprised.","Even in this form, Vormir had recognized him instantly.","Yet after remembering how mysterious true dragons were, that surprise quickly faded.","\"Hehe,\" Max chuckled deeply, the sound rumbling like distant thunder. \"I am still human, but I have the ability to transform into a dragon as well.\"","Vormir stopped midair and nodded with extreme seriousness.","\"Oh, that must be wonderful,\" he said proudly. \"A very honorable moment for you.\"","Max stared for a second before bursting into laughter.","Even newly hatched, this little dragon carried overwhelming pride in his race.","To Vormir, becoming a dragon was clearly the highest blessing imaginable.","\"You really think highly of dragons, don’t you?\" Max said with amusement.","Vormir puffed out his tiny chest.","\"As I should.\"","Max laughed again.","Then he lifted his gaze toward the distance where a towering mountain rose above the surrounding lands, its peak piercing through clouds.","\"Do you see that mountain far away?\" he asked.","Vormir turned immediately and focused ahead.","After spotting it, he nodded eagerly.","\"I see it!\"","Max’s eyes gleamed.","\"Then let us race there and see who arrives first.\"","The moment he finished speaking, his colossal wings spread wide.","A raging wind burst outward as Max shot forward like a black comet, tearing through the skies with terrifying speed.","For a second, Vormir was stunned.","Then he shouted indignantly.","\"Big Brother Max, you are cheating!\"","The little dragon flapped his tiny wings with all his might and chased after him at full speed.","Though his body was small, his natural talent as a true dragon was extraordinary. He darted through the air like a streak of black light, weaving through the winds created by Max’s passage.","What followed was a ridiculous sight.","One was a majestic colossal black dragon large enough to shake worlds.","The other was a tiny hatchling roaring angrily while chasing after him with desperate determination.","Max occasionally slowed just enough to let Vormir get close before surging ahead again, causing the little dragon to shout in protest every single time.","\"That does not count!\"","\"You started early!\"","\"You are using big dragon wings!\"","Max laughed so hard he nearly lost altitude.","Soon, the skies of Orion were filled with the sight of the two dragons racing toward the distant mountain, one mighty and ancient-looking, the other tiny, furious, and absolutely determined not to lose."]},{"number":1606,"title":"Chapter 1606: Leaving the Dragon Death Valley","paragraphs":["After spending time racing through the skies and playing with the little dragon, Max felt genuinely happy.","It had been a long time since he had enjoyed such a simple and carefree moment. There were no schemes, no life-and-death struggles, no burdens of cultivation or hidden enemies waiting in the shadows. For a short while, he had simply laughed in the open sky with a newborn dragon whose pride was larger than his body.","Eventually, Max slowed near the mountain they had raced toward and hovered in the air.","Vormir came flying in a moment later, panting dramatically despite still trying to maintain a proud expression.","\"I would have won,\" the little dragon declared, \"if Big Brother Max had not cheated from the start.\"","Max shook with laughter.","\"Of course. I am sure that was the only reason.\"","Vormir nodded seriously, completely convinced of it.","After a few more moments, Max’s expression softened slightly.","\"Vormir,\" he said, \"it is time for you to return to the Dimension of Spirit.\"","The little dragon blinked.","Then his tiny face immediately changed.","\"No.\"","Max raised a brow.","\"No?\"","Vormir crossed his forelimbs in the air as best as a hatchling dragon could and lifted his chin stubbornly.","\"I refuse,\" he said. \"A true dragon should soar freely beneath endless skies, travel across mountains, rivers, storms, and worlds. I was not born to live inside a pocket world.\"","He flapped his wings dramatically and turned in a circle.","\"I want freedom. I want to be unrestrained in the whole world.\"","Max looked at the little dragon in silence for a moment before sighing helplessly.","\"You were born less than a day ago.\"","\"That changes nothing,\" Vormir replied proudly.","\"It changes quite a lot,\" Max said dryly. \"Right now you are still small, inexperienced, and weak.\"","Vormir’s eyes widened in outrage.","\"Weak?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"I am a true dragon!\"","\"And still weak.\"","The little dragon looked deeply offended.","Max could not help smiling, but his tone became gentler.","\"Listen carefully. This world is not peaceful. There are beasts stronger than you, cultivators who would covet your bloodline, and dangers you cannot yet understand. If I let you roam freely now, you would not be free for long.\"","Vormir’s prideful expression slowly weakened.","Max continued.","\"The Dimension of Spirit is not a prison. It is a place where you can grow safely, train, and become stronger. Once you are powerful enough to protect yourself, I will personally take you with me on my adventures.\"","The little dragon looked at him carefully.","\"Truly?\"","Max nodded.","\"I promise.\"","Vormir hovered in silence, thinking very hard. His tail swayed from side to side while he considered the offer.","\"Will there be battles?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Hidden treasures?\"","\"Most likely.\"","\"Dangerous enemies for me to defeat?\"","Max smiled. \"If you become strong enough.\"","The little dragon straightened proudly.","\"Then I shall train.\"","He flew closer and landed on Max’s great dragon snout.","\"But remember your promise, Big Brother Max. A true dragon never forgets words once spoken.\"","Max chuckled softly.","\"And neither do I.\"","At last, Vormir gave a reluctant nod.","\"Very well. I shall return to the Dimension of Spirit for now.\"","With a wave of power, Max opened the connection once more. A gentle light wrapped around the little dragon.","Vormir vanished from the open sky and reappeared inside the Dimension of Spirit.","Before disappearing fully, he shouted one final sentence.","\"Tell everyone I returned by choice!\"","Max burst into laughter after hearing that.","Then he looked toward the endless horizon, still smiling.","For all his arrogance and childish pride, the little dragon had already become something precious to him.","Following that, Max remained in his true dragon form for a while longer and continued roaming through the skies of Orion.","Now that he had no immediate danger pressing upon him, he allowed himself to fully experience the body of a true black dragon. He flew above endless mountain chains, crossed ruined plains scarred by ancient battles, and passed over seas that reflected his colossal shadow like a moving eclipse.","Every movement filled him with a sense of overwhelming power.","When he beat his wings, storms formed behind him. When he dove downward, the air screamed apart around his body. When he rose through the clouds, sunlight gleamed across his scales like black metal forged by heaven itself.","Countless beasts below fled in panic the moment they sensed him. Some ancient creatures hidden within forests or caverns only peeked outward briefly before retreating deeper into hiding.","Even the atmosphere of Orion seemed to acknowledge his presence.","Max laughed more than once while testing the limits of his dragon body. He twisted through the skies, accelerated through thunderclouds, and circled several massive peaks simply because he could.","Yet after enough time had passed, his excitement gradually settled.","He still had matters to handle.","Turning in the air, Max headed back toward Dragon Death Valley.","The forbidden zone soon came into view once more, its vast scar across the world still wrapped in heavy draconic mist. He descended toward the core region where the ancient black dragon corpse had once lain.","Now that corpse was gone.","Only a vast basin of cracked earth and drifting dust remained, a silent testament to what he had devoured.","Hovering above the ruined center, Max took one final glance around before withdrawing the transformation.","The immense black dragon body began shrinking rapidly.","Wings folded inward and dissolved into black light. Scales receded into his skin. Colossal limbs compressed. The savage draconic aura settled back into his bloodline.","Within moments, Max stood there once again in human form.","Even so, traces of majesty still lingered around him.","His eyes were sharper, his body stronger, and every movement carried hidden draconic force.","He flexed his fingers lightly and smiled.","\"Useful ability.\"","Without wasting more time, Max began making his way out of the core region.","Now that the dragon corpse was gone, the oppressive draconic aura in the area had weakened considerably. The corruption was still present, but nowhere near as terrifying as before. Combined with Keeper’s Dominion and his strengthened bloodline, the return journey became far easier.","He crossed the core region first, then entered the inner region once more.","Many draconic beasts sensed him and instinctively retreated. Some trembled as though recognizing a superior bloodline ruler. Others lowered themselves to the ground and did not dare move.","Max paid them little attention.","He continued through the twisted lands, crossed the unstable zones of the middle region, and eventually stepped into the outer region once more.","Minutes later, he finally emerged from Dragon Death Valley."]},{"number":1607,"title":"Chapter 1607: Making a Lie!","paragraphs":["At the cliffs outside the forbidden zone, Lucia and Rose were still there.","Lucia had clearly been waiting anxiously despite trying to hide it. The moment she saw Max walking out alive, her eyes widened before relief washed across her face.","\"You finally came back,\" she said, quickly stepping forward. \"Do you know how long you were inside?\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"Long enough to gain something worthwhile.\"","Rose, standing slightly behind Lucia, studied him carefully.","The moment her gaze settled on him, her expression subtly changed.","She could sense it. The Max who had entered Dragon Death Valley and the Max who had returned were not the same.","His aura was deeper and so was his presence.","Even standing still, he carried a pressure that hinted at terrifying growth.","Rose narrowed her eyes. \"You found something in there.\"","Max glanced at her and smiled. \"You could say that.\"","Lucia looked between them, then crossed her arms.","\"You two can discuss mysteries later. First explain why the sky shook earlier and why I heard a dragon roar from inside the valley.\"","Max coughed lightly. \"That... may have been related to what I found.\"","Lucia stared at him in disbelief.","Rose remained silent, but for the first time since meeting him, even she felt genuine curiosity about just what this man had done inside Dragon Death Valley.","\"It’s like this...\" Max began, seeing that neither Lucia nor Rose intended to let the matter go.","He folded his arms and looked back toward Dragon Death Valley for a brief moment before continuing.","\"When I was still in the mortal world, I obtained an ancient treasure by chance. At first, I did not fully understand what it was, but later I realized it had merged into my body.\"","Lucia’s brows rose slightly. \"Merged into your body?\"","Max nodded.","\"It was not an ordinary artifact that could simply be carried in a storage ring or used whenever convenient. It became part of me. Since then, it has continuously influenced my bloodline and physical foundation.\"","Rose’s eyes sharpened.","\"A treasure capable of integrating with the body and strengthening bloodline potential...\"","Even someone as composed as her understood how rare such a thing would be.","Max continued in a calm tone, revealing only what he wished them to know.","\"My bloodline has always possessed unusual qualities. That treasure helped awaken and refine it over time, but refinement alone was not enough. It still required nourishment powerful enough to push it to a higher stage.\"","Lucia slowly began understanding.","\"And the black dragon corpse...\"","\"Yes,\" Max said with a faint smile. \"The moment I learned Dragon Death Valley contained the remains of an ancient black dragon, I became interested. A corpse that could still influence an entire forbidden zone after death clearly held terrifying essence within it.\"","He tapped his chest lightly.","\"If my bloodline could absorb even a portion of that essence, it might evolve significantly.\"","Rose looked toward the valley again, her expression thoughtful. \"So that was your true reason for coming here.\"","Max nodded.","\"That was the main reason.\"","Lucia crossed her arms and narrowed her eyes at him.","\"You entered one of Orion’s most dangerous forbidden lands because of a theory?\"","Max chuckled.","\"It was more than a theory. I could feel my bloodline reacting the closer I got to the core region.\"","He then shrugged lightly.","\"And fortunately, I was right.\"","Lucia let out a slow breath somewhere between annoyance and relief.","\"You speak as though risking your life in a place where people become monsters was a minor inconvenience.\"","Max smiled helplessly.","\"If I do not take risks, how can I grow?\"","Lucia stared at him for a few seconds before shaking her head.","\"You are impossible.\"","Rose, however, was still studying him.","\"And the dragon roar?\"","Max coughed lightly.","\"The strengthening process had... some side effects.\"","Lucia immediately looked suspicious again.","\"Side effects?\"","Max smiled with practiced innocence.","\"Nothing dangerous.\"","Lucia’s expression made it clear she did not believe that for even a moment.","Rose remained silent, but inwardly she understood something important.","Whatever ancient treasure Max spoke of, and whatever had happened inside Dragon Death Valley, his gains were far greater than he was admitting.","That only made him more dangerous than before.","Max stretched lightly and looked toward the horizon.","\"In any case, what I came for has been achieved.\" Then he glanced at the two women beside him. \"So, shall we leave this place?\"","\"Hmm.\" Lucia nodded.","Truthfully, she had no desire to remain on Orion any longer. The planet was filled with danger, hidden schemes, forbidden zones, and far too many people capable of turning hostile at any moment. Even though valuable opportunities existed there, she felt more than ready to leave.","She then turned toward Rose with genuine gratitude in her eyes.","\"Rose, thank you for all your help this time.\"","As she spoke, Lucia took out a storage pouch and handed it forward.","\"There are one thousand divine crystals inside. Consider it payment for guiding us and helping throughout this journey.\"","Rose glanced at the pouch, then calmly shook her head.","\"No,\" she said. \"Keep it.\"","Lucia froze.","Her eyes widened in complete disbelief.","\"I do not believe this,\" she said, staring at Rose as though she had become another person entirely. \"You are refusing money?\"","As far as Lucia had always known, Rose valued profit above nearly everything else. She was the kind of person who would calculate gains before offering a smile. To see her reject a thousand divine crystals so casually was almost more shocking than anything they had encountered in Dragon Death Valley.","Rose only smiled faintly.","Then she shifted her gaze toward Max.","\"I would rather become friends with Max,\" she said. \"Since that is the case, how could I charge friends for such a small favor?\"","Lucia looked between them suspiciously, clearly unconvinced that kindness alone explained this change.","Max, however, laughed softly.","\"Hehe, Miss Rose, I appreciate that.\"","He gave her a sincere nod.","\"If you consider me a friend, then I will do the same. If you ever need help in the future, ask me. If it is within my ability, I will certainly do something about it.\"","Rose’s smile deepened slightly.","\"Oh, I definitely need help,\" she said. \"But right now, you are still too weak for the matter I have in mind.\"","Her tone carried teasing honesty rather than insult.","\"I suppose I will wait until you become a little stronger before asking.\"","Max smiled helplessly but did not deny it."]},{"number":1608,"title":"Chapter 1608: A Terrifying Potential!","paragraphs":["Lucia crossed her arms.","\"You two became close rather quickly.\"","Neither of them answered directly.","What Lucia did not know was that Rose had not chosen to befriend Max simply because of what she had witnessed so far.","Her true reason lay elsewhere.","Rose possessed a rare and unusual class ability, one that very few people knew about. That ability allowed her to perceive the future potential of geniuses. It did not reveal exact destinies, nor did it grant complete foresight, but it gave her a sense of how far a person might one day rise.","However, the ability had strict limitations.","It only worked if the target remained near her long enough for the connection to form. Brief encounters meant nothing. Passing meetings gave no result.","Because of that, it had remained dormant during their earlier interactions.","Only after Max returned from Dragon Death Valley and spent enough time near her did the ability finally activate.","And the moment it did, Rose had nearly lost control of her composure.","What she saw had shaken her to the core.","Around Max, she did not perceive the outline of an ordinary genius.","She saw a towering presence that seemed to rise beyond stars, beyond realms, beyond even the boundaries of the universe itself.","It was vast.","Terrifying.","Unclear in shape, yet overwhelming in scale.","Even more shocking, every other figure standing near that vision appeared dim and insignificant by comparison, as though they were destined to become background shadows in the wake of his ascent.","Rose had seen many talented people before.","She had judged heirs of great clans, disciples of supreme forces, and monstrous prodigies praised across star realms.","None of them came remotely close to what she saw around Max.","That was why she refused the divine crystals.","That was why she chose friendship instead of profit.","To her, one thousand divine crystals was valuable.","But the favor of someone like Max could one day become priceless.","\"I will see you again at the Cosmic Ascension Conference,\" Max said to Rose as the three of them began leaving the area outside Dragon Death Valley.","Rose looked at him with a faint frown.","\"You are participating in that tournament as well?\"","Her gaze swept over him once, measuring his current cultivation.","\"Are you not still a little too weak for something of that level?\"","Max only shrugged casually.","\"I am joining mainly to gain experience,\" he replied. \"And if by some miracle I end up winning the whole thing, that would make it even better, would it not?\"","Rose stared at him for a moment before bursting into laughter.","\"Keep dreaming.\"","Though her tone was mocking, there was a trace of curiosity hidden beneath it.","\"Come on,\" she said as she turned ahead. \"I will guide you both back to the camp.\"","The three of them soon departed from the cliffs surrounding Dragon Death Valley and traveled back through the harsh lands of Orion. Along the way, the oppressive atmosphere of the forbidden zone gradually faded behind them, replaced once more by the rough but comparatively safer terrain of the outer regions.","Hours later, the distant lights of the temporary camp came into view.","Various star shuttles rested on open ground, their metallic hulls reflecting the dim sky of Orion. Members of different forces moved in and out of the area, preparing supplies, tending injuries, or making arrangements to leave the planet after the chaos surrounding the secret domain and Dragon Death Valley.","When Max and Lucia arrived, several gazes immediately turned toward them.","Many recognized Max by now, and whispers spread quietly among the gathered cultivators. Between the matters involving Sword God Palace and War God Palace, his reputation had grown considerably.","Max paid little attention to it.","He turned toward Rose.","Lucia also stepped forward and gave her a sincere nod.","\"Thank you again,\" Lucia said. \"Without you, reaching Dragon Death Valley and returning safely would have been much harder.\"","Rose waved a hand dismissively.","\"You paid me enough through entertainment alone.\"","Lucia rolled her eyes while Max laughed.","Then Rose looked at Max one last time.","\"Do not die before the Cosmic Ascension Conference,\" she said. \"I am now curious how far you can actually go.\"","Max smiled.","\"I was about to say the same to you.\"","Rose snorted softly.","\"You should worry about yourself first.\"","Despite the teasing words, there was clear respect between them now.","After a final exchange, Max and Lucia boarded their star shuttle together. The sleek vessel hummed to life as formations across its body awakened and streams of energy flowed through its frame.","Rose remained outside, standing with her arms crossed as she watched them.","Through the transparent side panel, Lucia waved once.","Max gave Rose a nod.","Then the shuttle rose from the ground, gathering speed before shooting into the heavens like a streak of light.","Its destination was the Verdant Sky Realm.","As the vessel disappeared into the upper atmosphere, Rose continued watching for several moments before turning away.","A faint smile rested on her lips.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference...\" she murmured softly. \"That gathering may become far more interesting than I thought.\"","As the star shuttle cut through the sea of stars, streams of light passed beyond the viewing panels like flowing rivers of silver. The steady hum of the vessel’s formations filled the cabin, creating a calm contrast to everything they had recently experienced on Orion.","Lucia sat across from Max, appearing far more relaxed now that they had finally left that dangerous planet behind.","Max, however, had fallen into thought.","After a while, he looked toward her and asked, \"Lucia, do you know anything about the combat tower I entered during that trial before?\"","Lucia turned her head slightly, curious at the sudden question.","\"What about it?\"","Max leaned back in his seat, his tone sounding casual, though his eyes carried interest.","\"I was wondering whether there might be another tower like it somewhere else.\"","Lucia blinked once, then nodded without much hesitation.","\"There is.\"","Max’s posture straightened immediately.","\"There is another one?\" he asked.","His voice remained controlled, but inwardly he was genuinely surprised.","He had not expected a direct answer.","Truthfully, he had only been probing her. He wanted to observe her reaction and see whether she knew anything related to the mysterious combat tower. He had assumed she might dismiss the topic or know nothing at all.","Instead, she had confirmed the existence of a second tower so casually.","Lucia noticed the sudden intensity in his expression and gave him an amused look.","\"Yes, there is another tower of that kind somewhere within the Divine Realm.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened.","\"Where?\"","This time he did not bother hiding his eagerness. The second tower contained the second part of the Overlord Body Codex which contained the methods to open the last three divine veins of the Seven Divine Veins.","The Overlord Body Codex Max possessed only explained how to open the first four divine veins, and so Max desperately needed the other part."]},{"number":1609,"title":"Chapter 1609: Smelting Trial","paragraphs":["\"It is in the hands of the Violet Star Palace,\" Lucia said, her voice calm yet carrying a trace of respect. \"They are regarded as one of the strongest third-rate forces within this region of the Divine Realm.\"","Max repeated the name under his breath.","\"Violet Star Palace...\"","The words stirred something faint in his memory, like a ripple spreading across still water. He frowned slightly as he searched through his thoughts, then a scene surfaced in his mind.","\"Was there not an elder from that force who came to our trial grounds before?\"","Lucia gave a small nod.","\"Yes. He came to Cyrus personally.\"","Her gaze shifted toward the transparent crystal wall of the star shuttle, where rivers of starlight flowed endlessly outside. The vessel moved smoothly through the dark void, silent and steady, as if gliding across a sea of eternity.","\"He came to deliver an invitation to our Black Dragon Clan for the upcoming Smelting Trial.\"","Max turned toward her fully this time, interest appearing clearly in his eyes.","\"Smelting Trial?\"","The phrase was unfamiliar. It carried weight, yet he had never heard it before. That alone was enough to make him curious.","\"What exactly is that?\"","Lucia did not seem surprised by the question. Instead, she adjusted her posture and spoke with the patience of someone explaining a matter of common knowledge to an outsider.","\"The Smelting Trial is a large-scale preparatory event held across many regions of the Divine Realm before the Cosmic Ascension Conference begins.\"","Her tone gradually became more serious.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference gathers the finest geniuses of countless forces, clans, palaces, and ancient lineages. It is a place where reputations are forged, alliances are born, and futures are decided. Naturally, no force wishes to send its younger generation unprepared.\"","She paused briefly, letting the importance of those words sink in.","\"That is why the Smelting Trials exist.\"","Max listened in silence.","Lucia continued, her eyes reflecting distant stars.","\"These trials are created to temper disciples through pressure and danger. Some take place inside temporary secret realms that open only once every few decades. Some are ancient ruins filled with lost inheritances and hidden treasures. Others are battlefields specially prepared by major powers, where participants compete for resources while fighting one another under controlled rules.\"","A faint smile curved her lips.","\"In simple terms, they are meant to smelt raw ore into refined steel. Talent alone means little if it has never been tested. Potential alone means nothing if it has never faced danger. The Smelting Trials turn gifted youths into true weapons before they step onto the grand stage.\"","Max slowly nodded.","\"So it is a final chance to become stronger before the conference.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Lucia’s expression shifted again, becoming slightly colder.","\"Most Smelting Trials are organized by second-rate forces. They often cooperate with the strongest third-rate forces under their influence. Hosting such an event requires enormous resources, territory, formations, guards, healers, and enough prestige to make others obey the rules.\"","She gave a quiet, helpless laugh.","\"As for our Black Dragon Clan...\"","Her voice trailed for a moment.","\"We are considered one of the weaker third-rate powers. Under normal circumstances, we would never be invited.\"","Max glanced at her, already understanding where this was going.","\"But this time we did get an invite.\" Lucia’s eyes curved with amusement. She lifted a finger and pointed directly at him. \"Because of you.\"","Max raised an eyebrow.","\"Me?\"","\"Yes, you.\"","Now there was clear admiration mixed with her teasing expression.","\"You took the sword of the Sword Sovereign and became famous in the entire Divine Realm. Almost every star realms had heard of you. Half an year ago, it wouldn’t be an understatement that you were the most famous young man in the entire Divine Realm. Whether people praise you, fear you, or hate you, they all know who Max is.\"","She crossed her arms.","\"And when your fame rose, the status of the Black Dragon Clan rose with it.\"","Max said nothing.","Lucia continued in a measured tone.","\"Many outside powers now view our clan differently. Some suspect we have hidden foundations that were concealed for generations. Some believe our younger generation has begun producing true monsters. Some merely want to see with their own eyes whether the rumors are real.\"","She shrugged lightly.","\"No matter their motive, the result remains the same. The Violet Star Palace sent us an invitation to participate in the Smelting Trial.\"","A faint smile appeared on Max’s face.","\"So I raised the clan’s standing without even trying.\"","Lucia snorted softly.","\"You also made many enemies without trying.\"","\"That sounds less glorious.\"","\"It is more truthful.\"","For a brief moment, both of them laughed. The tension in the room lightened, and even the vast darkness outside the shuttle seemed less cold.","Then Lucia’s gaze sharpened once more.","\"You should understand something clearly, Max.\"","Her voice dropped slightly.","\"This invitation is not simply an honor.\"","Max’s expression became serious.","\"It is also a test.\"","His eyes narrowed.","Lucia nodded.","\"Many participants will want to measure your strength. Some will seek fame by defeating you. Some will want to crush your reputation before the Cosmic Ascension Conference even begins. Others may smile to your face while plotting in the shadows.\"","Silence filled the cabin after those words.","Max turned his head and looked beyond the crystal wall, toward the endless sea of stars stretching across the void. Countless lights burned in the darkness like silent witnesses to the ambitions of all living beings.","Then he smiled.","\"That sounds more interesting than dangerous.\"","Lucia closed her eyes and sighed.","\"I already knew you would say that.\"","\"Haha, by the way, you have become much stronger since the time we came to Orion,\" Lucia said as she looked at Max more carefully. \"The eighth level of the Law Awakening Realm already? Your growth speed is truly monstrous.\"","There was clear amazement in her voice.","When they had first arrived on Orion, Max had only been at the peak of Rebirth Realm. In what was, to many cultivators, an extremely short span of time, he had risen eight levels as though such breakthroughs were ordinary.","For most people, advancing even one level at that realm could require years of accumulation, insight, and fortune.","Yet for Max, it seemed to happen whenever he disappeared into dangerous places."]},{"number":1610,"title":"Chapter 1610: Returning to Black Dragon Clan!","paragraphs":["Max only gave a wry smile.","Truthfully, even he had not expected such an outcome.","After devouring the corpse of the ancient black dragon, he had assumed nearly all of the absorbed essence would be used to refine his bloodline and push the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline to its highest stage.","Instead, after the bloodline completed its transformation, the remaining power had surged through his body and raised his cultivation from the fifth level of the Law Awakening Realm straight to the eighth.","Even now, when he thought about it, the gains were absurd.","Lucia watched his expression and narrowed her eyes slightly.","There was something suspicious about the whole matter.","She knew Max had gone into Dragon Death Valley and returned stronger, but the extent of that growth was too unreasonable. Three levels at his stage, along with the deepened aura he now carried, clearly meant he had gained far more than he admitted.","Still, she did not press him.","Everyone had secrets, and Max had more than most.","Instead, she simply gave him a meaningful look.","\"You really are impossible to measure.\"","Max laughed softly.","\"I will take that as praise.\"","\"You should.\"","Then, after a short pause, Max asked the question that mattered next.","\"So when are we heading to Violet Star Palace for this Smelting Trial?\"","Lucia answered without hesitation.","\"In one week.\"","She leaned back in her seat and crossed her arms.","\"The clan will need time to gather the selected participants, prepare supplies, and arrange the route. Violet Star Palace is not some nearby branch force. Even with star travel, reaching their territory requires proper planning.\"","Max nodded calmly.","\"One week...\"","That was enough time to consolidate his recent gains, become familiar with his new bloodline abilities, and perhaps make a few more preparations before entering another major opportunity.","Lucia glanced at him and smirked.","\"Do not tell me you are already planning how to cause trouble there.\"","Max looked out toward the stars through the shuttle window and smiled faintly.","\"I am planning how to become stronger.\"","Lucia sighed.","\"That answer somehow worries me even more.\"","----","A few hours later, after traveling through countless streams of starlight and crossing several spatial routes, the star shuttle finally entered the territory of the Verdant Sky Realm.","The moment they crossed into its borders, the atmosphere outside the vessel subtly changed.","The stars here seemed brighter, and the surrounding spiritual currents were far richer than those near Orion.","Vast celestial islands floated in the distance, connected by rivers of light that drifted through space like living streams. Ancient mountain chains hung suspended above cloud oceans, while enormous beasts could occasionally be seen gliding between realms as naturally as birds crossing the sky.","Even the air carried a sense of old prosperity.","This was not a chaotic battlefield world like Orion.","This was a true realm shaped and ruled by powerful forces over countless years.","Lucia looked outside with a familiar calm, while Max observed everything with quiet interest.","\"The Verdant Sky Realm...\" he muttered.","Compared to many places he had seen recently, this realm possessed both order and strength.","The shuttle continued descending through layers of cloud and defensive formations. Brilliant runes lit up across the hull as it passed several checkpoints before being recognized and allowed through.","A few minutes later, the vessel lowered toward a secluded region hidden among enormous black mountains.","The area was isolated from the bustling zones of the realm, surrounded by towering peaks that curved inward like natural walls.","Thick forests covered the lower slopes, and dark mist drifted between the cliffs. Streams rich with energy flowed through the valleys, while ancient formations shimmered faintly across the land, concealing the region from ordinary eyes.","Then Max saw it.","The Black Dragon Palace.","It rested deep within the mountain basin like a silent sovereign fortress.","Its structures were built from dark stone and black metal, rising in grand layered halls and towering spires shaped with draconic motifs. Massive statues of black dragons coiled around pillars, while banners bearing the clan insignia moved in the wind. The palace did not flaunt luxury like some divine sects.","Instead, it radiated strength, discipline, and ancient pride.","The star shuttle descended slowly before landing on a wide stone platform near the outer palace grounds.","A deep mechanical hum faded as the vessel settled.","The hatch opened.","Max stepped out first and felt the familiar dense energy of the area brush against his skin immediately. It was many times richer than ordinary places and perfectly suited for cultivation unlike the chaotic aura of Orion.","He looked around the secluded basin and found there to be empty.","Lucia stepped out beside him and stretched lightly.","\"We are home.\"","Max glanced toward the Black Dragon Palace once more.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"And just in time.\"","One week remained before the Smelting Trial.","\"I think you should go and check on Aunt Virelia before going anywhere else,\" Lucia said as they stood near the landing platform. \"She must have been worried about you this whole time.\"","Max nodded.","That had already been his intention. No matter how many opportunities he encountered outside, returning and meeting his master first was only natural. Lady Virelia had supported him from the beginning, and after everything that had happened on Orion, she would certainly want answers.","Just as Max was about to leave, Lucia suddenly spoke again.","\"Wait.\"","He turned back.","Lucia crossed her arms and looked at him directly.","\"You should release Isabella first.\"","Max blinked once, then immediately understood what she meant.","Lucia continued in a practical tone.","\"She is one of the stronger young geniuses of our side and will likely be among those heading to Violet Star Palace for the Smelting Trial. We only have seven days left. If she remains hidden away any longer, she will lose valuable preparation time.\"","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","\"And if she finds out you kept her inside your secret world while everyone else was preparing, she may personally try to kill you.\"","Max coughed lightly.","\"That is also possible.\"","He could not deny her logic.","The Smelting Trial would gather elites from powerful factions. Even for someone talented like Isabella, entering such an event unprepared would be foolish."]},{"number":1611,"title":"Chapter 1611: Meeting Master!","paragraphs":["\"Fine,\" Max said with a nod.","With a thought, he opened a connection to the Dimension of Genesis.","Space rippled beside them, and Isabella stepped out from the hidden world into the open mountain basin of the Black Dragon Palace. She looked around briefly, taking in the familiar surroundings before her gaze landed on Max.","\"So we are back.\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"We are. And you should prepare well.\"","His tone became more serious.","\"The Smelting Trial at Violet Star Palace begins soon. Use these seven days wisely. Strengthen yourself as much as possible.\"","Isabella’s eyes brightened immediately.","She had naturally heard of the Smelting Trial before. For disciples of third-rate forces, receiving the chance to participate in such an event was both opportunity and recognition.","\"I am also heading there?\" she asked.","Lucia answered before Max could.","\"You were always likely to be selected as you are the Saintess of the Black Dragon Clan. Now stop wasting time and start preparing.\"","Isabella snorted softly but did not argue.","Then she looked back at Max, a faint smile appearing.","\"You had better not grow too far ahead again in just seven days.\"","Max chuckled.","\"I was about to say the same to you.\"","She rolled her eyes, though amusement remained clear on her face.","With that, Max left the two women together near the platform while they began discussing clan matters, trial participants, and possible preparations.","He then turned toward the deeper regions of the Black Dragon Palace and began walking alone.","Towering halls rose ahead of him, ancient and solemn beneath the mountain sky.","Soon Max arrived before the office of Lady Virelia.","The familiar corridor leading to her chambers carried the same quiet authority as before. Black stone walls lined with ancient carvings reflected the heritage of the Black Dragon Clan, while subtle defensive formations pulsed beneath the floor.","Even after everything he had experienced recently, returning here brought a strange sense of steadiness.","He raised his hand and knocked.","\"Come in.\"","Without hesitation, Max opened the door and stepped inside.","Lady Virelia was seated comfortably on a long couch near a low table where tea had already been prepared. Sunlight from the side windows fell across the room, giving the otherwise stern office a warmer atmosphere.","Max walked forward and sat on the couch opposite her.","Lady Virelia looked at him for several moments before narrowing her eyes slightly.","\"It seems Orion treated you rather generously,\" she said. \"You left at the fifth level of the Law Awakening Realm and returned at the eighth. That is not the kind of progress one makes from sightseeing.\"","Max smiled wryly.","\"Some things happened.\"","He then began recounting part of what had occurred on Orion. He spoke of the secret domain, the chaos among the gathered forces, the dangers of the forbidden regions, and the events that led to the conflict with Sword God Palace. However, he carefully omitted matters that should remain hidden, including the deeper truths of his personal gains.","Lady Virelia listened in silence while calmly sipping tea.","When he finished, she set the cup down gently.","\"I already heard much of what happened,\" she said. \"The news from Orion has spread throughout this side of the Divine Realm.\"","Her gaze sharpened.","\"Those who escaped the secret domain returned shaken. Most of them still cannot explain what truly happened inside. They only know they were facing suppression from a terrifying existence one moment, and the next they were suddenly back on Orion.\"","Max nodded.","\"That is more or less what it felt like.\"","He leaned back slightly.","\"One moment we believed we might die, and the next we were alive again. Whatever the truth behind it is, I am not complaining.\"","Lady Virelia gave him a brief look that suggested she suspected he knew more than he admitted, but she did not press the matter.","Instead, she asked another question.","\"I also heard that the four Primarchs of the Primordial Race appeared.\"","Max nodded.","\"They did. Even from a distance, their presence was overwhelming.\"","Lady Virelia’s expression became solemn.","\"Beings of that level rarely move without reason. If they appeared personally, then something inside that domain was significant.\"","She then changed topics.","\"And then there is your matter with Sword God Palace.\"","Max remained calm.","Lady Virelia’s lips curved faintly.","\"You truly know how to cause trouble. Offending Sword God Palace is not something ordinary disciples manage to accomplish in a lifetime, yet you did it in a single trip.\"","Max coughed lightly.","\"They started it. They wanted my sword and they were so shameless about it that they wanted to kill me to take my sword away.\"","\"Even so you did beat up the Young Miss of the Sword God Palace.\"","Even so, amusement flickered in her eyes.","She continued.","\"I also heard about your interaction with War God Palace.\"","Her gaze became more meaningful now.","\"Forming even a temporary alliance with 1st rate forces like War God Palace with them has raised your standing considerably. Many forces now view you, and by extension the Black Dragon Clan, differently.\"","Max nodded slowly.","\"I understand.\"","Lady Virelia folded her hands before her.","\"Good. Then understand this as well.\"","Her voice grew firmer.","\"In seven days, the delegation heading to Violet Star Palace for the Smelting Trial will depart. You are no longer just another promising disciple.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"You will be one of the main faces of the Black Dragon Clan there.\"","Max straightened slightly.","She continued.","\"Your name has already spread. Some know you as the one connected to the Sword Sovereign’s weapon. Some know of your conflict with Sword God Palace. Others know that War God Palace openly treated you with respect.\"","Her tone sharpened.","\"That fame is useful, but it is also dangerous.\"","Max listened quietly.","\"At the Smelting Trial, geniuses from many third-rate forces will be present. Some will want to test you. Some will want to humiliate you. Some may target you simply to weaken the Black Dragon Clan’s momentum.\"","She leaned forward slightly.","\"So use these seven days well. Consolidate your cultivation. Prepare your methods. Do not grow complacent because of what happened on Orion.\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"I never planned to be complacent.\"","Lady Virelia studied him for a moment, then gave a satisfied nod.","\"Good.\"","She lifted her tea once more.","\"Because whether you like it or not, many eyes are now waiting to see if you are truly worthy of the noise surrounding your name.\""]},{"number":1612,"title":"Chapter 1612: Vein of Strength","paragraphs":["\"Anyway, here are a few resources,\" Lady Virelia said as she took out a storage ring and placed it on the table before sliding it toward Max.","\"It should be enough to raise your cultivation several times if used properly.\"","Max picked up the ring and sent a trace of his senses inside.","Even with only a brief glance, he could tell the contents were generous. Divine crystals, spirit medicines, condensed energy stones, and several rare materials were neatly arranged within. Any ordinary disciple would consider such wealth a fortune.","Lady Virelia continued calmly.","\"I do not fully understand how your Seven Divine Veins function, but I also placed body-refining treasures inside. Some of them should help you attempt the opening of the third vein.\"","Max’s eyes brightened slightly.","\"Oh.\"","He looked genuinely pleased.","\"I really needed this.\"","He clenched the storage ring lightly.","\"Recently my body has become far stronger than before. I can feel it clearly. If I have enough resources, opening another one or even two of the Seven Divine Veins should not be impossible.\"","Lady Virelia raised a brow.","\"You say such outrageous things too casually.\"","Max laughed.","\"I only speak according to what I feel.\"","She shook her head, though there was clear satisfaction in her expression. Max’s monstrous progress had long surpassed normal standards, and by now she had stopped trying to compare him with ordinary geniuses.","Then her tone became serious once more.","\"With that said, use the remaining seven days entirely for training.\"","She tapped the table lightly.","\"Do not waste time wandering around, provoking people, or chasing random opportunities.\"","Max coughed softly.","\"I was not planning to.\"","Lady Virelia gave him a long look that made it clear she did not fully believe him.","\"If you need assistance, techniques, resources, or access to restricted training grounds, come to me at any time during these seven days.\"","Her voice softened slightly.","\"You are carrying much of the clan’s hopes into this Smelting Trial. I will support you where I can.\"","Max’s expression turned more sincere.","\"I understand.\"","He gave a firm nod.","Lady Virelia leaned back into her seat.","\"Good. Then leave and begin immediately.\"","Max stood up at once.","He bowed respectfully toward her.","\"Thank you, Master.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Go.\"","Without saying anything further, Max turned and left the office.","The corridor outside was quiet, the palace halls still carrying their solemn atmosphere. As he walked through them, the storage ring in his hand felt heavier than its physical weight.","Not because of the treasures inside.","But because of the expectations placed upon him.","Soon, he exited the central palace grounds and headed toward his own residence within the Black Dragon Clan territory.","The path ahead was clear.","Seven days.","Seven days to grow stronger, open new veins, stabilize his gains from Orion, and prepare for the Smelting Trial at Violet Star Palace.","As he looked toward the distant silhouette of his house, a faint smile rose on his lips.","\"That should be enough time.\"","Arriving back at his house, Max wasted no time. He went straight into the training chamber, sealed the room, activated the protective formations, and then entered the Dimension of Time.","The endless white world unfolded around him in silence.","Max sat cross-legged in the middle of that vast emptiness and took out all the body cultivation resources Lady Virelia had given him. One by one, he placed them before himself. There were blood-red crystals filled with violent vitality, bottles of thick golden marrow liquid, dark stones that released heavy physical pressure, and several strange herbs whose roots pulsed like living veins.","All of them were treasures meant to strengthen the body.","For ordinary cultivators, using even one of these resources recklessly could damage the meridians, tear muscles apart, or overload the bones. But Max was different now. After devouring the corpse of the ancient black dragon, his physique had changed completely.","His body contained 5000 Draconic Essences, each one like a miniature furnace of raw draconic power. His 5000 Dragon Scales had also strengthened his flesh, bones, blood, and organs to an astonishing level.","Because of that, his body was no longer fragile in front of violent energy.","It was like a divine weapon waiting to be further tempered.","Max closed his eyes and activated the method of the Seven Divine Veins.","The first two Divine Veins within his body responded immediately. They pulsed with deep power, guiding the flow of energy through him. After a few breaths, Max focused his senses on the hidden location of the third Divine Vein.","The Vein of Strength.","Unlike ordinary veins or meridians, the Divine Veins were not simple channels of energy. They were ancient gates hidden within the body, each representing a different form of physical power. The Vein of Strength was buried deep within his flesh and bones, connected to every muscle fiber, every tendon, and every part of his physical foundation.","To open it, Max did not need delicate comprehension.","He needed overwhelming bodily force.","He needed to awaken the raw power sleeping inside his body and force it to recognize him as its master.","Max picked up the first blood-red crystal and crushed it in his palm.","A thick wave of vitality surged out and entered his body like molten blood. At the same time, he drank the golden marrow liquid and swallowed several body-refining herbs. The combined power of these resources exploded inside him almost instantly.","Boom!","His body trembled.","For a normal cultivator, that violent eruption would have been dangerous. It would have torn through the body like a storm. But the moment the energy spread, the 5000 Draconic Essences inside Max awakened together.","They absorbed, refined, and controlled the incoming force.","The chaotic vitality was dragged into his bones. The marrow liquid seeped into his spine and limbs. The medicinal power of the herbs entered his muscles and tendons. Instead of harming him, all of it became fuel.","Max’s skin began glowing faintly.","Underneath his flesh, black dragon patterns appeared one after another, moving like living marks across his body. His blood flowed faster, each beat of his heart echoing like a war drum inside the silent white world.","He guided all the power toward the third Divine Vein.","At first, the Vein of Strength remained still.","It was like a sealed mountain gate, heavy and ancient, refusing to open no matter how much energy struck it."]},{"number":1613,"title":"Chapter 1613 - 9th level of Law Awakening Realm!","paragraphs":["Max was not surprised.","He took out more resources and consumed them without hesitation.","This time, the pressure in his body increased severalfold. His muscles expanded slightly, then compressed again. His bones released crisp cracking sounds as they were washed by the gathered power. Every inch of his flesh felt as though it was being hammered by invisible divine blacksmiths.","But Max did not show pain.","Compared to the torment he had endured in the past, this was nothing.","More importantly, his body was too strong now.","The 5000 Dragon Scales formed a hidden protective layer beneath his skin, preventing the violent energy from damaging his physical structure. The 5000 Draconic Essences acted like anchors, stabilizing every surge of power and forcing it to move according to his will.","Because of this, the process that should have been extremely dangerous became almost smooth.","Max continued gathering force.","One wave.","Two waves.","Ten waves.","All of the energy slammed into the sealed Vein of Strength again and again.","Gradually, the hidden Divine Vein began to react.","A deep rumbling sound echoed inside his body.","Max’s eyes snapped open for a brief moment.","\"Found it.\"","He immediately activated Dragon Scales Transformation, but only partially. Thin black scales appeared across his arms, chest, and shoulders, strengthening his body even further. At the same time, his draconic aura surged, causing the endless white space around him to tremble slightly.","Then Max clenched both fists and roared inwardly.","\"Open.\"","The gathered energy transformed into a violent current and rushed toward the third Divine Vein.","Bang!","The first impact shook his entire body.","Bang!","The second impact caused cracks to appear across the invisible barrier sealing the vein.","Bang!","The third impact made the Vein of Strength shine with a deep crimson-gold light.","Max did not stop.","He burned through more body cultivation resources and pushed every strand of energy toward that single point. His heart pounded harder. His blood boiled. His muscles trembled not from weakness, but from the rising force waiting to erupt.","Then, finally, the seal shattered.","BOOM!","A terrifying wave of strength exploded from within Max’s body.","The third Divine Vein opened.","The Vein of Strength awakened.","In an instant, Max felt as if a new source of power had been born inside him. It spread through his body with brutal simplicity, strengthening his arms, legs, back, chest, bones, tendons, and organs.","It did not feel like energy being added from the outside. It felt as though his body had remembered a power it was always meant to possess.","His muscles became denser.","His bones became heavier and stronger.","His flesh gained a terrifying explosive force.","Every movement of his body now carried a deeper physical dominance than before.","The 5000 Draconic Essences also reacted to the opening of the Vein of Strength. They pulsed together, synchronizing with the new Divine Vein. His Dragon Scales grew even tougher, and the physical strength contained within each scale increased.","Max slowly stood up.","The moment he rose, the ground of the Dimension of Time trembled beneath his feet.","He looked down at his hands and clenched them lightly.","Crack.","The air around his fist distorted from the pressure alone.","A smile appeared on his face.","\"The third Divine Vein...\"","He could feel it clearly.","The Vein of Strength had not simply increased his raw power. It had multiplied the efficiency of his entire body. Every punch, every kick, every sword swing, and every movement would now carry far greater force than before.","With his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline complete, 5000 Draconic Essences, 5000 Dragon Scales, and now the Vein of Strength opened, his physical body had reached a level that even many higher-realm geniuses would find terrifying.","Max took a slow breath and allowed the remaining medicinal power to settle.","The process had gone smoother than he expected.","If he had attempted this before devouring the black dragon corpse, opening the third Divine Vein would have been difficult and dangerous. But now, with his transformed physique, the barrier that once seemed challenging had become something he could break through with steady force.","He looked at the remaining resources before him.","\"There is still some left.\"","His eyes gleamed faintly.","\"Then I should not waste it.\"","Max looked at the remaining resources spread before him and did not waste a single moment.","The opening of the third Divine Vein had consumed a large portion of the body cultivation treasures, yet Lady Virelia’s preparations had been generous.","Several bottles of condensed divine essence still remained, along with spirit stones rich in law energy, two rare fruits wrapped in natural runes, and a cluster of pale crystals that released pure cultivation force.","For many disciples, this leftover amount alone would have been enough to support months of training.","For Max, it was another step forward.","He sat down once more in the endless white world of the Dimension of Time and calmed his breathing. The newly opened Vein of Strength pulsed steadily within him, while the first two Divine Veins resonated in harmony. His body now felt heavier, denser, and vastly more powerful than before.","Then he began cultivating.","Max crushed the pale crystals first.","They dissolved into streams of radiant energy that entered his pores and flowed directly into his meridians. He followed by swallowing the two spirit fruits, whose rich essence spread through his organs like warm currents of liquid light. Finally, he opened the bottles of divine essence and drank them one after another.","At once, a tremendous amount of energy gathered inside him.","Ordinary cultivators would have needed to stop and carefully refine each layer of power, but Max’s body was no longer ordinary.","The complete Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline refined energy with frightening efficiency.","The 5000 Draconic Essences absorbed impurities and converted raw force into nourishment.","The 5000 Dragon Scales stabilized his physique.","The three opened Divine Veins pulled in energy like hungry stars.","Even so, Max’s body required an absurd amount of resources.","What would fill a lake for others only became a river for him.","He activated his cultivation art and drew every strand of power inward. Waves of energy circled around him again and again, compressed, refined, and pushed toward the barrier of the next level.","Hours passed within the Dimension of Time.","The pressure inside his dantian rose steadily.","The aura around him thickened.","Then, with a deep rumble, the final layer of resistance gave way.","Boom.","A surge of force erupted from Max’s body and swept across the white world like a shockwave.","His cultivation advanced.","Ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","Max slowly opened his eyes. They shone with deeper power than before.","He exhaled and let the remaining traces of energy settle.","\"If this were another cultivator...\" he murmured.","He knew the truth clearly.","With the same quantity of resources, many geniuses would have broken through two or even three levels. Some ordinary cultivators might have advanced even more.","But Max’s foundation was too monstrous.","Every realm of his required vast oceans of energy because each breakthrough strengthened not only cultivation, but also bloodline, body, Divine Veins, and countless hidden foundations.","What others gained in speed, he gained in depth.","And Max was fully satisfied with that.","A weak foundation that rose quickly meant little.","A terrifying foundation that rose steadily could shake worlds.","He stood up and clenched his fist lightly.","The aura of the ninth level of Law Awakening Realm flowed naturally through him, perfectly stable and without the slightest sign of instability.","Combined with the Vein of Strength and his completed bloodline, his combat power had risen far beyond what a simple level increase suggested.","Max smiled faintly.","\"One more step closer.\"","And he was far from finished preparing."]},{"number":1614,"title":"Chapter 1614: Gathering of True Disciples!","paragraphs":["After reaching the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm, Max carefully examined his condition and quickly came to a clear conclusion.","For the moment, he had reached the limit of what he could improve through direct cultivation.","He had already opened the third Divine Vein of the Seven Divine Veins, the Vein of Strength. Every remaining resource given by Lady Virelia had also been fully consumed to support his breakthrough into the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","His internal growth had not stopped forever, but it had paused until he obtained new opportunities.","\"My body is still strong enough to open the fourth Divine Vein,\" Max muttered to himself. \"The Vein of Speed should be within reach.\"","He clenched and relaxed his hand slowly, sensing the terrifying vitality in his flesh.","\"But I do not have enough resources.\"","Opening a Divine Vein required more than toughness. It demanded vast treasures, body-refining materials, and enough energy to force open another ancient gate hidden within the physique.","Max was not discouraged.","Instead, his eyes sharpened with anticipation.","\"The Smelting Trial should provide what I need.\"","He believed that an event jointly organized by powerful forces would contain inheritances, treasures, and rare resources beyond what ordinary cultivators could imagine. If fortune favored him there, opening the fourth Divine Vein and reaching the tenth level of Law Awakening Realm before the Cosmic Ascension Conference was entirely possible.","That thought alone was enough motivation.","\"Then I should use the remaining time to sharpen what I already have.\"","With that, Max rose from where he sat in the endless white world of the Dimension of Time.","\"Let us see whether the inheritance chambers have anything new for me.\"","He stepped forward and entered the Dimension of Flames for a new inheritance technique.","After leaving the Dimension of Flames, Max did not remain idle for even a moment. He continued moving through one dimension after another, entering the Dimension of Sword, the Dimension of Ice, the Dimension of Light, the Dimension of Lightning, the Dimension of Space, and several other worlds connected to his growing dimensional inheritance.","Each world possessed its own inheritance chamber, and within each chamber were techniques preserved from powerful beings of the past.","Once his choices were complete, Max returned to the Dimension of Time. The endless white world welcomed him with its usual silence, a place where one hour outside equaled one full year within. The moment he arrived, he began training without hesitation.","Days passed first, then months, and eventually years. Outside, only seven short days moved by. Inside, decades of relentless cultivation unfolded.","Max trained sword techniques until every slash, thrust, and counterattack became second nature. He practiced movement arts until he could transition from lightning speed to light acceleration and then into spatial displacement without even needing conscious thought.","He refined close combat methods until every punch and kick carried monstrous force through the awakened Vein of Strength.","He repeated elemental techniques countless times. He fused methods together, tore apart flaws, and reshaped inheritances into forms more suitable for himself. Fire techniques gained sharper killing intent.","Lightning arts became more efficient. Spatial methods became harder to predict. Whenever one cycle of training ended, another began immediately. There was no laziness, no wasted time, and no room for complacency.","By the time the seven days in the outside world had passed, decades had flowed for Max within the Dimension of Time. His cultivation realm remained at the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm, yet his true strength had increased dramatically.","His aura became deeper and more restrained, his instincts sharper, and his movements smoother. He now carried the calm pressure of someone who had tempered himself through long years of isolation and battle practice.","At last, Max slowly opened his eyes and exhaled a steady breath. He could clearly feel the connection between the outer world and the Dimension of Time shifting.","\"Seven days have passed,\" he muttered softly.","With that, he left the Dimension of Time and returned to his house.","The familiar training chamber greeted him once more. Max quickly washed away the dust of long training, took a proper bath, and changed into clean robes.","Afterward, he sat down and ate a meal in peace. Even something as ordinary as food felt refreshing after spending decades focused only on cultivation and combat.","Just then, a powerful voice echoed throughout the entirety of the Black Dragon Palace. It rolled through halls, courtyards, mountains, and training grounds like thunder striking the heavens.","\"All True Disciples, report at the Central Region of the Black Dragon Palace.\"","Max looked up calmly as the announcement repeated across the clan territory. He set down the last of his meal, stood from his seat, and adjusted his robes.","\"It is time,\" he said quietly.","He then stepped out of his house and headed toward the Central Region of the Black Dragon Palace.","When Max arrived at the Central Region of the Black Dragon Palace, the place was already bustling with activity.","The Central Region was one of the grandest areas within the clan territory, built upon a vast elevated platform surrounded by towering halls, training arenas, and black stone pillars carved with dragon patterns. Ancient banners fluttered in the wind, and layered formations shimmered faintly beneath the ground, revealing the importance of the place.","At the center of the platform, a group of true disciples had already gathered.","Max’s gaze swept over them once and immediately sharpened.","There were a little over thirty of them in total.","Some stood calmly with arms folded. Others conversed in low voices with familiar allies. A few sat cross-legged in meditation despite the gathering, as though using every moment to cultivate. Their expressions varied, but one thing was common among them all.","They were strong.","Very strong.","The aura coming from this group far surpassed that of ordinary disciples. These were the elite geniuses of the Black Dragon Clan, the younger generation chosen to represent the clan in major events.","Max silently observed them more carefully.","Most of them possessed cultivation beyond the fifth level of the Law Manifestation Realm. Several had already reached the seventh and eighth levels, their presence stable and imposing. A smaller number stood out even more, carrying dense pressure that caused those nearby to unconsciously keep some distance.","Those few had already reached the ninth and tenth levels of the Law Manifestation Realm."]},{"number":1615,"title":"Chapter 1615: Wonders of Chaos Fruit!","paragraphs":["Even Max’s eyes narrowed when he sensed them.","He had known the Black Dragon Clan would send its strongest talents, but seeing the group gathered together in one place still made the reality clearer.","These were not ordinary geniuses.","They were individuals who had grown within one of the Divine Realm’s weakest third rate force. Max could only imagine what sort of geniuses the 1st rate forces would have in the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","As Max looked at them, he recalled his earlier conversation with Lucia during their journey to Orion.","At that time, she had spoken of how nearly every genius in the Divine Realm sought to reach the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm before the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Now, standing here and seeing this scene, Max could not help but admit that her words had not been wrong.","Almost all true talents in the Divine Realm clearly aimed for that same benchmark.","And the Black Dragon Clan was no exception.","The disciples gathered before him were proof of it.","Many had likely spent years preparing for this period. They had tempered themselves, accumulated resources, and suppressed breakthroughs at key moments in order to arrive at the Smelting Trial in their strongest possible condition.","Max’s own cultivation at the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm stood noticeably lower than nearly everyone present.","Yet he did not feel pressured.","Instead, his interest only deepened.","The stronger the competition, the greater the value of surpassing it.","Some disciples soon noticed his arrival.","A few eyes immediately changed when they recognized him. Others began whispering quietly among themselves. Several looked openly curious, while some gazes carried challenge or doubt.","After all, Max’s reputation had spread recently, but reputation and cultivation were two different matters.","Many had heard stories.","Now they were seeing the man himself.","Max ignored their reactions and simply walked forward with calm steps before taking a place among the gathered disciples.","His aura remained restrained, giving little away.","Yet beneath that calm exterior, his eyes were bright.","The Smelting Trial had not even begun, and already he could feel the pressure of true competition gathering around him.","\"Max!\"","Soon after he joined the gathered disciples, Lucia and Isabella made their way toward him through the crowd.","Both women stood out immediately.","Lucia carried her usual composed confidence, while Isabella’s presence seemed sharper and brighter than before, as though something fundamental within her had changed.","Max’s eyes first landed on Lucia.","With only a brief sense of her aura, he could tell that her strength had advanced again. She had already reached the sixth level of the Law Manifestation Realm. Her cultivation was steady, refined, and clearly consolidated after the progress made during the past week.","Then his attention shifted toward Isabella.","The moment he sensed her properly, Max’s expression changed.","\"Huh?\"","He stared at her for a moment.","\"Isabella... your cultivation...\"","There was genuine shock in his voice.","Her aura was no longer that of someone at the Law Awakening Realm.","She had already reached the fifth level of the Law Manifestation Realm.","Max remembered clearly that the last time he had checked, Isabella had only been at the second level of the Law Awakening Realm. Yet in the span of a single week, she had crossed the entirety of the Law Refinement Realm and broken through multiple smaller realms beyond that.","Such progress was outrageous even by genius standards.","Isabella folded her arms and lifted her chin proudly.","\"Hehe, surprised?\"","Max looked at her silently for another second.","\"That is one way to put it.\"","Her smile widened.","\"When I was training last week, my Imperial Bloodline fully awakened.\"","The pride in her voice was impossible to miss.","\"The moment it awakened, my cultivation began breaking through repeatedly. The elders examined me afterward and said my strength should continue rising steadily until I eventually reach the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Max blinked once.","Even for him, hearing that was absurd.","A bloodline awakening that could continue pushing cultivation forward over time was the kind of blessing countless people would dream about.","\"Hehe, good for you,\" Max said with a smile that looked sincere enough on the surface.","Unfortunately for him, the faint trace of jealousy hidden in his eyes was far less convincing.","Lucia nearly laughed on the spot.","Isabella noticed it immediately and became even more pleased.","\"Hehe, thank you, Max.\"","Her voice then sounded directly in his mind through divine transmission.","\"Without the fruit you gave me, my Imperial Bloodline would not have awakened so soon.\"","Max’s expression shifted slightly.","She continued privately.","\"That fruit was miraculous. It not only transformed my foundation and gave me a divine body, but it also stimulated the dormant Imperial Bloodline within me.\"","Her tone carried real gratitude now.","\"Without it, I would likely have needed several more years before my bloodline fully awakened.\"","Max listened carefully.","The fruit she referred to was the Chaos Fruit he had once given her.","At the time, he had known it was precious and powerful, but even he had not expected it to trigger the awakening of a hidden bloodline.","\"I see,\" Max replied inwardly.","He glanced at Isabella again, this time with deeper understanding.","So that was the reason behind her explosive growth.","The Chaos Fruit had refined her body, strengthened her foundation, and accelerated the awakening of her Imperial Bloodline all at once.","No wonder her cultivation had risen like a flood breaking through a dam.","Lucia looked between the two of them suspiciously.","\"You two are being strangely quiet.\"","Max immediately smiled.","\"We were just appreciating how talented Isabella has become.\"","Isabella nodded seriously.","\"That is true.\"","Lucia narrowed her eyes, clearly unconvinced.","Still, she said nothing further.","Around them, several gathered disciples had also begun noticing Isabella’s transformed aura and discussing it in low voices. Others looked toward Max with renewed curiosity, wondering what kind of people were suddenly rising around him.","Max exhaled softly.","In only one week, both Lucia and Isabella had improved greatly."]},{"number":1616,"title":"Chapter 1616: Towards the Violet Star Palace!","paragraphs":["Max looked around the gathering once more.","A little over thirty true disciples stood assembled across the vast platform, each one carrying a powerful aura and the confidence of someone selected from among the clan’s younger generation.","Yet considering the size and reputation of the Black Dragon Clan, the number still felt smaller than expected.","He turned toward Lucia.","\"Is this all?\"","Lucia raised a brow.","\"All?\"","Max gestured lightly toward the gathered crowd.","\"I mean, is this the full number of true disciples in the Black Dragon Palace?\"","Lucia immediately understood what he meant and smiled.","\"No, of course not.\"","She folded her arms and glanced around the platform.","\"These are only the true disciples eligible to attend the Smelting Trial.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","\"There is a requirement?\"","\"Naturally.\"","Her tone carried the faint amusement of someone explaining something obvious.","\"The Smelting Trial is not a sightseeing trip. It is an event where talented disciples from many forces compete for opportunities, inheritances, and resources. Sending weaker disciples would only embarrass the clan and waste precious slots.\"","She then spoke more clearly.","\"For this trip, only true disciples whose cultivation has reached the fifth level of the Law Manifestation Realm or higher were selected.\"","Max nodded inwardly.","That explained the strength of nearly everyone present.","Those below that threshold had likely been excluded no matter how talented they were. The clan clearly intended to send only those with enough power to compete immediately.","Then Lucia looked at him with a teasing smile.","\"Of course...\"","\"You are an exception.\"","Max gave her a flat look.","\"I had guessed that.\"","Lucia laughed softly.","\"You should.\"","She stepped a little closer and lowered her voice.","\"You are going because of your status as the Saint of the Black Dragon Clan.\"","Several nearby disciples subtly reacted when they heard the title.","Though many already knew, hearing it spoken aloud still carried weight.","Lucia continued.","\"Your cultivation may still be at the Law Awakening Realm, but your position is different. You are no ordinary disciple being judged only by realm.\"","She glanced at him meaningfully.","\"The elders also know very well that your real combat strength cannot be measured by cultivation level alone.\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"So I was carried in through privilege.\"","Lucia snorted.","\"If it were only privilege, many people here would object.\"","Her gaze swept across the platform.","\"The reason no one openly complains is because they know you have already proven enough.\"","Max followed her gaze.","Several disciples were indeed looking toward him with mixed emotions. Some were curious. Some doubtful. Some openly competitive.","But none appeared dismissive enough to protest his presence.","Lucia then added one final remark.","\"Still, being the exception means something else.\"","\"What?\"","\"It means more people will watch you fail.\"","Max laughed softly.","\"And if I succeed?\"","Lucia’s smile deepened.","\"Then they will hate you even more.\"","Isabella, who had been listening nearby, nodded seriously.","\"That sounds accurate.\"","Max looked at the gathered elites of the Black Dragon Clan and then toward the distant palace towers beyond them.","Soon, powerful auras descended one after another over the Central Region.","The gathered true disciples immediately became serious as elders of the Black Dragon Clan appeared in the sky above the platform. Each elder stood calmly in midair, radiating strength and authority. Their arrival alone caused the atmosphere below to become tense and disciplined.","Then seven figures stepped forward at the front of the elders.","The moment they appeared, everyone recognized them instantly.","These were the heads of the Seven Main Families, the true ruling pillars of the Black Dragon Clan.","At the center stood Mathew Grimes, leader of the Grimes Family and the current highest authority overseeing the clan.","He stood with his hands behind his back, his presence steady and heavy like a mountain. His sharp eyes swept across the gathered disciples, causing the last whispers below to disappear.","When complete silence fell, he spoke.","\"The Smelting Trial begins now.\"","His calm voice echoed across the entire region.","\"You were chosen because you are the strongest of this generation. At Violet Star Palace, you will face geniuses from many forces. Some will underestimate you. Some will challenge you.\"","He paused briefly.","\"Do not forget that when they look at you, they see the Black Dragon Clan.\"","Many disciples straightened unconsciously.","\"Fight well. Win what you can. Protect the dignity of our clan.\"","His eyes sharpened.","\"And if anyone thinks we are easy to bully...\"","A faint pressure spread from him.","\"Prove them wrong.\"","The blood of many disciples stirred instantly.","Then Mathew raised one hand toward the sky.","\"Prepare to depart.\"","With his short speech finished, Mathew Grimes lifted one hand and waved it calmly through the air.","The space above the Central Region trembled.","A deep mechanical hum echoed across the platform as a massive star shuttle slowly emerged from a spatial fold high above them. Its appearance immediately drew every gaze upward.","The vessel was enormous.","Its body was forged from dark metallic material that shimmered with faint runic light. Layers of formations glowed across its surface like living constellations. Dragon patterns were carved along the outer hull, while black crystal wings extended from both sides, giving it the appearance of a celestial beast prepared to cross the void.","The pressure radiating from it made clear that this was no ordinary transport craft.","This was a true clan vessel built for long-distance star travel and protected against dangers of the cosmic void.","As it descended, powerful currents of wind swept across the platform. The shuttle then came to a stop above the ground, lowering a wide staircase of light toward the gathered disciples.","An elder stepped forward and announced firmly.","\"All selected true disciples, board immediately.\"","At once, movement began.","The gathered disciples advanced in orderly lines, one after another entering the star shuttle. Though many were proud geniuses, no one acted recklessly in front of the family heads and elders.","Max watched calmly for a moment before stepping forward.","Lucia moved beside him with her usual composed expression, while Isabella walked on his other side, carrying herself with visible confidence after the awakening of her Imperial Bloodline.","The three of them approached the staircase together.","As Max stepped onto the light bridge, he glanced once at the enormous vessel above and could not help admiring the Black Dragon Clan’s foundation. Even a weaker third-rate force still possessed strength and wealth far beyond ordinary powers.","They soon entered the shuttle interior.","Inside, the space was far larger than what the exterior suggested. Wide halls, rows of seats, cultivation rooms, private chambers, and formation chambers had all been built within. The walls glowed with protective runes, and dense spiritual energy flowed through the vessel like hidden rivers.","As Max, Lucia, and Isabella moved inward, Max’s eyes shifted toward another entrance.","There, Lady Virelia was also stepping into the shuttle along with several elders.","Their eyes met briefly.","Lady Virelia gave him a calm nod that carried both approval and warning.","Max returned the gesture respectfully.","It was clear she would be accompanying the younger generation to Violet Star Palace.","One by one, the remaining disciples continued boarding until the final selected genius entered the vessel. Soon after, the staircase of light withdrew, and the outer gates sealed with a heavy sound.","Inside the shuttle, the atmosphere turned expectant.","Some disciples closed their eyes to meditate. Some whispered among friends. Others looked outward through crystal viewing panels, eager for what awaited them.","Then the formations of the star shuttle activated fully.","Runes across the vessel ignited with brilliant light.","A low vibration spread through the floors.","Outside, the giant craft slowly rose into the air above the Central Region of the Black Dragon Palace. Elders and clan members below looked upward as the vessel ascended higher and higher.","Then, with a sudden burst of celestial light, the star shuttle shot forward.","It tore through the sky like a black star, crossed the clouds in an instant, and vanished into the endless sea of stars.","The journey to Violet Star Palace had begun."]},{"number":1617,"title":"Chapter 1617: Arriving at the Violet Star Palace!","paragraphs":["Hours passed as the star shuttle traveled through the cosmic void.","Protected by powerful runes and guided through stable star routes known only to major forces, the journey remained smooth. During that time, many disciples cultivated quietly, while others observed the passing wonders beyond the crystal viewing panels.","At last, the atmosphere inside the vessel shifted.","An elder announced that they had entered the territory of the Violet Star Realm.","Max stepped near one of the viewing panels and looked outside.","What he saw immediately drew his attention.","Before them stretched an enormous star realm filled with life and structure. Countless planets revolved through the vastness of space, each following precise celestial patterns.","Some worlds glowed with rich spiritual light. Others were wrapped in rings of mist or elemental storms. Massive floating fortresses drifted between planetary routes, while streams of star traffic moved in controlled lanes.","There were thousands of planets within the Violet Star Realm.","It was a realm far grander and more developed than many places Max had seen before.","Lucia stood beside him and spoke quietly.","\"The Violet Star Palace controls all of this.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The scale alone revealed why Violet Star Palace was considered one of the strongest third-rate forces in the Divine Realm.","Then he noticed something else.","Their star shuttle was not heading toward one of the ordinary planets.","It was flying toward the largest world in the entire realm.","That planet dominated the surrounding space like a celestial king among lesser stars. Its surface shimmered with oceans, continents, mountain chains, and giant cloud formations visible even from far away. Several moons circled it, while countless smaller transport vessels moved around its orbit like insects around a giant beast.","As the Black Dragon Clan shuttle approached the planetary vicinity, a ripple suddenly formed in the void ahead.","An old man appeared in front of the vessel as though space itself had opened to release him.","He wore violet robes embroidered with stars and carried no visible weapon. Yet the moment he appeared, every disciple inside felt immense pressure descend. His aura was calm and restrained, but even the slightest trace of it made many younger cultivators tense instinctively.","The shuttle slowed immediately.","Several elders of the Black Dragon Clan stepped forward respectfully.","The old man spoke in an indifferent voice.","\"What force are you from?\"","Mathew Grimes answered personally.","\"We are the Black Dragon Clan of the Verdant Sky Realm, invited for the Smelting Trial.\"","The old man’s gaze swept across the vessel for a brief moment, as though examining every person inside at once.","Then he nodded.","\"The identity is confirmed.\"","Without another wasted word, he turned and moved forward through the void.","\"Follow me.\"","The star shuttle resumed movement and followed behind him.","As they passed through layers of planetary defenses, Max sensed countless formations surrounding the great world. Some concealed the atmosphere, some controlled entry routes, and others radiated killing intent powerful enough to erase intruders instantly.","Soon they entered the planet itself.","The moment they crossed the atmosphere, Max’s eyes sharpened.","The scale of the world was astonishing.","This planet was vastly larger than any he had seen so far in the Divine Realm. Its mountain ranges stretched like continents of stone. Rivers looked like silver seas from above. Forests were so immense that some regions appeared as green oceans. Giant cities covered lands larger than ordinary kingdoms, linked by roads of light and flying formations.","Even the energy here was denser and purer than most planets he had visited.","The old man continued leading them across the skies.","Below, Max saw territories, ancient towers, floating islands, giant arenas, and countless cultivators moving through the air as though such scenes were everyday life.","\"This is only the outer regions,\" Lucia said softly.","Max looked at her.","\"If this is the outer region, then the core of Violet Star Palace must be absurd.\"","Lucia smiled faintly.","\"That is why they are one of the strongest 3rd rate forces.\"","The star shuttle continued forward under the guidance of the old man, crossing vast distances over landscapes so immense that even with their speed, minutes passed before one region fully ended and another began.","For the first time since arriving in the Divine Realm, Max truly felt the scale of a top third-rate force. It made him think if a top third rate force had such grandeur then what about the second rate forces and the firs rate forces.","The old man continued guiding them through the vast grounds of the Violet Star Palace’s outer region, his pace steady and unhurried. The deeper they traveled, the more astonished the disciples became.","Roads made from polished violet stone stretched in every direction, lined with glowing trees whose leaves shimmered faintly beneath the evening sky. Streams of spiritual water flowed beside the pathways, carrying a refreshing aura that calmed the mind the moment one drew near.","Soon, an enormous mansion-like palace rose before them.","It stood proudly atop a raised platform of white jade, its towering walls carved with stars, moons, and ancient furnace symbols that radiated age and dignity.","Rows of elegant pillars supported grand balconies, while lanterns of violet crystal hung from every corner, casting gentle light across the surroundings. The structure looked less like a temporary residence and more like the estate of a noble force.","Yet what shocked them even more was that this was not the only one.","As they drew closer, everyone noticed that similar mansion palaces were scattered across the entire region. Some stood beside lakes, others near gardens of spiritual herbs, while a few rested upon floating platforms connected by stone bridges.","At a glance, there were dozens of such residences, each grand enough to house an entire sect delegation.","Max narrowed his eyes as he observed the scene.","This was clearly a designated guest district of the Violet Star Palace, specially prepared for outside forces attending the Smelting Trial. The scale of it alone revealed how often large events were held here and how powerful the palace truly was. Even lodging for guests carried an aura of wealth that many lesser forces could never match."]},{"number":1618,"title":"Chapter 1618: Training!","paragraphs":["The old man finally stopped in front of one of the mansions and turned toward them.","\"You will stay here tonight.\"","His calm voice echoed lightly through the courtyard.","\"The Smelting Trial will officially begin tomorrow morning. Use this time to recover yourselves and prepare. Once dawn arrives, representatives from every invited force will gather.\"","He swept his gaze across the disciples, his expression remaining indifferent.","\"Do not wander recklessly. Certain areas of the Violet Star Palace are forbidden. Remain within the guest district unless summoned.\"","After speaking, the old man lightly waved his sleeve. The mansion gates slowly opened on their own, revealing a spacious inner courtyard, training grounds, and several luxurious chambers within.","\"Rest well.\"","With those final words, the old man stepped away and soon vanished into the distance like drifting smoke.","For a moment, silence remained.","Then many disciples inhaled sharply as they stared at their temporary residence with shining eyes.","\"This is where we stay for one night?\"","\"One night here is better than a year in some dormitories.\"","\"The Violet Star Palace truly deserves its reputation.\"","Even Lucia’s usually calm eyes flickered with surprise, while Isabella quietly admired the beauty of the courtyard.","Once inside the mansion, the disciples of the Black Dragon Clan were immediately shown the scale of Violet Star Palace’s hospitality.","The interior was vast and elegant, with halls lined by smooth crystal walls that reflected streams of soft violet light. Every room carried a rich concentration of spiritual energy, making even breathing feel refreshing. Spacious guest chambers had already been prepared, each furnished with cultivation mats, medicinal incense burners, and polished furniture crafted from rare spirit wood.","The younger disciples quickly dispersed.","Some entered secluded rooms to meditate and stabilize their cultivation in preparation for tomorrow. Others took out weapons and began polishing them with serious expressions. A few gathered in small groups, discussing rumors about the Smelting Trial and the geniuses who would participate from other forces. Nervousness and anticipation could be felt everywhere.","No one wished to embarrass the Black Dragon Clan tomorrow.","Max had only just entered the courtyard when a familiar voice sounded behind him.","\"Max. Lucia. Isabella. Follow me.\"","Lady Virelia stood there with her arms crossed, her long hair swaying gently as she looked at the three of them with sharp eyes. There was no trace of leisure on her face.","The three exchanged glances before immediately following.","She led them deeper into the mansion grounds until they arrived at a private training field located behind the residence. The area was surrounded by high formation walls, while the ground itself was forged from dark star metal capable of enduring heavy impacts. Ancient runes glowed faintly beneath the surface.","Lady Virelia turned around and spoke calmly.","\"You three will train a little before resting.\"","Lucia smiled faintly, already understanding what was coming.","Isabella blinked once, then looked toward Max with interest.","Lady Virelia pointed at the center of the field.","\"A three-way battle. Lucia and Isabella against Max.\"","Max almost thought he heard wrong.","\"Against both of them?\"","Lady Virelia’s lips curved slightly.","\"You heard correctly. If I am not wrong you will be targeted heavily tomorrow and so you might as well be prepared for this. But don’t use any techniques in this battle. Just use your basic attacks to fight. \"","Max exhaled slowly before stepping onto the field.","He knew very well that among the three, he was currently the weakest in direct cultivation. Lucia possessed deep and steady strength with frightening combat control, while Isabella’s Imperial Bloodline gave her a natural superiority that even elders respected.","Yet Max’s eyes did not waver.","The moment Lady Virelia waved her hand, the battle began.","Lucia moved first.","Her figure blurred like a phantom as she closed the distance instantly, her palm carrying compressed force of black flames strong enough to crack mountains. At the same time, Isabella raised one hand and released streams of black dragon flames that curved through the air like living serpents, sealing Max’s retreat paths.","A normal disciple would have been defeated in the opening breath.","But Max stepped forward instead of back.","Lightning exploded beneath his feet as he twisted through the narrow gap between the flames, then tilted his body just enough to avoid Lucia’s palm by a hair’s breadth. The force of her strike blasted the ground behind him apart.","Without hesitation, Max countered with a fist toward Lucia’s ribs.","Lucia blocked, but her eyes flickered slightly at the force hidden in the strike.","Before either could continue, Isabella descended from above with black fire condensed around her leg. Max raised both arms and received the blow head-on. The impact drove him several meters backward, his boots carving deep lines across the star metal floor.","Lady Virelia watched silently.","The battle only intensified.","Lucia attacked with relentless close-range precision. Isabella dominated the field with wide destructive pressure. Their teamwork was not intentional, yet both naturally cornered Max from two directions.","Still, Max refused to collapse.","He moved constantly, reading their attacks through his Dimensional Sovereign Body. He used speed to break angles, timing to create openings, and ruthless counters whenever either underestimated him. Several times he was struck and sent reeling, yet every time he rose instantly and charged back in.","At one point, Lucia’s palm locked onto his chest while Isabella’s flame spear descended from behind.","Even Lady Virelia narrowed her eyes.","Yet Max suddenly spun low, using Lucia’s incoming force to redirect himself sideways. Her palm missed by inches while Isabella’s spear passed through the space Max had occupied. Max then drove an elbow into Lucia’s shoulder and kicked Isabella backward before leaping away.","Lucia laughed softly.","\"You are such a tough guy to fight.\"","Isabella’s usually calm eyes shone brighter.","\"He is troublesome.\"","Minutes turned into an hour.","Sweat covered the three geniuses. Cracks spread across the training field. Shockwaves repeatedly slammed into the barrier walls.","Yet one fact remained clear.","Though Max was the weakest in realm and raw power, he had not been defeated.","He stood there breathing heavily, bruised and battered, but still upright. His eyes burned hotter than before.","Lady Virelia finally raised a hand, ending the match.","The field fell silent.","She looked at Max for a long moment before speaking.","\"Good.\"","That single word from her carried more praise than a hundred compliments.","Then she turned toward all three.","\"This is enough for now. Go ahead and rest you three.\"","Max wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth and smiled faintly before heading to his respective room to rest.","Only Lady Virelia remained standing on the training ground."]},{"number":1619,"title":"Chapter 1619: Lady Virelia’s Worry!","paragraphs":["The night wind passed quietly through the shattered field, carrying traces of scorched stone and scattered spiritual energy. Around her lay the aftermath of the battle. Cracked star metal flooring, faded rune marks, and the lingering pressure of three young geniuses who had fought with everything they had.","Max, Lucia, and Isabella had already withdrawn to recover.","Lady Virelia alone stayed behind, her sharp eyes fixed on the broken ground where Max had stood.","\"His combat awareness is excellent,\" she murmured softly. \"But will that alone be enough to stand against the true monsters gathered here?\"","Her voice was calm, yet a trace of concern hid beneath it.","She had deliberately arranged the three-way battle for one purpose.","It was never meant to test Max’s raw strength.","She already knew he lacked the cultivation foundation to dominate opponents of the same generation through power alone. What she wanted to witness was his instinct, his adaptability, and the speed of his decisions when trapped under pressure from multiple enemies.","And the result had exceeded expectations.","Max had stood his ground against Lucia and Isabella simultaneously. He had read openings that others would never notice. He had evaded fatal attacks by the narrowest margins. He had turned enemy momentum into his own advantage again and again.","That kind of battle sense could not be taught easily.","It was the experience of someone who had fought countless battles.","Yet Lady Virelia’s expression did not relax.","Because she understood something Max perhaps did not yet fully grasp.","Lucia and Isabella were talented, but among the countless geniuses invited to the Smelting Trial, they belonged to the lower ranks of this gathering. Strong enough to shine in ordinary places, yet not enough to terrify the stage that would open tomorrow.","The real opponents were different.","Those monsters stood at the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm. They had deeper foundations, stronger bloodlines, greater resources, and years of brutal tempering behind them. Many of them could suppress lesser geniuses with a single move. Some likely possessed abilities so absurd that even elders would take notice.","Against such figures, combat awareness alone might not be enough.","Lady Virelia slowly looked toward the distant sky where stars glimmered above the Violet Star Palace.","\"I can only hope the Smelting Trial is not decided purely by cultivation realm or brute strength,\" she said quietly. \"If it values battle sense, judgment, and adaptability... then he still has a chance.\"","She knew large trials often contained strange tests.","Some measured comprehension. Some tested control. Some rewarded courage under pressure. Others threw participants into chaotic battlefields where instinct mattered more than realm.","If tomorrow favored that kind of environment, Max could shock everyone.","If not, then the road would become dangerous.","After standing there for several moments, Lady Virelia finally turned and walked back toward the mansion.","Her footsteps were slow, thoughtful.","When she entered her chamber, the doors closed softly behind her.","The night deepened.","And across the vast guest district of the Violet Star Palace, countless geniuses rested in silence, each believing themselves destined to rise tomorrow.","Yet somewhere within the vast territory of the Violet Star Palace, beneath the calm surface of this grand gathering, a conspiracy was already taking shape.","Far from the guest mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan, another luxurious residence stood quietly among the many scattered across the district. From the outside, it appeared no different from the others. Elegant walls, glowing crystal lanterns, silent guards stationed in hidden positions. Nothing about it suggested danger.","But inside one of its sealed chambers, the atmosphere was cold and sinister.","The room was dimly lit, with formation barriers layered across every wall to block sound, aura, and spiritual probing. At the center stood a black table engraved with communication runes. Above it floated a holographic projection of a young woman, her figure formed from streams of pale blue light.","She was beautiful.","But the beauty in her face was overshadowed by the malice in her eyes.","Standing before the projection was a young man dressed in rich robes embroidered with silver stars. His eyebrows were sharp like blades, his features handsome, and his bearing carried the confidence of someone long accustomed to being admired.","The holographic woman spoke first.","\"Have the people from the Black Dragon Clan arrived?\"","Her tone was casual, yet an undercurrent of impatience hid beneath it.","The young man clasped his hands behind his back and smiled faintly.","\"They arrived not long ago.\"","The woman’s expression shifted instantly.","\"And Max?\"","The moment she spoke that name, the pleasant mask on her face twisted into naked hatred. Her eyes darkened, and even through the projection, the venom in her emotions was obvious.","The young man noticed this and found it amusing.","\"He is here as well.\"","\"Good.\"","The woman’s lips slowly curled upward into a cruel smile that carried no warmth at all.","\"I do not care what methods you use. I do not care whether it is during the trial, outside the arena, or through others.\"","Her voice became colder with every word.","\"I want Max dead.\"","The young man’s eyes narrowed slightly.","This was no small request. Killing a participant during an event hosted by the Violet Star Palace was dangerous, especially with so many forces present. But he remained calm, waiting for what came next.","The woman leaned forward slightly within the hologram.","\"In return, I will personally ensure you are carried into the top one hundred of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The room fell silent for a breath.","Then the young man laughed softly.","Top one hundred.","That ranking represented glory beyond imagination. Countless geniuses across regions would kill for such an opportunity. To secure it through one transaction was worth almost any risk.","\"It is a deal then.\"","He smiled as he spoke, confidence and greed shining in his eyes.","The woman’s twisted expression softened into satisfaction.","\"I hope to hear good news tomorrow.\"","Her laughter rang through the chamber, sharp and cruel like glass scraping metal.","A moment later, the holographic figure dissolved into scattered light.","The room darkened once more.","That woman was none other than Mira, daughter of the Master of the Sword God Palace, the same arrogant princess whom Max had humiliated and taught a bitter lesson within the secret domain of Orion.","The young man remained where he stood, eyes gleaming with calculation.","\"To enter the top one hundred of the Cosmic Ascension Conference...\"","He chuckled and slowly clenched his fist.","\"And all I need to do is kill a genius from one of the weakest third-rate forces.\"","His smile gradually became vicious.","\"What a generous bargain.\"","Outside the mansion, the night remained peaceful.","Inside, murder had already been decided."]},{"number":1620,"title":"Chapter 1620: Celestial Forge Pavilion!","paragraphs":["The next day arrived beneath a sky of brilliant violet light.","As the first rays of dawn spread across the enormous planet of the Violet Star Palace, the entire guest district came alive. Doors opened one after another. Disciples emerged in fresh robes, weapons at their sides, eyes sharp with anticipation. Elders moved with calm expressions, yet even they carried a faint seriousness today.","This was the day the Smelting Trial would begin.","Within the Black Dragon Clan residence, Max stepped out after a night of cultivation. He appeared very calm and composed. Lucia and Isabella soon joined him, both looking refreshed and composed.","Lady Virelia appeared last.","Her gaze swept over the younger generation before she spoke only one sentence.","\"Do your best out there.\"","Then she turned and led them out.","Across the guest district, similar scenes were unfolding in every mansion. Delegations from one third-rate force after another emerged and headed toward the central grounds of the Violet Star Palace. Some traveled in groups with imposing discipline.","Others laughed loudly, radiating confidence. A few walked in silence, their auras restrained so deeply that they felt more dangerous than those who flaunted power.","As the Black Dragon Clan group advanced, Max observed everything carefully.","There were disciples wearing crimson robes marked by blazing sun emblems. Others wore silver armor etched with beast symbols. Some carried giant sabers, while others floated above the ground without even walking. Bloodlines, physiques, strange energies, and hidden killing intent could be sensed everywhere.","This gathering was far beyond anything an ordinary competition could compare to.","Soon, they arrived at the central square.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The square was colossal, so vast that entire cities from mortal worlds could fit within it. The ground was paved with star-patterned jade tiles that shimmered faintly under the sunlight.","Towering statues of ancient experts stood around the perimeter, each one radiating a pressure that made weaker cultivators instinctively lower their heads.","At the far end rose a massive platform suspended above the square, clearly meant for the Violet Star Palace elders and trial overseers.","And the square was already filled.","Thousands upon thousands of young geniuses from different third-rate forces had gathered there, standing in clusters according to their factions. Every direction was packed with youth at the peak of talent, each one carrying pride, ambition, and the desire to rise above the rest.","The atmosphere was tense.","Invisible clashes of aura spread constantly through the crowd as disciples sized one another up. Some looked arrogant. Some calm. Some eager for battle. Others hid themselves like crouching beasts waiting for the right moment to strike.","The younger generation stood together at the center of the square.","Meanwhile, the elders of each force gathered at a distance behind their disciples, separated from the main crowd. They formed their own rows, speaking quietly among themselves while observing the young talents with measuring eyes.","Lady Virelia stood with the Black Dragon Clan elders, arms crossed, her gaze fixed on Max and the others.","Max, Lucia, and Isabella took their place among the Black Dragon Clan geniuses.","For the first time, Max truly felt it.","This was not a local contest.","This was a gathering of countless stars.","And every single one of them wished to shine brighter than the rest.","It was then a huge platform appeared in the air. The sheer size of the platform was massive.","The massive square gradually sank into complete silence as every gaze turned toward the platform above. The restless energy that had filled the crowd moments ago disappeared almost instantly.","Thousands of geniuses from different third-rate forces stood upright with solemn expressions, while even the elders gathered at the rear became visibly more respectful.","A powerful presence had arrived.","High above the platform, dozens of figures descended from the sky with calm and measured steps. None of them displayed any flashy movement technique, yet each stride carried them across hundreds of meters as though space willingly shortened beneath their feet.","They wore deep azure robes embroidered with golden threads, and on the chest of every robe was the same insignia, a celestial furnace surrounded by nine revolving stars.","The moment they landed, the atmosphere of the entire square changed.","Max narrowed his eyes immediately. These people were on a completely different level from the experts he had sensed since entering the Violet Star Palace. Their auras were restrained to the extreme, but that very restraint made them more dangerous.","At the center of the group stood an old man with silver hair flowing down his back. His face was lined by age, yet his posture was straight as a spear. His eyes were deep and steady, carrying the weight of countless years. He did not release the slightest pressure, but simply standing there made everyone below instinctively pay attention.","He stepped forward.","His voice was not loud, yet it spread across the colossal square with perfect clarity.","\"Welcome, juniors of the various forces, and greetings to the elders who have escorted them here.\"","\"I am Elder Cael Varion of the Celestial Forge Pavilion.\"","The moment the name was spoken, visible ripples moved through the crowd. Some younger disciples drew in sharp breaths, while several elders lowered their heads slightly in greeting.","The Celestial Forge Pavilion was not a force that could be compared to ordinary regional powers. It was a genuine second-rate force whose influence stretched across many star realms. It controlled trade routes, inheritance grounds, forging domains, and countless subordinate factions.","The Violet Star Palace itself, mighty in the eyes of many, was merely one of the prominent third-rate forces under its sphere of influence.","Elder Cael allowed the murmurs to settle before continuing.","\"This Smelting Trial is organized by the Violet Star Palace under the supervision of our Celestial Forge Pavilion. It exists to temper promising juniors, reveal hidden talent, and prepare worthy participants for the path ahead.\"","His calm gaze swept across the sea of young cultivators below.","\"Some among you have come for fame. Some seek resources. Some desire to test yourselves against rivals from distant realms. Others hope to gain good rankings for the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","His tone grew firmer.","\"Whatever your reason may be, only those who prove themselves here shall move forward.\"","The square became even quieter after those words."]},{"number":1621,"title":"Chapter 1621: Weapon Master Trial!","paragraphs":["Then Elder Cael raised his right hand slowly.","Space behind him trembled. A moment later, dozens of enormous stone gates emerged from the air itself and settled above the platform. Each gate bore the carved image of a different weapon, and ancient martial intent seeped from every surface.","There was a sword gate sharp enough to make onlookers feel cut by sight alone. A spear gate stood tall and domineering like a battlefield general. A sabre gate radiated savage ferocity. There were gates for bows, daggers, staffs, hammers, axes, chains, and many other weapon paths.","The sight alone stirred the blood of the gathered disciples.","\"The first trial,\" Elder Cael declared, \"is the Weapon Master Trial.\"","A wave of anticipation spread through the younger generation.","\"This is not a trial of brute force. It is a trial of perception, affinity, comprehension, and martial foundation.\"","He extended his hand toward the floating gates.","\"Within each gate lies a Weapon Hall. Every disciple present may choose the weapon path most suited to them. Once inside, you will encounter remnants, inheritances, and imprints left behind by masters who once walked that path.\"","The expressions of many geniuses changed immediately.","Even obtaining a glimpse of advanced weapon techniques was a rare blessing for disciples from third-rate forces. To receive direct exposure to remnants left by true masters was an opportunity that might never come twice in a lifetime.","Elder Cael continued in an even tone.","\"How much you gain will depend entirely on yourselves. If your talent is lacking, you may emerge having learned nothing. If your foundation is steady, you may deepen your understanding significantly. If your perception is extraordinary, one day inside may change the direction of your weapon path forever.\"","His final sentence struck the hearts of many like thunder.","Lucia’s eyes sharpened instantly.","Isabella’s expression grew more serious than before.","Even Lady Virelia, standing among the elders, revealed surprise she did not bother to hide.","Max fixed his gaze on the sword gate.","Elder Cael spoke once more.","\"You will have one full day within the Weapon Master Trial. When the gates close, your gains shall be assessed through your performance and resonance.\"","He slowly lowered his hand, and the gates emitted a low ancient hum.","\"Now step forward.\"","\"Choose your path and show whether you are worthy of being called geniuses.\"","The moment Elder Cael lowered his hand, the dozens of ancient gates suspended above the platform began to tremble.","Deep rumbling sounds echoed through the vast square as lines of light spread across their surfaces like awakening veins. Ancient runes that had remained dormant for who knew how many years suddenly ignited one after another.","Sword intent, spear momentum, sabre ferocity, hammer weight, bow precision, and countless other martial auras surged outward from the gates, causing the air itself to feel heavy.","Then, with a thunderous vibration that shook the square, the gates opened.","What lay beyond them was not visible clearly from the outside. Each entrance was covered by a swirling layer of light that concealed the internal world within. Yet the aura spilling from every passage was enough to make hearts race wildly.","The gathered geniuses no longer remained calm.","One after another, disciples from the various third-rate forces rushed forward according to the weapon paths they cultivated. Some moved with excitement, while others advanced with measured confidence. Many carried expressions of fierce determination, knowing this opportunity might decide their future.","A tall young man wearing crimson armor laughed loudly as he charged toward the sabre gate with several companions behind him. A graceful woman in silver robes floated toward the bow gate, her long fingers already resting on the string of her spirit bow.","Two burly disciples carrying giant hammers strode toward the hammer gate like walking mountains. Everywhere one looked, talented youths were choosing the road most suited to them.","The square that had been packed with people moments ago quickly became a flowing tide of movement.","Among the Black Dragon Clan group, Lucia glanced toward Max and Isabella.","Her usually calm face carried a faint smile.","\"It seems we part here for now.\"","She looked first at Max.","\"Do not embarrass yourself inside.\"","Then she turned toward Isabella.","\"And do not become too arrogant if you gain more than others.\"","Isabella gave a soft snort, though the corner of her lips lifted slightly.","Lucia then gave them a nod.","\"Good luck to both of you.\"","Without waiting for a reply, her figure flashed forward.","She moved with clean and powerful steps, weaving through the crowd before arriving at the spear gate. The ancient gate seemed to react faintly to her presence, emitting a low hum. Then Lucia stepped through the curtain of light and disappeared within.","Max watched her vanish before shifting his gaze toward the sword gate in the distance.","\"She is uses a spear?\" He was surprised a bit seeing her entering the spear gate. He certainly didn’t see her using any weapon so far.","Beside him, Isabella was already looking in the same direction.","For a moment, neither spoke.","The sword gate towered high above the others nearby, carved with countless overlapping blade marks that seemed to contain the history of endless battles. A chilling yet noble sword intent drifted from within, making many sword cultivators instinctively straighten their backs.","Isabella finally spoke, her voice calm and proud.","\"Try not to fall too far behind once inside.\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"You should worry about yourself.\"","A spark of challenge flashed in Isabella’s eyes.","Then the two moved at the same time.","They crossed the square side by side, drawing glances from nearby disciples who could sense both their unusual presence. One carried the regal aura of the Imperial Bloodline. The other possessed a quiet sharpness that made others uneasy.","When they reached the entrance, the sword gate trembled subtly as though acknowledging new arrivals.","Max looked once at the swirling light beyond the threshold.","Without hesitation, he stepped forward.","Isabella entered at the same instant beside him.","Their figures vanished into the sword gate as the light swallowed them whole."]},{"number":1622,"title":"Chapter 1622: Combat Puppets!","paragraphs":["Once Max entered the sword gate, the scenery around him changed instantly.","The grand square of the Violet Star Palace disappeared as if it had never existed. The sounds of thousands of people, the pressure of gathered geniuses, and the towering gates all dissolved into nothingness.","A violent current of spatial energy swept past him, making the world blur for a brief moment before everything stabilized again.","When Max opened his eyes fully, he found himself standing alone in a vast arena.","It was an enormous circular battlefield, so wide that even large-scale wars could have been fought within it. The ground beneath his feet was forged from dark metallic stone covered in countless intersecting sword marks.","Some were shallow scratches, while others were deep clefts that radiated lingering sharpness. Each scar on the arena floor seemed to tell the story of battles fought long ago.","Towering walls rose around the perimeter, their surfaces engraved with ancient formations that glowed faintly from time to time.","Above stretched a gray and endless sky with no sun, no stars, and no visible limit. The entire place felt detached from the outside world, like a sealed dimension created purely for testing those who entered.","There was no one else present.","There were no spectators, no rivals, and no elders watching from afar.","Only silence and pressure.","Max’s eyes moved carefully across the arena as his instincts sharpened. This place was not ordinary. The aura within it was cold, structured, and devoid of any unnecessary emotion. Everything here existed for a single purpose.","To judge.","At that exact moment, a pillar of pale light descended from the sky and enveloped him completely.","Max’s body tensed at once, but he quickly realized the light carried no hostility. Instead, it passed through him in layers, scanning every inch of his body.","It moved through flesh, meridians, bloodline, dantian, and aura with frightening precision, as though an unseen intelligence was dissecting his strength without touching him.","A cold mechanical voice then echoed through the arena.","[Participant detected.]","[Beginning cultivation assessment.]","The pale light brightened for several breaths before fading away.","[Assessment complete.]","[Participant cultivation realm: Ninth Level of Law Awakening Realm.]","Max’s gaze sharpened immediately.","This was no ordinary rune formation. It was an advanced artificial trial system capable of detecting cultivation and tailoring challenges accordingly. The foundation required to create something like this was terrifying. Even many great forces would not possess such means.","Then glowing lines of text formed in the air before him.","[Beginning Supreme Tier Assessment]","[Sword Trial Phase One]","[Trial Type: Combat Evaluation]","[Participant Realm: Ninth Level of Law Awakening Realm]","[Assigned Opponents: 100 Combat Puppets]","[Opponent Strength Standard: Five Levels Above Participant]","[Opponent Current Realm: Fifth Level of Law Refinement Realm]","Max read every line without blinking.","Law Refinement Realm was already beyond his current realm, and these puppets would not merely be one level higher. They would stand five full levels above him within that realm. For most so-called geniuses, such a trial would be impossible.","The glowing text shifted once more.","[Reward Determination Rule]","[The number of Combat Puppets defeated will determine the level of Sword Inheritance granted for comprehension.]","[Low Performance: Basic Sword Inheritance]","[Qualified Performance: Advanced Sword Inheritance]","[Outstanding Performance: Elite Sword Inheritance]","[Exceptional Performance: Supreme Sword Inheritance]","A final line then appeared slowly.","[If unable to conquer, survive.]","Max looked at the message for several moments before a faint smile formed on his face.","So this trial did not care about status, background, or bloodline. It only cared about results. If one wanted a greater inheritance, one had to seize it through battle.","Suddenly, the arena trembled.","At the far edges of the battlefield, one hundred stone doors rose from the ground in a perfect circle. Their surfaces split open one after another with deep metallic sounds that echoed across the empty arena.","From within them emerged figures clad in black armor.","They were humanoid in shape, tall and broad-shouldered, with expressionless metal faces and eyes glowing crimson. In each of their hands was a sword of identical design. Their movements were smooth, disciplined, and unnaturally precise.","One after another, they stepped forward until all one hundred stood on the battlefield.","Then their auras erupted together.","The pressure of a hundred enemies at the Fifth Level of Law Refinement Realm surged outward like a violent storm. Even the air seemed to grow heavier beneath their combined presence.","Yet Max did not retreat a single step.","He took out his sword flickering with severing sword concept.","Seven colored lightning flickered faintly around his fingers as battle intent rose steadily from his body. His gaze locked onto the advancing puppets without the slightest trace of fear.","He understood that this battle would decide the quality of inheritance he received.","If he performed poorly, he would leave with scraps.","If he dominated, he would seize a sword legacy that countless geniuses would envy.","Max tightened his grip on the hilt.","A dangerous smile gradually appeared on his face as he stared at the army before him.","If the inheritance was decided by kills, then he had only one goal.","He would take the highest reward this arena could offer.","With that the one hundred Combat Puppets began to move.","They did not rush forward like mindless machines. Their steps were measured, synchronized, and terrifyingly disciplined. The first ranks advanced directly toward Max while the outer lines curved outward to surround him from both flanks. Rear units held position with swords raised, clearly prepared to strike the instant an opening appeared.","It was the formation of an army.","Max immediately understood that this trial was not merely testing raw strength. It was testing how a participant handled overwhelming pressure, superior cultivation, and coordinated enemies all at once.","Yet there was no fear in his eyes.","Instead, a dangerous calmness spread across his face.","He inhaled slowly, and in the next instant, seven-colored lightning erupted from within his body.","The seven currents merged around Max’s body, coursing through his flesh, bones, meridians, and bloodline.","The Storm King’s Inheritance had awakened.","His muscles tightened with explosive force. His senses sharpened dramatically. Even the air around him began to distort under the violent pressure of divine lightning.","Cracks spread beneath his feet.","Then Max vanished.","A thunderous explosion rang across the arena as he crossed the battlefield in a single burst of speed. Before the leading puppets could fully react, Max appeared before them and swung his sword in a simple horizontal slash.","There was no profound sword art behind the strike.","There was no dazzling inheritance technique.","It was merely a basic sword slash taught to beginners.","Yet in Max’s hands, enhanced by seven-colored lightning and terrifying timing, that ordinary strike cut through three puppet necks in one motion. Their armored heads spun into the air before their bodies even realized they had died."]},{"number":1623,"title":"Chapter 1623: Perfect Rating!","paragraphs":["The broken corpses had not yet fallen when Max moved again.","He stepped diagonally and thrust forward.","A plain and direct stab pierced through the chest core of one puppet, then continued through the body of another standing behind it. Sparks and shattered metal burst outward as both collapsed.","He twisted his wrist.","A common upward cut rose from below and split the next puppet from waist to shoulder.","Every movement he used was simple.","Slash.","Thrust.","Parry.","Step.","Cut.","Turn.","Reverse strike.","Nothing he displayed was glamorous. They were the most fundamental sword motions imaginable.","But the terrifying truth was that Max had mastered those basics to a frightening degree.","He knew exactly where joints were weakest. He knew precisely when enemy momentum could not be withdrawn. He understood angles, timing, spacing, rhythm, and pressure with instinctive clarity.","The Combat Puppets immediately responded.","The rear ranks advanced while the side units collapsed inward. Dozens of swords attacked at once, sealing escape routes from every direction.","Max’s eyes flashed sharply.","Seven-colored lightning surged again.","His body accelerated another level as he moved through the incoming storm of blades with impossible precision. One sword passed so close it sliced a strand of hair. Another scraped sparks from his sleeve. A third struck the ground where he had stood an instant earlier.","Yet not one landed cleanly.","Then Max retaliated.","He parried one sword just enough to redirect it into another puppet’s shoulder. Before either recovered, he stepped between them and delivered a basic downward chop that split both helms at once.","He pivoted low, sweeping his blade across ankle joints and toppling three puppets together. Before they hit the ground, he stabbed downward through each core in succession.","He leaped backward, then launched forward again like living thunder.","Ten puppets fell.","Twenty followed soon after.","The arena floor became littered with broken armor, severed limbs, and shattered swords.","Still, the remaining puppets showed no fear.","Their formation changed again, this time dividing into smaller combat squads. Some attacked directly while others attempted to restrict Max’s movement and exhaust his stamina.","Max laughed softly as battle intent burned hotter in his eyes.","This was exactly what he wanted.","He no longer moved like a normal swordsman.","He moved like a storm unleashed across the battlefield.","Sometimes he burst forward with raw speed and decapitated enemies before they could blink. Sometimes he halted abruptly, allowing attacks to pass before stepping into the blind angle of multiple opponents. Sometimes he used one fallen puppet’s body as cover, then stabbed through both corpse and enemy behind it.","Every strike remained basic.","Every strike remained efficient.","Every strike killed.","Thirty became fifty.","Fifty became seventy.","The thunder of seven-colored lightning never ceased as Max carved through enemies far above his realm through pure combat mastery.","By the time only twenty remained, his eyes were flashing with intense battle intent. There was no sign of any exhaustion from him.","His current combat power was around the peak of Law Refinement Realm and even beyond it. These 5th level Law Refinement Combat Puppets didn’t stand a chance against him at all.","The final twenty puppets spread into a perfect killing ring around him.","Then they attacked simultaneously.","Sword lights descended from every direction, sealing sky, ground, and all lines of retreat.","Max planted one foot firmly into the cracked arena floor.","Seven-colored lightning exploded outward from his body in a radiant wave, illuminating every broken corpse scattered across the battlefield.","Then he moved.","He stepped forward and unleashed nothing but a flawless chain of basic sword attacks.","A slash took one throat.","A thrust pierced another core.","A turn placed him behind two enemies.","An upward cut split one open.","A reverse stab ended another.","A downward strike crushed helm and body alike.","His movements flowed one into another without pause, smooth as water and violent as thunder.","Within moments, the ring collapsed entirely.","The last Combat Puppet remained standing for a single breath with its sword still raised.","Then a crack spread from the top of its helmet to the center of its body.","Its frame split apart and crashed onto the ground in two halves.","Silence descended over the arena.","All one hundred Combat Puppets had been destroyed.","Max stood alone amid a battlefield of wreckage, his sword lowered at his side while faint strands of seven-colored lightning still danced around his body. Broken armor covered the arena like fallen leaves after a divine tempest.","\"I wonder what sort of sword art I would get to comprehend with this.\" Max muttered, very excited about the result of this small assessment.","Silence lingered across the ruined arena.","For several moments, nothing happened.","Then the gray sky above began to vibrate.","Ancient runes appeared one after another in the empty air, rotating in vast circles above the arena. Pillars of pale light descended around Max, scanning the battlefield, counting every destroyed puppet, every strike mark, every fluctuation of energy, and perhaps even the method by which victory had been achieved.","The same cold mechanical voice echoed once more.","[Combat Evaluation Complete.]","[Scanning participant performance.]","[Total Combat Puppets Assigned: 100]","[Total Combat Puppets Destroyed: 100]","[Participant Survival Status: Optimal]","[Damage Sustained: Minimal]","[Energy Efficiency: Exceptional]","[Weapon Technique Usage: Foundational Sword Arts]","[Combat Adaptability: Extraordinary]","[Cross-Realm Battle Capability: Beyond Standard Parameters]","Max narrowed his eyes slightly as he read each line.","The system was not merely counting kills. It was measuring everything, from efficiency to technique selection to how far he exceeded expected limits.","The glowing messages paused for a moment.","Then the entire arena shook.","A deeper light erupted from the sky, brighter than before, causing even the shattered remains on the ground to tremble. New lines of text appeared in enormous characters before Max.","[Standard Reward Tiers:]","[Low Performance]","[Qualified Performance]","[Outstanding Performance]","[Exceptional Performance]","The messages faded one by one.","For a brief moment, the arena became completely dark.","Then golden light burst forth like a rising sun.","The mechanical voice, which had remained emotionless until now, seemed to carry the faintest trace of distortion.","[Unregistered Result Detected.]","[Participant Performance Has Exceeded Existing Standard Reward Tiers.]","[Recalculating...]","[Recalculating...]","[Recalculation Failed.]","Max’s expression changed slightly.","Even the trial system could not process the result properly.","Then the sky split open with blinding radiance as the final judgment descended.","[Final Performance Rating: PERFECT]","The word hung above the arena in colossal golden letters, illuminating everything below.","A heavy pressure spread through the battlefield, not hostile, but ancient and dignified, as though the creators of this inheritance space themselves had acknowledged the result.","The system voice continued.","[Perfect Performance is not included within the four announced public reward tiers.]","[Perfect Performance is reserved for participants who achieve total domination beyond projected limits.]","[Conditions met:]","[Destroyed all assigned opponents.]","[Won across multiple realm disparity.]","[Displayed supreme combat awareness.]","[Used basic sword arts to surpass advanced parameters.]","[No external assistance detected.]","[Eligibility Confirmed.]","Max slowly exhaled as the golden word reflected in his eyes.","So the four reward tiers announced outside had not been the complete truth.","There had always been a hidden fifth level.","Not for ordinary geniuses.","Not even for excellent ones.","Only for someone who completely shattered the expectations of the trial itself.","The system messages shifted once more.","[Reward Upgrade Initiated.]","[Perfect Grade Sword Inheritance Preparing.]","[Highest Comprehension Chamber Unlocking.]","The arena floor trembled as all the broken puppet remains dissolved into streams of light. Ancient sword marks across the battlefield began to glow one after another, and in the center of the arena, a massive stone platform slowly rose from below.","Atop the platform stood a portal."]},{"number":1624,"title":"Chapter 1624: To a different world!","paragraphs":["Just as Max neared the portal atop the platform, trial messages appeared once more before Max.","[Perfect Grade Sword Inheritance Chamber Unlocked.]","[Enter Portal to Receive Reward.]","Max looked once at the portal, then at the shattered arena around him.","He had fought for this opportunity.","Without hesitation, he stepped forward and entered.","The moment his body crossed the threshold, a sharp current of energy swept through him. The world blurred again, yet this time the sensation was different from the previous teleportation. It felt deeper, older, as though he were being carried not through space alone, but through layers of time and history.","Then everything stabilized.","Max opened his eyes and found himself standing in an entirely different world.","The sky above was bright and vast, painted in shades of pale blue and silver. Gentle winds moved across an endless plain covered in short green grass. Mountains could be seen far in the distance, while rivers of crystal water cut across the land like shining ribbons.","Yet what caught Max’s attention first was not the scenery.","It was the people.","Many humans could be seen roaming across the plain. Some wore simple robes. Others carried swords on their backs. A few sat cross-legged in meditation. Their appearances varied greatly, but each one carried the aura of a swordsman.","Even stranger, none of them seemed to notice Max’s sudden arrival.","They moved naturally, spoke among themselves, trained, walked, and lived as though he were invisible.","An illusion world.","Or perhaps a preserved memory realm.","’Is this a real world or an illusion created by the trial?’ Max wondered as he looked around. His Dimensional Sovereign Body couldn’t determine if it was real or illusion which made Max think that this might be real world and he was sent here by the trial.","Before Max could think further, he noticed that the majority of these people had gathered in the distance.","Thousands stood in a broad circle, all facing the same direction with expressions of awe, seriousness, or deep concentration.","Max followed their line of sight.","Then his eyes narrowed sharply.","At the center of the gathering stood an enormous boulder.","It was massive, rising like a small hill from the earth, its surface dark gray and weathered by ages. At first glance, it seemed like nothing more than ancient stone.","But the moment Max’s senses touched it, his heart shook.","A terrifying sword intent was pouring from that boulder like an invisible ocean.","The pressure was immense, ancient, and so pure that the surrounding air itself seemed sliced apart by its presence. Every gust of wind near it carried sharpness. Every patch of grass around it bent instinctively away.","Max focused harder.","Then he saw it.","Countless sword marks covered the entire boulder.","Some were thin lines no wider than a finger. Others were broad clefts deep enough for a man to stand inside. Some crossed each other in chaotic patterns, while others stood alone with simple dignity.","Every single mark emitted sword intent.","Not faint remnants.","Not dying traces.","Living sword intent that had survived who knew how many years.","The moment Max truly perceived them, his expression changed.","His Severing Sword Concept trembled inside him.","The concept he had painstakingly built through battle and comprehension was being suppressed merely by standing before this boulder. It was as though a village stream had been brought before an endless sea.","Even more shocking, his half-formed Cosmic Path for Sword, something tied to a far greater road, also became subdued under the pressure radiating from those marks.","This was not because his path was weak.","It was because the level contained in these sword marks was absurdly high.","Far beyond his current understanding.","Far beyond what he had imagined possible.","Max slowly steadied his breathing as he stared at the giant boulder.","What kind of existence had carved these marks?","What kind of swordsman could leave behind traces so powerful that even after ages they could still suppress concepts of later generations?","And why had the so-called Perfect Grade reward brought him here?","For the first time since entering the Smelting Trial, Max felt not excitement, but genuine reverence.","Max continued staring at the enormous boulder for several breaths before forcing himself to calm down.","The pressure radiating from the countless sword marks was too intense to ignore. Every instinct in his body urged him to study it immediately, yet he understood that blindly rushing into comprehension without knowing its origin would be foolish.","He looked around and soon noticed a young man standing nearby who appeared close to his own age. The man wore gray robes, had a sword strapped to his waist, and was staring toward the boulder with an expression of deep concentration.","Max stepped closer and lightly tapped his shoulder.","\"Brother, can you help me a bit?\"","The young man frowned at being disturbed. He turned with irritation in his eyes, but the moment he saw how youthful Max appeared, his anger lessened somewhat.","\"What do you want?\"","Max pointed toward the giant stone.","\"What is this boulder, and why do I feel such fierce sword intent coming from it?\"","The young man blinked twice.","Then he looked at Max as though staring at a complete fool.","\"Are you kidding me?\"","His voice rose enough to draw a few glances from nearby people.","\"How can you not know what this boulder is?\"","Max coughed awkwardly and quickly improvised.","\"Ahem... I have never really left home before. Today my uncle brought me here, and I happened to encounter this place.\"","The young man still shook his head in disbelief.","\"Even then, how could you not know this?\"","He narrowed his eyes suspiciously.","\"Tell me honestly. Are you from a mortal realm that recently ascended into the Divine Realm?\"","Max immediately nodded with exaggerated sincerity.","\"Right. Exactly that. I only ascended not long ago.\"","The young man’s suspicion instantly faded.","\"Now that explains your ignorance.\"","He turned back toward the boulder, and when he spoke again, his tone carried reverence that had not been present earlier.","\"The sword marks on this boulder are not ordinary remnants. In truth, no one knows with certainty where they came from. There are many records, many rumors, and many fabricated stories. Truth and falsehood have mixed together for so long that few can separate them anymore.\"","He paused briefly before continuing.","\"But the greatest and oldest legend says that every mark on this stone was left behind by one man.\"","\"The Sword Saint.\""]},{"number":1625,"title":"Chapter 1625: Sword Art of the Sword Saint!","paragraphs":["Max’s eyes sharpened.","The young man noticed and gave a faint nod.","\"Yes. Even someone from a mortal realm should understand what the title Sword Saint means.\"","\"It is not merely a realm title. It is a title acknowledged by heaven and by generations of swordsmen. It refers to one whose understanding of the sword surpassed ordinary paths and entered sanctity.\"","His gaze grew distant as he continued.","\"It is said the Sword Saint was born in an era of endless war when forces slaughtered forces, empires shattered worlds, and sword cultivators filled the heavens like stars. In that age, countless supreme swordsmen rose, each believing themselves unmatched.\"","\"But when the Sword Saint appeared, every blade in the world dimmed.\"","Max remained silent, listening carefully.","The young man’s voice lowered as though speaking of a taboo existence.","\"Some legends say he carried no famous weapon and used a plain iron sword taken from a village forge. Some say he used a wooden branch and defeated divine blades. Others claim he wielded no sword at all, and that the world itself became his blade.\"","\"No one knows which tale is true.\"","\"What all records agree upon is that wherever he went, sword concept transformed.\"","He pointed toward the boulder.","\"It is said this stone once stood at the center of an ancient battlefield where millions fought. When the Sword Saint arrived, he did not kill everyone with one technique like in exaggerated stories. Instead, he stood before this boulder and practiced sword arts.\"","Max frowned slightly.","\"Practiced?\"","The young man nodded.","\"Yes. Practiced.\"","\"That is what terrifies later generations the most.\"","\"These marks were not supposedly created during life-and-death combat. They were said to be casual traces left while refining and evolving his sword art.\"","Max’s pupils contracted.","The young man continued with increasing awe.","\"Every slash represented a variation. Every thrust represented a change in principle. Every shallow cut reflected a solved flaw. Every deep scar contained a complete transformation of intent.\"","\"In other words, the boulder is believed to record the evolution of the Sword Saint’s supreme sword art from imperfection to transcendence.\"","Max instinctively looked again at the countless marks.","Suddenly they seemed even more terrifying.","The young man spoke on.","\"That sword art has many names in different eras. Some call it the Heaven-Cutting Scripture. Some call it the Nameless Saint Sword. Some call it the Path of One Blade.\"","\"But the most respected name is the Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","\"Because many believe every modern sword inheritance can trace some fragment of philosophy back to it.\"","His tone became bitterly admiring.","\"Do you know what that means?\"","\"It means countless sword forces may proudly guard their so-called supreme arts, yet those arts might only be descendants of scraps born from these marks.\"","Max’s breathing grew slower.","The young man pointed toward the front rows where powerful cultivators sat motionless.","\"You see those people closest to the boulder?\"","\"Some have sat here for hundreds of thousands of years attempting to comprehend what lies within. Some are Divine King Realm experts. Some are Holy Lord Realm tyrants. There are even Holy King Realm existences among them.\"","He shook his head.","\"Any one of them could establish a third-rate force, dominate star realms, gather endless resources, and live like emperors.\"","\"But they chose to remain here.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Because if even one fragment of the Sword Saint’s sword art is truly understood, it may be worth more than ruling ten thousand worlds.\"","He laughed softly.","\"Yet none have fully succeeded.\"","\"Some gained sharper sword intent. Some created new techniques inspired by a single mark. Some broke bottlenecks after staring at the stone for millennia.\"","\"But no one has ever confidently declared that they comprehended the complete sword art hidden within.\"","His eyes returned to the boulder with burning desire.","\"That is why this place never empties.\"","\"Generations come and fail. Then new generations arrive and dream again.\"","Max said nothing for a long while.","His gaze fixed on the countless marks carved across the ancient stone.","If those traces truly recorded the rise of a Sword Saint’s supreme art, then the opportunity before him was far greater than any inheritance he had imagined.","And suddenly he understood why the Perfect Grade reward had brought him here.","Max continued staring at the ancient boulder, yet his mind was no longer focused solely on the countless sword marks carved into its surface.","A memory had risen from deep within him.","The Tower of Truth.","Within that tower had been one place he would never forget.","Tomb of the Sword Saint.","Max’s eyes narrowed slowly as the connection became clearer and clearer.","\"I once entered the Sword Saint’s Tomb within the Tower of Truth to comprehend my Severing Sword Concept.\"","At that time, he had only regarded the name as grand and mysterious. Countless ancient inheritances used exaggerated titles, so he had not thought too deeply about it.","But now he stood in a place where Divine Kings, Holy Lords, and ancient experts remained seated for hundreds of thousands of years before a stone marked by a Sword Saint.","Now the title carried terrifying weight.","Could two unrelated places both bear the name Sword Saint by coincidence?","The more Max thought about it, the less likely that seemed.","The Tower of Truth had belonged to a Primordial, and Primordials were existences tied to the deeper history of the Divine Realm itself. If such a being had deliberately preserved a location known as the Sword Saint’s Tomb, then the Sword Saint referenced there was almost certainly no fabricated figure.","Max slowly turned his gaze back toward the giant boulder.","The Sword Saint whose sword marks still suppressed modern experts.","The Sword Saint whose traces made his own concepts tremble.","The Sword Saint whose legacy still drew generations of swordsmen into obsession.","A strong possibility formed in his heart.","They were the same person.","That realization alone was enough to stir his emotions, but then another thought struck him with even greater force."]},{"number":1626,"title":"Chapter 1626: Connection with the Concept of Severing Sword!","paragraphs":["\"Wait a minute...\"","His pupils contracted.","\"I comprehended the Severing Sword Concept from within the Sword Saint’s Tomb.\"","The memory became vivid.","An endless burial ground stretched before him. Thousands upon thousands of swords had been embedded into the earth like a forest of graves. Some swords were snapped in half. Some had rusted with age. Some still radiated traces of killing intent so sharp that they seemed unwilling to die.","They had not looked decorative.","They had looked real.","They had looked like the remains of fallen swordsmen.","Among all of them, Max had chosen the sword resting at the highest peak visible to him. That sword had resonated with his heart, and through it he had comprehended the path of severance.","Now, standing before this boulder, the meaning of that scene felt entirely different.","\"If those swords were genuine relics...\"","His breathing unconsciously slowed.","\"Then did each blade belong to someone who once fought the Sword Saint and died?\"","The thought was terrifying.","It would mean the tomb was not simply a memorial. It would be a mountain of defeated sword paths. Every buried blade could represent a once-famous genius, a master in sword, a heavenly sword sovereign, or some ancient monster who challenged the Sword Saint only to fall.","Their swords would remain as silent witnesses.","Their pride would remain buried in steel.","Their defeat would become part of the Sword Saint’s legend.","Max clenched his fist slightly.","Then what of the sword he had chosen?","What of the Severing Sword Concept hidden within it?","Could it have belonged to the final inheritor of a fearsome severing path, someone who sought to cut apart heaven and earth, fate and existence itself and yet still lost to the Sword Saint?","If so, then the concept Max now cultivated had come from a defeated challenger whose legacy survived only through that abandoned weapon.","Yet another possibility arose.","One even more shocking.","\"Or...\"","Max’s eyes locked onto the sword marks covering the boulder.","\"What if the Severing Sword Concept belonged to the Sword Saint himself?\"","That possibility sent a chill through him.","If the Sword Saint had once cultivated severance as one branch of his concept, then the sword Max found might not have belonged to a defeated enemy at all. It might have been one of the Sword Saint’s own swords from an earlier era.","A sword once used, then abandoned.","A concept once mastered, then transcended.","A stage of growth cast aside after he walked toward something greater.","If that were true, then the concept Max had treasured as a major achievement might only be a fragment of the Sword Saint’s past road.","A single leaf fallen from an ancient world tree.","Max’s scalp tingled as he considered it.","There was no way to know the truth yet.","Perhaps the tomb preserved the weapons of defeated rivals.","Perhaps it contained swords once wielded by the Sword Saint himself.","Perhaps it was both, a burial ground of challengers mixed with the remnants of the Sword Saint’s own journey.","Whatever the truth might be, one fact had become impossible to deny.","His path had already intertwined with this mysterious Sword Saint long before today.","The comprehension he gained in the Tower of Truth, the Severing Sword Concept he carried, and the opportunity that had now brought him before this boulder all seemed tied together by an invisible thread.","Max slowly exhaled and steadied his mind.","Whether this was fate or coincidence no longer mattered.","He had once touched the shadow of the Sword Saint in a tomb.","Now he stood before another remnant of that same legend.","\"I would advise you not to get honey-trapped by the sword marks on that boulder.\"","The young man beside Max spoke while still staring forward, his tone carrying the weariness of someone who had seen too many people lose themselves here.","\"Unless you want to become like those old monsters who have spent thousands upon thousands of years sitting before this stone.\"","He subtly gestured toward the figures nearest the boulder.","Some of them looked ancient beyond words. Their robes were faded by time, yet their auras were vast and terrifying. Others appeared middle-aged or even youthful, but the stillness in their eyes carried the heaviness of endless years. They sat unmoving like statues, each one immersed in the sword marks as though the outside world no longer existed.","\"One day becomes one year,\" the young man continued quietly. \"One year becomes ten thousand. Many came here seeking enlightenment. In the end, enlightenment became their prison.\"","Max listened carefully.","The warning was not without reason.","There was something deeply addictive about the boulder. Every sword mark seemed to contain mystery. Every trace seemed to hint at a higher truth just beyond reach. It was easy to imagine how a swordsman could stare at it for centuries believing the next moment would bring breakthrough.","Then centuries more would pass.","Max nodded calmly.","\"Hm. I will keep that in mind.\"","The young man gave him one last glance, then seemed satisfied.","\"Good. Curiosity is fine, but obsession ruins more geniuses than enemies ever do.\"","With that, he turned and walked away, disappearing into the crowd of wandering cultivators.","Max remained where he stood.","His eyes returned to the giant boulder covered in countless sword marks. Winds moved around it in faint spirals, carrying threads of sharpness that could be felt even from a distance.","His thoughts drifted back to what he had considered earlier.","If his guess was correct, and the final inheritor of the Severing Sword Concept had once challenged the Sword Saint and died, then that battle must have been extraordinary beyond imagination.","The Concept of Severing Sword was not ordinary.","Max knew that better than anyone.","It was a path that pursued absolute cutting power. It sought to sever flesh, sever mountains, sever energy, sever formations, sever destiny, and perhaps even sever intangible principles themselves. It was tyrannical, direct, and terrifyingly pure.","Even in his incomplete state, the concept had already granted him fearsome offensive power.","What, then, of the last true bearer who had fully matured that path?","Such a person would have been a heaven-shaking swordsman.","Yet even that existence may have fallen.","Max’s gaze deepened.","\"If that person truly challenged the Sword Saint and died...\"","\"Then what kind of concept did the Sword Saint possess?\"","Could it have been a concept stronger than severance itself?","The thought sounded simple, yet it shook Max internally."]},{"number":1627,"title":"Chapter 1627: Into a different plane!","paragraphs":["Because concepts were not ranked like ordinary techniques. They were manifestations of understanding, reflections of one’s concept, embodiments of truth grasped through countless battles and insights.","Could one simply say one concept was stronger than another?","Perhaps in direct destructive power, severance stood among the highest.","To cut all things apart was already near the extreme of offense.","So what could surpass it?","A concept of origin that rewrote what was cut?","A concept of unity that denied division itself?","A concept of return that restored what had been severed?","A concept of nothingness that made cutting meaningless because nothing remained to cut?","Or perhaps something even more terrifying.","A concept so complete that it did not oppose severance, but contained it as one small part.","Max slowly narrowed his eyes.","He had doubts such concepts even existed.","The Concept of Severing Sword already felt sharp enough to challenge heaven. To imagine something naturally above it was difficult.","Yet the boulder before him was suppressing his Severing Sword Concept merely through old marks left behind.","That fact alone contradicted his doubts.","Either the Sword Saint’s cultivation had reached an absurd level beyond concepts Max understood...","Or the Sword Saint truly had grasped a sword path standing above severance.","Max felt both excitement and pressure rise within him.","The farther he walked, the more he realized how small his current understanding remained.","What he once viewed as a great peak might only be a foothill on an endless mountain.","Still, instead of discouraging him, that realization ignited something in his chest.","He looked at the countless marks again.","\"If there really is a sword path beyond severance...\"","\"Then I will see it for myself.\"","Max’s eyes shone with brilliance as he slowly began walking toward the giant boulder.","Every step closer increased the pressure radiating from the countless sword marks. The surrounding air felt sharper, as though invisible blades drifted through space. Even the earth beneath his feet carried traces of sword intent that had seeped downward through ages of suppression.","Yet Max did not stop.","Once he reached a suitable distance, he halted and steadied his breathing.","Then he activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","A subtle ripple spread through his senses. The world around him changed instantly. Layers of space became visible. The flow of energy between heaven and earth unfolded in intricate patterns. Distortions hidden from ordinary sight appeared like threads suspended in the air. The deeper functions of reality opened before him.","His gaze locked onto the sword marks covering the boulder.","Immediately, countless details revealed themselves.","He could see how each sword mark had not merely scarred the surface, but had cut through the surrounding spatial layers when first created. Some marks twisted depth unnaturally. Others folded force inward. Some still carried residual trajectories frozen in dimensional traces.","From a three-dimensional perspective, the marks were already profound beyond reason.","Yet after observing for several breaths, Max’s expression gradually changed.","He could see them.","But he could not understand them.","The Dimensional Sovereign Body allowed him to perceive structure, depth, and hidden patterns, but what lay within these marks exceeded pure geometry or spatial analysis. The essence behind them was sword truth itself, something born from comprehension rather than shape.","It was like a mortal staring at divine scripture. The letters were visible, yet meaning remained sealed.","Max narrowed his eyes.","\"So even this can only help me this far.\"","He did not feel disappointed.","Instead, his fighting spirit rose.","If sight alone was insufficient, then he would test the boulder directly.","Within his sea of consciousness, the Concept of Severing Sword stirred sharply. Max guided a strand of that concept outward, sending it toward the giant stone like an invisible blade of intent.","The moment his Severing Sword Concept touched the boulder, everything changed.","The entire boulder erupted in blinding golden light.","The countless sword marks ignited simultaneously as though awakened from slumber. Ancient brilliance flooded the plain, and an overwhelming sword pressure descended from above.","Before Max could fully react, one of the glowing marks split open.","A golden sword slash burst forth from the boulder and shot toward him with impossible speed.","It came without warning.","It came without buildup.","It crossed distance as if distance did not exist.","Max’s scalp exploded with danger.","He had nearly been caught completely off guard.","In that critical instant, his battle instincts roared to life. Max drew Dragonheart and swung with everything he had.","Steel met golden light.","A violent impact shook the surrounding area as Dragonheart barely deflected the slash away from his body. The golden attack changed direction and flew sideways into the distance, cutting through mountains far away as though they were paper before vanishing beyond the horizon.","Max staggered backward several steps.","Blood leaked from the corner of his mouth.","His arms trembled violently from the force of the collision, and sharp pain spread through his internal organs.","Even after successfully parrying it, the recoil alone had injured him.","Max’s eyes filled with shock.","That slash had not been unleashed by a living swordsman.","It was merely a reaction from one ancient mark.","Yet what made him feel even stranger was not the power.","It was the silence around him.","The countless experts seated before the boulder remained exactly as before. None opened their eyes. None reacted. None showed the slightest sign of witnessing the boulder explode with golden radiance or a terrifying slash being released.","They remained immersed in meditation as though nothing had happened.","Max slowly wiped the blood from his lips.","\"That is impossible.\"","He immediately activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body once more.","This time, instead of focusing on the sword marks, he observed the surrounding reality itself.","Then his pupils contracted.","Something was wrong.","Or more accurately, something had changed.","Through the perception of his Dimensional Sovereign Body, Max discovered that he was no longer standing on the same spatial layer as the others. Their figures were present, yet faintly displaced, as though separated by an invisible membrane.","He could still see them.","But they were not truly sharing the same plane as him.","Max himself now stood in a parallel plane overlapping the original world.","The grassy land, the boulder, the sky, and the people all still existed visually, yet spatially he had shifted into another layer of existence.","Understanding dawned instantly.","That was why the others had not been disturbed.","That was why no one reacted to the golden slash.","That attack had occurred only within this parallel plane.","And the trigger had been clear.","The moment his Severing Sword Concept touched the boulder, the boulder had responded and dragged him into this hidden dimensional layer.","Max slowly lifted his head and looked at the glowing sword marks once more.","His heartbeat quickened.","This was no ordinary inheritance site.","The boulder had recognized his concept to send him to a different plane.","Meaning he had triggered the inheritance Sword Saint might or might not have put this on the boulder."]},{"number":1628,"title":"Chapter 1628: Meaning behind the Sword Slashes!","paragraphs":["After realizing that he stood in a different plane from everyone else, Max completely withdrew his attention from the countless cultivators gathered around the giant boulder.","Whether they were Divine Kings, Holy Lords, or ancient experts who had remained seated here for unknown ages, none of them mattered to him at this moment. Their bodies were still present in the same open space, their auras still filled the surroundings, and their silent figures still carried the weight of terrifying cultivation, but Max understood that they were no longer standing in the same layer of reality as him.","They could not see the golden light he had seen. They could not sense the attack that had struck him. They could not feel the sharp pressure that had almost split his perception apart.","To them, perhaps he was still seated quietly before the boulder like everyone else, but to Max, the world had already changed.","This hidden plane belonged only to him now.","Max slowly turned his gaze back toward the giant boulder. The golden brilliance from the previous reaction had already faded, and the countless sword marks on its surface had returned to their ancient stillness.","They looked weathered and silent, as though they had been carved there by time itself. Yet after experiencing that sudden golden slash, Max could no longer regard the boulder as a simple stone. It felt alive in a strange and profound way.","It was not alive like a beast. It was not alive like a spirit with thoughts and emotions. It was alive through intent, through sword principles, through the terrifying will hidden inside every mark left behind on its surface.","Max narrowed his eyes as countless thoughts moved through his mind.","\"If that attack was not meant to kill me, then what was its purpose?\" he muttered softly.","The recoil from the first clash still lingered within his body. His arms felt numb, his internal organs had been shaken, and a trace of blood still stained the corner of his lips. Yet Max felt no fear. Instead, a stronger curiosity surged in his heart.","He wanted to know what lay behind those sword marks. He wanted to know what kind of sword truth could force even his Severing Sword Concept to tremble. More than that, he wanted to understand why the boulder had answered him in such a direct and violent way.","Max inhaled slowly and forced his mind to calm.","Then he guided his Concept of Severing Sword outward once more.","This time, he did not act recklessly. He condensed the concept into a thinner and purer thread of sword intent, making it sharper, more restrained, and more focused than before. It drifted through the air without sound, like an invisible blade moving through a world that ordinary eyes could never perceive.","Under Max’s careful control, the thread of Severing Sword Concept touched one of the sword marks on the boulder.","The reaction was immediate.","The entire boulder erupted with golden light.","Every sword mark ignited at the same time, turning the ancient stone into a radiant sun of sword intent. A terrifying pressure descended upon the hidden plane, so sharp and majestic that even the air around Max seemed to be sliced into countless invisible fragments.","The ground beneath his feet trembled faintly, and the space around the boulder distorted under the weight of the sword aura.","Then one sword mark near the center shone brighter than all the others.","From within that mark, a golden sword slash burst out.","It was even faster than the first one.","No, calling it fast was not accurate. Speed still belonged to movement, but this slash almost ignored movement itself. The instant it appeared, it had already crossed the distance between the boulder and Max. Its line was direct, flawless, and impossible to predict through ordinary perception.","Max’s pupils contracted sharply as he instantly activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","His battle instincts erupted.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand before his conscious thoughts fully formed. Max stepped diagonally, twisted his waist, and raised his sword at the most efficient defensive angle he could create in that brief instant.","Steel collided with golden light.","A violent shockwave exploded outward. Sparks scattered through the air like fragments of shattered stars, and the force behind the golden slash rushed through Dragonheart, entered Max’s arms, and crashed deep into his body like a falling mountain.","Max was blasted backward dozens of meters.","His boots tore long trenches into the ground as he struggled to stabilize himself. Even after forcing himself to stop, blood surged up his throat and spilled from his mouth. Pain spread through his chest, his meridians, and his arms, but Max ignored all of it.","His eyes were brighter than ever.","He had blocked the second slash.","More importantly, this time he had sensed something deeper.","The attack was not chaotic. It was not a wild burst of power released without control. Its force had been distributed with terrifying precision. Its angle contained no wasted motion. Its trajectory was the shortest and cleanest path between origin and target. Every inch of the slash had been refined until nothing unnecessary remained.","Max slowly lowered Dragonheart and fell into deep thought.","\"What is the meaning behind these attacks?\"","Why did the boulder react only when his Severing Sword Concept touched it?","Why did it answer with sword slashes instead of visions, manuals, or spoken teachings?","Why did each attack feel less like hostility and more like a demonstration?","Max replayed the two clashes again and again in his mind. The first slash had nearly overwhelmed him through suddenness. The second slash had been clearer, purer, and even more complete. There had been no killing intent within either attack.","There had been no cruelty, no arrogance, and no desire to crush a weaker junior.","There had only been sword.","As this thought surfaced, Max’s breathing gradually slowed.","Then realization struck him.","\"This is not just a sword attack,\" Max murmured, his gaze locking onto the glowing marks.","\"The sword attacks are guiding me in the way of the sword.\"","The boulder was not attacking him. It was teaching him.","Each time he offered his Severing Sword Concept, the marks answered with a sword principle capable of confronting it. These golden slashes were not random attacks. They were lessons delivered through collision.","Perhaps the Sword Saint had never left behind written scriptures because true sword concepts could not be transmitted through words alone. Words could be misunderstood. Diagrams could be copied without comprehension. Manuals could be memorized by fools who never touched the essence behind them.","But a sword slash could not lie.","Only by facing it directly could one understand the truth hidden within.","Max lifted his head and stared at the ancient boulder. The pain in his body still had not faded, but excitement began to burn in his eyes. If his judgment was correct, then every golden slash released by this boulder was worth more than countless treasured sword manuals.","Each strike contained a truth refined by an existence whose sword concept had reached an unimaginable level.","And he had only received two so far."]},{"number":1629,"title":"Chapter 1629: A Symphony of Sword Slashes!","paragraphs":["After reaching that understanding, Max no longer hesitated. If the golden slashes were teachings, then he would force the boulder to teach him until nothing remained hidden.","His gaze sharpened, and a fierce hunger rose from the depths of his heart. The pain in his arms, the blood at the corner of his lips, and the trembling in his meridians all became insignificant before the opportunity standing in front of him.","Without wasting another moment, Max extended his will and sent his Concept of Severing Sword into the boulder once more.","The response was immediate.","Golden light burst from the ancient stone with blinding brilliance. Every sword mark across its weathered surface ignited simultaneously, causing the massive boulder to resemble a radiant sun forged from sword intent.","A terrifying pressure descended upon the hidden plane, so sharp and majestic that even the surrounding air seemed to split apart under its presence.","Then another slash came.","It crossed the distance in an instant, moving with such terrifying speed that it seemed to ignore the concept of travel itself. One moment it was born from the boulder, and the next it had already arrived before Max.","His battle instincts exploded.","Dragonheart rose in both hands as Max twisted his waist and met the strike head on.","Steel and golden light collided with a thunderous sound. Violent force surged through the blade and into his arms, numbing his fingers and shaking his bones. The impact drove him backward several steps, tearing long scars into the earth beneath his boots.","Before he had even fully stabilized himself, Max’s eyes flashed again.","He sent his Severing Sword Concept back into the boulder.","Another golden slash answered.","He blocked again.","Then he attacked the boulder with his concept once more.","Another slash came.","Again he blocked.","This cycle repeated without pause. Golden brilliance erupted over and over across the hidden plane as the boulder answered every challenge with another sword strike. Max responded each time with all the strength, skill, and willpower he possessed.","His wrists began to bleed from repeated strain.","The skin of his palms split open against Dragonheart’s hilt.","His internal organs shook violently from the transmitted impacts.","His chest tightened, his muscles screamed, and blood rose repeatedly into his throat.","One must know that Max’s body was super strong right now. With 5000 Dragon Scales passively protecting his body, it should have been impossible for mere sword slashes to even hurt him but here it was like he was a mortal facing those slashes.","Yet Max refused to stop.","He kept sending his concept forward.","He kept receiving the slashes.","He kept blocking.","Again and again.","Again and again.","At first, every sword slash felt overwhelming. Though similar in essence, each strike possessed subtle differences that revealed terrifying depth.","Some cuts were direct and straight, carrying absolute simplicity that crushed resistance through purity alone. Some curved slightly in motion, changing their line at the final moment like serpents striking from concealment.","Some descended with crushing authority as if they sought to split mountains apart. Others rose upward with hidden momentum, like dragons emerging from deep waters to challenge the heavens.","Max forced himself to memorize every one of them with his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Even while blood dripped from his hands and pain thundered through his body, his mind worked with frightening clarity.","Between collisions, he replayed each slash repeatedly within his thoughts. He examined how force entered the blade, how intent condensed before release, how movement remained simple while containing endless refinement. There was no wasted motion in any strike. Every action existed because it was necessary.","Then, amid this endless exchange, the boulder suddenly changed.","The golden light coating its surface trembled violently. The countless sword marks began to move like rivers of radiance flowing across stone. One by one, they converged toward the center. Ancient lines merged together, and the shape of the boulder blurred before Max’s eyes.","The massive stone transformed into the shadow of a man.","The figure stood tall and indistinct, formed entirely from darkness edged in gold. Its face could not be seen. Its clothing shifted like smoke. No aura of cultivation could be sensed from it, yet its mere presence carried a pressure deeper than mountains and older than time.","Only one thing was perfectly clear.","It held a sword.","Max’s heart trembled violently at the sight.","Before he could gather another thought, the shadowy man stepped forward and swung.","The motion was clean, simple, and flawless.","From that one swing, a golden sword slash was born and shot toward Max.","Max reacted on instinct, raising Dragonheart with desperate speed.","The collision blasted him backward across the ground, yet Max no longer cared about the force of the strike. His full attention was fixed upon the movement that had created it. He studied the step, the turn of the waist, the line of the shoulder, the angle of the wrist, and the precise instant power traveled from the body into the blade.","That strike had not been random.","It had demonstrated form.","Without allowing himself to lose concentration, Max immediately sent his Severing Sword Concept outward again.","The shadowy man answered with another swing.","Then another.","Then another.","Again and again, the figure raised its sword and released golden slashes. Again and again, Max blocked while studying every subtle movement. He watched how breath matched rhythm. He watched how balance shifted before each attack. He watched how attack and defense were hidden inside the same motion.","He was no longer merely defending.","He was learning an art.","At first, Max could imitate only fragments. He copied a slight change in stance. He mimicked the sharper turning of a shoulder. He adjusted the angle of interception. He learned how force flowed more directly from body to blade.","With every clash, his understanding deepened.","The shadowy figure swung downward, and Max began to answer with the same descending path. The figure rotated into a diagonal slash, and Max gradually mirrored the same rotation to neutralize it. The figure drew a short horizontal line that concealed a hidden thrust at the end, and Max eventually responded with the same transition to break the attack before completion.","The more he blocked, the more he learned.","The more he learned, the more he could reproduce.","The more he reproduced, the less pressure each clash placed upon him.","Soon the battlefield entered a strange rhythm. The shadowy man attacked, and Max responded with the same move. The shadowy man changed sequence, and Max changed with it. The shadowy man advanced one step and cut, and Max advanced one step and cut in return.","Golden slashes crossed the hidden plane endlessly as phantom and challenger mirrored one another in a storm of steel and light. Their movements grew faster, cleaner, and simpler. Each strike appeared plain to the eye, yet each one contained layers of profound sword truth.","Time gradually lost meaning.","Max forgot pain.","He forgot fatigue.","He forgot the countless experts seated outside this hidden plane.","He forgot even himself and unconsciously entered the state of his half baked cosmic path of emotion severing sword.","In his mind only sword remained.","At some unknown moment, all the scattered pieces of understanding within Max suddenly connected. Every repeated slash, every form, every transition between offense and defense, every simple motion hiding infinite depth became one complete whole inside his mind.","It was one sword art.","Not separate techniques.","Not isolated moves.","One continuous scripture expressed through countless slashes.","The instant Max grasped this truth, something within him transformed.","He moved before the shadowy man did.","He stepped forward with perfect balance. His waist turned naturally. His shoulders aligned without force. His breath sank calmly into his core. Dragonheart swung in one seamless motion carrying the exact essence he had comprehended.","A golden slash burst from his blade.","It collided with the figure’s incoming attack and shattered it completely.","Silence filled the hidden plane.","For the first time, the shadowy figure stopped moving. It slowly lowered its sword and seemed to look at Max one final time. No words were spoken, yet Max felt an unmistakable acknowledgment pass between them.","The next breath, the figure dissolved into countless streams of golden light.","Those streams returned to the ancient stone.","The boulder reappeared in its original form.","All brilliance faded.","The countless sword marks became silent once more.","Max stood there breathing heavily. His body was battered, bloodied, and exhausted. Every muscle screamed in pain, and yet his eyes shone brighter than ever before.","He sent his Severing Sword Concept toward the boulder again.","Nothing happened.","No golden light emerged.","No slash was released.","No response came.","The lesson was over.","Max slowly tightened his grip on Dragonheart and gazed at the silent boulder before him. He had not merely endured its attacks. He had not merely copied a few techniques.","He had inherited the sword art hidden within them.","Saint Origin Sword Art."]},{"number":1630,"title":"Chapter 1630: A Conflict?","paragraphs":["After the hidden plane fell silent and the boulder returned to its ancient, unmoving state, Max remained standing where he was for a long time. His chest rose and fell with heavy breaths, each inhalation carrying the lingering tremor of the countless impacts he had endured.","Blood still stained his palms, and his arms felt as though they had been struck by mountains again and again, yet none of that occupied his thoughts anymore. His entire focus had already shifted inward.","It was on the sword.","Max slowly lifted Dragonheart.","He did not rush into movement. Instead, he allowed the understanding he had gained to settle within him. Every slash he had blocked, every motion he had observed, every subtle transition in the shadowy figure’s movements replayed clearly within his mind.","The complete sword art he had pieced together felt vivid, as though it had been etched directly into his bones rather than merely remembered.","Then he took a step forward.","His foot landed lightly, yet firmly.","His waist turned with controlled precision.","His shoulders aligned without stiffness.","Dragonheart descended in a single clean arc.","The blade cut through the air.","There was no explosion of golden light this time, no overwhelming pressure bearing down on the surroundings. However, the moment the sword moved, a faint change occurred in the air around him. It was subtle, almost imperceptible, but there was a sense that the space itself acknowledged the refinement of that motion.","Max did not stop there.","His first slash flowed into the next. The downward cut transitioned into a diagonal movement, and the diagonal naturally shifted into a horizontal line. That horizontal line carried within it a hidden continuation, a point where it could transform into a thrust without breaking its rhythm.","The sequence unfolded smoothly.","It was continuous.","It was complete.","Max slowly came to a stop.","But with a faint frown appeared on his face.","Because he sensed something was wrong with the sword art. He couldn’t put his mind on where but he definitely felt like the sword art was resisting to him.","He lowered Dragonheart slightly and closed his eyes. His consciousness turned inward as he began to feel the sword once more, not through sight, but through perception.","He traced every movement he had just executed, examining the flow between actions, the way force gathered and released, and the invisible rhythm connecting one strike to the next.","\"Is that the Saint Origin Sword Art?\" Max muttered quietly.","The name rose naturally in his mind.","It carried a sense of origin, of something fundamental and complete. The sword art he had learned did not rely on complexity or overwhelming power. Instead, it emphasized simplicity taken to its absolute limit, where every motion existed only because it was necessary and every transition was part of a greater whole.","His sword moves...","Max’s brows slowly drew together.","They were correct.","Yet they did not feel right.","He opened his eyes and raised Dragonheart again. This time, he infused his Concept of Severing Sword into the movement. The familiar sharpness emerged at once, carrying the will to divide, to cut apart, to bring everything to a definitive end.","The moment the concept merged with the sword art, something subtle shifted.","The flow was no longer seamless.","It did not break outright, but it faltered slightly at certain points. The transitions lost a fraction of their natural continuity, as though an external force had been introduced into a perfectly balanced system.","Max stopped mid-motion.","He remained still, his eyes deep in thought.","\"My concept of severing sword is conflicting with the sword art,\" he murmured under his breath.","He raised the sword again and began repeating the sequence, this time slowing each movement deliberately. He paid attention to how the sword art guided his body. It emphasized continuity. Every action flowed into the next without interruption, forming an unbroken chain of motion.","Then he infused his Severing Sword Concept again.","The same result appeared.","The sword art sought flow. It was a continuous sword art that didn’t have an end.","The concept sought conclusion. It meant to be used a strike to end things.","The sword art moved like an endless stream, where no motion truly ended because it simply became the beginning of the next.","The concept moved like a final cut, where everything before it led toward a decisive end.","Because of this, a conflict between them occurred when he used them at the same time.","Max exhaled slowly as his grip on Dragonheart tightened slightly.","\"It is as though they were not made for each other.\"","His thoughts deepened as he stood there in silence.","The Saint Origin Sword Art represented a path of continuity, a complete cycle where every strike was both an end and a beginning at the same time. It did not emphasize destruction. It did not emphasize domination. It emphasized the pure expression of sword, where nothing was wasted and nothing was unnecessary.","His Severing Sword Concept was fundamentally different.","It was built on severance.","It existed to divide, to sever, to bring things to a definitive end.","Max closed his eyes once more, allowing both understandings to exist side by side within his mind. He replayed the movements of the shadowy figure again, observing that perfect continuity, that seamless rhythm, that absence of any excess force. Then he compared it to his own sword, sharp and decisive, filled with the will to end everything it touched.","A faint realization began to take shape.","\"This is not a flaw,\" Max whispered softly. \"It’s like my concept is following a different path than the sword path.\"","His Severing Sword Concept had its own path.","The Saint Origin Sword Art had its own path.","At this moment, they had not yet become one.","Max slowly opened his eyes, and the confusion within them began to settle into clarity. The conflict he felt was not a sign of failure. It was a sign that his understanding had deepened enough to perceive the difference between two complete yet incompatible principles.","He raised Dragonheart once more.","This time, he did not force the fusion.","He executed the sword art as it was, allowing its natural flow to guide his body. Then, in the next movement, he infused a trace of his Severing Sword Concept. The same slight disruption appeared, but Max did not stop.","Instead, his gaze sharpened.","\"If they do not align... then I will make them align.\"","Max’s voice was calm, yet carried an unyielding determination.","Before he could explore this realization any further, the space around him twisted. A familiar force wrapped around his body and pulled him away. In the next instant, the mountain vanished, and Max found himself standing once again in the arena where he had fought the hundred puppets.","A cold, mechanical voice echoed through the space.","[Test of the Sword Art begins]","The surroundings shifted once more.","The arena dissolved, replaced by an even more imposing scene. Max now stood before a colossal mountain that stretched endlessly in all directions. Its size was overwhelming, and even with his Dimensional Sovereign Body, he could not perceive its limits.","Another voice followed.","[According to how much damage you do to the mountain, your score for the Weapon Trial will be decided.]","Max listened carefully before giving a small nod.","\"I see,\" he said quietly.","His grip on the sword tightened slightly as his eyes grew focused.","\"That means I can only rely on the Saint Origin Sword Art.\""]},{"number":1631,"title":"Chapter 1631: A Dud?","paragraphs":["Max stood before the mountain in complete stillness, his gaze unwavering as he slowly lifted his sword. He could feel it clearly now, the subtle rejection between his sword art and his concept. The two forces did not belong together, and they resisted each other at every moment. Even so, Max did not retreat.","A quiet certainty rose within him. The Saint Origin Sword Art alone was not enough. It required something deeper, something that could push it beyond its limits. Only by forcing his concept into it could he awaken its true power.","He drew in a steady and stepped forward.","The moment his sword fell, he poured everything into that single strike. The Saint Origin Sword Art surged through the blade while his concept followed closely behind, the two clashing violently within his control. The energy trembled, unstable and unwilling to fuse, yet Max forced them together through sheer determination.","The strike reached the mountain.","And nothing happened.","There was no sound, no tremor, no visible change. The mountain stood as it always had, vast and immovable, as though his attack had never existed. The stillness pressed against him, heavy and suffocating.","Even Max’s expression shifted as doubt crept into his mind. For a fleeting moment, he questioned himself. Had he failed to grasp the essence of the sword art? Had his strike been too weak to leave even the slightest mark?","\"Is my sword strike a dud?\" Max wondered frowning seeing no scratch to the mountain.","Then something changed.","A line appeared.","It was so thin that it almost did not exist, beginning at the point where his blade had struck. It stretched forward in silence, gliding across the surface of the mountain with an eerie precision. Max’s eyes followed it as it extended further and further, reaching distances far beyond what he could normally perceive.","Still, there was no reaction.","The mountain did not tremble. The air did not stir.","Everything remained exactly the same.","Max did not move. A strange unease settled in his chest as his instincts warned him that what he saw was not the truth.","Without hesitation, he activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body and let his perception sink deep into the mountain.","In that instant, everything became clear.","Max’s pupils contracted sharply.","His breath stopped.","The mountain was already divided.","Not broken. Not damaged.","Completely severed in two.","The cut was so precise, so absolute, that the two halves remained perfectly aligned, as if they had never been separated. There was no collapse, no falling debris, no sign of destruction. The blade had passed through with such overwhelming authority that the mountain had not even realized it had been cut.","For a moment, Max felt his mind go blank.","A deep shock rose from within him, far stronger than anything he had expected. This was no ordinary sword strike. It was something that defied his understanding, something that stood on a level he had not yet reached. The realization struck him with force.","It truly felt like a sword art of the Sword Saint now.","A faint chill ran through his body as the weight of that truth settled into his mind. Even with his current strength, even with his comprehension, he had only touched the surface of what this technique truly represented.","Max slowly lowered his sword.","His voice was calm, yet beneath that calm was a firm and unshakable resolve.","\"So this... is the true power of the Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","The silence lingered after Max’s words, heavy and suffocating, as though the world itself had yet to catch up with what had just occurred.","Then the mountain responded.","A deep and distant rumble spread through its massive structure, subtle at first, almost impossible to detect unless one paid close attention. The thin line that Max had drawn across its surface slowly deepened, revealing a truth that had been hidden beneath that unnatural stillness.","The mountain began to part.","The movement was slow, deliberate, and absolute, as if the outcome had already been decided long before it revealed itself. The two halves shifted away from each other with perfect precision, the separation extending from where Max stood to a distance so far that even his enhanced perception could not fully trace its end.","There was no violent collapse, no chaos, no sound of destruction.","Only a clean, undeniable division.","Max watched it unfold without moving, his expression calm, yet his eyes carried a depth that reflected the weight of what he had just witnessed. Even though he had already seen the truth through his Dimensional Sovereign Body, witnessing the mountain physically separate brought a far greater impact.","This was not destruction.","This was something far more terrifying.","Before he could dwell further on that realization, a cold and emotionless voice echoed across the space.","[Damage Evaluation Complete]","The voice paused briefly, as if processing something far beyond ordinary parameters, before continuing with a series of assessments.","[Analyzing Depth of Impact...]","[Analyzing Range of Effect...]","[Analyzing Energy Consumption...]","[Analyzing Structural Disruption...]","Each word seemed to carry a strange weight, as though the system itself was struggling to fully define what had just been executed.","Max remained silent, his grip on the sword steady, while his gaze stayed fixed ahead. He understood that this trial was not simply measuring raw power, but something far more refined. It was judging precision, control, and the fundamental nature of the technique itself.","The results began to appear.","[Weapon Trial: Sword Path]","[Participant: Max Morgan]","[Technique Used: Saint Origin Sword Art]","[Damage Assessment: Absolute Severance]","[Penetration Depth: Complete]","[Range of Effect: Beyond Measurable Parameters]","[Energy Efficiency: Perfect Conversion]","[Control and Precision: Flawless Execution]","The information settled into place with a quiet finality, yet the system did not stop there.","A brief pause followed, one that felt longer than it should have.","Then the final evaluation appeared.","[Final Score: 100/100]","[Evaluation: Supreme Grade]","[Result: Perfect Completion]","For a moment, everything fell silent again.","Max looked at the panel without speaking, his expression unreadable, yet within his eyes there was a subtle shift. A perfect score was expected after such a strike made Max smile.","Then, as if responding to something unseen, the panel flickered again.","The voice of the system returned, this time carrying a faint distortion that had not been present before.","[Hidden Condition Detected]","[Performance Exceeds Standard Limits]","[Re-evaluating Score...]","The light of the panel trembled slightly as the values began to change.","[Final Score: 120/100]","[Evaluation: Transcendent Grade]","[Result: Limit-Break Completion]","[Reward Tier: Highest Inheritance Unlocked]","The new result settled into place, radiating a presence far more imposing than before.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly as he took in the change, a quiet understanding forming within him. A score that exceeded the maximum limit was not something that should exist within a controlled trial. This was no longer a simple acknowledgment of skill. It was recognition of something that stood beyond the boundaries of the system itself.","\"I guess using the sword art of the Sword Saint himself has its perks.\"","He lowered his gaze for a brief moment, his thoughts steady as the weight of that realization settled within him.","When he looked up again, his expression had returned to calm, yet there was now a firm and unyielding determination hidden beneath that calm exterior.","His fingers tightened slightly around the hilt of his sword as he spoke in a low and steady voice.","\"Even so this Saint Origin Sword Art and my concept are still conflicting. I will need a long time before I will be able to use my concept with the sword art without causing any conflict.\""]},{"number":1632,"title":"Chapter 1632: Suspicions of Lucia and Isabella!","paragraphs":["Following the assessment of the trial system, Max’s figure disappeared from the trial ground and he appeared in a big square of the Violet Star Palace.","The surroundings were completely different, filled with towering structures and an ancient aura that carried immense authority. The Violet Star Palace stood in all its grandeur, its presence alone enough to make even the strongest feel insignificant.","Max remained still for a brief moment before his Dimensional Sovereign Body activated instinctively.","His perception spread outward, sweeping across the entire area.","He saw figures appearing at different intervals, each one materializing in flashes of light as more participants completed their trials and were transported here.","Some looked disoriented.","Some looked relieved.","Some looked unwilling to accept their results.","Max observed them quietly before withdrawing his perception.","A faint smile appeared on his face, subtle yet knowing.","\"Looks like I am one of the few who completed the weapon master trial early,\" he muttered under his breath.","And so he began to wait.","Hours slipped by slowly, and the difference between those who had already completed the Weapon Master Trial and those still struggling inside became painfully clear.","The portals continued to flicker at irregular intervals, releasing participants one after another, each arrival carrying the weight of exhaustion or frustration.","Some staggered out with pale faces and trembling hands, while others clenched their fists in silent anger, clearly dissatisfied with their performance. The earlier excitement that had filled the square had long faded, replaced by a thick tension that pressed down on everyone present.","Max remained where he was, his posture relaxed, his breathing steady, as if the passing time meant nothing to him. His calm demeanor stood in stark contrast to the restless crowd around him, and yet he did not draw attention to himself.","He simply observed, quietly watching as the number of participants steadily increased.","After what felt like an eternity to many, two familiar figures finally emerged from their portals.","Lucia stepped out first, her expression composed but her eyes betraying a trace of fatigue. A faint sheen of sweat lingered on her forehead, and her grip on her spear tightened briefly before she exhaled and relaxed.","Not long after, Isabella appeared as well, her landing far more controlled, her posture straight and her aura sharp. Unlike Lucia, she showed no visible signs of exhaustion, yet the slight narrowing of her eyes suggested that the trial had not been entirely effortless even for her.","Both of them immediately noticed Max.","Lucia walked over first, her steps steady, her gaze fixed on him with a mix of curiosity and suspicion. Isabella followed without a word, her presence carrying a quiet pressure that caused nearby participants to instinctively give way.","Lucia stopped in front of Max and crossed her arms.","\"How did it go?\" She asked curiously.","\"It was good.\" Max said smiling. \"I was one of the few people who finished the trial early and came here hours ago.\"","Lucia’s expression turned solemn hearing him.","\"It took me hours to finish that trial,\" she said, her tone calm but probing. \"And yet you have been standing here since the beginning. Do not tell me you barely passed.\"","Max looked at her, then at Isabella, who was already watching him closely, her sharp eyes searching for any hint of truth.","\"Anyway, I scored 73.\" Lucia said about her score and asked Max and Isabella. \"What about you two?\"","\"I scored 78.\" Isabella said sighing. \"I couldn’t fully master the sword art and so my results weren’t that good.\" She sighed heavily.","\"What about you Max?\" Lucia then asked Max. Isabella also turned to look at him at this.","Max smiled wryly inwardly. What did he suppose to say that he got 120 score in the weapon master trial?","\"I did good too.\" Max said vaguely.","Lucia’s brows furrowed immediately.","\"Good?\" she repeated, her lips pressing into a thin line. \"You are being vague on purpose.\"","Isabella let out a quiet breath, her gaze turning colder.","\"The trial system gives a clear assessment,\" she said, her voice carrying a faint edge. \"Why are you hiding your score from us?\"","Max gave a faint smile, one that revealed nothing.","\"Haha, why you two are so adamant about my score?\" he shrugged calmly. \"You will see my score once the rankings are announced.\"","Lucia stared at him for a few seconds longer, her suspicion deepening rather than fading.","\"You are definitely hiding something.\" She said her eyes narrowing.","Max did not deny it, nor did he confirm it. His silence lingered just long enough to make the answer obvious without words.","Isabella’s eyes narrowed further, and for a brief moment, a flicker of annoyance passed through her gaze.","\"You finished early,\" she said. \"That alone means your result is not ordinary. Yet you refuse to speak of it. Either you performed far better than expected, or something unusual happened inside.\"","Max shrugged slightly, his expression unchanged.","\"Perhaps both,\" he said.","Lucia let out a quiet sigh, clearly frustrated.","\"You are such an annoying guy sometimes,\" she muttered, though her eyes still lingered on him as if trying to peel away whatever he was hiding.","Before either of them could press further, a sudden shift in the air drew everyone’s attention.","A powerful aura descended upon the square.","Elder Cael appeared in the sky above them, his figure standing tall as his gaze swept across the gathered participants. The moment he arrived, the murmurs in the crowd died down, replaced by a heavy silence filled with anticipation.","Without wasting a moment, Elder Cael raised his hand and pointed toward the massive screen that hovered high above the square.","\"The Weapon Master Trial has concluded,\" he announced, his voice echoing clearly across the entire area. \"All participants have now been evaluated by the trial system.\"","A faint glow began to spread across the screen.","\"The rankings of every participant will now be displayed,\" he continued. \"The top ten will receive rewards from the Violet Star Palace. The top three will receive greater rewards. And the one who stands at the peak will receive a special reward personally prepared.\"","The moment his words ended, the screen flickered to life.","Names began to appear rapidly, forming a long list that extended downward as more and more participants were revealed.","The crowd immediately stirred.","Eyes shot upward, scanning the rankings with urgency. Voices rose as people searched for their names, some filled with relief upon finding themselves in a decent position, while others grew visibly tense as they realized how far they had fallen behind.","Lucia’s gaze sharpened as she scanned through the list, her focus unwavering. Isabella’s eyes moved even faster, her expression calm but intense as she searched for her position.","The noise grew louder with every passing second.","Then suddenly, it broke."]},{"number":1633,"title":"Chapter 1633: Parting Ways with Lucia and Isabella!","paragraphs":["A strange silence spread through the crowd, as if an invisible force had pressed down on everyone at once.","Because at the very top of the list, above every other name, there was only one.","Max Morgan.","For a brief moment, no one reacted.","Then the shock erupted.","\"What is this?\"","\"How can that be him?\"","\"I heard out of all the participants present in the Smelting Trial, his cultivation is the weakest at the 9th level of Law Awakening Realm.\"","\"That name... he was standing here the entire time.\"","Lucia’s eyes widened as she stared at the screen, her breath catching slightly.","\"...Max,\" she murmured, disbelief clear in her voice.","Beside her, Isabella froze for a fraction of a second before her gaze snapped toward him, sharp and piercing.","But there was something even more unsettling than his position.","There was no score.","Every single name on the list had a number displayed beside it, representing their performance within the trial.","Except his.","Next to Max Morgan, there was nothing.","No number.","No record.","Only his name, standing alone at the very top.","The crowd erupted once more, this time filled with confusion, suspicion, and disbelief.","\"That is impossible. How can there be no score?\"","\"The system would never fail to record a result.\"","\"Then how is his name at the top?\"","Voices began to turn harsher.","\"He has the Sword Sovereign’s weapon. That must be the reason.\"","\"That weapon must have interfered with the trial system.\"","\"No, this is more than interference. This looks like manipulation.\"","\"He cheated.\"","The accusations spread quickly, fueled by jealousy and confusion, as more and more participants tried to rationalize what they were seeing.","Lucia remained silent, her gaze still fixed on the screen, her thoughts racing.","Isabella’s expression hardened, though beneath that cold exterior, there was a flicker of something else. She really felt the more she spent time with Max, the more she realized how extraordinary this guy seemed to be.","Max showed no reaction at all. He stood quietly where he was, his gaze resting on the glowing screen, his eyes calm and steady, as if the uproar surrounding him had nothing to do with him.","The waves of shock, doubt, and accusation that spread through the crowd did not reach him in the slightest, and his expression remained as composed as ever.","Yet beneath that calm exterior, he understood everything clearly.","The trial system had not made a mistake, nor had it failed to record his result. It had simply chosen not to display it.","His final score had reached one hundred and twenty, a value that had already surpassed the maximum limit of the system itself. If such a number had appeared beside his name for all to see, Max was certain that the chaos would have grown far worse than it already was.","At that point, no one would have believed in his ability. They would have only concluded that the trial system had malfunctioned and produced an impossible result.","Before the murmurs could spiral completely out of control, a powerful voice echoed across the entire square.","\"Everyone, calm down.\"","Elder Cael’s voice carried an unquestionable authority that immediately suppressed the rising noise. The crowd fell silent almost instantly, though the tension in the air remained thick.","\"There is no cheating,\" Elder Cael continued, his tone firm and unyielding. \"The trial system is fair and operates without error. Max Morgan stands at the top because he has received a hidden reward from the system. There is no other reason.\"","His words settled over the crowd, easing some of the doubt, though not completely erasing the shock that lingered in the hearts of many.","Elder Cael then shifted his gaze slightly before speaking once more.","\"The rewards for the Weapon Master Trial will be distributed shortly. The second trial will begin in six hours. Use this time to rest and prepare yourselves.\"","With that, he waved his hand lightly, signaling the end of the gathering.","The pressure of his presence faded, and the crowd began to disperse slowly. Groups of disciples gathered among themselves, whispering in low voices, their gazes occasionally drifting toward Max with complicated expressions that ranged from awe to hostility.","Lucia observed the reactions around them, her brows knitting slightly as she sensed the growing tension directed at Max. Without wasting time, she turned toward him and Isabella.","\"Let’s head back,\" she said, her tone decisive.","She had already noticed the unfriendly looks being cast in their direction, and she knew that remaining here any longer would only invite unnecessary trouble.","Isabella gave a slight nod, clearly understanding the situation as well, and Max followed without objection.","The three of them began making their way back toward their residence, the noise of the dispersing crowd fading behind them.","They had only covered half the distance when Max suddenly spoke.","\"You two go ahead,\" he said calmly. \"I want to take a look at the Combat Tower here in the Violet Star Palace.\"","Lucia stopped immediately, her expression tightening as she turned toward him.","\"No,\" she said without hesitation.","Her refusal came quickly and firmly, leaving no room for ambiguity.","\"You have already drawn too much attention,\" she continued, her voice carrying a trace of concern. \"Many disciples from other third rate forces are not pleased with what just happened. If you wander off alone now, there is a real chance someone will try to provoke you.\"","Max listened quietly before giving a small shrug, his demeanor still relaxed.","\"It does not matter,\" he replied. \"This is the Violet Star Palace. I doubt anyone would dare to cause trouble here openly. I will be fine. You should both head back. I will join you later.\"","Lucia’s expression darkened slightly, clearly unconvinced by his reasoning.","Before she could respond, Max had already made his move.","His figure shot forward, disappearing into the distance in a blur of speed.","\"Max!\" Lucia called out sharply, her voice filled with frustration.","But he was already gone.","Isabella watched the direction he had vanished in before letting out a quiet sigh.","\"Forget it, Lucia,\" she said, her tone calmer. \"He will be fine. That man is far too monstrous to be bullied by anyone here.\"","Lucia remained silent for a moment, her brows still furrowed, the concern in her eyes refusing to fade.","\"I would not be this worried,\" she said slowly, \"if there were not geniuses from all the third rate forces gathered here, many of them already in the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","She let out a soft breath, trying to ease her own thoughts.","\"Still... you are right as well,\" she admitted after a pause. \"Let’s return first. We should inform Aunt Virelia before he ends up causing trouble somewhere.\"","With that, the two of them turned and continued toward their residence, while far ahead, Max moved alone toward the next place that had already caught his interest."]},{"number":1634,"title":"Chapter 1634: Jonathan and Julie","paragraphs":["Even though Max had no clear idea where the Combat Tower of the Violet Star Palace was located, he did not slow down or hesitate. His Dimensional Sovereign Body spread outward silently, extending his perception across the vast surroundings like an invisible tide. Every structure, every pathway, every fluctuation of energy began to reveal itself within his awareness as he searched with precision.","After a brief moment of scanning, he found it.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Found it,\" he thought.","Without wasting another second, his figure shot forward, cutting through the air as he rushed in that direction with controlled speed.","The Combat Tower had always been one of his primary objectives.","From the very beginning, one of the main reasons Max had chosen to participate in the Smelting Trial was because of the existence of these towers. Now that he had finally arrived at the Violet Star Palace, there was no way he would ignore such an opportunity. The thought of entering the tower and uncovering what lay within stirred a quiet anticipation within him.","More importantly, he had a very specific goal in mind.","The other part of the Overlord Body Codex.","That fragment was somewhere within this tower, and Max had no intention of delaying its acquisition. He wanted to secure it as quickly as possible and put the matter to rest, so that his full attention could return to the Smelting Trial itself.","After experiencing the first trial, his perspective had shifted.","He had underestimated it at first, but now he clearly understood its true value. The Smelting Trial was not merely a test of ability. It was an opportunity to refine oneself, to push limits, and to achieve breakthroughs that would otherwise take far longer under normal circumstances. If he used it properly, his strength could rise significantly before the start of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","That alone made it something he could not afford to neglect.","\"I just hope entering the Combat Tower and taking the remaining part of the Overlord Body Codex does not create unnecessary trouble,\" Max muttered quietly as his speed slowed.","Soon, the towering structure came into view.","The Combat Tower stood tall and imposing, its presence radiating an ancient aura that seemed to press against the senses. It felt less like a building and more like a silent guardian that had existed for countless years, watching over those who dared to challenge it.","Max stopped a short distance away, his gaze lifting slightly as he observed it.","From what he understood, the Combat Towers across different forces were not completely independent. There was a deeper connection between them.","Since he had already reached the hundredth floor in the Combat Tower of the Black Dragon Clan, he believed that this tower would recognize that achievement. If his assumption was correct, he should be able to bypass the lower levels and directly access the highest floor here as well.","That thought alone made his eyes sharpen slightly.","However, before he could take a single step forward, a voice called out from behind him.","\"Are you Max?\"","The tone carried a mixture of curiosity and challenge.","Max paused and turned around.","A group of figures was approaching him.","As his gaze fell upon them, his expression shifted, becoming slightly more serious.","He did not recognize them personally, yet their faces were not unfamiliar.","They were all among the top ten of the Weapon Master Trial.","During the ranking display earlier, the system had not only shown names and scores but had also revealed the faces of the participants. Max had taken the time to observe them briefly, committing their appearances to memory.","Now, those same individuals stood before him.","Their presence was far from ordinary.","Each of them carried a powerful aura that set them apart from the rest of the participants. The pressure they emitted was steady and refined, a clear sign that they had all reached the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm. Even within a gathering filled with geniuses, their presence stood out without the need for words.","Yet among them, four individuals were noticeably different.","They did not simply stand out because of their cultivation, but because of the quiet authority in their bearing, as if they were accustomed to being at the center of attention. Their expressions remained calm, their gazes steady, and even the others in the group seemed to unconsciously give them more space.","A young man stepped forward first, a faint smile resting on his face as he looked directly at Max.","\"Hehe, we have been looking forward to meeting you,\" he said, his tone relaxed and friendly, though there was a hint of curiosity hidden beneath it.","He placed a hand lightly on his chest as he introduced himself.","\"Let me introduce myself. I am Jonathan Myres, a true disciple of the Violet Star Palace. You can simply call me Jonathan.\"","As he spoke, he gestured toward the group behind him, clearly intending to introduce the others as well.","\"And they are—\"","Before he could continue, a young woman stepped forward with graceful composure, her movements smooth and confident. Her presence carried a subtle elegance, yet there was no mistaking the strength hidden beneath it.","\"I am Julie, from the Storm Alliance,\" she said, her voice calm and pleasant. \"I have heard quite a lot about you.\"","Max looked at the two of them and gave a slight nod, acknowledging them without any unnecessary expression.","\"Jonathan. Julie. It is good to meet you,\" he replied.","He recognized them immediately.","Jonathan had taken the second position in the first trial, while Julie had secured the third. Their strength and standing made their approach far more meaningful than that of the others.","However, the moment of civility did not last long.","A figure stepped forward from the side, his expression twisted with disdain, a cold sneer spreading across his face as he looked Max up and down.","\"You do not look strong at all,\" he said, his voice filled with mockery. \"So tell us, how exactly did you cheat your way to first place?\"","Another stepped forward immediately after, his tone even more aggressive.","\"Go on, say it. How did you do it, you cheater?\"","The hostility in their voices was unmistakable.","Several others in the group watched silently, their expressions unreadable, as if they were waiting to see how Max would respond."]},{"number":1635,"title":"Chapter 1635: Meeting Saint Reiner again!","paragraphs":["Max glanced at them briefly, his gaze calm and indifferent, as though their words carried no weight at all. He did not react, nor did he attempt to defend himself. To him, their accusations were nothing more than noise.","At that moment, Julie’s voice sounded quietly within his mind through a transmission.","\"Do not mind them,\" she said.","Her tone remained composed, though there was a faint hint of understanding behind her words.","\"There are several third rate forces here that maintain close ties with first rate powers. The factions those two belong to happen to have connections with the Sword God Palace.\"","She paused for a brief moment before continuing.","\"After what you did to the young lady of the Sword God Palace, this kind of hostility is to be expected.\"","Max listened without changing his expression.","Then, a faint smile appeared on his lips as he realized the situation here.","\"Max, what are you doing here?\"","Jonathan’s voice broke the tension, drawing the attention of everyone present.","Max glanced at him briefly before shifting his gaze toward the towering structure ahead. His eyes lingered on the Combat Tower, as if measuring something far beyond its visible form.","\"I have already reached the highest floor of the Combat Tower in the Black Dragon Clan,\" he said calmly. \"So I became curious about the one here in the Violet Star Palace.\"","A faint change appeared in Jonathan’s expression as he heard that. The curiosity in his eyes deepened, though he did not show any outward surprise.","\"You want to enter it?\" Jonathan asked, his tone carrying a hint of interest. Then a smile spread across his face. \"If that is the case, I can take you inside.\"","Max turned to look at him properly this time, a trace of surprise appearing in his eyes.","\"I can?\"","He had not expected such an offer, especially not from someone he had just met.","\"Of course you can,\" Julie said with a soft smile, her voice smooth and confident. There was a natural warmth in her expression as she glanced at Jonathan before looking back at Max. \"Jonathan would not joke about something like the Combat Tower.\"","The ease in her tone, along with the subtle glance she gave Jonathan, did not go unnoticed.","Max observed the two of them for a brief moment, and then a knowing smile appeared on his face. It was a quiet smile, but it carried enough meaning to make Jonathan’s expression stiffen slightly.","A faint hint of embarrassment flickered across Jonathan’s face before he cleared his throat.","\"So, are you coming or not?\" he asked, trying to maintain his composure, though the earlier confidence in his voice had softened just a little.","Max’s smile deepened slightly.","\"I am coming,\" he replied.","\"Good,\" Jonathan said quickly, as if eager to move past the moment. \"Let’s head inside.\"","He turned and began walking toward the entrance of the Combat Tower. The others who had come with him did not follow. Instead, they slowly retreated, casting one last glance at Max before leaving the area altogether.","Before long, only the three of them remained.","They arrived at the massive entrance of the tower, where ancient runes glowed faintly across its surface. The air around it felt heavier, filled with an energy that seemed to test anyone who approached.","Jonathan stepped forward and extended his hand toward the runes.","His fingers moved lightly across them, activating something unseen.","A subtle shift passed through the structure, almost imperceptible, yet real.","\"Go ahead and enter,\" Jonathan said without turning around. \"I have temporarily disabled the detection mechanisms around the tower. Even if you reach the hundredth floor, no one will be alerted.\"","Max raised an eyebrow slightly as he heard that.","That was not something an ordinary disciple could do.","For a moment, he studied Jonathan more carefully, reassessing him in silence. However, he did not sense any hostility, nor any hidden malice. Whatever Jonathan’s reasons were, they did not seem harmful.","In the end, Max nodded.","\"Thank you,\" he said simply.","Without hesitation, he stepped forward and pushed open the doors of the Combat Tower.","Then he walked inside.","The moment Max stepped through the entrance of the Combat Tower, the world around him shifted.","There was no sense of ascending floor by floor, no gradual transition through the lower levels that others would normally experience. The space folded silently, and in the next instant, his surroundings changed completely.","He stood at the very top.","The hundredth floor.","A vast and ancient hall stretched before him, filled with a quiet grandeur that carried the weight of countless years. The air itself felt different, dense with a presence that could not be described with simple words. It was not oppressive, yet it demanded respect from anyone who stood within it.","And at the center of that space, a familiar figure appeared.","A faint golden glow gathered, forming into an illusion-like silhouette.","Saint Reiner.","His figure looked the same as before, calm and dignified, his presence radiating a quiet authority that seemed to transcend time itself. His eyes fell upon Max, and for a brief moment, he simply observed him in silence.","Then, a smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"Good,\" Saint Reiner said, his voice gentle yet profound. \"It seems someone has finally managed to clear the first tower.\"","His gaze lingered on Max, and there was a subtle trace of approval within it when he saw Max had already opened the first three divine veins of the Seven Divine Veins.","More than that, there was recognition.","Max did not hesitate.","The moment he saw Saint Reiner, he lowered his head slightly and bowed with respect. It was not out of obligation, but out of genuine acknowledgment of the man before him.","Saint Reiner watched this and smiled faintly.","\"There is no need for such formality,\" he said, his tone carrying a hint of warmth. \"You may call me brother, as I will call you mine.\"","Max straightened slowly, meeting his gaze once more.","Before he could speak, Saint Reiner raised his hand.","A golden light gathered within his palm, condensing into a small, ancient scroll. The surface of the scroll shimmered faintly, as if it contained a power that had long been waiting to be awakened."]},{"number":1636,"title":"Chapter 1636: A Warning for Max!","paragraphs":["\"This is the remaining part of the Overlord Body Codex,\" Saint Reiner said as he extended his hand.","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Without hesitation, he stepped forward and accepted it.","The moment his fingers touched the scroll, he could feel a familiar resonance, as if the fragment he already possessed was reacting to its missing half. The two pieces called out to each other, forming a complete whole that sent a subtle ripple through his body.","Saint Reiner observed him quietly, his smile deepening just a little.","\"You have done well to reach this point,\" he said. \"The path ahead will only become more difficult, but I believe you will walk it further than most.\"","There was a brief pause.","Then his gaze turned distant, as if he was looking far beyond the present.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference,\" he continued slowly. \"That is where the true stage begins.\"","His eyes returned to Max, carrying a quiet expectation.","\"I would like to see you there.\"","Those were his final words.","The golden light around his figure began to intensify, his form gradually breaking apart into countless particles that drifted into the air.","Within moments, the illusion faded completely.","The vast hall returned to silence once more.","Only Max remained, standing at the very peak of the Combat Tower, holding the complete Overlord Body Codex in his hands.","\"Saint Reiner does not seem to recognize me,\" Max muttered, a faint frown forming on his face as he looked at the empty space where the figure had just disappeared. \"It looks like the soul fragments in the two Combat Towers are not connected. They exist as separate fragments, each carrying its own awareness.\"","The thought lingered in his mind for a moment, but before he could dwell on it any further, the space around him shifted once again.","In the next instant, he was already outside the tower.","Jonathan and Julie were waiting near the entrance, their gazes immediately turning toward him the moment he appeared.","\"How did it go?\" Jonathan asked, his tone calm, though there was a hint of curiosity beneath it.","\"It went well,\" Max replied with a nod. \"I should thank both of you for this opportunity.\"","Jonathan and Julie both acknowledged his words with a slight nod, but at that moment, a trace of hesitation appeared on their faces. It was subtle, yet noticeable enough for Max to catch it immediately.","He was about to ask what was on their minds when Jonathan spoke first.","\"Let us leave this place for now,\" he said, his tone turning slightly serious. \"It would not be wise to stay here for too long.\"","Max did not question it. He simply nodded and followed them.","The three of them moved away from the Combat Tower, leaving the area behind as they headed toward the guest mansions where the various forces were staying.","Only after they had reached a quieter part of the palace grounds did Jonathan speak again.","\"Max, there is something you should be careful about Ray,\" he said, his expression now completely serious.","Max glanced at him.","\"Ray Willer?\" he asked.","Jonathan gave a small nod.","\"Yes. Ray Willer, the one who ranked fourth in the first trial. He comes from the Supreme Sword Faction, which has deep ties with the Sword God Palace.\"","His voice lowered slightly as he continued.","\"I have heard him mention that he wants to teach you a lesson, but I do not believe his intentions stop there. I have a bad feeling about him. From everything I know, he is not someone who holds back. He is ruthless, and he is willing to do anything if it benefits him, whether it is for power, wealth, or recognition.\"","Jonathan paused briefly before adding, \"And right now, I believe he has set his sights on you.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly as he listened.","He had expected hostility from certain factions, especially those connected to the Sword God Palace, but this sounded different. This was not simple dissatisfaction or wounded pride. This carried the intent of something far more dangerous.","From Jonathan’s tone, Max could clearly sense that this was not just about confrontation.","It was about killing intent.","A faint realization surfaced in his mind as he recalled the hesitation he had seen earlier on Jonathan and Julie’s faces.","So that was the reason.","\"Thank you for the warning,\" Max said, his voice calm as he gave a slight nod.","Jonathan nodded in return.","\"In that case, we should not keep you any longer,\" he said.","Max did not object.","Soon after, Jonathan and Julie took their leave, their figures rising into the air as they headed back toward their own residence.","Max watched them for a brief moment before turning away and walking toward the mansion where the members of the Black Dragon Clan were staying.","He did not dwell too much on the matter.","At least not outwardly.","...","Meanwhile, as Jonathan and Julie made their way back, Julie could not hold back her thoughts any longer.","\"Do you think we should have asked him about it?\" she asked, her tone carrying a hint of uncertainty.","Jonathan let out a slow breath, his expression becoming more complicated.","\"I am not sure,\" he admitted. \"Max does not seem like someone we should approach so casually with such a request. He appears straightforward, but I do not want him to feel that we are trying to take advantage of him.\"","He paused for a moment before continuing.","\"We should observe him a little longer before bringing it up. From what I have seen, he seems to have connections with several first rate forces, especially the War God Palace. Only forces at that level would have access to something like the Poison Erosion Fruit, which has nearly disappeared from the Divine Realm.\"","Julie’s eyes shifted slightly as she listened.","Jonathan continued, his tone turning more thoughtful.","\"Even the Celestial Forge Pavilion no longer has it. They have already declared it extinct. If there is still any chance of finding it, it would most likely be within the War God Palace.\"","He looked ahead, his gaze steady.","\"And right now, the only link we have to them is Max. That is exactly why I do not want to rush this. If we push too soon, it might make it seem as though we are only approaching him for our own benefit.\"","Julie fell silent after hearing that, her thoughts settling as she understood his reasoning.","For now, all they could do was wait."]},{"number":1637,"title":"Chapter 1637: Second Trial","paragraphs":["After returning to the mansion where the members of the Black Dragon Clan were staying, Max went straight to meet Lady Virelia and informed her that he was fine. Only after reassuring her did he withdraw quietly to his room, his expression calm but his mind already focused on the next step.","The moment he entered, he did not waste even a breath. His figure blurred and vanished as he stepped into his Dimension of Time. Within that isolated space, where every second stretched far beyond the outside world, Max drew his sword and began practicing the Saint Origin Sword Art.","Time flowed in silence.","Again and again, he repeated the same movements, each strike carrying deeper intent than the last. The memory of the mountain being split so cleanly that even he had failed to notice it lingered in his mind.","He tried to recreate that feeling, to understand the terrifying subtlety hidden within the sword art. His concept resisted at times, clashing faintly with the technique, yet Max did not stop. He forced them together, refining his control with relentless focus.","Hours passed like drifting smoke within that dimension.","By the time the six hours of rest in the outside world came to an end, Max finally lowered his sword. A faint sharpness lingered in his eyes as he stepped out of the Dimension of Time and returned to his room.","Soon after, he made his way back to the square of the Violet Star Palace.","The vast plaza was already filled with disciples from various forces, their voices low as anticipation built in the air. The echoes of the previous trial still lingered in their minds, especially the shocking outcome that had placed Max at the very top.","At that moment, a powerful aura descended from above.","Elder Cael appeared in the sky, his figure standing tall as his gaze swept across the gathered geniuses. The murmurs in the square died down instantly as everyone turned their attention toward him.","\"The first trial has concluded,\" Elder Cael said, his voice steady yet carrying across the entire plaza with ease. \"What you have shown so far is only the foundation of your strength. The true test begins now.\"","He paused briefly, allowing his words to sink in before continuing.","\"The second trial is known as the Heavenly Reflection Arena.\"","A faint ripple spread through the crowd at the unfamiliar name.","\"In this trial, each of you will face a reflection of yourself,\" Elder Cael explained calmly. \"This reflection is not merely a copy of your appearance. It will possess your current cultivation, your techniques, and even your combat instincts.\"","A few expressions changed at once. Some grew serious while others frowned.","\"You will not be allowed to rely on luck or brute force alone,\" he continued. \"To pass this trial, you must surpass yourself. You must either defeat your reflection or endure its attacks for a fixed duration of time.\"","His gaze sharpened slightly.","\"However, understand this clearly. Your reflection will not hold back. It will fight with the same intent you would use in a life and death battle. If your will wavers, you will be eliminated.\"","A brief silence followed his words.","\"The rules are simple,\" Elder Cael said. \"You will enter one by one. Once inside, you will be transported into your own battle space. The trial will end when you achieve victory, reach the time limit, or lose consciousness. Your performance will be evaluated based on combat efficiency, control, and adaptability.\"","He raised his hand slightly, and a series of glowing portals began to form across the square, each one radiating a faint, distorted aura as if reflecting the figures standing before them.","\"Step forward when your name is called.\"","The first name echoed across the plaza.","Without hesitation, a disciple stepped out from the crowd. His expression was tense, yet determined as he approached one of the portals. For a brief moment, he stood before it, took a deep breath, and then stepped inside. His figure vanished instantly.","Soon after, the second name was called.","Another disciple walked forward, his steps slower but steady. He glanced once at the others before entering his portal.","One after another, the disciples began to move.","Some walked with confidence, their expressions calm as if they had already prepared themselves for such a challenge. Others hesitated for a moment before stepping in, their eyes filled with caution. A few clenched their fists tightly, forcing themselves forward despite the pressure.","The portals continued to flicker as each participant disappeared within them.","Max stood quietly among the crowd, his gaze fixed on the glowing entrances ahead. There was no change in his expression, yet a faint sharpness flickered in his eyes.","Facing oneself.","A trial like this was not merely about strength.","It was about breaking limits.","Not long after the first wave of participants disappeared into the portals, the sky above the square began to shimmer with a soft, rippling glow. A massive formation activated silently, and in the next moment, enormous translucent screens unfolded high in the air, spreading across the heavens like a second layer of reality.","Each screen revealed a different battlefield.","Each battlefield showed a disciple standing face to face with an exact reflection of themselves.","A wave of astonishment swept through the crowd as countless battles began to unfold at once. On one screen, two identical figures clashed with brute force, their fists colliding again and again until the very ground beneath them shattered.","On another, a pair of swordsmen moved in perfect harmony, every strike mirrored, every step anticipated before it even began. There were battles filled with roaring flames that consumed entire sections of the arena, while others were dominated by sharp flashes of lightning that tore through the sky like divine punishment.","Every battle carried the same oppressive truth.","No one held an advantage.","Because no one could surpass themselves easily.","The atmosphere grew heavier with each passing second as more disciples were pushed back by their reflections, their expressions turning grim under the relentless pressure."]},{"number":1638,"title":"Chapter 1638: Center of Attention!","paragraphs":["Some attempted to overwhelm their copies with brute force, yet they were met with equal resistance. Others tried to outmaneuver their reflections, only to find their movements predicted and countered without fail.","Names continued to echo across the square as more participants were called forward.","Then, suddenly, a name resounded with a clarity that cut through all noise.","\"Max Morgan.\"","In that instant, the entire plaza fell into complete silence.","Every gaze shifted toward him at once.","Some looked on with curiosity, others with skepticism, while a few revealed open hostility in their eyes. Yet beneath all those emotions lay a single undeniable fact. Max had already carved his presence deeply into the minds of everyone present through his performance in the previous trial.","Max stepped forward calmly, his expression unchanged despite the overwhelming attention. His movements were steady, his breathing even, as though the weight of countless gazes held no meaning to him.","Far above the square, Elder Cael stood in silence, his gaze fixed steadily on the massive screen where Max’s figure had appeared. Although his expression remained calm, the faint shift in his eyes revealed that his attention had sharpened far beyond before.","\"This is the one they were speaking about,\" a nearby elder from the Violet Star Palace said quietly, his tone carrying a trace of doubt. \"The one who supposedly took away the sword of the Sword Sovereign.\"","Another elder frowned slightly as he studied Max’s figure on the screen. \"He does not look particularly impressive. His aura is steady but he is too weak only at the 9th level of Law Awakening Realm. I don’t even know why the Black Dragon Clan send him to the Smelting Trial.\"","Elder Cael remained silent for a moment before speaking in a measured voice. \"I don’t know about that but being chosen by the sword of the Sword Sovereign was already the greatest acknowledgement one can get in the Divine Realm. A weapon like that does not choose lightly. Whether he appears weak or not is irrelevant. The fact that he was acknowledged is enough to prove there is something unusual about him.\"","The first elder narrowed his eyes slightly. \"Then what about the first trial? A hidden result beyond the system’s visible scoring... I have never seen such a thing before.\"","\"That is precisely what makes this interesting,\" Elder Cael replied calmly. \"The trial system does not give without reason.\"","In the distant pavilion, the elders of the Celestial Forge Pavilion had also begun discussing in low voices, their attention completely locked onto Max.","\"So it is him,\" one elder said, his brows raising slightly. \"The one who took the Sword Sovereign’s blade.\"","Another elder let out a faint scoff, though his gaze remained sharp. \"Took it? Or was he simply lucky? There are many ways to obtain a weapon, but being worthy of it is another matter entirely.\"","A third elder leaned forward slightly, his eyes narrowing as he observed Max’s calm stance. \"Luck alone cannot explain the hidden result from the first trial. That system has existed for countless years. Not once has it displayed something it could not quantify.\"","\"That is what troubles me,\" the second elder replied, his tone growing more serious. \"A score beyond the system’s range suggests one of two things. Either he broke the limits of the trial... or the system failed to evaluate him properly.\"","The first elder shook his head slowly. \"A failure of the system is unlikely. That formation was created by ancient experts. It has judged countless geniuses without error.\"","\"Then that leaves only one possibility,\" the third elder said quietly.","They all fell silent for a brief moment.","\"His results surpassed the highest ceiling set by the system.\"","Back in the square, elders from various third-rate forces were also exchanging glances as they watched Max appear on the screen.","\"So that is the boy everyone has been talking about,\" one elder said, his tone filled with skepticism. \"He looks no different from the others. Are we truly to believe that he obtained the Sword Sovereign’s weapon? Moreover he is too weak. A brat at the 9th level of Law Awakening Realm has no right to present here.\"","Another elder folded his arms, his gaze unwavering. \"There were witnesses. Too many to dismiss. The question is not whether he obtained it, but how.\"","A third elder let out a low breath, his eyes narrowing slightly. \"And how he achieved that hidden result. I have seen many trials in my lifetime, yet never have I heard of a result that could not even be displayed.\"","\"Perhaps it was some kind of trick,\" the first elder suggested, though his voice lacked confidence.","\"Do you truly believe that?\" the second elder asked, glancing at him.","The first elder hesitated, then shook his head slowly. \"No. Not under the eyes of so many elders of the Celestial Forge Pavilion. If it were a trick, it would have been exposed already.\"","Another elder spoke up, his tone more thoughtful. \"If both of those things are true, then we are looking at someone who either possesses an extraordinary inheritance... or an ability that we cannot yet understand.\"","Silence settled among them as their gazes returned to the screen.","Above all of them, Elder Cael continued to watch without interruption. His eyes remained fixed on Max, the faint interest within them now carrying a deeper meaning.","\"Whether he is worthy of that sword... whether he truly surpassed the trial system...\" Elder Cael murmured softly, his voice almost lost to the wind. \"This battle will give us the answer.\"","Max stepped into the portal without hesitation, his figure vanishing from the square as if swallowed by light.","In the very next moment, his image appeared on one of the largest screens suspended high in the sky, and the attention of the entire plaza shifted toward him as though pulled by an invisible force. Conversations ceased, and even those who had been skeptical earlier found themselves watching in silence.","Inside the battlefield, Max stood motionless, his posture steady and his gaze fixed straight ahead.","Before him stood his reflection."]},{"number":1639,"title":"Chapter 1639: Shock of Jonathan and Julie!","paragraphs":["It carried the same calm expression, the same restrained aura, and the same hidden depth of power that lay beneath the surface. Even the subtle fluctuations of energy within its body mirrored his own perfectly, leaving no room for deception or misjudgment.","Max studied it carefully, his eyes narrowing slightly as he took in every detail. \"Seems like an exact replica of mine. Even the aura it is releasing as same as mine.\"","This made Max wondered how the Celestial Forge Pavilion managed to create this trial. He was very curious about it.","There was no difference between them on the surface.","There was no flaw.","If he wished to win, he could not rely on what he already possessed.","He had to go beyond it. \"Let’s see if it can utilize the full power of the Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","A slow breath left his lips as his grip on the sword tightened.","Then the aura around him began to change.","It did not erupt outward in a violent surge, nor did it create a storm of overwhelming pressure. Instead, it gathered inward, compressing into something far more terrifying. The energy around his body became increasingly refined, as though every trace of excess was being stripped away, leaving behind only the purest and sharpest form of power.","The space around him seemed to grow heavier as that aura sharpened further, taking on a cutting quality that made even the distant observers feel a faint chill.","High above, Elder Cael’s eyes narrowed slightly as he watched.","\"That aura... it is condensing to an extreme degree,\" he murmured quietly.","Within the pavilion, one of the elders from the Celestial Forge Pavilion leaned forward, his relaxed expression completely gone. \"He is not preparing for a prolonged battle. He intends to end it immediately. But that could only be possible if his current strength has already surpassed the moment when he entered the trial.\"","Inside the battlefield, Max slowly raised his sword.","Every movement was deliberate.","Every motion carried precision.","The Saint Origin Sword Art began to flow through him.","It was not grand or overwhelming in appearance, yet it carried a terrifying depth. The energy did not scatter outward but instead gathered into the blade, compressing further and further until it reached a point where even the air seemed to distort slightly around it.","Across from him, the reflection reacted instantly.","It mirrored his movement without delay, raising its own sword and forming the same technique with identical structure and power.","To the outside observers, there was no visible difference between the two.","Both wielded the same sword art.","Both possessed the same strength.","Both executed the same movement.","Yet as the technique took shape, a subtle difference emerged.","Max’s aura continued to refine itself, growing sharper and more focused with each passing moment. Within his strike, there was something deeper than mere technique, something that could not be described through energy alone.","It was the essence of the Sword Saint, a comprehension that went beyond form and entered the realm of true understanding.","The reflection lacked that.","It replicated the movement perfectly.","It matched the energy flawlessly.","But it could not grasp the essence behind it.","Max stepped forward.","His sword descended.","At the same instant, the reflection also attacked, executing the Saint Origin Sword Art with identical precision.","For a brief moment, it seemed as though the two attacks would collide once again.","Then the difference revealed itself.","Max’s strike did not meet resistance.","It cut through.","The reflection’s sword art shattered instantly, unable to withstand the refined essence embedded within Max’s attack. The copied technique collapsed as though it had never truly existed, breaking apart under a force it could not comprehend.","A thin line appeared across the reflection’s body.","The next moment, it split apart cleanly.","The entire exchange ended in a single move.","Silence fell over the plaza as the scene unfolded across the massive screens in the sky.","No one spoke.","No one reacted immediately.","Because what they had just witnessed defied expectation. So far they had seen many battles happening in the screens but none of these battles ended as fast as Max’s battle.","\"He... ended it in one strike,\" someone finally muttered, his voice barely above a whisper.","\"But that was the same sword art... both of them used it...\"","\"Then why did one break so easily...\"","High above, Elder Cael’s gaze deepened as he continued to observe Max.","\"The reflection copied the form, but it failed to copy the essence,\" he said slowly, his voice carrying a quiet certainty. \"But what was that sword art? It looked terrifying.\"","Within the pavilion, one of the Celestial Forge Pavilion elders exhaled deeply, his expression filled with shock. \"That was not simply a technique. That was comprehension taken to a higher level during the execution itself. As for the sword art itself, I have no recollection of seeing it anywhere.\"","Another elder nodded, his eyes fixed on Max without wavering. \"I also think that the sword art was a little strange. It looked too simple on the surface but the seeing how reflection used the same sword art and ended up in defeat spoke volumes about it.\"","Around the square, the elders of the various forces remained silent, their earlier doubts completely erased.","Because what they had witnessed was not luck.","It was mastery.","Inside the battlefield, Max lowered his sword calmly, his aura returning to its restrained state as though nothing had happened.","\"As I figured.\" Max muttered. \"The reflection could never copy the essence of the Sword Saint contain in the sword art itself.\"","Among the crowd, Jonathan Myres stared at the screen with widened eyes, his usual composed expression completely broken.","\"...That’s it?\" he said under his breath, his voice carrying disbelief. \"He ended it like that?\"","Beside him, Julie remained silent for a moment, her gaze still fixed upward as if trying to process what she had just seen.","\"I think we underestimated him a lot,\" she said slowly, her tone filled with shock. \"His reflection didn’t even last more than a single exchange.\"","Jonathan let out a quiet breath, shaking his head slightly as he tried to collect himself. \"But that was the Heavenly Reflection Arena. It creates a perfect copy. Strength, techniques, instincts... everything should have been identical.\"","Julie’s eyes narrowed slightly as she spoke, her voice lowering. \"Identical in form, not in understanding. Did you not feel it? That sword strike... it was different.\"","Jonathan fell silent for a moment, replaying the scene in his mind.","\"...You’re saying he improved mid-battle?\" he asked, his voice uncertain.","Julie did not answer immediately, but the look in her eyes was enough.","\"That’s not something normal geniuses can do,\" she finally said, her tone turning serious. \"Even holding against your reflection is difficult. But to surpass it instantly... that’s another level entirely. I have only seen such things among the \"","Jonathan let out a dry laugh, though there was no amusement in it. \"And to think I felt that I understood his strength. No wonder he is the talk of the town in the Divine Realm these days.\"","He looked back at the screen, his expression gradually turning solemn.","Not far from them, Ray Willer stood with his arms crossed, his gaze locked onto the same screen.","Unlike Jonathan and Julie, there was no shock in his expression.","Only a cold, simmering hostility.","\"So that’s your trick,\" Ray muttered quietly, his voice low enough that only he could hear it clearly. \"A refined sword art... and some deeper comprehension.\"","His eyes narrowed further, a faint sneer forming on his lips.","\"Do they really think that makes you invincible?\"","He let out a soft scoff, though his gaze did not leave the screen for even a moment.","\"Defeating a reflection means nothing. It only proves you can surpass your current self. But no matter how strong you become, in the end you are only at the Law Awakening Realm.\"","A faint killing intent flickered within his eyes.","\"The next trial is where the legend of Max Morgan comes to and end.\"","Ray’s expression darkened slightly as he turned away, yet the tension in his posture betrayed the thoughts running through his mind."]},{"number":1640,"title":"Chapter 1640: End of the Second Trial!","paragraphs":["Inside the battlefield, the space around Max began to distort the moment his reflection was destroyed. The thin line that had split his opponent faded into nothingness, and the shattered remnants of the copied figure dissolved into particles of light that scattered into the air before vanishing completely.","A faint hum echoed across the arena as the trial formation responded.","Max stood where he was, his sword still lowered, his aura already returning to its restrained state. There was no sign of excitement or relief on his face, as though what had just occurred was nothing more than a simple exercise.","A moment later, a beam of light descended from above and enveloped his figure.","The battlefield blurred.","The next instant, Max’s body disappeared from the arena.","Back in the square of the Violet Star Palace, a ripple of energy spread through one of the portals as Max stepped out from within it. His arrival drew immediate attention, as many of the disciples and elders who had just witnessed his battle instinctively turned toward him.","For a brief moment, the noise of the plaza diminished.","Some looked at him with awe, others with confusion, while a few could not hide the lingering shock in their eyes. The image of that single strike still lingered vividly in their minds, refusing to fade no matter how hard they tried to rationalize it.","Max, however, did not react to any of it.","He simply walked forward calmly, his expression unchanged, as though the countless gazes directed at him held no meaning.","High above, Elder Cael observed his return with a quiet gaze before shifting his attention back to the trial.","\"The next batch will proceed,\" his voice echoed across the entire square, steady and authoritative.","At his command, the formation around the plaza flickered once more.","The portals that had dimmed after the previous group began to glow again, their surfaces rippling with energy as a new set of names was called out. Disciples who had been waiting stepped forward one after another, their expressions ranging from determination to tension as they approached the entrances.","Some walked with firm steps, their eyes filled with resolve after witnessing the battles before them. Others hesitated briefly, clearly shaken by the difficulty of the trial, yet forced themselves forward under the watchful eyes of the elders.","As they entered, their figures vanished into the portals, and almost immediately, new images appeared on the massive screens in the sky.","Another wave of battles began.","Two identical figures clashed once more in each displayed arena, their techniques colliding as sparks of energy erupted across the screens. The sounds of impact, though muted by the formation, still carried a sense of intensity that could be felt by everyone watching.","The cycle continued.","Batch after batch of participants entered the Heavenly Reflection Arena, each one facing the same merciless trial. Some managed to hold their ground, others were quickly overwhelmed, and a rare few showed signs of breaking through their limits under the pressure.","Yet despite the many battles unfolding, a subtle shift had taken place within the crowd.","Every now and then, gazes would drift back toward Max.","The memory of his single strike remained etched in their minds, becoming an unspoken standard against which all others were now measured.","And no matter how fierce the battles on the screens became, none had yet reached that same level of quiet, overwhelming dominance.","Time passed as the final batches of disciples entered the Heavenly Reflection Arena, and one after another, the battles displayed across the massive screens gradually came to an end.","Some emerged victorious after long and exhausting struggles, while others were forced out of the trial with pale faces and unwilling expressions, having been completely suppressed by their own reflections.","As the last participant exited the portal, the formation above the square slowly dimmed.","The enormous screens flickered once, then dissolved into countless streams of light that faded into the sky, leaving behind a heavy silence that lingered over the entire plaza.","All eyes turned upward.","A powerful aura descended once more as Elder Cael stepped forward, his figure appearing high above the square. His gaze swept across the gathered disciples, pausing for a brief moment before he spoke.","\"The second trial has concluded.\"","His voice echoed clearly, carrying an undeniable authority that silenced even the faintest whispers.","\"What you have experienced is a battle against yourselves. Some of you have endured. Some of you have failed. A very few... have surpassed the limits.\"","A subtle pause followed his words.","Then, with a simple motion of his hand, the sky above the square trembled once again.","A massive screen reappeared.","This time, it did not display battles.","It displayed rankings.","Names began to form one after another in glowing light, arranged from top to bottom, each position radiating a faint brilliance that reflected its standing.","Beside each name, a single detail appeared.","The time taken to defeat their reflection.","The moment the list stabilized, the entire plaza seemed to freeze.","At the very top—","Max Morgan.","And beside his name—","5 seconds.","A ripple of shock spread instantly through the crowd.","\"Five seconds...?\"","\"That’s not even enough time to exchange more than one move...\"","\"How is that even possible...\"","Voices rose, disbelief clear in every tone as eyes locked onto that number again and again, as though trying to confirm it was not an illusion. And it wasn’t. They had seen with their own eyes how Max had destroyed his own reflection with a single sword move.","Because of this, they were shocked a bit but not surprised.","Below his name, the second rank appeared.","The name shone brightly, yet the number beside it told a completely different story.","Jonathan - 3 minutes and 42 seconds.","And below that, the third rank—","Ray Willer - 5 minutes and 18 seconds.","The gap was so vast that it felt unreal.","Even those who had performed well in the trial found their expressions turning stiff as they stared at the difference. What had taken them several minutes of struggle had been reduced to mere seconds in Max’s case.","High above, Elder Cael observed the reactions calmly before speaking once more.","\"The rankings reflect not only victory, but efficiency, control, and the ability to surpass one’s limits.\"","His gaze shifted slightly, landing briefly on Max’s figure below.","\"A difference in seconds may represent a difference in understanding that cannot be bridged easily.\"","In the distant pavilion, one of the elders from the Celestial Forge Pavilion exhaled slowly, his voice filled with disbelief.","\"Five seconds... he ended it almost instantly.\"","Another elder shook his head, his eyes still fixed on the screen. \"No. It was not simply speed. It was a complete suppression. The moment he moved, the outcome was already decided.\"","Back in the square, the murmurs only grew louder.","Some disciples clenched their fists, unable to accept the gap. Others simply stared, their expressions blank as they struggled to process what they were seeing.","Meanwhile, Max stood quietly among them.","His gaze rose briefly toward the rankings, yet there was no change in his expression. It was as though the result held no meaning to him at all.","However, to everyone else present, that single number beside his name had already etched itself deeply into their minds.","Max was looking at the rankings and noticed Ray Willer who had killing intent towards him ranked third this time and Julie ranked fourth.","A faint glint passed through Max’s eyes as he noted the time displayed beside their names.","\"Only a few seconds of difference between them,\" he muttered softly, his voice low and thoughtful.","Although the gap between them was small, it was still enough to decide the ranking. In a trial like this, even the smallest difference represented a clear distinction in control and efficiency.","Just as Max was about to shift his gaze away, a voice cut through the air behind him.","\"Max, is it?\"","The tone was calm, yet carried an unmistakable arrogance, as though the speaker already stood above everyone else present.","Max turned.","A tall figure was approaching him.","The man’s presence was imposing, his frame straight and unyielding as he walked forward with steady steps. His eyes were locked onto Max without the slightest attempt to conceal the hostility within them.","Max recognized him instantly.","Ray Willer."]},{"number":1641,"title":"Chapter 1641: A replica of Cosmic Ascension Conference!","paragraphs":["\"You are Ray Willer.\" Max said smiling. \"I saw you did good in the second trial.\"","Ray smiled as he arrived just beside the right side of him and whispered. \"I am not here to talk with you. I am here to warn you. The next trial is going to be a survival trial and in that trial, you will be my prey and I will be the hunter. Haha, it will be a treat to hunt down the most viral genius in the Divine Realm.\"","Just as Max was about to say something to Ray about what he just said, Max found Ray disappeared into the crowd with other disciples and was gone.","Max’s gaze lingered on the place where Ray Willer had just vanished, yet there was no trace of tension on his face. The faint smile at the corner of his lips did not fade. Instead, it deepened, carrying a quiet confidence that seemed almost out of place after such a direct threat.","\"You want to hunt me?\" he murmured softly to himself, his eyes narrowing just a fraction. \"Then you better be prepared for what kind of prey I am.\"","There was no anger in his tone. No irritation. Only a calm, almost chilling certainty.","In his mind, Ray Willer’s words replayed once more. A survival trial. Hunter and prey. The intention behind those words was obvious.","Max exhaled slowly.","\"Will the Celestial Forge Pavilion really care if someone like him disappears during the trial?\" he wondered inwardly, his expression returning to normal as if nothing had happened.","His thoughts came to a halt as two familiar figures approached him through the crowd.","Lucia arrived first, her steps quick, her eyes bright with excitement that she clearly could not suppress. Isabella followed just behind her, her calm demeanor intact, yet even she could not hide the curiosity in her gaze.","Lucia did not waste a single moment.","\"What was that sword move?\" she asked, her voice filled with disbelief and excitement. Her eyes were locked onto Max as if she was trying to dissect him entirely. \"You defeated your reflection in a single strike!\"","She stepped closer, her tone growing more animated.","\"After seeing that, I thought I could do the same,\" she continued, a slight frustration slipping into her voice. \"But the moment I faced my reflection, I realized just how ridiculous that thought was. It took me nearly twenty minutes to bring mine down.\"","Isabella nodded from the side, her gaze steady but filled with the same curiosity.","\"Lucia is right,\" she said calmly. \"That kind of sword art... it is not something ordinary disciples can use. Where did you learn it, Max?\"","For a moment, both of them simply stared at him, waiting.","Max looked at the two of them, then suddenly let out a soft laugh.","\"You are overthinking it,\" he said lightly, a teasing smile forming on his face. \"I am just that talented.\"","Lucia blinked.","Isabella narrowed her eyes slightly.","\"And as for the sword art...\" Max continued, his tone dropping just a little as his smile turned mysterious. \"That is a secret.\"","Isabella’s expression instantly shifted into a small pout, her brows knitting together in clear dissatisfaction.","\"A secret?\" she repeated, clearly not pleased with that answer.","Lucia crossed her arms, though the hint of a smile still lingered on her face. \"You always say that.\"","Seeing their reactions, Max chuckled again before raising his hand slightly.","\"Alright, alright,\" he said. \"No need to look at me like that.\"","His expression softened just a little.","\"I do have some inheritance arts with me,\" he added. \"Once the Smelting Trial ends, I will pass something suitable to both of you.\"","Isabella’s expression immediately eased, and she gave a small nod.","\"Good,\" she said simply, as if that was the only answer she needed.","Lucia also smiled, her earlier frustration gone as quickly as it had appeared.","Before any of them could continue the conversation, a powerful voice suddenly echoed across the entire square.","\"Alright. It is time for the next and final trial to begin.\"","Elder Cael’s voice resounded like a bell, instantly silencing the noisy crowd. Every disciple, every elder, every observer turned their attention toward the sky where his figure stood.","\"The rewards for the second trial will be distributed shortly,\" he continued, his tone steady and authoritative.","A slight pause followed, as if he was allowing his words to sink in.","\"As all of you know, this Smelting Trial exists for one purpose,\" Elder Cael said, his gaze sweeping across the countless participants. \"To prepare you for the upcoming Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the atmosphere shifted.","Even those who were previously relaxed straightened their backs unconsciously.","\"The third and final trial,\" he continued slowly, \"will be a small replication of the environment and conditions of the Cosmic Ascension Conference itself.\"","For a brief moment, silence blanketed the entire square.","Then—","\"What?\"","\"A replication of the Conference?\"","\"How is that even possible?\"","Whispers erupted from every direction as shock spread like wildfire among the disciples.","Even the elders from the various third rate forces could not maintain their composure. Their expressions changed one after another, disbelief clearly written across their faces.","\"They never mentioned this before...\"","\"To simulate the Cosmic Ascension Conference... the Celestial Forge Pavilion is going this far?\"","\"Celestial Forge Pavilion has prepare well this time.\"","High above, Elder Cael remained unmoved as he watched their reactions.","Meanwhile, Max stood quietly among the crowd, his expression calm, yet his eyes had sharpened.","\"A survival trial... and a replica of the Conference.\"","His lips curved slightly.","\"Now this is getting interesting.\"","Max only knew a single concrete detail about the Cosmic Ascension Conference, and that was the suppression of cultivation to the peak of the Law Refinement Realm for every participant who entered it.","Beyond that one fact, everything else remained unknown to him, like a vast territory covered in fog. He did not know how the Conference was structured, he did not know what rules governed it, and he had no understanding of how one was expected to survive or rise within such an event.","Entering something like that without knowledge or preparation was no different from stepping onto a battlefield where every opponent knew the terrain except you. Even for Max, who had always relied on his strength and adaptability, that kind of uncertainty carried risk.","But now, as he listened to Elder Cael reveal that the final trial had been designed as a replica of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, a subtle shift occurred within him.","The uncertainty did not disappear, but it transformed into something else. His eyes sharpened, and a faint excitement began to stir deep within him. This was not just another trial. This was an opportunity to understand the battlefield that awaited him in the future."]},{"number":1642,"title":"Chapter 1642: Importance of the Last Trial!","paragraphs":["\"As all of you already know, the cultivation of every participant in the Cosmic Ascension Conference will be suppressed to the peak of the Law Refinement Realm,\" Elder Cael’s voice rang out clearly, carrying across the entire square without the slightest obstruction.","A quiet murmur spread through the crowd, though most of the disciples had already heard of this rule before. Even so, hearing it again in such a setting made the reality of it feel heavier.","\"This trial will replicate that exact condition,\" Elder Cael continued, his tone steady and controlled. \"It will allow each of you to personally experience what it means to fight under those limitations and prepare yourselves for what lies ahead.\"","As his words settled, he raised his hand slightly, and the space above the square began to tremble as if something was being pulled into existence.","Moments later, a massive painting appeared in the sky.","It stretched wide, far larger than any ordinary canvas, almost as if a piece of another world had been unfolded and hung in the air for all to see. Within the painting was a dense forest, ancient and vast, its towering trees casting long shadows that seemed to shift even without wind. The deeper one looked, the more unsettling it felt, as though the forest itself was watching.","It did not feel like a lifeless image.","It felt real.","\"This,\" Elder Cael said as his gaze fell upon the painting, \"is a treasure that the Celestial Forge Pavilion recently obtained from an ancient site.\"","His voice paused briefly before he continued.","\"It is called the Soul Sealing Painting.\"","The moment its name was spoken, a visible change passed through the elders present. Some narrowed their eyes, while others straightened slightly, clearly recognizing that this was no ordinary artifact.","\"With this treasure, one’s soul can be sealed within the painting,\" Elder Cael explained, his tone growing more serious. \"Once inside, everything operates according to the rules that have been set beforehand. Whether you live or die, whether you succeed or fail, all of it depends on those rules.\"","He let his words linger before continuing.","\"In essence, it is a self-contained world.\"","Max’s gaze remained fixed on the forest within the painting as he listened. He could sense something unusual from it, a fluctuation that did not come from energy or aura, but from something deeper. It resonated faintly with his soul, as though the painting was not merely an object but a gateway.","\"The rules within this Soul Sealing Painting have already been configured,\" Elder Cael continued, \"to match those of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","A ripple of surprise spread through the crowd once more.","\"For those of you who are unaware, the Cosmic Ascension Conference consists of two rounds,\" he said, raising his hand slightly as if to emphasize the structure.","\"The first round exists to determine the top one hundred participants.\"","\"The second round exists to determine the final victor among those one hundred.\"","His gaze swept across the disciples, and even those who had been whispering fell silent under the weight of his words.","\"Because of this structure, the first round takes the form of a battle royale,\" he continued, his tone calm yet carrying an undeniable pressure. \"This battle does not end until the number of participants is reduced to a mere one hundred.\"","A heavy silence fell over the square.","\"You must understand,\" Elder Cael added, his expression growing more solemn, \"that the Cosmic Ascension Conference gathers geniuses from across the entire Divine Realm. The number of participants is not in the thousands or millions. It often reaches into the trillions.\"","Even those who had heard of this before felt their expressions change. The sheer scale of it was enough to shake anyone who truly thought about it.","\"Imagine a battlefield of that size,\" he said slowly. \"A battle royale where trillions enter, and only one hundred remain.\"","Max stood quietly, but his mind had already begun to picture it. Endless combat. Countless enemies. No safe ground. No time to rest. Survival alone would be a challenge, let alone rising above all others.","\"That kind of trial,\" Elder Cael said, \"is beyond anything most of you have ever experienced.\"","He then turned his attention back to the massive painting.","\"However, such numbers are not necessary for this trial,\" he added, his tone returning to its usual calm.","A faint, almost knowing smile appeared on his face.","\"This Soul Sealing Painting is more than capable of hosting a battle royale for a limited number of participants. For this trial, it will accommodate around a hundred of you.\"","His words settled into the minds of everyone present.","A smaller battlefield.","Fewer participants.","But the same rules.","The same objective.","The same ruthless elimination.","Max’s lips curved into a faint smile as he looked at the forest within the painting.","Now that he understood what awaited him, the excitement within him grew stronger.","\"The last round of the Smelting Trial... is called the Survival Trial,\" Elder Cael continued, his voice steady yet carrying a weight that pressed upon every disciple present.","The moment those words were spoken, the atmosphere in the square changed completely. The earlier excitement and curiosity were still there, but they were now mixed with something heavier. Tension. Anticipation. A faint sense of danger that no one could ignore.","Elder Cael’s gaze swept across the crowd before he spoke again.","\"There are a total of seven hundred and forty two disciples participating in this round,\" he said, each word clear and deliberate. \"And this trial will only come to an end... once that number is reduced to fifty.\"","He added. \"Dying in the painting means you are eliminated and your soul will return to the body.\"","A wave of silence spread instantly.","Even those who had been whispering earlier fell quiet as the meaning behind his words sank in.","\"In other words,\" Elder Cael continued without pause, \"you are not competing for victory in the traditional sense. You are competing to survive.\"","His voice did not rise, yet it echoed deeply within everyone’s mind.","\"You must remain alive within the Soul Sealing Painting until the number of participants is reduced to fifty.\"","The simplicity of the rule made it even more brutal.","There were no complicated conditions. No hidden scoring system. No external judgment.","Survive... or be eliminated.","That was all.","Some disciples unconsciously clenched their fists. Others exchanged uneasy glances. A few, however, had already begun to smile, their eyes filled with excitement as if they had been waiting for something like this.","Max stood among them, his expression calm as ever, but his eyes had sharpened noticeably.","Seven hundred and forty two participants.","Fifty survivors.","That meant more than six hundred would fall.","\"This is closer to the real Conference than I expected,\" he thought, a faint glint appearing in his eyes.","High above, Elder Cael raised his hand and pointed toward the massive painting that hovered in the sky like a gateway to another world.","\"Now,\" he said, his tone carrying a finality that left no room for hesitation, \"all participants, step forward.\"","His finger remained directed at the Soul Sealing Painting, the forest within it seeming darker than before, as if it was already waiting to swallow them whole.","\"Stand before the painting,\" he commanded, \"and prepare yourselves for the last and final trial of the Smelting Trial.\"","For a brief moment, no one moved.","Then—","One disciple stepped forward.","Then another.","Soon, the entire crowd began to shift as hundreds of figures advanced toward the painting, their expressions varying from excitement to fear, from determination to cold indifference.","Lucia moved closer to Max, her earlier excitement now mixed with seriousness.","\"All the best, Max.\" She said smiling.","\"I don’t need it but thanks.\" Max said calmly.","\"I will do my best to enter top 50 this time.\" Isabella also came to his and said to herself.","Max nodded. \"You two will be fine. Just be careful and don’t take fights when there are more people around.\"","Both Lucia and Isabella nodded."]},{"number":1643,"title":"Chapter 1643: Into the Painting World!","paragraphs":["\"Alright,\" Elder Cael said as he stood high above the square, his voice carrying clearly across the silent crowd. \"I will now send your souls into the Soul Sealing Painting.\"","The moment his words fell, both of his hands began moving rapidly, forming one hand seal after another with astonishing precision. Streams of divine energy gathered around him, causing the air itself to tremble faintly.","Then—","Golden light descended from the sky.","The light spread across the entire square like a divine curtain, enveloping every disciple standing before the Soul Sealing Painting. It was warm at first, almost gentle, but within moments, everyone felt a strange pulling sensation coming from deep within themselves.","It was not their bodies being dragged.","It was their souls.","Max immediately felt an invisible force latch onto his consciousness. Before he could fully examine it, the world around him blurred violently. The square, the disciples, the elders, and even the enormous painting in the sky all twisted into streaks of light.","Then everything went dark for a brief moment.","When Max opened his eyes again, he found himself standing in the middle of a forest.","Tall ancient trees stretched endlessly in every direction, their thick trunks covered in dark moss while massive branches blocked most of the light above. The air carried a damp earthy smell, and faint mist drifted between the trees, giving the forest an eerily realistic atmosphere.","Max slowly looked around, his eyes narrowing slightly.","\"Are we truly inside a painted world?\" he muttered softly.","He crouched slightly and touched the ground beneath him. The soil felt real. The rough bark of the nearby tree felt real. Even the cold moisture lingering on the leaves brushing against his hand felt no different from an actual world.","There was no sense of illusion at all.","For a moment, Max could not help but admire the absurdity of such a treasure. A painting capable of sealing souls and creating a world realistic enough to deceive all five senses was far beyond ordinary imagination.","As that thought crossed his mind, another realization followed closely behind.","If even this Soul Sealing Painting could create such a massive environment for only hundreds of participants, then what kind of method did the true Cosmic Ascension Conference use to contain trillions of geniuses at once?","The scale alone was terrifying to imagine.","\"I wonder how the Conference itself handles something on that level,\" Max murmured quietly as he straightened up. \"A battlefield for trillions of participants... something like a painting should not even be enough.\"","The more he thought about it, the more he realized how terrifying the foundations of the Cosmic Ascension Conference truly were.","However, Max did not remain standing there for long. Since the trial had already begun, wasting time was meaningless.","He began moving through the forest calmly, his senses spread outward while his Dimensional Sovereign Body silently scanned the surroundings.","The forest was unusually quiet.","Too quiet.","Then suddenly—","Max stopped.","The atmosphere around him changed.","Rustling sounds echoed from every direction as large shadows emerged from between the trees one after another. Heavy footsteps shook the ground faintly, and low growls filled the air.","In just a few breaths, Max found himself completely surrounded.","However, they were not disciples.","They were monsters.","Max’s eyes swept across them calmly while his Dimensional Sovereign Body instantly analyzed every single creature present.","\"There are twenty seven of them,\" he thought.","The creatures surrounding him looked savage and grotesque. Some resembled enormous black wolves with crimson eyes and razor sharp fangs dripping with corrosive saliva.","Others were humanoid beasts covered in dark scales with long clawed arms powerful enough to tear apart steel. There were even massive spider-like monsters clinging to the trees above, their countless eyes glowing coldly within the shadows.","What shocked Max the most was not their appearance.","It was their strength.","Every single one of them possessed cultivation at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.","A normal disciple at the same realm would instantly panic after being surrounded by twenty seven peak Law Refinement monsters simultaneously.","Yet Max merely stood there quietly.","The monsters growled as they slowly closed in around him, their killing intent spreading heavily through the forest.","Then—","One of the wolf-like beasts suddenly lunged toward him.","The instant it moved, the others followed.","The forest erupted into chaos as twenty seven monsters charged at Max from every direction at terrifying speed. Some leapt from the ground while others attacked from above, sealing nearly every possible path of escape.","However, Max did not retreat.","His expression remained calm as he slowly took his sword out.","A faint sword hum echoed softly through the forest.","In the next moment, Max moved.","There was no explosion of energy.","No flashy wave of power.","He simply stepped forward and swung his sword once.","Saint Origin Sword Art.","For a brief instant, nothing seemed to happen.","The monsters continued charging forward as if Max’s attack had completely failed.","Then—","Thin silver lines suddenly appeared across the bodies of every monster surrounding him.","The world became silent.","A second later, blood erupted into the air.","The enormous wolf beasts split cleanly into pieces. The scaled humanoid monsters were sliced apart so smoothly that their upper bodies slid from their waists before crashing to the ground. Even the giant spiders hanging from the trees were severed in half before they could release a single screech.","Twenty seven monsters.","All dead.","And Max had only used a single strike.","The terrifying part was that the surrounding forest remained almost untouched. The trees still stood tall, and the ground barely showed signs of battle. It was as though the sword strike had selectively erased only the lives of the monsters themselves.","Max slowly lowered his sword, his gaze calm as he looked at the corpses littering the forest floor.","Even now, the Saint Origin Sword Art still amazed him.","The attack had been so refined and concentrated that the monsters had not even realized they were already dead. Only after the sword intent completely passed through their bodies did the destruction reveal itself.","A faint smile appeared on Max’s face.","\"This sword art...\" he muttered softly. \"The more I use it, the more terrifying it becomes.\""]},{"number":1644,"title":"Chapter 1644: Interesting Painting World!","paragraphs":["After killing the monsters with a single strike of the Saint Origin Sword Art, Max had barely lowered his sword when a series of notifications suddenly appeared before his eyes.","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]",".....","The notifications continued appearing one after another at astonishing speed, filling his vision continuously until all twenty seven kills had been accounted for.","Max blinked slightly as he looked at the messages floating before him.","\"So killing monsters here grants points?\" he muttered with visible surprise.","His gaze swept across the notifications again as he quickly calculated the total.","\"Ten points from each monster...\" he said thoughtfully. \"Which means a peak tenth level Law Refinement Realm monster is worth ten killing points.\"","The moment that thought crossed his mind, another change suddenly occurred.","A small translucent screen appeared directly within his field of vision.","It floated quietly before him, simple in appearance yet extremely clear.","[Name: Max Morgan]","[Killing Points: 270]","[Rank: 6]","Max narrowed his eyes slightly as he studied the information displayed before him.","\"A ranking system?\" he murmured.","His expression turned thoughtful almost immediately.","\"Is this updating in real time based on accumulated killing points?\"","Until now, he had assumed the Survival Trial would simply be a chaotic battle royale where participants fought to remain among the last survivors. However, the appearance of this ranking system made him realize the trial was far more structured than he initially thought.","The Soul Sealing Painting was not merely a battlefield.","It was an entire self-regulating world with its own laws and systems.","The deeper Max observed it, the more shocked he became by the sophistication behind it all. Everything had been carefully arranged to imitate the Cosmic Ascension Conference as closely as possible.","Just as he was contemplating the depth of this artificial world, his Dimensional Sovereign Body suddenly detected movement nearby.","Rustling sounds echoed from all directions.","Without warning, another group of monsters emerged from the forest and surrounded him once more.","Max raised an eyebrow slightly.","\"Another horde already?\" he said, sounding genuinely surprised this time. \"This really is a survival trial.\"","The monsters before him were no weaker than the previous group. Large beast-like creatures with vicious claws and bloodshot eyes slowly circled him while releasing low threatening growls. Their auras clearly indicated that every single one of them stood at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.","However, Max showed no intention of wasting time.","The moment the monsters lunged toward him, his sword moved again.","A cold flash of sword light swept through the forest.","The Saint Origin Sword Art erupted silently once more.","For a brief instant, the monsters continued charging as though nothing had happened.","Then their bodies split apart simultaneously.","Blood sprayed across the forest as corpses crashed heavily onto the ground one after another.","Once again, the terrifying precision of the Saint Origin Sword Art revealed itself completely. There were no massive shockwaves or destructive explosions. The sword strike was so refined that only the targets themselves were destroyed.","Moments later, the familiar notifications began appearing rapidly before Max’s eyes again.","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]","[+10 Killing Points]","....","The notifications stacked continuously until the entire group had been accounted for.","Soon, the screen before him updated once again.","[Name: Max Morgan]","[Killing Points: 500]","[Rank: 5]","\"Rank five...\" Max muttered quietly as he looked at the updated ranking.","However, he did not pay too much attention to it.","With his current strength, climbing the rankings was not difficult. What truly interested him was something else entirely.","A thoughtful look appeared in his eyes.","He already understood that if someone died within the Soul Sealing Painting, their soul would simply be expelled and returned to their original body outside. In other words, elimination here did not mean true death.","But another question quickly surfaced in his mind.","\"What happens if a participant kills another participant?\" Max wondered inwardly.","His eyes flickered faintly.","\"Do their killing points disappear...\"","\"Or are they transferred to the killer?\"","The more he thought about it, the more likely the second possibility seemed.","And if that was true—","Then the real danger of this Survival Trial was not the monsters.","It was the participants themselves.","\"I need to find other participants,\" Max muttered quietly as he looked into the depths of the endless forest before him.","The moment those words left his mouth, seven colored lightning suddenly burst out around his body.","Boom!","The ground beneath Max instantly shattered apart as his figure shot forward at astonishing speed.","His body transformed into a streak of seven colored light that tore through the forest like a meteor. Massive trees blurred past him one after another while violent winds exploded outward in his wake.","As he moved, his Dimensional Sovereign Body continuously spread through the surroundings, scanning everything within range.","Since killing monsters granted killing points, Max was almost certain that participants themselves were the true source of points within this trial. After all, a survival trial designed to imitate the Cosmic Ascension Conference would never remain a simple monster hunt.","The real danger had always been the other geniuses.","And just as Max expected, it did not take long before he sensed powerful energy fluctuations erupting somewhere ahead.","Boom!","A violent explosion echoed through the forest.","The sounds of weapon clashes followed immediately after, mixed with angry shouts and bursts of spiritual energy.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Without slowing down, he immediately changed direction and rushed toward the source.","Soon, he arrived above a large clearing hidden deep within the forest.","The scene below him was chaotic.","More than a dozen disciples were fighting fiercely against one another while several monster corpses lay scattered across the battlefield. Trees had already been uprooted while deep craters covered the ground from the intensity of the battle.","A young man wielding a massive spear roared furiously as he forced another participant backward.","\"Hand over your points and eliminate yourself!\" he shouted. \"You already lost!\"","The disciple being pressured spat out blood before glaring fiercely.","\"You think you can scare me?\" he roared back angrily. \"If you want my points, then come and take them yourself!\"","Nearby, another participant suddenly sneered coldly while wiping blood from the corner of his lips.","\"Stop pretending like any of us are here to cooperate,\" he said mockingly. \"Everyone already understands the rules. The monsters are just bait. The fastest way to gain points is by hunting other participants.\"","Several people nearby remained silent, but the greed within their eyes made it clear they agreed completely.","Nobody trusted anyone.","Nobody wanted to form alliances.","After all, only fifty participants could survive.","That meant everyone else had to fall.","Just then, one of the participants suddenly sensed movement above the clearing.","His expression changed immediately as he looked toward the sky.","\"Wait...\" he said abruptly before pointing upward. \"Someone’s there!\"","The fierce battle below instantly slowed as every participant turned their attention upward.","Then they saw him."]},{"number":1645,"title":"Chapter 1645: Finding Others!","paragraphs":["Max Morgan.","For a brief moment, the entire clearing fell silent.","Several disciples visibly stiffened the instant they recognized his face. Their expressions turned serious almost immediately as memories of the previous two trials surfaced within their minds.","\"That’s Max Morgan...\"","\"The one who ranked first in both trials?\"","\"The genius who killed his reflection in only five seconds?\"","A faint wave of tension spread through the group.","Even the disciples who had been trying to kill each other moments earlier unconsciously stopped moving as they stared at Max with caution and vigilance.","After all, Max’s performance in the previous trials had been far too shocking.","Whether it was dominating the Weapon Master Trial or defeating his own reflection almost instantly in the second trial, he had already become one of the most talked about geniuses among all the participating third rate forces.","Above the clearing, Max floated calmly in the air while seven colored lightning crackled faintly around his body. His expression remained relaxed as his gaze slowly swept across the disciples below as though he was merely observing a group of ordinary people.","That calmness alone placed enormous pressure on everyone present.","One participant gripping a long sword swallowed nervously before speaking quietly.","\"This is bad...\"","Another disciple narrowed his eyes as he carefully sensed Max’s aura.","\"If it’s really him...\" he muttered seriously, \"then none of us can fight him alone.\"","However, just as the atmosphere became increasingly tense, a sharp eyed young man suddenly frowned deeply.","\"Wait.\"","His gaze sharpened.","\"There’s something wrong.\"","Several people immediately looked toward him.","The young man continued staring at Max carefully before his expression slowly changed.","\"That cultivation...\"","The surrounding participants quickly sensed Max’s aura once more.","Then suddenly—","Shock appeared on multiple faces.","\"He’s only at the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm?\"","\"What?\"","\"That can’t be right!\"","A ripple spread through the clearing instantly.","The nervous expressions many participants previously held slowly began changing.","A burly disciple carrying a massive battle axe suddenly burst into loud laughter.","\"Hahaha! So that’s what it is!\"","He pointed his axe toward Max mockingly.","\"I was wondering why his aura felt weaker than expected.\"","Another participant immediately sneered after sensing Max’s cultivation more carefully.","\"So the famous Max Morgan is actually weaker than everyone here.\"","The woman holding twin daggers narrowed her eyes while observing Max calmly.","\"In the previous trials, talent and comprehension played a huge role,\" she said slowly. \"But this trial is different.\"","Her lips curved slightly.","\"This is a survival battlefield.\"","Several disciples nodded in agreement.","After entering the Soul Sealing Painting, every participant had their cultivation suppressed to the peak of the Law Refinement Realm. Most of the disciples present originally possessed cultivation above that level, which meant they now stood equally at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.","However, Max was different.","His actual cultivation realm was only at the ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","Even after entering the painting, his aura still remained noticeably below theirs.","The black saber disciple stared at Max before suddenly laughing softly.","\"So the strongest genius from the previous trials is actually the weakest person here in terms of cultivation.\"","Another disciple crossed his arms confidently.","\"Hmph. Talent is useless if your cultivation is too low.\"","\"One or two minor realms might not matter normally,\" a spear wielding participant added calmly, \"but the gap between the Law Awakening Realm and the peak of the Law Refinement Realm is enormous.\"","His eyes gleamed faintly.","\"That difference is enough to crush him.\"","The atmosphere gradually shifted.","The fear everyone initially felt toward Max slowly transformed into confidence and greed.","A young man wielding a heavy hammer laughed loudly.","\"We really got scared over nothing.\"","Another disciple smirked coldly.","\"In this trial, we actually hold the advantage over him.\"","The black saber disciple nodded slowly while keeping his eyes fixed on Max.","\"No matter how monstrous his talent may be, cultivation is still the foundation of strength,\" he said calmly. \"This is not a trial where talent alone can overturn everything.\"","The woman holding twin daggers still remained cautious.","\"Even so, don’t underestimate him carelessly,\" she warned quietly. \"Anyone capable of taking first place in two consecutive trials cannot be simple.\"","\"Of course,\" the battle axe wielder replied with a grin. \"But there are more than fifteen of us here, all standing at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.\"","He lifted his axe onto his shoulder confidently.","\"And he’s just a ninth level Law Awakening cultivator.\"","Several people immediately began smiling.","The fear in their hearts had almost completely vanished by now.","In its place came greed.","A spear wielder suddenly narrowed his eyes thoughtfully.","\"Actually... this might be a huge opportunity for us.\"","The others looked toward him.","\"If killing participants transfers killing points,\" he continued slowly, \"then someone like Max should already have an enormous amount of points on him.\"","The moment those words were spoken, several disciples’ eyes lit up immediately.","A young man carrying a hammer inhaled sharply.","\"He’s basically a walking treasure chest.\"","Another disciple laughed greedily.","\"If we kill him here, our rankings might instantly soar into the top fifty.\"","The expressions of the surrounding participants gradually turned dangerous.","The black saber disciple slowly raised his weapon toward Max.","\"Then it’s settled,\" he said coldly.","His gaze swept across the others.","\"We stop fighting among ourselves for now.\"","\"We work together first...\"","His eyes locked onto Max above the clearing.","\"And eliminate him.\"","One after another, the surrounding disciples nodded in agreement.","In just moments, the same participants who had been trying to kill each other moments earlier suddenly formed a temporary alliance.","Their weapons slowly turned upward.","Every single killing intent became focused on Max alone.","Meanwhile, Max quietly listened to their entire discussion from above without interrupting even once.","The seven colored lightning around his body flickered faintly as the corners of his lips slowly curved upward.","There was no anger on his face.","No frustration.","Only amusement.","\"They truly believe cultivation level alone determines victory,\" Max thought calmly as he looked down at the confident group below.","The faint smile on his face deepened slightly."]},{"number":1646,"title":"Chapter 1646: Vein of Strength - 1","paragraphs":["Seeing every weapon aimed directly at him while more than a dozen killing intents locked onto his body at the same time, Max remained completely calm as though the situation before him carried no threat whatsoever, and not even the slightest trace of nervousness appeared on his face despite the overwhelming hostility surrounding him from every direction.","Instead, a smile slowly appeared across his face.","However, this was not the calm and composed smile that people usually associated with him. This smile carried an unmistakable sense of excitement, almost as though he had finally found something worthy of entertaining him after a long period of boredom.","There was anticipation within his eyes, a dangerous eagerness that only intensified the more greed and confidence he sensed from the disciples standing below him.","Those participants genuinely believed that because Max’s cultivation realm was lower than theirs, they could suppress him through sheer numbers alone, and the certainty within their expressions made the battle spirit inside Max rise even further.","In their eyes, this trial favored them completely.","They believed Max was weak.","They believed his previous performances had merely been luck or temporary brilliance that could never overcome the advantage of superior cultivation.","And Max found that line of thinking amusing beyond words.","The seven-colored lightning surrounding his body crackled violently as he slowly descended from the sky with complete composure, stopping only a few meters above the ground while his gaze calmly swept across every participant gathered around him.","The faint smile on his face gradually widened as though he had already seen the outcome of the battle long before it even began.","\"So all of you decided to target me first?\" Max asked lightly, his tone carrying neither anger nor fear, but instead sounding almost entertained by the situation.","The disciple wielding the massive battle axe immediately let out a cold sneer as he stepped forward slightly and pointed the heavy weapon toward Max.","\"You should feel honored,\" he mocked arrogantly. \"Not everyone gets treated like such a valuable target during the trial.\"","Another participant standing nearby laughed harshly while gripping his weapon tighter.","\"You only have yourself to blame for standing out too much during the previous trials,\" he said coldly. \"Now everyone wants your points.\"","The disciple holding the black saber slowly raised his weapon as a sharp glint flashed through his eyes.","\"You should surrender your points and eliminate yourself peacefully,\" he said in a calm but threatening voice. \"Otherwise, what happens next is going to become extremely painful for you.\"","Hearing those words, Max merely chuckled softly under his breath as though he had just heard something genuinely funny.","Then he spoke a single word.","\"Come.\"","The instant that word left his mouth, the entire atmosphere changed completely.","Boom!","A terrifying pressure erupted violently from Max’s body like a sleeping monster finally awakening. The ground beneath him exploded apart instantly as massive cracks spread across the clearing at an astonishing speed, tearing through the earth while nearby trees trembled fiercely under the force of the pressure wave.","Countless leaves were blown away into the sky as the sheer power radiating from Max distorted the surrounding air itself.","The expressions of the disciples surrounding him changed immediately.","\"What is this pressure?!\" one participant shouted in shock as his face paled.","\"This aura...\" another disciple muttered while instinctively stepping backward.","Before anyone could react any further, Max slowly clenched his fist.","At that exact moment, the Third Divine Vein within the Seven Divine Veins opened completely inside his body.","Vein of Strength.","Boom!!!","An overwhelming surge of power exploded from within Max like a volcanic eruption that had been suppressed for far too long. The blood flowing through his body roared violently as unimaginable physical strength flooded every muscle, every bone, and every cell with terrifying force.","Veins glowing faintly beneath his skin pulsed with immense energy while the surrounding space distorted under the pressure radiating from him.","This was the first time since opening the Third Divine Vein that Max had fully unleashed the Vein of Strength during an actual battle.","And the effect was horrifying.","The surrounding disciples felt as though an invisible mountain had descended directly onto their shoulders, causing several participants to stagger backward instinctively as fear began to appear within their eyes.","\"This...\" the black saber disciple muttered in disbelief while staring at Max with widened eyes.","\"How can a ninth level Law Awakening cultivator release this kind of power?!\"","Max slowly raised his head, and at that moment, even without using concepts, laws, or combat techniques, the raw physical might erupting from his body alone already felt overwhelmingly oppressive to everyone present.","It was pure strength.","Absolute strength.","The Vein of Strength amplified Max’s physical power to such an absurd level that even the slightest movement of his body caused the surrounding air to tremble faintly, as though space itself struggled to endure the monstrous force flowing within him.","The woman wielding twin daggers felt her heartbeat accelerate uncontrollably as danger instincts screamed within her mind.","\"This pressure... it’s dangerous!\" she said with visible fear in her voice.","The battle axe wielder gritted his teeth as sweat slowly formed across his forehead.","\"No,\" he said forcefully while trying to steady himself. \"He’s bluffing. There’s no way his real strength can match this aura.\"","Yet even as he spoke those words, uncertainty had already appeared deep within his eyes.","Max lowered his gaze toward his own hand slowly while feeling the immense power coursing throughout his body, and the sensation almost felt intoxicating. Endless strength overflowed from deep within him with such overwhelming intensity that it genuinely felt as though he could shatter mountains apart with his bare fists alone.","Then suddenly—","Max disappeared.","Boom!","The ground where he had been standing exploded apart instantly from the force of his movement alone.","Several disciples’ pupils contracted violently.","\"So fast!\"","Before anyone could properly react, Max had already appeared directly in front of the battle axe wielder.","The disciple’s expression changed drastically as instinctive fear exploded within his mind. He roared loudly while raising his battle axe and pouring every ounce of his power into defense.","However, Max simply threw a punch forward.","He did not use sword intent.","He did not use lightning.","He did not use concepts, laws, or martial techniques.","It was merely a single punch empowered by the Vein of Strength.","The moment that punch collided against the massive axe—","Boom!!!","A deafening explosion erupted across the clearing as the enormous battle axe shattered apart instantly under the terrifying force of Max’s strike. The disciple behind it spat blood violently while his defenses were crushed completely, and his body flew backward like a broken ragdoll before smashing through dozens of giant trees one after another.","The entire clearing fell silent.","Everyone stared at the scene in horror.","One punch.","Only one punch.","And a peak Law Refinement Realm participant had been completely overwhelmed without any ability to resist.","Before the others could even recover from their shock, Max moved again.","His figure flashed across the battlefield like a phantom moving faster than their eyes could follow.","Boom!","A spear shattered into countless fragments.","Boom!","A massive hammer exploded apart instantly.","Boom!","Another participant was blasted high into the air while coughing blood uncontrollably.","Everywhere Max passed, destruction followed behind him.","The truly terrifying part was that he still had not used a single concept or combat technique throughout the battle.","He relied purely on the raw physical strength granted by the Vein of Strength.","And that strength alone was already enough to completely dominate peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses as though they were powerless before him."]},{"number":1647,"title":"Chapter 1647: Vein of Strength - 2","paragraphs":["Panic rapidly spread throughout the clearing.","\"This monster...\"","\"How is this even possible?!\"","\"He’s not even using concepts!\"","The expressions of the disciples who had mocked Max only moments earlier were now filled entirely with fear and disbelief as the reality before them shattered everything they thought they understood.","Only now did they finally realize something terrifying.","They had assumed cultivation level was Max’s greatest weakness.","But the truth was far more horrifying.","Even without relying on cultivation, Max was already strong enough to crush every single one of them.","The entire clearing had already descended into complete chaos as shattered trees littered the battlefield in every direction while enormous craters spread across the ground from the terrifying force behind Max’s attacks.","The once dense forest had been devastated beyond recognition, with broken trunks, collapsed earth, and countless fragments of stone scattered everywhere. Several disciples lay sprawled across the ruined battlefield while blood continuously dripped from their mouths, and the confidence they once possessed when surrounding Max earlier had now completely disappeared, replaced entirely by fear and disbelief.","Meanwhile, Max himself stood calmly in the center of the destruction as though the devastation around him had nothing to do with him at all.","Seven-colored lightning crackled faintly around his body while violent currents of power continued surging through every part of him without slowing in the slightest.","The Third Divine Vein remained fully active.","Vein of Strength.","Max slowly clenched his fist as he carefully felt the terrifying physical power coursing through his body like an endless torrent. Every muscle within him overflowed with monstrous force while every movement carried enough weight to distort the surrounding air faintly.","Even now, despite the destruction he had already caused, Max could clearly feel that he was still subconsciously restraining himself to some extent because the overwhelming power flooding his body had already surpassed the level these participants could possibly endure.","\"I’m already holding back...\" Max thought quietly while his gaze swept across the terrified disciples surrounding him.","His eyes slowly moved from one participant to another as he observed the fear spreading across their faces.","\"And yet I can still crush peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses this easily.\"","The realization caused even Max himself to feel slightly surprised deep inside.","These participants were not weak cultivators by any means. Every single person gathered here was considered a genius within their respective third-rate forces, individuals who normally stood above ordinary cultivators and possessed enough talent to dominate those below them.","Under normal circumstances, a peak Law Refinement Realm cultivator should have been more than capable of suppressing a ninth-level Law Awakening Realm cultivator with overwhelming ease.","Yet before the Vein of Strength—","They appeared utterly powerless.","A faint smile slowly formed on Max’s face as he continued feeling the terrifying power surging throughout his body.","\"If this is the result while I’m restraining myself...\"","The light within his eyes gradually sharpened.","\"Then what happens if I stop holding back entirely?\"","The moment that thought surfaced within his mind—","Boom!!!","A horrifying shockwave erupted violently from Max’s body.","The surrounding ground collapsed instantly beneath the pressure as countless cracks spread across the clearing like massive spiderwebs tearing through the earth. Violent winds exploded outward in every direction while the nearby participants felt their expressions change drastically as the pressure radiating from Max suddenly multiplied at an astonishing rate.","Several disciples instinctively staggered backward in horror.","\"What... what is this?!\" one participant shouted while trembling uncontrollably.","\"He was still holding back before?!\" another disciple exclaimed with disbelief written all over his face.","The black saber disciple’s face turned pale instantly as cold fear surged through his heart.","\"No... this is impossible...\" he muttered in shock.","Max slowly raised his head.","At that moment, the pressure radiating from him no longer resembled the aura of a normal cultivator at all.","It felt like a humanoid beast standing before them.","A monster wearing human skin.","Then suddenly—","Max disappeared once more.","Boom!!!","The place where he had been standing exploded apart violently from the sheer force of his movement.","The next instant, he appeared directly before a disciple wielding a long spear.","The young man’s pupils contracted violently as terror exploded within his mind.","\"Wait—!\"","Before he could even finish speaking, Max’s fist had already descended toward him.","There was no martial technique.","No concept.","No law.","Only absolute physical power.","Boom!!!","The disciple’s body exploded instantly upon contact.","There was no blood spraying through the air.","No flesh remaining behind.","The instant Max’s fist struck him, the participant’s entire body shattered directly into countless golden particles that scattered through the air like dust illuminated by sunlight.","He had been eliminated from the Survival Trial instantly.","At the same moment, a system notification appeared before Max’s eyes.","[+350 Killing Points]","Max did not even pause after seeing the notification.","Boom!","Another participant exploded apart into golden particles.","Boom!","A hammer-wielding genius disappeared instantly after Max’s punch shattered his body completely.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","Everywhere Max moved, participants vanished one after another as though they were incapable of resisting him even slightly.","No one could stop him.","No one could even defend against a single attack.","The most horrifying part of all was that Max still had not used any laws, concepts, sword arts, or lightning techniques throughout the massacre.","He was relying purely on the monstrous physical strength granted by the Vein of Strength alone.","And that strength by itself was already enough to completely overwhelm peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses without giving them the slightest opportunity to resist.","Panic instantly spread throughout the clearing.","\"This monster!\"","\"He’s killing people with his bare hands!\"","\"How can someone this strong exist at the Law Awakening Realm?!\"","The woman wielding twin daggers suddenly turned around and desperately attempted to flee as fear completely overwhelmed her courage.","However, before she could even escape more than a few meters—","Boom!!!","Max appeared directly behind her like a phantom.","She barely had enough time to widen her eyes in terror before his fist descended mercilessly.","Her body shattered into countless golden particles instantly.","[+420 Killing Points]","The notifications before Max’s eyes began increasing rapidly one after another.","[+380 Killing Points]","[+410 Killing Points]","[+360 Killing Points]","[+450 Killing Points]","One participant after another was completely eliminated from the trial.","The clearing gradually fell silent.","Only countless golden particles drifted slowly through the air like glowing dust while the shattered ground, destroyed trees, and massive craters stood as silent proof of the massacre that had just taken place.","Moments later—","The final remaining disciple staggered backward while staring at Max with absolute terror written across his face.","The greed and confidence he possessed earlier had long vanished completely.","Only fear remained.","\"You... you monster...\" he muttered while trembling uncontrollably.","Max calmly walked toward him step by step.","Every footstep caused the ground beneath his feet to crack faintly from the overwhelming force within his body.","The disciple’s face turned deathly pale as he desperately attempted to retreat further.","However—","Boom!!!","Max’s fist struck forward once again.","The final participant exploded into countless golden particles instantly.","Silence completely returned to the clearing.","Max slowly lowered his fist while the seven-colored lightning surrounding his body flickered faintly around him.","Then the system notifications continuously appeared before his eyes one after another.","[+350 Killing Points]","[+420 Killing Points]","[+390 Killing Points]","[+410 Killing Points]","...","His Killing Points skyrocketed at an astonishing speed.","Soon afterward, the ranking screen before him updated rapidly.","[Name: Max Morgan]","[Killing Points: 6,820]","[Rank: 3]","Max calmly looked at the screen for several moments before a faint smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"So this is how the Survival Trial works...\" he murmured softly.","Then his gaze slowly shifted deeper toward the endless forest stretching far ahead of him.","The anticipation within his eyes gradually sharpened.","\"If that’s the case...\"","A faint crackle of seven-colored lightning echoed around him once more.","\"Then this trial is perfect for farming Killing Points.\""]},{"number":1648,"title":"Chapter 1648: Arriving before a tower!","paragraphs":["Having personally experienced the true power of the Third Divine Vein, Max could not help but feel deeply satisfied.","As the violent energy of the Vein of Strength gradually settled within his body, he slowly flexed his fingers while feeling the terrifying physical force still coursing through his muscles and bones. Even now, every movement carried an explosive sense of power, as though his body had transformed into a weapon capable of crushing mountains barehanded.","What truly surprised Max was the sheer amplification the Vein of Strength provided.","The increase was far beyond what he had initially expected.","Before opening the Third Divine Vein, Max already possessed frightening physical strength due to his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, his Dragon Scales Transformation, and the terrifying boost granted by his five thousand Draconic Essences.","Yet now—","The Vein of Strength had elevated that raw power to an entirely different level.","\"If I combine the Vein of Strength with all five thousand Draconic Essences and activate Dragon Scales Transformation at the same time...\" Max thought quietly to himself.","A faint glint appeared within his eyes.","\"Then just how terrifying would my physical strength become?\"","Even Max himself found it difficult to estimate the answer.","The thought alone was enough to make his blood stir slightly.","However, he quickly pushed the idea aside.","There was no point thinking too deeply about it now. The Survival Trial had only just begun, and there would be plenty of opportunities later to fully test the limits of his strength.","Soon, Max’s gaze shifted toward the ranking screen floating before him once again.","[Name: Max Morgan]","[Killing Points: 6,820]","[Rank: 3]","Max raised an eyebrow slightly.","Even after eliminating so many participants and obtaining such a massive number of killing points in one go, he was still only ranked third.","This immediately sparked his curiosity.","\"Who exactly is above me?\" he muttered softly.","Almost as though the system had heard his thoughts, another translucent screen suddenly appeared before his eyes.","It displayed the current rankings in detail.","[Rank 1: Jonathan Myres — 15,672 KP]","[Rank 2: Ray Willer — 10,357 KP]","[Rank 3: Max Morgan — 6,820 KP]","[Rank 4: Julie — 5,632 KP]","...","\"Hm,\" Max murmured quietly as he looked at the list. \"So it’s Jonathan and Ray.\"","The results themselves were not particularly surprising.","Jonathan Myres was the strongest true disciple of the Violet Star Palace and one of the most powerful participants in the entire Smelting Trial. As for Ray Willer, Max had already expected him to climb the rankings quickly considering both his strength and personality.","However, Ray’s name reminded Max of something else entirely.","\"That reminds me...\" Max thought calmly. \"Ray specifically said he intended to hunt me down.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"But how exactly is he planning to kill me?\"","Within the Soul Sealing Painting, death was not real death. The moment a participant was defeated, their soul would simply be expelled from the painting and returned safely to their physical body outside.","In other words, being killed here only meant elimination from the trial.","Nothing more.","\"So where does his confidence come from?\" Max wondered briefly.","Ray’s earlier words clearly carried genuine killing intent.","It did not sound like mere provocation.","For a moment, Max considered the possibility that Ray possessed some unknown method capable of affecting souls directly within the Soul Sealing Painting. However, after thinking about it for a while, he ultimately stopped dwelling on the matter.","No matter what schemes Ray possessed, Max had absolute confidence in his own strength.","If Ray truly came looking for him—","Then Max would simply crush him directly.","With that thought, Max calmly continued moving deeper into the forest.","Seven colored lightning flickered faintly around his body as his figure traveled rapidly through the massive world inside the Soul Sealing Painting. Along the way, he occasionally encountered scattered monsters or small groups of participants, but none of them were worth slowing down for.","Some participants fled the moment they sensed his aura.","Others tried attacking him greedily after noticing his ranking.","Every single one of them ended the same way.","Eliminated instantly.","As time passed, Max gradually moved farther and farther from the region where he initially entered the trial.","Then suddenly—","His eyes narrowed slightly.","In the far distance, beyond the endless sea of ancient trees, he spotted something enormous rising into the sky.","It was a tower.","A massive black tower stood towering over the forest like an ancient giant. Its height was so absurd that even from an enormous distance away, it remained clearly visible above the treetops.","The tower radiated a strange oppressive aura that immediately caught Max’s attention.","\"Hm?\"","Curiosity appeared in Max’s eyes almost instantly.","\"What is that?\"","Without hesitation, he changed direction and began moving toward the tower.","The closer he got, the clearer the structure became.","The tower looked ancient and weathered, as though it had existed for countless years. Dark stone covered its entire body while strange glowing symbols occasionally flickered across its surface.","However, what truly surprised Max was not the tower itself.","It was the chaos surrounding it.","Even before fully arriving, Max could already hear the sounds of explosions, weapon clashes, and furious shouting echoing throughout the area.","Boom!","A violent shockwave erupted near the lower levels of the tower while countless figures fought fiercely around it.","When Max finally arrived close enough to properly see the scene, even he became slightly surprised.","Hundreds of participants had gathered around the tower.","The surrounding area had turned into complete chaos.","Disciples from various forces were fighting everywhere while blood stained the stone ground surrounding the tower. Techniques continuously exploded through the air while screams and angry roars echoed endlessly.","Some participants fought desperately against one another while others climbed rapidly upward along the outer structure of the tower itself.","Only then did Max notice something unusual.","The tower was filled with caves.","Countless cave openings existed across the outer walls of the massive structure, stretching from the lower sections all the way toward the heavens. Some caves glowed faintly while others radiated dense spiritual fluctuations.","And the participants...","Were fighting madly for them.","\"Get lost!\"","\"This cave belongs to me!\"","\"You think a trash disciple like you deserves a cultivation cave on the upper levels?!\"","Boom!","A young man was blasted directly off the tower after losing a battle, his body crashing violently into the ground below.","Elsewhere, several participants worked together to force another group away from one of the higher cave entrances.","The higher the cave—","The fiercer the fighting became.","Max quietly observed the chaotic battlefield before him while his eyes slowly narrowed.","Clearly—","Those caves were extremely important."]},{"number":1649,"title":"Chapter 1649: A Tower of Treasures!","paragraphs":["\"What exactly is this tower for?\" Max muttered quietly to himself as his eyes remained fixed on the enormous structure towering above the forest.","He truly had not expected something like this to exist within the Soul Sealing Painting.","At first, Max assumed the Survival Trial would simply be a brutal battlefield where participants hunted monsters, slaughtered one another, and accumulated killing points until only fifty people remained.","However, the appearance of this tower immediately made him realize that he had underestimated the complexity of the final trial once again.","This was not merely a simple survival game.","The Celestial Forge Pavilion had clearly designed this trial with far more depth than he initially imagined.","Boom!","Another explosion echoed nearby as several disciples fought fiercely over one of the lower cave entrances.","Max calmly observed the chaotic scene for a moment before deciding not to waste time guessing. Instead, he descended toward the ground near the outer area of the battlefield where a wounded participant was resting against a broken stone pillar while trying to recover his breath.","The young man appeared exhausted, and blood stained parts of his robe. Clearly, he had just lost a battle for one of the caves.","Max walked toward him calmly.","The participant instinctively raised his head after sensing someone approach.","Then—","His expression froze instantly.","\"Ma... Max Morgan?!\"","Shock spread across his face almost immediately as he stared at Max in disbelief.","Clearly, Max’s reputation had already spread throughout the Survival Trial.","The participant quickly straightened his posture subconsciously despite his injuries.","Max ignored the reaction and calmly asked,","\"What is this tower?\"","The wounded disciple blinked for a moment as though he did not expect Max to ask something so basic.","Then suddenly, he let out a bitter laugh.","\"Hah...\"","He shook his head helplessly.","\"First Jonathan Myres arrived here...\"","\"Then Ray Willer came...\"","\"And now even you are here too.\"","His tone carried clear frustration.","\"It seems all the monsters gathered in this trial are slowly gathering at this tower.\"","Max simply looked at him calmly without responding.","Seeing that Max genuinely wanted an answer, the participant quickly explained.","\"This tower appeared not long after the trial began,\" he said while glancing upward toward the massive structure. \"At first, nobody understood what it was either.\"","His expression gradually became more serious.","\"But eventually, people discovered something.\"","He pointed toward the countless caves spread across the surface of the tower.","\"The caves inside the tower contain treasures.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Treasures?\"","The participant nodded immediately.","\"Yes. Different kinds of treasures.\"","\"Cultivation resources, artifacts, inheritances, techniques, rare ores, and all kinds of valuable materials.\"","As he spoke, even his own eyes revealed traces of greed and unwillingness.","\"The important thing is...\" he continued slowly, \"those treasures are not illusions.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened faintly.","The participant inhaled deeply before continuing.","\"Once someone touches a treasure within a cave, the Soul Sealing Painting records it automatically.\"","He paused briefly before adding,","\"And after the trial ends, the Celestial Forge Pavilion will reward that participant with the actual treasure in reality.\"","The moment those words fell, even Max became slightly surprised.","So the treasures inside this world were essentially rewards reserved for the participants.","No wonder the fighting around the tower had become so intense.","A place like this would naturally attract everyone.","The wounded disciple looked toward the tower once more before speaking again.","\"However, not all caves are equal.\"","Max followed his gaze upward.","\"The lower caves usually contain ordinary rewards,\" the participant explained. \"But the higher you climb...\"","His expression gradually became more solemn.","\"The more valuable and powerful the treasures become.\"","Max’s eyes slowly traveled upward along the massive tower.","The higher sections were almost hidden among the clouds themselves, radiating a faint ancient pressure even from a distance.","Meanwhile, the battles near those upper caves were clearly far more intense than the fighting below.","Powerful fluctuations continuously erupted from those areas as geniuses fought desperately to secure positions there.","\"The upper caves...\" the wounded participant said quietly, \"are where the true treasures are located.\"","He then looked back at Max with a complicated expression.","\"With your strength, you’ll probably try climbing higher.\"","A bitter smile appeared on his face.","\"People like us can only fight over the lower caves.\"","Max remained silent for a moment while observing the towering structure before him.","Now everything made sense.","The Survival Trial was not merely about slaughter and killing points.","The tower itself acted as another battlefield.","A place where opportunities, treasures, and competition all converged together.","And judging from the current situation—","The higher one climbed...","The more dangerous things would become.","After listening to the explanation, Max finally understood why the area around the tower had become such a battlefield.","Treasure caves.","Real rewards.","And the higher one climbed, the greater the rewards waiting above.","The Celestial Forge Pavilion truly had gone all out for this Survival Trial.","Max slowly shifted his gaze upward once more toward the enormous tower piercing into the sky. Countless caves covered its outer surface while violent battles erupted across every level. Some participants fought desperately to defend caves they had already claimed, while others attempted to climb higher in search of better treasures.","The scene resembled a battlefield of greed and ambition.","Max then looked back toward the wounded participant.","\"Thanks for the explanation,\" he said calmly.","The young man hurriedly nodded.","\"No problem...\"","Although he tried to remain composed, traces of nervousness still lingered on his face while standing before someone like Max.","After all, the stories surrounding Max within the trial had already begun spreading rapidly.","Max did not say anything further.","The next moment—","Crack!","Seven colored lightning suddenly erupted around his body.","Violent arcs of crimson, gold, silver, blue, violet, black, and green lightning wrapped around him as his aura surged sharply.","Boom!","The ground beneath his feet shattered instantly.","Max’s figure transformed into a streak of seven colored light as he shot directly toward the massive tower at astonishing speed.","The wounded participant stared blankly at the scene.","\"So fast...\" he muttered unconsciously.","Meanwhile, Max rapidly closed the distance toward the upper sections of the tower.","Since the higher caves contained better rewards, there was naturally no reason for him to waste time competing for the lower ones.","The violent winds screamed around him while the seven colored lightning pushed his speed to terrifying levels.","However—"]},{"number":1650,"title":"Chapter 1650: Climbing the Tower!","paragraphs":["The moment Max neared the tower itself—","His expression suddenly changed slightly.","Boom!!!","An overwhelming pressure descended from above without warning.","The air around the tower instantly became unimaginably heavy.","Max felt as though an invisible mountain had suddenly crashed down onto his body.","The seven colored lightning surrounding him flickered violently as his forward momentum came to an abrupt halt.","\"What?\"","Max’s eyes narrowed instantly.","The pressure around the tower was terrifying.","It was not ordinary suppression.","The closer he approached the tower, the heavier the invisible force became, almost as though the entire structure itself rejected flight.","Boom!","Max attempted to push forward forcefully using his physical strength and lightning movement technique.","However, the pressure only intensified further.","The surrounding space distorted heavily while the force pressing down upon him multiplied explosively.","Even someone with Max’s monstrous body felt his movements slowing drastically.","Then suddenly—","Bang!","Max’s body was violently slammed against the outer wall of the tower.","Stone cracked beneath the impact as the enormous pressure forced him downward.","The seven colored lightning around him exploded chaotically while his body slid several meters across the dark stone surface before finally stopping.","Below, several participants witnessed the scene and immediately reacted.","\"Hah! Another one got slammed down!\"","\"I told you flying is impossible near the tower!\"","Even some participants fighting nearby briefly looked upward in shock after recognizing Max.","\"That’s Max Morgan!\"","\"He got forced down too?\"","Max ignored the voices around him while slowly stabilizing himself against the wall of the tower.","Then his eyes gradually sharpened with realization.","\"So that’s how it works...\"","He could now clearly feel the strange force enveloping the entire tower.","The closer one moved toward it, the stronger the suppression became.","It was specifically designed to prevent flight.","No matter how powerful a participant’s movement technique or flying ability was, they would eventually be forced down onto the tower itself.","In other words—","Everyone had to climb physically.","No shortcuts existed here.","Max slowly looked upward toward the countless caves spread across the tower.","Now he finally understood why all the participants were climbing manually instead of simply flying toward the upper caves.","The force surrounding the tower made aerial movement nearly impossible.","To claim the treasures hidden within the caves, one had to ascend step by step while enduring the pressure of the tower itself and fighting against countless other participants along the way.","The higher one climbed—","The stronger the pressure would likely become.","A faint smile slowly appeared on Max’s face.","\"This tower...\" he murmured quietly.","\"It really was designed to force everyone into competition.\"","At that moment, another violent battle erupted not far above him as several participants fought fiercely for control over a middle level cave.","Shockwaves spread across the tower while disciples continuously climbed upward like ants struggling to ascend a mountain.","Max looked upward calmly.","Then—","Without hesitation—","He placed his hand against the tower wall and began climbing upward himself.","Max climbed steadily along the surface of the enormous tower while seven colored lightning flickered faintly around his body.","The pressure surrounding the tower truly was extraordinary.","The higher he climbed, the heavier the invisible force pressing down upon him became. It felt as though the entire tower was trying to drag every participant back downward, forcing them to rely solely on their own strength to ascend.","Along the way, Max passed countless caves scattered throughout the lower regions of the tower.","Some caves had already been occupied by participants who sat within them while absorbing treasures or recovering their strength. Other caves had become battlefields where disciples fought desperately to drive one another away.","The tower was in complete chaos.","Explosions echoed continuously while spiritual energy fluctuations erupted from every direction. Participants occasionally lost battles and fell screaming from higher layers of the tower before crashing far below.","However, Max did not stop moving.","The treasures in the lower regions failed to interest him.","He continued climbing upward calmly while enduring the increasingly terrifying pressure surrounding the tower.","Eventually—","He reached the Fifth Layer.","The moment Max pulled himself onto the platform connected to the fifth layer, his eyes narrowed slightly as he observed the scene before him.","Unlike the lower levels, the number of participants here had decreased drastically.","The pressure in this region was already intense enough that weaker disciples could not even remain standing comfortably for long periods of time. Every movement required far more effort than before, and even circulating spiritual energy felt noticeably slower.","Clearly, reaching this level was already difficult for ordinary participants.","In front of Max stood a massive cave entrance embedded directly into the black stone wall of the tower. Ancient runes faintly glowed around the cave while waves of dense spiritual fluctuations seeped outward from within.","Even without entering, it was obvious that the treasure inside this cave was far superior to anything located in the lower layers.","However, the cave was currently occupied.","Or rather—","Contested.","Several participants were fiercely battling on the wide stone platform located directly outside the cave entrance.","Boom!","A violent shockwave erupted as two disciples clashed head on, causing cracks to spread across the platform beneath them. Nearby, another participant attempted to sneak toward the cave entrance itself only to be forced back by sword energy from another group.","The fighting was intense.","No one was willing to back down.","After all, everyone understood how valuable the treasures within the fifth layer caves likely were.","At that exact moment—","Max stepped fully onto the platform.","Crack.","The faint sound of his footsteps echoed lightly across the battlefield.","It was not loud.","Yet strangely—","Almost everyone present instinctively noticed him immediately.","The chaotic battle slowed slightly as one participant after another turned toward the newly arrived figure.","Then their expressions changed.","\"That’s...\"","\"Max Morgan?!\"","\"The number one genius from the previous trials?\"","Shock spread across the platform almost instantly.","Even the disciples currently fighting stopped momentarily as their attention shifted completely toward Max.","The seven colored lightning flickering faintly around his body made him extremely recognizable, especially after the earlier rumors that had already spread throughout the Survival Trial.","A spear wielding disciple’s expression became serious immediately.","\"What is he doing here already?\"","Another participant frowned deeply.","\"To reach the fifth layer this quickly...\"","\"He really is monstrous.\"","A young man standing closest to the cave entrance narrowed his eyes sharply while gripping his sword tighter.","The atmosphere on the platform immediately became tense.","Unlike the lower participants earlier who underestimated Max because of his cultivation, the geniuses capable of reaching the fifth layer were far more cautious. They clearly understood that someone capable of ranking among the top participants in two consecutive trials could never be simple.","Moreover they had also seen Max ranked 3rd in this trial too and because of that they were even more cautious.","Even if Max’s cultivation appeared lower—","No one here dared to truly underestimate him carelessly.","Max himself calmly looked around the platform while ignoring the various gazes directed toward him.","His eyes briefly landed on the cave entrance before slowly scanning the surrounding participants.","There were around ten people here.","And every single one of them was strong.","Far stronger than the participants he previously eliminated below.","At that moment, one of the disciples suddenly spoke while staring directly at Max.","\"You came for this cave too?\"","The platform instantly fell silent.","Every gaze remained fixed on Max, waiting for his answer."]},{"number":1651,"title":"Chapter 1651: Max’s Terror!","paragraphs":["\"I will give all of you one chance,\" Max said calmly as his gaze slowly swept across the six participants standing before the cave entrance, his expression remaining completely composed despite the tension in the atmosphere. \"Leave this platform peacefully.\"","His tone was neither arrogant nor overbearing.","He did not shout those words loudly, nor did he release any killing intent while speaking.","Yet the calmness within his voice carried an invisible pressure that gradually caused the expressions of the six disciples to change subtly as the weight behind his words settled heavily upon them.","\"Otherwise...\" Max continued slowly while maintaining eye contact with them, \"I will have no choice but to eliminate all of you.\"","The moment those words fell, silence instantly descended across the platform.","The six participants instinctively tightened their grips around their weapons while staring at Max with increasingly wary expressions. The confidence they carried earlier had clearly weakened, yet none of them spoke immediately as the atmosphere around the cave suddenly became incomparably heavy.","If those exact same words had come from someone else, they would have laughed mockingly without hesitation and attacked immediately.","However, the person currently standing before them was Max Morgan.","The same Max Morgan who had ranked first in the previous two trials.","The same Max Morgan whose name currently stood at Rank 3 within the Survival Trial rankings.","And inside this Survival Trial, rankings represented far more than simple fame or reputation.","They represented strength.","Real strength earned through countless eliminations and battles.","One of the participants subconsciously swallowed as his gaze flickered toward the floating ranking screen visible nearby.","[Rank 3: Max Morgan — 6,820 KP]","That number alone was enough to place enormous pressure upon every person standing there.","To accumulate such terrifying killing points in such a short amount of time, Max must have already eliminated a shocking number of participants within the tower.","And none of them believed those victories had been achieved through mere luck.","The six disciples quietly exchanged uneasy glances with one another.","On one hand, none of them wanted to abandon the cave before them.","The treasure hidden within a fifth-layer cave was undoubtedly extraordinary. Just the energy fluctuations leaking faintly from the cave entrance alone were enough to cause greed to burn within their hearts uncontrollably. The dense energy radiating from within clearly indicated that whatever treasure existed inside possessed immense value.","If they successfully obtained the treasure hidden there, their strength and future could improve tremendously.","However—","On the other hand—","None of them truly wanted to fight Max.","Not after hearing the increasingly terrifying rumors spreading throughout the Survival Trial.","Not after seeing his current ranking.","And certainly not after personally sensing the oppressive pressure radiating faintly from his body at this very moment.","One of the spear-wielding disciples frowned deeply as internal conflict appeared within his eyes.","\"We’re six against one...\" he muttered quietly, almost as though he was trying to convince himself more than anyone else.","\"Yes...\" another participant replied slowly while gripping his weapon tighter, but the confidence within his voice was noticeably lacking. \"But this is still Max Morgan.\"","A heavy silence followed once more.","The hesitation on their faces became increasingly obvious as none of them seemed willing to make the first move.","Some participants unwillingly glanced toward the cave entrance while others continued staring at Max cautiously, their expressions revealing the fierce internal struggle occurring within their minds.","The treasure was extremely tempting.","But if they lost here—","Then everything would become meaningless.","Not only would they fail to obtain the treasure within the cave, but they would also be completely eliminated from the Survival Trial itself.","At that moment, one of the older-looking participants suddenly let out a long sigh that broke the silence.","The others immediately turned toward him.","He slowly lowered the weapon in his hand before shaking his head helplessly.","\"This isn’t worth it,\" he said calmly.","His gaze shifted briefly toward the cave behind him before returning toward Max once more.","\"A fifth-layer treasure is definitely valuable,\" he admitted honestly, \"but it’s not valuable enough for me to risk elimination against someone like you.\"","A bitter laugh escaped his mouth afterward.","\"If I get eliminated here, then I leave with absolutely nothing.\"","The participant slowly stepped backward while loosening his grip on his weapon.","\"It’s better to let you have this cave than lose everything trying to fight over it.\"","After speaking those words, he directly turned around and left the platform without any hesitation.","The remaining participants fell silent once again.","However, his departure had clearly affected them heavily.","The hesitation within their expressions deepened further.","Soon afterward, another disciple sighed heavily.","\"He’s right,\" she admitted unwillingly while lowering her guard slightly. \"There are still other caves inside this tower.\"","Her expression became complicated as she looked toward Max.","\"But there’s only one life in this trial.\"","After saying those words, she also stepped away from the platform and began retreating.","Seeing two people leave consecutively instantly weakened the resolve of the remaining participants completely.","One of the disciples clicked his tongue in frustration before lowering the sword in his hand unwillingly.","\"Tch. Fine.\"","\"I didn’t climb this far just to get eliminated fighting over a single cave.\"","Another participant nodded slowly in agreement.","\"Fighting you now would simply be too risky.\"","One after another, the remaining participants gradually backed away from the cave platform while maintaining cautious gazes toward Max.","None of them looked happy about the situation.","The unwillingness within their expressions was extremely obvious.","Yet despite their frustration, none of them dared challenge Max directly.","After all, the man standing before them currently ranked third within the entire Survival Trial.","And nobody believed such a ranking could possibly be achieved without possessing terrifying strength.","Soon, all six participants had completely left the platform.","The previously tense and chaotic atmosphere instantly became silent.","Only Max remained standing calmly before the cave entrance while the heavy pressure of the tower continued descending from above like an invisible mountain.","The participants who retreated glanced back at him one final time before finally disappearing into the distance in search of other caves deeper within the tower.","Meanwhile, Max calmly watched them leave without making any move to stop them.","Then slowly—","His gaze shifted toward the cave behind him.","A faint smile gradually appeared on his face.","\"Good choice,\" he murmured quietly."]},{"number":1652,"title":"Chapter 1652: Good Treasure!","paragraphs":["With the six participants having completely retreated from the platform, the atmosphere surrounding the cave gradually returned to silence once more.","The violent clashes and chaotic battles occurring across the other sections of the tower could still be heard faintly in the distance as muffled explosions and occasional shockwaves echoed throughout the enormous structure, yet the platform Max now stood upon had already become completely calm.","The tension from earlier had disappeared entirely, leaving only shattered stone, scattered spiritual fluctuations, and the oppressive pressure of the ancient tower descending endlessly from above.","Max did not waste any time lingering outside.","After briefly glancing toward the direction the six participants had departed, he calmly turned around and walked toward the cave entrance behind him with steady steps.","The moment he crossed into the cave, a faint wave of spiritual energy immediately brushed across his body.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The interior of the cave was not particularly large, yet the environment within clearly differed greatly from the outside world. Dark stone walls surrounded the entire interior while ancient symbols and mysterious runic markings glowed faintly across the surfaces, illuminating the cave with a dim silver radiance that gave the place an ancient and mysterious atmosphere.","The pressure within the cave also felt noticeably denser than outside.","Even the energy floating through the air seemed purer and more concentrated, causing the surroundings to feel far more oppressive despite the cave’s relatively small size.","At the very center of the cave—","There was a chest.","Max’s gaze immediately focused upon it as he slowly walked closer.","The chest itself appeared ancient, forged from some kind of black metallic material covered entirely in strange runic carvings that faintly pulsed with spiritual light. Dense spiritual energy continuously leaked from within it, making it immediately obvious that whatever treasure was hidden inside was definitely no ordinary item.","\"So this is how the rewards are stored...\" Max muttered quietly while observing the chest carefully.","Without wasting any time, he directly reached forward and opened it.","The moment the lid lifted—","A burst of dazzling golden light erupted outward instantly, illuminating the entire cave.","At the same time, an astonishing wave of dense vitality energy flooded outward like a tidal wave, causing even Max’s expression to shift slightly in surprise.","Inside the chest rested a dark crimson crystal fruit roughly the size of a fist.","Golden veins spread throughout its surface like flowing rivers of molten gold while powerful fluctuations of blood energy continuously radiated from within it in rhythmic pulses. The fruit almost appeared alive, and merely staring at it caused the blood flowing through Max’s body to stir faintly.","\"What strong body cultivation energy...\" Max said softly while observing the fruit closely.","At that exact moment, a translucent notification suddenly appeared before his eyes.","[Discovered Treasure: Heavenly Titan Blood Fruit]","[Treasure Grade: Low Divine]","[Description: A rare body cultivation treasure capable of strengthening flesh, bones, and blood essence. Long-term consumption can significantly improve physical strength and bodily endurance.]","[The treasure has been recorded and will be awarded to Max Morgan after the trial ends.]","Max’s eyes immediately brightened after reading the notification.","A body cultivation treasure.","And clearly not an ordinary one either.","The Heavenly Titan Blood Fruit possessed astonishingly powerful effects specifically suited toward strengthening the physical body. Even for someone like Max, whose body had already reached terrifying levels due to the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, Dragon Scales Transformation, and the Vein of Strength, this treasure would still provide considerable benefits.","The mere fact that such a valuable treasure existed within only a fifth-layer cave immediately made Max realize something important.","\"If treasures of this level already exist on the fifth layer...\"","His gaze instinctively lifted upward as though he could see directly through the cave ceiling toward the higher sections of the tower.","\"Then what kind of treasures are hidden above?\"","A faint excitement gradually surfaced within his eyes.","The higher layers of the tower likely contained treasures far beyond this.","Perhaps High Divine Tier resources.","Perhaps ancient inheritances left behind by terrifying experts.","Or perhaps treasures so valuable that even top geniuses within the Divine Realm would fight desperately over them.","The more Max thought about it, the more interested he became.","Then suddenly—","Another thought surfaced within his mind.","His eyes narrowed faintly as the idea formed completely.","\"If I can sweep through enough of the higher caves...\" Max muttered slowly to himself.","A faint crackle of seven-colored lightning unconsciously flickered around his body.","\"Then I might finally gather enough resources...\"","The light within his eyes sharpened immediately afterward.","\"To force open the Fourth Divine Vein.\"","The Fourth Vein among the Seven Divine Veins.","Vein of Speed.","Even after successfully opening the Third Divine Vein, the Vein of Strength, Max had never forgotten the existence of the remaining Divine Veins hidden within his body.","The Vein of Strength alone had already amplified his physical power to such a monstrous extent that he could casually crush peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses with nothing but his bare fists.","If the Fourth Vein truly amplified speed with the same terrifying intensity—","Then the increase to his combat strength would become almost unimaginable.","Especially when combined with his seven-colored lightning.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face as anticipation gradually rose within his heart.","\"It seems this tower is far more valuable than I originally expected,\" he murmured quietly.","Then he slowly turned around and walked back toward the cave entrance.","As he stepped outside once more, his gaze instinctively lifted toward the towering upper layers stretching endlessly above him.","At that moment, the desire to climb even higher within the tower became stronger than ever before within Max’s heart.","Max did not waste any more time remaining inside the cave after obtaining the Heavenly Titan Blood Fruit.","After taking one final glance around the dimly illuminated interior, he calmly stepped back outside onto the platform before immediately lifting his gaze toward the towering upper sections of the enormous ancient tower stretching endlessly into the sky above him."]},{"number":1653,"title":"Chapter 1653: Terror spreading across the 6th and 7th layer!!","paragraphs":["The higher layers radiated an increasingly ancient and oppressive pressure that seemed to grow heavier the farther upward one looked. Violent battles continued erupting throughout different regions of the tower while countless participants desperately climbed higher in search of treasures, inheritances, and opportunities capable of changing their futures completely.","However, now that Max finally understood the true value hidden within these caves, his interest toward the tower had increased tremendously.","If a treasure of that level could already appear within a mere fifth-layer cave, then the rewards hidden within the higher layers would undoubtedly become even more astonishing.","Crack!","Seven-colored lightning erupted violently around Max once more.","The next instant, his figure shot upward along the towering wall of the ancient structure at astonishing speed like a streak of divine lightning piercing through the sky.","As Max climbed higher, the pressure surrounding the tower became increasingly intense.","The suppression force descending from above continuously strengthened with each passing layer, enough to make ordinary participants struggle even to move properly. Yet throughout the climb, Max’s expression remained completely calm.","The Vein of Strength continuously surged within his body, allowing him to resist the terrifying pressure far more easily than ordinary cultivators ever could.","Soon—","Max arrived at the Sixth Layer.","Compared to the lower regions, the atmosphere here had changed drastically.","The number of participants had noticeably decreased while the pressure covering the tower had become significantly heavier than before. Even the battles erupting across the sixth layer carried far greater intensity because the geniuses capable of reaching this level were clearly much stronger than ordinary disciples.","However, Max did not stop moving for even a moment.","The instant he arrived upon the sixth layer, he immediately headed toward the nearest cave platform.","Several participants were already fighting fiercely outside the cave when Max arrived.","Boom!","Sharp sword energy exploded violently through the air while two disciples exchanged attacks near the cave entrance with fierce expressions.","However, the moment Max stepped onto the platform—","The battle abruptly slowed.","One participant after another instinctively turned toward him.","Then their expressions changed instantly.","\"Max Morgan...\"","\"He reached the sixth layer already?!\"","The pressure surrounding the platform immediately became tense.","Max calmly looked toward the gathered disciples before speaking in an indifferent tone.","\"Leave the platform.\"","His voice remained calm and steady, yet carried unquestionable certainty.","\"I am taking this cave.\"","The participants exchanged uneasy glances with one another.","Some of them clearly felt unwillingness rising within their hearts, yet after sensing the terrifying aura radiating faintly from Max’s body while recalling the increasingly horrifying rumors surrounding him, hesitation rapidly appeared upon their faces.","Several moments later, one disciple finally let out a bitter sigh.","\"This cave isn’t worth risking elimination over,\" he admitted unwillingly.","Soon afterward, several others slowly nodded as well before retreating from the platform without resistance.","Seeing them leave, Max simply entered the cave calmly, opened the chest hidden within, recorded the treasure with his name, and immediately departed once again without wasting time.","Then he headed toward the next cave.","And then the next.","And then another.","As Max continued climbing through the sixth layer, the same scenes began repeating themselves again and again.","Whenever he arrived upon a cave platform, the ongoing battles would immediately slow down as participants recognized him.","Sometimes—","The disciples would choose to retreat instantly.","No one wished to gamble their survival against someone currently ranked among the top participants within the entire Survival Trial.","However, not everyone was willing to surrender so easily.","At another cave platform, a group of disciples refused to retreat even after Max arrived.","A tall young man wielding twin sabers sneered coldly while stepping forward.","\"Max Morgan or not, this cave already belongs to us.\"","Another participant standing nearby nodded grimly in agreement.","\"We climbed this far with our own strength,\" he said coldly. \"Why should we hand it over simply because you appeared?\"","Max calmly looked at them for several moments before finally speaking.","\"So you’ve chosen to stay.\"","The next instant—","Boom!!!","The Vein of Strength erupted completely.","Terrifying physical power exploded outward from Max’s body while the entire platform cracked violently beneath his feet.","The expressions of the surrounding participants changed drastically.","Before they could even react—","Max moved.","Boom!","One punch shattered directly through a disciple’s defensive technique before destroying his body into countless drifting golden particles instantly.","[+520 Killing Points]","Boom!","Another participant exploded apart before he could even properly raise his weapon.","Panic immediately spread across the platform.","\"He’s too strong!\"","\"Run!\"","However, it was already too late.","Max swept across the platform like a storm of destruction.","Every punch carried overwhelming force capable of instantly erasing peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses completely.","Within mere moments, the entire platform had already fallen silent once more.","Only drifting golden particles remained floating through the air.","Afterward, Max calmly entered the cave, claimed the treasure hidden inside, and immediately continued upward again.","And just like that—","The sixth layer gradually began falling under Max’s control.","One cave after another was looted by him.","One platform after another became empty the moment he arrived.","The rumors spreading throughout the tower also became increasingly intense.","\"Max Morgan is sweeping through the sixth layer!\"","\"He already claimed more than ten caves!\"","\"Anyone who resists gets eliminated instantly!\"","Many participants began retreating immediately the moment they sensed Max approaching nearby.","Others still attempted to challenge him greedily, hoping to seize his killing points and treasures for themselves.","None of them succeeded.","By the time Max completely crossed through the sixth layer, his Killing Points had already skyrocketed once more.","Yet even then—","He still did not stop.","Crack!","Seven-colored lightning exploded around his body again as he continued climbing even higher.","Soon—","He arrived at the Seventh Layer.","The pressure here became even more terrifying than before.","The tower’s suppression force felt several times heavier than the lower layers, enough to make ordinary participants struggle simply to remain standing. The number of disciples present here had decreased drastically compared to the sixth layer, yet the strength of those who remained had increased sharply.","The battles occurring here were incomparably more brutal.","Participants capable of reaching the seventh layer were no longer ordinary geniuses.","Yet even here—","Max continued sweeping through the caves relentlessly.","Whenever he arrived upon a platform, he would calmly ask the participants present to leave.","Sometimes they obeyed immediately after sensing the terrifying pressure radiating from him.","Sometimes they stubbornly chose battle instead.","And every single time someone chose to fight—","They were eliminated completely.","Gradually, the entire seventh layer descended into chaos because of Max’s existence.","Warnings rapidly spread throughout the tower among the remaining participants.","\"If you see seven-colored lightning approaching, leave immediately!\"","\"Don’t fight Max Morgan!\"","\"He’s a monster!\"","However, Max himself remained completely calm throughout everything.","He simply continued moving from platform to platform, cave to cave, collecting treasures while steadily climbing higher and higher within the ancient tower.","By the end—","Almost every cave across both the sixth and seventh layers had already fallen into Max’s hands.","And just when he was nearing the 8th layer, Max sensed terrifying energies from high above. He immediately sensed Jonathan, Julie, Ray and many of the top ten were fighting in the same platform through his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","\"Hehe this is interesting.\" Max muttered as his figure flashed towards that very platform in the 8th layer."]},{"number":1654,"title":"Chapter 1654: Ray’s Announcement!","paragraphs":["Seven-colored lightning crackled wildly around Max’s body as he moved through the air at astonishing speed, leaving behind flashes of dazzling light while the already terrifying pressure surrounding the tower continued increasing rapidly with every layer he crossed.","Soon—","Max finally arrived near the Eighth Layer.","The atmosphere here was completely different from anything below.","The suppression force radiating from the ancient tower had reached an absurd level, so overwhelming that even the stone beneath one’s feet felt incomparably heavy. The pressure covering the surroundings resembled an invisible mountain descending endlessly from above, causing ordinary participants to struggle even to breathe properly.","Compared to the lower floors, the number of participants here had drastically decreased.","However, the remaining geniuses were all terrifying individuals capable of standing above countless others.","Every person who managed to climb this far possessed extraordinary strength.","And directly ahead—","A massive platform stretched outward from the wall of the ancient tower.","Violent battles were erupting throughout the entire area.","Boom!","Sharp sword energy and powerful spiritual techniques collided continuously as terrifying shockwaves exploded outward across the battlefield. Several peak geniuses fought fiercely against one another while desperately attempting to force everyone else away from the enormous cave located behind them.","The cave itself radiated astonishing spiritual fluctuations.","Dense waves of energy continuously leaked outward from within it, causing even the surrounding air to distort faintly.","The moment Max sensed those fluctuations, his eyes narrowed slightly.","Even he could immediately tell that the treasure hidden inside that cave was likely far beyond anything found within the lower layers.","Then—","The moment Max stepped onto the platform—","Everything changed instantly.","Several participants immediately sensed his arrival.","One after another, their expressions shifted drastically.","\"That aura...\"","\"Seven-colored lightning?\"","\"Max Morgan!\"","The previously chaotic battlefield slowed noticeably as countless eyes turned toward the newly arrived figure standing calmly near the edge of the platform.","Jonathan Myres was the first to react.","At that moment, he had just forced back another genius using a fierce spear strike before suddenly noticing Max’s arrival from the side of the battlefield.","Then—","A grin immediately appeared across Jonathan’s face.","\"So even you made it here already?\" he said while laughing lightly.","Instead of annoyance or hostility, excitement could clearly be seen within his eyes. He wanted to fight Max and there was no better playground than this where they could go all out.","Not far away, Julie also noticed Max’s arrival.","Her beautiful eyes widened slightly before a faint smile slowly appeared on her face as well.","\"He is here,\" she said calmly while brushing away a strand of hair moved by the violent winds constantly sweeping across the battlefield.","Her gaze briefly shifted toward the cave behind them before returning toward Max once more.","Unlike the other participants present, neither Jonathan nor Julie appeared bothered by Max’s arrival in the slightest.","Instead—","They seemed genuinely excited.","After all, people capable of reaching the eighth layer already possessed absolute confidence in their own strength. To them, stronger opponents did not represent fear.","They represented challenge.","And challenge made the competition far more thrilling.","However—","Ray Willer’s reaction was completely different.","The instant his eyes landed upon Max—","A terrifying killing intent immediately flashed through them.","The atmosphere surrounding his body visibly grew colder.","Unlike Jonathan and Julie, Ray did not smile at all.","He simply stared silently toward Max while dark emotions churned deep within his gaze.","\"So you finally came...\" Ray muttered quietly as his cold gaze locked directly onto Max from across the chaotic battlefield.","The killing intent hidden within his voice was so intense that even several nearby participants instinctively distanced themselves from him the moment they heard those words.","The violent battle that had engulfed the platform only moments earlier gradually began slowing down as more and more people noticed the atmosphere changing rapidly.","Max calmly looked back toward Ray without the slightest trace of fear appearing on his face.","Seven-colored lightning flickered faintly around his body while his expression remained completely relaxed, as though the terrifying hostility directed toward him did not affect him in the slightest.","For a brief moment—","The two simply stared silently at one another across the battlefield.","Yet despite the silence between them, the surrounding participants could clearly feel the invisible pressure violently colliding in the air between the two monsters standing opposite each other.","The atmosphere instantly became incomparably tense.","Jonathan Myres slightly narrowed his eyes while observing the scene with visible interest.","Julie’s expression also gradually turned serious.","Even the other top geniuses present on the platform unconsciously stopped fighting temporarily as their attention shifted completely toward Max and Ray.","After all, everyone standing here already knew that hostility existed between the two. It wasn’t a secret that Ray Willer wanted to teach Max a lesson and in fact almost every of the top ten geniuses here knew this fact.","Ray Willer had announced this openly when Max ranked 1st in the first trial.","And now—","That hostility had finally surfaced openly before everyone.","Ray slowly raised his head while a faint smile gradually appeared across his face.","However, unlike Jonathan’s carefree grin, Ray’s smile carried coldness and danger that caused nearby participants to instinctively feel uneasy.","His eyes never left Max even for a single second.","Then suddenly—","Ray stepped forward.","Boom!","A violent aura erupted instantly from his body as terrifying sword intent exploded outward across the entire platform.","Several nearby participants immediately frowned after sensing the horrifying sharpness hidden within his aura.","It felt as though invisible blades had suddenly spread through the air itself.","Ray slowly swept his gaze across everyone present before speaking coldly.","\"Everyone...\"","His voice echoed clearly throughout the entire platform despite not being particularly loud.","\"Stay where you are.\"","The nearby participants immediately frowned after hearing those words.","Ray continued calmly,","\"This cave...\"","His gaze shifted back toward Max once more.","\"...I don’t want it but I do want to battle Max.\"","The instant those words fell, the expressions of many participants changed visibly.","Jonathan slightly raised an eyebrow.","Julie narrowed her eyes thoughtfully.","Meanwhile, Ray slowly lifted the sword in his hand before directly pointing it toward Max.","\"So none of you interfere,\" he said coldly. \"This fight is between us.\"","The surrounding atmosphere instantly became even heavier than before.","One participant frowned deeply while looking toward Ray.","\"You want us to stop fighting simply because you said so?\"","Another genius sneered coldly afterward.","\"Who exactly do you think you are to order everyone around?\""]},{"number":1655,"title":"Chapter 1655: Max’s Caution!","paragraphs":["However, before the complaints could continue any further—","Boom!!!","A terrifying wave of sword intent exploded violently from Ray’s body.","The sharp pressure sweeping across the platform caused several participants’ expressions to change instantly.","Ray’s eyes turned incomparably icy cold.","\"Anyone who interferes...\"","His voice became chilling to the extreme.","\"...will die first.\"","Silence immediately descended afterward.","No one doubted the seriousness hidden behind those words.","Ray Willer currently stood at Rank 2 within the Survival Trial.","And unlike ordinary participants from the lower layers, everyone standing upon the eighth layer clearly understood just how terrifying someone capable of reaching such a ranking truly was.","Jonathan suddenly burst into laughter from the side.","\"Hahaha! Interesting!\"","He casually rested his spear across his shoulder while looking back and forth between Max and Ray with obvious excitement.","\"So you finally want to settle things openly?\"","Julie also slowly stepped backward while brushing away the spiritual energy surrounding her body.","\"This platform is already chaotic enough,\" she said calmly. \"Watching the two of you fight might actually be more entertaining.\"","Several other top geniuses exchanged glances afterward.","Although some of them clearly appeared dissatisfied at being forced to stop competing over the cave, none of them truly wished to get caught between Max and Ray at this moment.","The killing intent radiating between the two had already become far too intense.","Soon afterward, one participant after another gradually stopped fighting before retreating toward the outer edges of the platform.","The center of the battlefield slowly became completely empty.","Only Max and Ray remained standing opposite one another.","Violent winds continuously swept across the eighth layer while both of their robes fluttered sharply in the air. Terrifying pressure spread constantly between the two as though the space around them itself had become unstable.","Ray’s sword intent grew sharper and sharper while he continued staring directly at Max.","Meanwhile, Max simply smiled faintly.","\"So impatient?\" Max asked calmly.","Ray’s eyes narrowed dangerously afterward.","\"You should know by now,\" he replied coldly, \"that I’ve been waiting for this moment since the trial began.\"","The killing intent within his voice no longer remained hidden in the slightest.","It erupted openly without restraint.","At that moment—","Everyone standing upon the platform clearly understood something.","This was no ordinary battle over a cave treasure.","This was a clash between two monsters standing at the very peak of the Survival Trial.","Max silently stared toward Ray with narrowed eyes while faint strands of seven-colored lightning flickered continuously around his body like restless dragons coiling through the air.","For some reason, Ray was giving him an unusually dangerous feeling.","It was not simply because of Ray’s strength, nor was it merely because of his terrifying ranking within the Survival Trial. Max had already faced many powerful geniuses before, including opponents whose combat ability far surpassed ordinary cultivators within the same realm. Throughout his journey, he had encountered countless monstrous talents and terrifying enemies.","Yet the feeling Ray gave him was completely different.","There was something hidden beneath the surface.","Something dangerous enough to make even Max instinctively cautious.","The memory of Ray’s earlier words gradually resurfaced within Max’s mind once more.","Hunter and prey.","Ray had openly declared from the very beginning that he intended to kill him inside the Survival Trial.","And the more Max thought about it, the more serious the situation gradually became in his mind.","Inside the Soul Sealing Painting, death was not supposed to be real.","Under normal circumstances, once a participant was defeated, their soul would simply be expelled from the painting before safely returning to their original body outside.","That was the fundamental rule governing the trial.","Yet despite knowing this clearly, Ray still spoke with absolute confidence about taking Max’s life.","\"Does he truly possess some method capable of killing me inside this place?\" Max wondered inwardly.","His expression gradually became more serious afterward.","Max had never underestimated the major powers of the Divine Realm.","Especially not a terrifying existence like the Sword God Palace.","That force stood at the absolute peak of sword cultivation within the entire Divine Realm. Their foundations were unimaginably deep while their methods and inheritances were so ancient and mysterious that ordinary people could never fully comprehend them.","And Ray Willer—","Clearly possessed connections with them.","That fact alone was already enough reason for Max to remain vigilant.","Even if Ray himself was not the true danger, the methods, treasures, and hidden cards connected to the Sword God Palace absolutely could be.","At that moment, Ray noticed that Max still had not attacked immediately.","A cold smile slowly appeared across his face afterward.","\"What?\" Ray asked mockingly. \"Are you backing down already?\"","His voice carried obvious ridicule and disdain.","The nearby participants immediately focused even more intensely upon the confrontation between the two monsters standing at the center of the platform.","Ray slowly lifted the sword in his hand while his gaze remained locked firmly upon Max.","\"You know...\" he said calmly, although the hatred hidden beneath his voice was becoming increasingly obvious with every passing second, \"I have wanted to teach you a lesson for a very long time.\"","Sharp sword intent gradually spread outward from Ray’s body while violent spiritual energy continuously swirled around him like a gathering storm.","\"I hated watching someone like you become famous overnight.\"","His tone became colder and colder with every word he spoke.","\"You appeared out of nowhere, picked up the sword left behind by the Sword Sovereign, and suddenly the entire Divine Realm started talking about you.\"","The grip around Ray’s sword tightened faintly.","\"And meanwhile...\"","A dangerous look slowly surfaced within his eyes.","\"I spent centuries fighting, cultivating, bleeding, and clawing my way upward.\"","His voice gradually rose as the emotions within him became increasingly unstable.","\"I worked harder than countless people.\"","\"I trained endlessly.\"","\"I defeated genius after genius.\"","The sword intent erupting from his body gradually became sharper and more violent.","\"But not once...\"","The killing intent surrounding Ray intensified drastically.","\"Not once did the world ever acknowledge me the same way they acknowledged you.\"","The surrounding atmosphere became increasingly tense as everyone silently listened to his words.","Even Jonathan Myres’ expression gradually turned thoughtful.","Meanwhile, Ray’s gaze toward Max grew colder and colder, almost as though years of resentment and frustration were finally exploding outward openly.","\"To them, you are the rising genius of this generation.\"","\"To them, you are the successor of the Sword Sovereign.\"","A sneer gradually appeared upon his face afterward.","\"But to me...\"","Boom!!!","His sword intent exploded violently across the entire platform.","\"You are nothing more than a lucky thief who happened to take away a sword!\"","Terrifying pressure erupted outward instantly as the stone beneath Ray’s feet shattered apart while sharp sword intent spread through the surroundings like invisible blades slicing across the air itself.","The nearby participants instinctively retreated even farther away after sensing the horrifying sharpness erupting from his body.","\"And today...\" Ray continued coldly while slowly pointing his sword directly toward Max, \"I am going to expose the truth to everyone.\"","His eyes flashed with deadly killing intent.","\"I will show the world exactly how weak you truly are.\""]},{"number":1656,"title":"Chapter 1656: Pseudo Cosmic Path","paragraphs":["\"Come on then,\" Max said with a faint smile as he slowly drew his sword from its sheath, allowing the cold metallic blade to catch the surrounding light while strands of seven-colored lightning began crackling around his body like restless currents of divine destruction.","Violent energy surged silently through the platform, but Max’s expression remained calm as he raised his sword and pointed its tip straight toward Ray without the slightest hesitation.","\"Show me what you’ve got.\"","Ray’s lips curled into a cold sneer after hearing those words, and his gaze became filled with unconcealed contempt.","\"As you wish.\"","The next moment, a long crimson spear appeared in his hand.","The spear was dark red, almost like flowing blood that had been forged into solid metal, while sharp scarlet runes spread across its surface like burning veins. The instant the weapon appeared, an oppressive aura swept outward from it, making the surrounding air grow heavier.","Several nearby participants immediately frowned after sensing the pressure coming from the spear.","Ray slowly circled Max while dragging the spear tip across the stone platform beneath his feet.","A piercing screech echoed through the battlefield as the sharp spearhead tore through the stone floor with frightening ease, leaving long cracks behind while sparks scattered into the air.","A mocking smile appeared on Ray’s face as he continued moving around Max like a predator calmly studying prey that had already fallen into its trap.","\"You do realize something, don’t you?\" Ray said calmly while keeping his eyes fixed on Max. \"Among everyone currently standing on this platform, your cultivation is the weakest.\"","The surrounding participants fell silent as Ray’s voice echoed clearly throughout the battlefield.","\"You performed well during the first and second trials because those trials tested talent, comprehension, and skill,\" Ray continued, slowly lifting the crimson spear in his hand. \"But this is different.\"","A dangerous smile gradually surfaced on his face.","\"This is an actual battlefield.\"","The atmosphere around Ray began to change, and the pressure surrounding his spear grew heavier with every passing breath.","\"And on a battlefield,\" he said coldly, \"your weakness will finally be exposed for everyone here to see.\"","The instant those words fell, a terrifying pressure erupted violently from Ray’s spear.","It was sharpness.","Pure sharpness.","An overwhelming concept of sharpness spread outward from the crimson spear like an invisible storm sweeping across the entire eighth layer. The pressure became so intense that even the surrounding participants instinctively stepped backward in shock.","The stone platform beneath Ray’s feet cracked apart continuously while violent energy fluctuations spread rapidly through the battlefield.","Even the enormous ancient tower itself trembled faintly.","The expressions of many participants changed instantly.","\"What terrifying sharpness!\"","\"This pressure...\"","\"It is only the fifth-level concept of sharpness, so why does it feel this overwhelming?\"","The atmosphere around the platform became heavier as the concept emanating from Ray’s spear intensified rapidly.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly.","He could immediately sense that something about Ray’s concept of sharpness was fundamentally different from ordinary concepts. It felt deeper, more complete, and almost as if it had already begun transforming into something far beyond the level of a mere concept.","At that exact moment, Jonathan Myres’ expression changed drastically.","His pupils contracted as he stared toward Ray in disbelief.","\"This...\"","A deeply shocked look appeared on his face.","\"This is a Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","The moment those words were spoken, the expressions of the surrounding participants changed immediately.","Even Julie’s previously calm face finally lost composure.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path?\" she repeated in visible shock before quickly turning back toward Ray.","Her beautiful eyes widened.","\"No way...\"","The surrounding geniuses instantly erupted into commotion.","\"A Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","\"How is that even possible?\"","Meanwhile, Ray stood there calmly while the terrifying aura surrounding him continued becoming sharper with every passing second.","At that moment, the pressure emanating from his spear no longer resembled the aura of a mere fifth-level concept. It already carried traces of something much higher, something that was slowly approaching the level of a true Cosmic Path.","Jonathan stared at Ray solemnly before speaking in a low voice.","\"A Pseudo Cosmic Path is the stage where someone has already stepped onto the road toward comprehending a true Cosmic Path,\" he explained, his expression extremely serious. \"It means that person has already achieved significant mastery over the foundation of that path, even if they have not fully completed it yet.\"","Julie’s eyes trembled faintly as she listened.","In simple terms, a Pseudo Cosmic Path represented someone who had already walked halfway toward the realm of true Cosmic Path comprehension.","And that was absolutely terrifying.","One had to understand that comprehending a true Cosmic Path was something cultivators normally pursued only after reaching the Divine Lord Realm. Only after arriving at that level would cultivators begin transforming their concepts into complete Cosmic Paths in order to continue advancing further along the cultivation road.","Yet now, Ray Willer had already touched the threshold of that power while still only standing at the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm.","This level of comprehension was absurd.","It completely surpassed the standards of ordinary geniuses from third-rate forces.","\"How did he even accomplish this?\" Julie muttered softly while staring at Ray in deep shock.","Her gaze gradually became more serious.","She understood very clearly that even among first-rate forces, only the absolute top geniuses occasionally managed to touch the threshold of a Pseudo Cosmic Path while still within the Law Awakening Realm. That fact alone was enough to classify them as monsters among monsters.","Yet Ray, a genius originating from a third-rate force, had somehow accomplished it as well.","The more Julie thought about it, the more unbelievable the situation became.","Jonathan slowly narrowed his eyes.","\"I have heard rumors before,\" he said solemnly. \"Ray Willer has connections with the Sword God Palace.\"","Julie immediately turned toward him.","Jonathan continued quietly, \"If I had to guess, then some elder from the Sword God Palace probably guided him personally. Otherwise, there is no possible way a genius from a third-rate force could comprehend a Pseudo Cosmic Path this early.\"","At that moment, the atmosphere throughout the entire eighth layer had completely changed.","The surrounding participants no longer looked at Ray with ordinary caution or wariness.","Now, they looked at him with genuine fear."]},{"number":1657,"title":"Chapter 1657: Crazy Max!","paragraphs":["\"You heard them correctly, didn’t you?\" Ray said as an arrogant smile slowly spread across his face while the crimson spear within his hand radiated increasingly terrifying pressure.","The sharpness surrounding his body continuously tore through the air like countless invisible blades while the oppressive aura emanating from him became heavier with every passing second. Nearby participants instinctively retreated farther away from the battlefield as the pressure sweeping from Ray’s body grew increasingly difficult to endure.","\"This...\" Ray continued proudly while slightly lifting the crimson spear upward, \"is a Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","His eyes gleamed with absolute confidence and superiority as though he already stood far above everyone present.","\"I am already only a few steps away from comprehending a true Cosmic Path.\"","The surrounding participants immediately felt their hearts tremble once again after hearing those words directly from Ray himself.","Even Jonathan Myres and Julie remained completely silent afterward.","After all, the significance behind a Pseudo Cosmic Path was simply too terrifying.","Ray slowly pointed the crimson spear toward Max while sneering coldly.","\"So tell me...\"","His voice carried obvious ridicule.","\"Do you truly believe you stand a chance against someone like me?\"","The pressure radiating from his body intensified once more.","The surrounding space distorted faintly while the concept of sharpness fused together with traces of the incomplete Cosmic Path, causing everyone nearby to feel overwhelming suffocating pressure descending upon them like a mountain.","Then suddenly, Ray laughed.","The reason was simple.","He had noticed the solemn expression appearing upon Max’s face.","Clearly, in Ray’s eyes, Max had finally realized the terrifying gap separating the two of them.","\"How about this?\" Ray said mockingly while casually spinning the crimson spear within his hand. \"Follow me quietly toward some isolated corner of this tower...\"","A dangerous smile gradually surfaced on his face afterward.","\"And I might choose to spare you there.\"","His tone suddenly became colder.","\"Otherwise...\"","The killing intent hidden within his eyes intensified sharply.","\"You’ll be eliminated here in front of everyone.\"","The surrounding participants remained silent while staring toward Max.","Many of them subconsciously believed Ray’s words were not merely empty arrogance.","After all, the pressure of a Pseudo Cosmic Path was genuinely overwhelming.","However, at that exact moment, Max suddenly spoke softly.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path...\"","His eyes remained fixed steadily upon Ray while he appeared to sink briefly into deep thought.","Then slowly, a smile appeared on Max’s face.","\"I truly didn’t expect you to walk this far along the road toward a Cosmic Path.\"","Ray’s sneer deepened slightly after hearing those words.","However, before he could respond, the smile upon Max’s face suddenly widened further.","Then, a trace of genuine excitement gradually surfaced within his eyes.","\"I never thought I would actually get an opportunity like this,\" Max said honestly while tightening his grip around his sword.","The seven-colored lightning surrounding his body crackled far more intensely afterward as violent divine energy fluctuations spread faintly throughout the battlefield.","\"To fight someone who has already reached the Pseudo Cosmic Path stage...\"","His voice now carried unmistakable excitement.","\"So stop wasting time and come fight me already.\"","The moment those words fell, several nearby participants became completely stunned.","Even Jonathan blinked slightly in surprise.","Julie’s beautiful eyes widened faintly while staring toward Max.","None of them had expected such a reaction from him.","Faced against someone who had already stepped halfway into the realm of Cosmic Paths, Max should have felt pressure, caution, or perhaps even fear.","Instead, he looked excited.","Genuinely excited.","And the more terrifying Ray’s comprehension appeared to be, the brighter the excitement within Max’s eyes became.","This was because Max clearly understood the true value hidden behind this battle.","Perhaps he still remained inexperienced regarding many matters within the Divine Realm.","Perhaps there were still countless hidden powers, ancient inheritances, and terrifying secrets that he did not fully understand yet.","But when it came to laws, concepts, and Cosmic Paths, Max’s understanding was absolutely not lacking.","He fully understood just how terrifying someone like Ray truly was.","A Pseudo Cosmic Path was not simply a stronger concept.","It represented someone who had already begun transforming their understanding into an entirely higher existence.","Someone who had already stepped onto the road leading toward the absolute peak of cultivation.","And precisely because Max understood this, he became even more excited.","Deep within him, Max’s own Severing Sword Concept faintly stirred.","Unlike Ray, Max had not yet reached the Pseudo Cosmic Path stage himself.","However, his mastery over the Severing Sword Concept had already advanced to an extremely high level. Although still incomplete, faint traces of the future Cosmic Path hidden within it had already begun forming silently.","Because of this, Max immediately realized the enormous opportunity standing directly before him.","If he exchanged blows against someone like Ray, if he personally experienced the pressure, structure, and transformation process of a Pseudo Cosmic Path during battle, then perhaps he could gain insight into how to push his own Severing Sword Concept even further.","Perhaps this battle itself would become the stepping stone allowing him to approach the Pseudo Cosmic Path stage in the future.","The more Max thought about it, the more excited he became.","Battles against ordinary geniuses no longer interested him much anymore.","But a battle against someone standing halfway toward a true Cosmic Path was completely different.","That was not merely a fight.","That was an opportunity.","A rare and precious opportunity capable of directly benefiting his future cultivation path.","The seven-colored lightning surrounding Max gradually intensified while the fighting spirit within his eyes rose sharply.","Meanwhile, Ray slowly frowned.","For the very first time since meeting Max, Ray genuinely felt that something was wrong with him.","No.","Not wrong.","Insane.","Any normal genius standing before a Pseudo Cosmic Path would feel pressure weighing down upon them like a mountain. They would hesitate after realizing the terrifying gap separating themselves from someone who had already stepped halfway onto the road of Cosmic Paths.","Yet Max was completely different.","Instead of fear, excitement had appeared within his eyes.","The more Ray revealed his strength, the brighter the fighting spirit radiating from Max became.","That reaction alone gradually caused the sneer on Ray’s face to disappear.","Then slowly, a cold smile returned.","\"Fine,\" Ray said while his eyes sharpened dangerously. \"Since you’re so eager to die...\"","The crimson spear in his hand suddenly trembled violently.","\"I’ll show you the true power of my Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Boom!!!","The moment those words fell, an overwhelming pressure erupted violently from Ray’s body once more.","The entire eighth layer shook violently.","Cracks spread rapidly across the platform beneath his feet while sharp scarlet energy exploded outward in every direction like a raging storm. Nearby participants instinctively retreated farther away as the terrifying aura surrounding Ray continued climbing higher and higher.","The crimson spear within his hand began radiating blinding red light.","At the same time, the concept of sharpness surrounding him transformed completely.","Before, it had merely felt sharp.","Now, it felt as though the very space around him could be sliced apart at any moment.","Thin distortions appeared throughout the surrounding air while countless invisible cuts spread continuously across the stone platform beneath him. Even without attacking, the pressure released from Ray alone was already tearing the battlefield apart."]},{"number":1658,"title":"Chapter 1658: True Power of Pseudo Cosmic Path","paragraphs":["Jonathan’s expression immediately became serious.","\"He’s pushing the Pseudo Cosmic Path even further now...\"","Julie also narrowed her eyes while staring toward Ray.","\"This pressure is already approaching the level of a true Cosmic Path.\"","The surrounding geniuses felt their scalps grow numb after hearing those words.","Several participants had already begun retreating farther away from the platform entirely, afraid of being caught within the aftermath of the upcoming clash.","Meanwhile, Ray slowly lowered his body.","His posture resembled a predator preparing to strike down prey in a single fatal attack.","The crimson spear rotated lightly within his hand while terrifying sharpness continuously gathered around its tip. The surrounding spiritual energy was drawn uncontrollably toward the spear, causing violent whirlwinds to form around him.","Then Ray took a single step forward.","Boom!!!","The entire platform trembled violently.","A massive crater instantly formed beneath his feet as the overwhelming pressure of the Pseudo Cosmic Path erupted outward without restraint.","The killing intent within Ray’s eyes intensified sharply while his gaze remained locked onto Max alone.","At that moment, there was only one thought within his mind.","Crush him completely.","Humiliate him completely.","Destroy the so-called genius who had stolen all the attention that should have belonged to him.","The crimson spear gradually emitted an ear-piercing hum as its pressure continued rising higher and higher.","Even the surrounding space itself seemed unable to endure the terrifying sharpness gathering around the spear any longer.","Thin black lines gradually began appearing throughout the air around Ray.","Spatial tears.","The surrounding participants immediately felt their hearts shake after seeing that sight.","One had to understand that only attacks possessing terrifying power and comprehension could damage space itself within the Divine Realm. Yet now, before Ray had even launched an attack, the pressure gathering around his spear was already beginning to tear apart the surrounding space.","Jonathan’s expression darkened further.","\"He’s serious now...\"","Julie remained silent while staring fixedly toward Ray.","Even she could no longer deny how terrifying Ray’s current strength had become.","Then slowly, Ray raised the crimson spear.","The spear tip pointed directly toward Max’s forehead.","A cold smile appeared on his face afterward.","\"Try surviving this first,\" he said quietly.","The next moment, the terrifying power of the Pseudo Cosmic Path exploded completely.","The moment Ray released his attack, the entire eighth layer seemed to darken beneath the overwhelming pressure erupting from the crimson spear.","Boom!!!","A terrifying scarlet beam exploded forward as overwhelming sharpness tore violently through the battlefield. The attack moved so quickly that many participants could barely follow it with their eyes. Wherever the spear light passed, the surrounding space distorted violently while deep cuts spread across the stone platform beneath it like countless invisible blades had carved through the battlefield.","This was no longer merely the power of a concept.","This was the terrifying might of a Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Even before the attack fully arrived, Max could already feel horrifying pressure crushing toward him from every direction. The sharpness contained within the spear strike was so overwhelming that it felt capable of severing everything standing in its path.","Yet Max did not retreat.","Instead, the excitement burning within his eyes only intensified further.","\"Good!\" Max shouted as seven-colored lightning exploded violently around his body.","The next moment, he raised his sword directly toward the incoming spear attack.","Boom!!!","Sword and spear collided head-on.","For a brief instant, the entire battlefield froze.","Then—","Crack.","A clear breaking sound echoed across the platform.","Jonathan’s eyes widened instantly.","Julie’s expression changed sharply.","The sword in Max’s hand shattered apart.","The moment the blade touched Ray’s spear attack, countless cracks spread across its surface instantly before the entire sword exploded into countless fragments.","Boom!!!","The terrifying spear force continued pressing forward without slowing down even slightly.","The surrounding participants immediately inhaled sharply.","\"It shattered his sword instantly?!\"","\"That’s the power of a Pseudo Cosmic Path?!\"","Even Jonathan’s expression became solemn after witnessing that scene.","However, to everyone’s shock, Max did not panic.","Not even slightly.","Instead, he smiled.","\"Amazing!\" Max laughed excitedly as shattered sword fragments scattered around him like falling stars.","The fighting spirit burning within his eyes erupted upward crazily.","At that moment, Max finally stopped holding back completely.","Boom!!!","A terrifying aura erupted violently from his body.","The First Divine Vein, the Vein of Origin, opened completely.","An overwhelming surge of raw power exploded from deep within Max’s body as his physical strength increased explosively once again. The muscles throughout his body tightened violently while terrifying force surged through every inch of his flesh.","At the same time, the Second Divine Vein, the Vein of Vitality, opened fully as well.","Boom!!!","Terrifying vitality surged throughout Max’s body like a raging ocean. His blood roared violently while endless life force erupted from every cell within him. The pressure radiating from his physical body alone began distorting the surrounding air.","Then the Third Divine Vein, the Vein of Strength, opened completely.","Crack!!!","The seven-colored lightning surrounding Max instantly became several times more violent.","The surrounding participants only saw the space around Max distort faintly as terrifying speed fluctuations erupted outward from him like a collapsing storm.","At that moment, all three Divine Veins operated simultaneously.","The increase in power was horrifying.","The raw physical strength surging from Max’s body instantly reached an absurd level. The surrounding platform cracked violently beneath his feet while the pressure erupting from him collided directly against Ray’s Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Jonathan’s expression changed completely.","\"This aura...\"","Julie’s beautiful eyes widened visibly.","\"How can his body withstand this much power?!\"","Even Ray’s confident expression shifted slightly for the first time.","He could clearly sense the explosive increase in Max’s physical abilities.","However, his spear attack had already descended completely.","The terrifying crimson spear light pierced directly toward Max.","And this time, Max did not use a sword.","Instead, he raised his bare hands.","Boom!!!","The moment Max grabbed the incoming spear force, the entire eighth layer exploded violently.","Terrifying shockwaves spread outward in every direction as the surrounding platform shattered continuously beneath the pressure. Countless participants were forced backward while nearby tower walls cracked apart violently from the impact alone.","Jonathan immediately retreated several meters.","Julie’s expression became incomparably serious.","\"This monster...\"","At the center of the collision, Max stood there with both bare hands gripping the terrifying spear attack directly.","The sharpness of the Pseudo Cosmic Path continuously tore through his body while violent scarlet energy exploded around him like countless blades trying to slice him apart.","Blood immediately burst from Max’s hands.","Then—","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","Countless crack marks suddenly spread across Max’s body.","The surrounding participants immediately stared in shock.","The cracks spread rapidly across his arms, shoulders, chest, and neck like shattered porcelain. At first glance, it looked as though Max’s entire body would collapse apart at any second beneath the overwhelming force of the Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Even Jonathan’s pupils contracted sharply.","\"He blocked it with his bare hands?!\"","The terrifying pressure of the Pseudo Cosmic Path continued crushing against Max violently.","Yet Max still did not retreat even a single step.","The crack marks covering his body became deeper and deeper while blood continuously leaked from them.","However, something even more shocking happened next.","The moment the destruction reached its peak—","Boom!!!","The Vein of Vitality erupted fully.","An overwhelming life force exploded throughout Max’s body instantly.","The countless crack marks covering him began healing at terrifying speed.","Shattered flesh regenerated rapidly.","Broken skin recovered instantly.","Even the blood leaking from his body disappeared almost immediately.","Within only a few breaths, Max’s body returned completely to normal.","Not a single crack remained.","Not a single injury remained.","The surrounding battlefield fell into absolute silence.","Everyone stared at Max as though they were looking at a monster wearing human skin.","Even Jonathan and Julie remained frozen momentarily after witnessing such terrifying regenerative ability.","Meanwhile, Max slowly lifted his head while still gripping the terrifying spear attack tightly with his bare hands.","A wild smile gradually spread across his face.","\"This...\"","His eyes burned with overwhelming excitement and battle intent.","\"This is the kind of battle I wanted!\""]},{"number":1659,"title":"Chapter 1659: A Fierce Battle!","paragraphs":["\"How can your body possibly be this strong?!\" Ray’s voice exploded across the battlefield as he staggered backward slightly, his crimson spear trembling faintly within his grasp.","The disbelief on his face was impossible to hide anymore. Ever since the battle had begun, he had maintained absolute confidence in himself, especially after revealing the terrifying power of his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","He had expected fear. He had expected hesitation. He had expected the surrounding geniuses to look at him with awe and despair.","And they did.","Every participant standing on the eighth layer had already realized how monstrous Ray’s comprehension truly was. Even Jonathan and Julie, two individuals acknowledged as monsters among monsters, had turned serious the moment Ray revealed traces of the Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Yet the person standing directly before him now had completely shattered all of Ray’s expectations.","Max had not retreated.","He had not used some profound defensive treasure.","He had not relied on any mysterious heaven defying shield or ancient protective art.","Instead, he had blocked the terrifying spear strike of a Pseudo Cosmic Path with nothing except his own flesh and blood.","The sight alone felt absurd beyond reason.","Ray could still clearly remember the moment his spear collided against Max’s body. He had felt the terrifying resistance behind those bare hands. It was as though his spear had not struck flesh at all but had instead smashed against an indestructible divine mountain.","What horrified him even more was what happened afterward.","The injuries.","The torn flesh.","The shattered skin.","All of it had regenerated instantly before everyone’s eyes.","That was what truly shook Ray to his core.","The surrounding participants were equally speechless. Many of them were still staring blankly at Max as though they could no longer understand what kind of existence he truly was. The expressions of the geniuses nearby had long since changed from shock to genuine fear.","Meanwhile, Max slowly loosened his grip on the crimson spear before calmly taking a step backward. Fresh blood still dripped from his fingers, yet his expression remained completely relaxed. In fact, the excitement within his eyes only seemed to grow stronger.","\"That attack...\" Max said honestly while slowly flexing his slightly bloodstained fingers, \"might be the strongest strike I have ever received from someone of my generation.\"","His voice carried no mockery.","No arrogance.","Only genuine excitement.","Then his gaze locked directly onto Ray once more.","The smile on his face widened further as seven colored lightning exploded violently around his body, illuminating the entire battlefield with dazzling brilliance.","\"So come on...\" Max said while lightning crackled around him like divine punishment descending from the heavens. \"Show me more of this so called Pseudo Cosmic Path, Ray Willer.\"","The moment those words entered Ray’s ears, the entire battlefield seemed to freeze briefly.","Ray’s expression stiffened.","Then slowly, his face darkened completely.","Humiliation surged through him like burning poison.","A deep and unbearable humiliation.","He had revealed the terrifying power of the Pseudo Cosmic Path before countless geniuses. He had shaken the entire eighth layer with his overwhelming comprehension. Everyone present understood how terrifying his future potential truly was.","Yet Max was not looking at him with fear.","Instead, Max was looking at him with excitement.","That was what Ray could not accept.","The way Max spoke.","The anticipation burning within his eyes.","It felt as though Max was not fighting for survival at all.","Instead, it felt as though Max was simply enjoying the opportunity to experience the power of the Pseudo Cosmic Path firsthand.","As though Ray himself had become nothing more than a tool for Max’s growth.","That realization instantly ignited the rage buried deep within Ray’s heart.","\"You...\" Ray growled as his fingers tightened violently around the crimson spear. Veins bulged across his arm while terrifying spear energy exploded outward uncontrollably. \"You’ll regret saying those words.\"","Boom!!!","A far more terrifying pressure erupted from Ray’s body.","The sharpness surrounding him instantly intensified to an astonishing degree as scarlet spear energy swept violently across the entire battlefield. The surrounding participants immediately retreated farther away, their expressions changing drastically as the atmosphere became incomparably dangerous.","\"You want to see more of my Pseudo Cosmic Path?\" Ray’s bloodshot eyes burned with fury.","\"Fine...\"","The crimson spear suddenly emitted a piercing shrill cry that echoed across the eighth layer.","\"I’ll show you enough to make you despair!\"","Boom!!!","Ray vanished instantly.","The next moment, a terrifying scarlet spear light descended directly toward Max from above like heavenly judgment itself. The speed was so overwhelming that many ordinary participants could not even follow the attack with their eyes.","\"Crimson Heaven Piercer!\"","Boom!!!","The spear strike tore through the air like a falling scarlet meteor while terrifying sharpness exploded outward from every direction simultaneously. The surrounding space distorted violently under the pressure alone.","However, Max did not retreat.","He did not dodge.","Instead, he simply raised his bare hand once more.","Boom!!!","His palm collided directly against the descending spear attack.","The violent impact caused the entire platform to tremble violently while terrifying shockwaves exploded outward in every direction. Deep cracks spread across the battlefield beneath Max’s feet as blood immediately burst from his palm.","Yet despite the horrifying force behind the attack—","He blocked it.","Using nothing but the power of the three Divine Veins.","Ray’s expression twisted violently.","Without giving Max even a single moment to breathe, he attacked again.","Boom!!!","The crimson spear swept horizontally across the battlefield while scarlet light sliced through the surrounding space like a divine blade.","\"Blood Severing Sky!\"","Max calmly crossed both arms before his chest.","Boom!!!","The spear strike slammed into him violently.","Crack marks instantly spread across Max’s arms while blood exploded outward from the impact. The sheer force behind the attack pushed him backward across the platform.","Yet immediately afterward—","The Vein of Vitality erupted.","The crack marks healed instantly.","Fresh flesh regenerated before everyone’s eyes.","The surrounding participants stared numbly at the unbelievable sight.","\"He blocked it again...\"","\"He’s using his body like a weapon...\"","Ray’s eyes grew increasingly furious.","Then he attacked again.","And again.","And again.","Boom!!!","Boom!!!","Boom!!!","Terrifying spear attacks continuously exploded across the eighth layer one after another. Every strike carried overwhelming sharpness fused together with the terrifying pressure of the Pseudo Cosmic Path itself. The surrounding tower walls began cracking apart while violent shockwaves swept across the battlefield endlessly."]},{"number":1660,"title":"Chapter 1660: Comprehending...","paragraphs":["Ray’s furious roars echoed throughout the platform alongside the names of his techniques.","\"Scarlet Soul Splitter!\"","\"Heaven Slaughtering Spear!\"","\"Crimson Void Collapse!\"","Each attack was stronger than the previous one.","Each strike possessed enough power to instantly annihilate ordinary peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses.","Yet Max blocked every single attack.","Sometimes he used his bare fists to smash apart the spear light directly.","Sometimes he crossed his arms to endure the attacks head on.","Sometimes he simply relied entirely on the terrifying durability of his body and allowed the spear strikes to collide against him directly.","The three Divine Veins operated at full capacity continuously.","The Vein of Origin amplified his raw physical strength to monstrous levels.","The Vein of Strength pushed his raw strength beyond ordinary comprehension.","And the Vein of Vitality regenerated his damaged body endlessly.","Again and again, Ray’s spear attacks tore apart Max’s flesh.","Again and again, cracks spread across his body like shattered porcelain.","Yet every single time—","His body healed instantly afterward.","The scene gradually became more horrifying with every exchange.","Jonathan’s expression had already turned extremely solemn as he watched the battle unfold.","\"He’s adapting...\" Jonathan muttered quietly, unable to hide the seriousness in his voice anymore. He could feel that Max was adapting to more and more of Pseudo Cosmic Path of Ray and was getting less and less injured as the battle went on.","Julie’s beautiful eyes trembled faintly as she stared at Max.","\"No...\" she whispered softly.","Her gaze remained locked firmly onto him.","\"He’s enjoying it.\"","That was the truly terrifying part.","The more Ray attacked, the brighter the excitement within Max’s eyes became.","At this moment, Max no longer resembled someone struggling desperately within a fierce battle.","Instead, he looked like a madman enthusiastically welcoming stronger and stronger attacks with his own body alone.","Meanwhile, Ray’s fury continued growing uncontrollably.","No matter how many attacks he unleashed...","No matter how terrifying his spear strikes became...","Max simply refused to fall.","\"Hahaha! More!\" Max’s loud laughter echoed across the shattered battlefield as he charged directly toward Ray once again without the slightest hint of fear upon his face.","The seven colored lightning surrounding his body exploded wildly while terrifying physical force radiated from every movement he made.","At this point, Max no longer looked like an ordinary cultivator at all. Instead, he resembled an ancient beast that had finally found an opponent capable of enduring his madness.","The surrounding participants could only stare at the battlefield with completely numb expressions.","None of them even knew how to react anymore.","What was unfolding before their eyes had already surpassed the level of a normal clash between geniuses. The eighth layer of the tower had long since become a scene of destruction.","Massive cracks spread endlessly across the platform while shattered debris floated throughout the air under the influence of the terrifying shockwaves erupting from every collision.","Boom!!!","Ray’s crimson spear descended once more like divine punishment itself, carrying overwhelming sharpness capable of splitting apart heaven and earth.","Yet Max directly met it head on with his bare fist.","The collision instantly caused the surrounding space to distort violently. The air exploded outward while enormous cracks spread beneath both of them across the already devastated platform.","Neither side retreated.","Instead, the battle only became fiercer.","Ray’s expression had already twisted from rage and disbelief as he continuously unleashed one terrifying spear technique after another.","The pressure radiating from his Pseudo Cosmic Path became increasingly violent with every attack he launched. Scarlet spear energy swept across the battlefield endlessly, tearing apart everything nearby.","Meanwhile, Max fought him directly without the slightest intention of avoiding the attacks.","He simply charged forward again and again using nothing except the monstrous physical strength granted by the three Divine Veins and his terrifying body.","Again and again, Ray’s sharpness tore apart Max’s flesh.","Again and again, blood exploded from Max’s body as horrifying wounds spread across him.","Yet every single time—","His flesh regenerated instantly afterward.","The Vein of Vitality continuously surged with endless life force, restoring his damaged body at a terrifying speed that left everyone speechless.","The more the battle continued, the brighter the excitement within Max’s eyes became.","However, beneath that excitement—","Something else had quietly begun changing.","As Max continuously clashed directly against Ray’s spear attacks, he gradually began sensing something hidden deeper within the structure of the Pseudo Cosmic Path itself.","At first, all he could feel was overwhelming sharpness.","An absolute sharpness capable of severing everything in existence.","But now—","The more attacks he exchanged with Ray, the clearer the structure behind the Pseudo Cosmic Path gradually became.","The sharpness surrounding Ray’s spear was not chaotic.","It was ordered.","Every movement.","Every fluctuation.","Every strand of spear energy.","All of it was connected together by a deeper foundation.","A strange and mysterious connection linked every attack into something far greater than an ordinary concept.","Max’s eyes gradually sharpened.","\"So this is how it works...\" he muttered inwardly.","Deep within him, the Severing Sword Concept trembled faintly but it was his emotion severing cosmic path that was violently reacting as if threatening to take over him.","As Max continued experiencing the Pseudo Cosmic Path firsthand, his own understanding began evolving rapidly. Every spear strike from Ray felt like a lesson. Every collision revealed another layer hidden behind the so called Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Gradually, Max began realizing something terrifying.","A true Cosmic Path was not simply a stronger concept.","It was the complete integration of one’s comprehension, intent, laws, and existence into a single unified whole.","And the Pseudo Cosmic Path—","Was the halfway point toward that transformation.","At that moment, countless insights flashed rapidly through Max’s mind like streaks of lightning. His Severing Sword Concept began evolving subtly while his terrifying comprehension accelerated at an astonishing speed.","Even Jonathan eventually noticed the strange changes occurring around Max.","\"Wait...\" Jonathan muttered suddenly, his expression shifting into visible shock.","Julie immediately turned toward him.","Jonathan’s eyes remained locked firmly onto Max as disbelief slowly appeared within them.","\"He’s comprehending Ray’s Pseudo Cosmic Path during the battle.\"","Julie’s expression changed completely afterward.","\"What?!\"","The surrounding geniuses immediately stared toward Max in disbelief after hearing Jonathan’s words.","Comprehending a Pseudo Cosmic Path during battle?","That was complete madness.","Meanwhile, Max himself had become increasingly immersed in the battle.","The surrounding world gradually faded from his awareness.","The shattered battlefield.","The surrounding geniuses.","The collapsing eighth layer.","None of it mattered anymore.","Only Ray’s spear remained within his vision.","Only the structure hidden behind the Pseudo Cosmic Path remained within his mind.","He was beginning to understand it.","Beginning to glimpse the road beyond ordinary concepts.","His comprehension surged wildly as his Emotion Severing Cosmic Path continuously evolved deeper and deeper.","And just as Max’s rapidly advancing understanding seemed on the verge of producing a true breakthrough—"]},{"number":1661,"title":"Chapter 1661: Ray’s Breakdown!","paragraphs":["Ray finally lost control completely.","\"Enough!!!\"","Boom!!!","An incomparably terrifying aura erupted violently from Ray’s body.","The surrounding participants immediately felt their expressions change drastically as overwhelming pressure swept across the entire eighth layer.","The crimson spear within Ray’s hand emitted blinding scarlet light while violent sharpness spread uncontrollably through the surrounding space.","Ray’s face had completely darkened by now.","He could feel it clearly.","Max was using him.","Using his Pseudo Cosmic Path as a stepping stone for his own comprehension.","That realization completely shattered the final traces of calmness remaining within Ray’s heart.","\"You think you can use me to improve yourself?!\" Ray roared furiously as terrifying killing intent exploded from his body like a storm.","His voice shook the battlefield violently.","\"I’ll kill you before that ever happens!\"","Boom!!!","The entire tower trembled violently.","Terrifying crimson energy gathered endlessly around Ray while the sharpness surrounding him became increasingly unstable and destructive. The surrounding participants immediately retreated farther away with pale expressions as they sensed the horrifying power gathering around him.","Jonathan’s expression changed sharply.","\"He’s using his ultimate attack!\"","Julie’s face immediately became solemn.","The pressure radiating from Ray had already reached a terrifying level where even the surrounding space itself began collapsing faintly beneath it.","Then—","Ray slowly raised his spear toward the sky.","At that moment, countless scarlet cracks spread throughout the surrounding air as though the world itself was being severed apart by invisible blades.","An enormous crimson phantom gradually appeared behind Ray.","It resembled a gigantic heavenly spear capable of piercing through heaven and earth themselves.","\"World Ending Crimson Heaven Spear!\"","Boom!!!","The instant Ray unleashed the attack, the entire eighth layer seemed to collapse.","A world destroying scarlet beam descended directly toward Max while horrifying sharpness tore apart everything along its path. The platform shattered continuously while even the surrounding tower walls cracked violently beneath the terrifying pressure.","This attack far surpassed every previous strike Ray had unleashed.","This was his true ultimate attack.","A terrifying strike empowered fully by the power of his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Even Jonathan’s expression changed drastically.","\"If that attack lands directly...\" Jonathan muttered, unable to finish his sentence.","Julie’s eyes trembled faintly.","\"He’ll really die...\"","Meanwhile—","At the very center of the destruction—","Max slowly raised his head.","For the very first time since the battle began, the excitement within his eyes gradually disappeared.","In its place—","A terrifying calmness emerged.","Then slowly—","Boom!!!","An overwhelming draconic aura suddenly erupted violently from Max’s body.","The surrounding participants immediately felt their bloodlines tremble instinctively beneath the terrifying pressure.","Max’s five thousand Draconic Essences exploded fully.","A faint dragon roar echoed throughout the eighth layer while monstrous physical power flooded every part of his body instantly.","The muscles across Max’s body expanded slightly while faint black dragon scales appeared beneath his skin. The surrounding air distorted violently from the sheer force radiating outward from him.","Then—","Max slowly clenched his fist.","Boom!!!","The three Divine Veins erupted simultaneously.","The Vein of Origin amplified his raw physical power explosively.","The Vein of Strength increased his strength beyond ordinary limits.","The Vein of Vitality caused endless life force to surge through him like an eternal river.","Combined together with the monstrous strength of five thousand Draconic Essences—","Max’s physical power reached an utterly horrifying level.","Then—","He punched forward.","No concepts.","No techniques.","No laws.","Only absolute strength.","Boom!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!","The instant Max’s fist collided directly against the descending world destroying spear attack—","The world itself seemed to explode.","A terrifying shockwave swept violently throughout the entire eighth layer while countless cracks tore across the surrounding space itself.","Then—","To everyone’s horror—","Ray’s ultimate attack shattered apart completely.","The enormous scarlet spear beam exploded into countless fragments before collapsing entirely beneath the overwhelming power of Max’s fist.","Jonathan’s pupils contracted violently.","Julie froze completely.","Every surrounding participant stared at the scene in absolute disbelief.","Meanwhile—","At the center of the destruction—","Max slowly lowered his fist while overwhelming dragon aura still swirled violently around his body.","Then a faint smile gradually appeared upon his face.","\"So this...\" Max muttered quietly while looking directly toward Ray, \"is the full power of your Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","Ray, on the other hand, looked completely devastated. His face had turned pale while disbelief filled his eyes as he stared at the destroyed remains of his attack. He simply could not accept what had just happened.","That attack had been created from the very essence of his Pseudo Cosmic Path. It was the strongest power he could currently unleash, yet Max had shattered it so easily that it almost felt unreal to him.","\"How is this even possible?!\" Ray roared in disbelief.","For a brief moment, hopelessness appeared within his eyes.","At that instant, memories of Mira’s warning resurfaced inside his mind. Before this trial began, she had repeatedly warned him not to underestimate Max. She had even handed him a special treasure from the Sword God Palace and told him to use it immediately to kill Max without giving him any opportunity to resist.","However, Ray had his own pride.","As one of the greatest geniuses of his generation, he never believed he would be forced into relying on an external treasure just to deal with someone at Max’s cultivation level. In his eyes, defeating Max with his own strength was the only acceptable outcome. Only after crushing Max personally did he intend to use the treasure to erase him completely.","But now, Ray finally realized how foolish that thinking had been.","In front of Max, his so-called strength no longer seemed worth mentioning. Even the pride he had always cherished so deeply felt laughable now.","\"You forced me to do this!\" Ray shouted furiously as madness gradually appeared across his face.","At that moment, he finally decided to use the treasure given to him by the Sword God Palace.","Ray suddenly pressed his hand against the sword-shaped rune engraved upon his palm.","The rune immediately erupted with dazzling white light.","Then, in the next instant, a sword appeared within Ray’s grasp.","The moment the sword manifested, the expressions of countless people changed drastically.","A terrifying sense of oppression swept across the entire battlefield like an invisible storm. Many participants instinctively felt their bodies grow cold as an overwhelming sensation of mortal danger flooded their minds.","Even Jonathan and Julie felt their hearts tremble after sensing the aura emitted by that weapon.","The sword itself was pure white in color, yet the energy radiating from it felt incredibly strange and unnatural. It was neither holy nor demonic. Instead, it carried an indescribable aura that made everyone feel deeply uncomfortable merely by looking at it.","\"Do you really think using a sword will make any difference?\" Max asked with a faint sneer on his face.","\"Hahaha!\" Ray suddenly burst into laughter.","However, his laughter no longer sounded normal. It carried madness, frustration, humiliation, and killing intent all mixed together.","Then Ray slowly raised the white sword toward Max.","\"Tell me, Max,\" Ray said while grinning like a madman, \"do you know the true difference between this trial and the Cosmic Ascension Conference?\"","\"What difference?\" Max asked calmly.","He genuinely did not know the answer.","From everything he had heard, this trial had been specifically created as a perfect imitation of the Cosmic Ascension Conference so that the geniuses of the many third-rate forces could prepare themselves in advance for the real event.","Because of that, Max had always believed there should not be any real difference between the two."]},{"number":1662,"title":"Chapter 1662: Eternal Hourglass","paragraphs":["\"Let me tell you the difference.\" Ray laughed softly as a wicked smile slowly spread across his face.","The madness within his eyes seemed to deepen further while the strange white sword in his hand emitted an increasingly unsettling aura.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference is held inside a supreme treasure known as the Eternal Hourglass,\" Ray continued slowly. \"That treasure is an omnipotent artifact of unimaginable value.\"","As he spoke those words, even the surrounding participants revealed shocked expressions.","Clearly, many of them had heard of the Eternal Hourglass before.","\"Legend says that the Eternal Hourglass has remained in the possession of the Primordials since ancient times,\" Ray said proudly. \"It is one of the Five Primal Treasures that have existed since time immemorial itself. Because of that, the laws within the Eternal Hourglass are far stricter and far more absolute than the rules governing this Soul Sealing Painting.\"","Ray’s grin widened further as he continued speaking.","\"Inside the Eternal Hourglass, once the rules are established, nobody can break them. No matter what happens during the Cosmic Ascension Conference, participants can never truly die within that world.\"","Then Ray slowly raised the white sword in his hand.","\"But this place is different.\"","The atmosphere around him instantly became colder.","\"The Soul Sealing Painting is powerful, but it is still far inferior to the Eternal Hourglass. The rules here are not absolute. Under certain conditions, they can be bypassed.\"","Max frowned slightly after hearing those words.","He naturally understood the significance of the Eternal Hourglass. A Primal Treasure that existed since the beginning of time itself was naturally incomparable to treasures like the Soul Sealing Painting.","However, what Max did not understand was what exactly Ray was trying to imply.","\"What are you trying to say?\" Max asked calmly while narrowing his eyes slightly.","Ray immediately sneered.","\"You see this sword?\" he said while lightly waving the white-white blade in his hand.","The moment the sword moved, countless people felt their souls tremble involuntarily.","\"This sword is one of the six treasured swords of the Sword God Palace,\" Ray declared proudly. \"Its name is the Soul Devouring Sword.\"","The strange energy radiating from the blade intensified further.","\"Anyone killed by this sword will have their soul devoured completely. Their soul will be trapped inside the sword for eternity without any possibility of escape.\"","As he spoke those final words, terrifying killing intent erupted from Ray’s eyes.","Then he slowly pointed the Soul Devouring Sword directly toward Max.","\"Normally, when participants die inside the Soul Sealing Painting, their souls are immediately returned safely to their original bodies outside.\"","Ray’s smile gradually became colder and colder.","\"But if someone is killed by the Soul Devouring Sword...\"","A horrifying aura suddenly spread across the battlefield.","\"Their soul will be devoured before the Soul Sealing Painting can return it.\"","Ray stared directly into Max’s eyes as madness filled his face completely.","\"And once your soul is devoured...\"","\"You will truly die.\"","\"I see.\" Max now realized the true terror of the white sword in Ray’s hand.","\"Hahaha! Now die before me, Max Morgan!\" Ray’s laughter echoed wildly across the battlefield as madness completely consumed his expression.","At that moment, he tightly gripped the Soul Devouring Sword with both hands.","The instant his fingers wrapped fully around the hilt, the strange white sword suddenly erupted with blinding white light.","Then—","A terrifying pressure descended upon the entire eighth layer.","The expressions of countless participants changed drastically.","Many people instantly felt their souls trembling violently inside their bodies as though an invisible force was trying to drag their consciousness out by force. Several weaker geniuses turned pale immediately while cold sweat poured down their backs uncontrollably.","Even breathing became difficult.","The aura emitted by the Soul Devouring Sword was simply too terrifying.","It was not merely physical pressure.","Instead, it directly targeted the soul itself.","Jonathan’s pupils contracted sharply.","Julie’s face changed completely.","Even they could feel intense danger radiating from that sword.","\"This sword...\" Jonathan muttered with a grave expression. \"It can truly harm souls.\"","The surrounding participants hurriedly retreated farther away in panic as fear gradually spread through the battlefield. Nobody dared remain too close to Ray anymore because the mere aura emitted from the Soul Devouring Sword made them feel as though their souls were being sliced apart little by little.","Meanwhile, the white light surrounding the sword grew brighter and brighter.","Then suddenly—","The blade began expanding rapidly.","In only a few moments, the originally normal-sized sword transformed into a gigantic white divine blade over ten times larger than before. The enormous sword radiated horrifying soul fluctuations while strange white runes flickered endlessly across its surface.","At the same time, countless miserable wails suddenly echoed faintly from within the sword itself.","Those sounds resembled the cries of tortured souls trapped in endless despair.","Hearing those screams caused many participants to feel chills spread through their entire bodies.","Ray’s grin became even more twisted after seeing everyone’s fearful reactions.","\"You should feel honored, Max,\" Ray said coldly while raising the enormous Soul Devouring Sword high above his head. \"Very few people are worthy of dying beneath this weapon.\"","Boom!!!","Terrifying white sword energy exploded into the sky.","The surrounding space distorted violently while the horrifying pressure emitted by the Soul Devouring Sword continued rising at an astonishing speed.","At that moment, Ray no longer held back any killing intent whatsoever.","He truly intended to kill Max here.","Then, with a crazed roar, Ray slashed the gigantic white sword downward toward Max.","The moment the attack descended, the heavens and earth themselves seemed to darken.","A colossal white sword light tore through the battlefield with unstoppable momentum while terrifying soul-devouring energy swept across the surroundings like a raging storm. Wherever the white slash passed, even space itself appeared to twist unnaturally.","The participants nearby retreated frantically once again, their faces filled with horror.","Many of them had a terrifying feeling.","If they were struck by that attack—","Not only would their bodies perish.","Even their souls would be erased forever."]},{"number":1663,"title":"Chapter 1663: Terror of the Soul Devouring Sword","paragraphs":["Max, who stood directly at the center of the attack, felt the terrifying pressure more clearly than anyone else present.","The moment the gigantic silver sword descended toward him, an overwhelming sensation of danger exploded throughout his entire body.","His expression immediately changed.","For the first time since the battle had begun, Max genuinely felt the aura of death approaching him.","It was not the danger of physical destruction.","Instead, it was something far more terrifying.","Max suddenly felt as though an invisible force had wrapped itself around his soul and was trying to rip it out of his body by force. The strange soul-devouring energy emitted by the Soul Devouring Sword continuously invaded his consciousness while a cold and sinister aura spread through every corner of his being.","Even his Soul Palace began trembling violently.","The deeper the gigantic silver sword descended, the stronger that horrifying pulling force became.","It felt as though countless invisible hands were clawing at his soul relentlessly, attempting to drag it toward the enormous blade in the sky.","\"This is bad...\" Max muttered as his eyes narrowed sharply.","At that moment, the Soul Devouring Sword had not even fully reached him yet.","The gigantic silver blade was still suspended high in the air.","Yet despite that, Max already felt such overwhelming terror that even he could no longer remain completely calm.","That alone proved how horrifying this weapon truly was.","Max had faced countless dangers before. He had confronted beings far stronger than himself and survived situations that should have been impossible to escape from. However, this feeling was entirely different from anything he had experienced previously.","This sword directly targeted the soul itself.","And deep within his instincts, Max could clearly feel one terrifying truth.","If that sword truly struck him—","His soul would genuinely be devoured forever.","Having personally experienced the horrifying nature of the Soul Devouring Sword, Max immediately understood how disastrous the consequences would be if even the slightest portion of his soul was injured by that weapon.","Damage to the body could still be healed.","But damage to the soul was entirely different. Max had already experienced this before.","Once the soul was harmed, countless hidden dangers and irreversible consequences could follow afterward.","\"Damn it!\" Max cursed inwardly as his expression darkened heavily. \"At a time like this, I truly wish I could use my real sword.\"","At that moment, the figure of the Dragonheart Sword immediately appeared within his mind.","If the Dragonheart Sword were in his hands right now, Max believed that no matter how terrifying the Soul Devouring Sword was, it would never be able to threaten him so easily. The Dragonheart Sword itself possessed extraordinary spirituality and overwhelming might.","Max was absolutely confident it could resist the strange soul-devouring power emitted by Ray’s weapon.","Unfortunately, the Dragonheart Sword remained with his true body outside the Soul Sealing Painting.","Inside this world, participants could only use the weapons provided by the Soul Sealing Painting itself.","Because of that restriction, Max had no choice but to rely on an ordinary sword.","However, Max was not completely without options.","At the same time that this battle was unfolding, Max’s clone had already rushed to unlock the Dimension of Soul. Max knew very clearly that if he could successfully unlock the Dimension of Soul, his control over soul-related powers would increase tremendously.","But the problem was time.","To fully unlock the Dimension of Soul, the clone first needed to pass the trial guarding it. That process could not be completed instantly.","Which meant Max only had one option right now.","He needed to stall for time.","Boom!!!","Seven colored lightning suddenly erupted violently around Max’s body as dazzling arcs of divine lightning crackled across the battlefield. The surrounding air exploded repeatedly under the overwhelming pressure released by the seven colored lightning.","Then, a sword condensed entirely from seven colored lightning appeared within Max’s grasp.","The moment the sword formed, Max’s aura rose sharply.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art!\"","Max’s eyes turned incomparably sharp as he unleashed the full power of the Saint Origin Sword Art without holding back anything whatsoever.","Boom!!!","A terrifying sword light instantly erupted from Max’s lightning sword as overwhelming sword intent surged into the heavens. The dazzling seven colored slash carried astonishing sharpness as it collided head-on against the gigantic silver Soul Devouring Sword descending from the sky.","For a brief instant, the entire battlefield trembled violently.","Then—","Boom!!!","A deafening explosion erupted across the eighth layer.","The seven colored sword light exploded with incredible force and actually managed to push the gigantic Soul Devouring Sword slightly upward.","The surrounding participants immediately widened their eyes in shock.","Even Ray’s expression changed faintly.","However—","Max’s expression did not improve at all.","Because although his attack had managed to repel the gigantic silver sword slightly, it had failed to destroy it completely.","The enormous Soul Devouring Sword merely trembled violently in the air before continuing its descent once again.","The terrifying soul-devouring aura radiating from it remained overwhelmingly powerful.","Seeing that scene, Max immediately understood one terrifying truth.","This weapon was far stronger than he originally expected.","\"Max, your struggles are completely futile!\" Ray’s laughter echoed madly across the battlefield as the gigantic Soul Devouring Sword continued descending from the sky with unstoppable force.","The silver light radiating from the enormous blade grew increasingly brighter while the horrifying soul fluctuations spreading from it became even more terrifying than before.","\"You still do not understand what kind of place this is!\" Ray shouted arrogantly while gripping the Soul Devouring Sword tightly with both hands.","At that moment, the strange energy surrounding the blade began absorbing the soul aura filling the Soul Sealing Painting itself. Countless silver streams of energy flowed toward the sword continuously, causing the pressure emitted by the weapon to rise further and further.","The expressions of the surrounding participants changed once again after witnessing that scene.","\"This sword...\" Jonathan muttered with a grave expression. \"It is actually drawing strength from the Soul Sealing Painting itself.\"","Julie’s face also became incomparably serious.","Clearly, the Soul Devouring Sword possessed terrifying compatibility with this world.","Ray immediately laughed even louder after noticing the shocked reactions around him.","\"This is a soul-type weapon!\" he declared proudly. \"And this entire world is governed purely by soul power. The longer this battle continues, the stronger the Soul Devouring Sword becomes!\"","Boom!!!","A terrifying wave of soul pressure erupted outward once again.","Many nearby participants instinctively retreated farther away while some weaker geniuses even coughed blood after being affected by the horrifying soul aura emitted from the blade.","At that moment, the Soul Devouring Sword no longer felt like a simple weapon.","Instead, it resembled a monstrous ancient entity that was gradually awakening within the battlefield itself.","Ray stared directly at Max with madness and killing intent filling his eyes completely.","\"You should stop resisting already,\" Ray sneered coldly. \"No matter what you do, your death has already been decided.\"","Then his expression twisted further as he laughed viciously.","\"You might as well give up and die!\""]},{"number":1664,"title":"Chapter 1664: Blocking the Soul Devouring Sword!","paragraphs":["Max could clearly feel that Ray was not lying.","The strength of the Soul Devouring Sword was truly increasing with every passing moment.","The longer the weapon remained within the Soul Sealing Painting, the more terrifying its aura became. Vast amounts of soul energy continuously flowed toward the gigantic silver blade from every direction, causing the pressure emitted by the sword to rise at an alarming speed.","At the same time, the pressure bearing down upon Max’s soul also intensified drastically.","The invisible pulling force trying to drag his soul out of his body became stronger and stronger. Max could even feel his sea of consciousness trembling violently as the horrifying soul-devouring aura invaded him relentlessly.","His instincts screamed danger continuously.","Max understood one thing with absolute certainty.","If that gigantic Soul Devouring Sword even touched him slightly—","His soul would immediately be devoured into the blade.","There would be no second chance afterward.","\"Just die already!\" Ray roared furiously as madness filled his face completely.","Boom!!!","Terrifying sword energy erupted from Ray’s body as he poured all of his strength into the Soul Devouring Sword once again. The gigantic silver blade instantly radiated blinding light before slashing downward toward Max with overwhelming destructive force.","The heavens and earth themselves seemed to shake violently.","The pressure released by the descending sword was so terrifying that cracks spread wildly across the battlefield beneath Max’s feet before the attack had even fully arrived.","Max’s expression immediately turned serious.","Without the slightest hesitation, seven colored lightning exploded violently around his body once again.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The dazzling lightning illuminated the entire battlefield as terrifying destruction energy surged outward from Max like an erupting storm.","Then Max tightly gripped the seven colored lightning sword in his hand.","At that moment, he no longer held back anything whatsoever.","The Vein of Strength erupted completely.","The Vein of Origin unleashed its full power.","The Vein of Vitality surged violently throughout his body.","At the same time, all 5000 Draconic Essences within Max awakened together.","Boom!!!","A terrifying draconic aura exploded from Max’s body as countless golden dragon patterns appeared faintly across his skin. The surrounding space trembled violently beneath the monstrous physical strength erupting from him.","Even the nearby participants widened their eyes in shock after sensing the overwhelming pressure radiating from Max.","\"This aura...\" Jonathan’s expression changed drastically.","Julie’s eyes also trembled slightly.","At that moment, Max’s physical strength had reached an absolutely horrifying level.","The muscles throughout his body bulged slightly while seven colored lightning and golden draconic energy intertwined around him like raging divine storms.","Then Max raised the seven colored lightning sword with both hands and directly faced the descending Soul Devouring Sword head-on.","He knew very clearly that retreating was meaningless.","If that sword touched him even slightly, his soul would be devoured instantly.","Because of that, Max poured every ounce of strength he possessed into this clash.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art!\"","Max roared as overwhelming sword intent erupted toward the heavens.","Then, with all of his power, Max swung the seven colored lightning sword upward toward the gigantic silver blade descending from the sky.","Boom!!!","The moment the seven colored lightning sword collided against the gigantic Soul Devouring Sword, a deafening explosion shook the entire eighth layer violently.","Terrifying shockwaves swept across the battlefield in every direction as silver soul energy and seven colored lightning intertwined fiercely in the sky. The surrounding space distorted repeatedly under the overwhelming pressure generated by the collision.","Then—","To everyone’s shock—","The gigantic Soul Devouring Sword actually stopped descending.","The enormous silver blade trembled violently in the air while Max’s seven colored lightning sword blocked it head-on from below.","For a brief moment, the two terrifying powers remained locked in stalemate.","The surrounding participants instantly widened their eyes in disbelief.","\"What?!\" someone shouted involuntarily.","Even Jonathan’s usually calm expression changed sharply.","Julie’s eyes trembled slightly as she stared at the unbelievable scene unfolding before her.","After all, everyone present had already sensed how horrifying the Soul Devouring Sword truly was. The pressure emitted by that weapon alone was enough to make countless geniuses feel despair.","Yet now—","Max had actually managed to stop it.","The dazzling seven colored lightning surrounding Max’s body exploded wildly while golden draconic energy surged continuously through his arms. Veins bulged across his muscles as he used every ounce of his terrifying physical strength to hold back the gigantic silver blade pressing down upon him.","The ground beneath Max’s feet shattered layer after layer from the overwhelming pressure.","However—","He still did not retreat even a single step.","Ray’s eyes widened completely after witnessing that scene.","Disbelief filled his face instantly.","Nobody understood the terrifying nature of the Soul Devouring Sword better than him.","This was one of the six treasured swords of the Sword God Palace.","A terrifying soul-type divine weapon capable of devouring souls directly.","Even among powerful treasures, the Soul Devouring Sword possessed an extremely terrifying reputation. Once its soul-devouring power was unleashed fully, ordinary geniuses would not even possess the courage to resist it directly.","Blocking the Soul Devouring Sword head-on should have been impossible for someone of Max’s level.","Yet Max had done exactly that.","At that moment, Ray finally realized something terrifying.","The strength Max possessed was far beyond anything he had originally imagined.","This realization caused Ray’s killing intent toward Max to rise even further.","Because the more terrifying Max appeared, the more Ray understood that he absolutely could not allow Max to continue growing.","Otherwise—","Once Max truly matured, even the Sword God Palace might no longer be capable of suppressing him.","\"You monster...\" Ray muttered unconsciously as his expression gradually twisted.","Then madness surged within his eyes once again.","\"No matter what...\" Ray growled furiously while tightening his grip on the Soul Devouring Sword even harder. \"You must die here today!\"","Boom!!!","A far more terrifying wave of soul power erupted from Ray’s body.","The silver light surrounding the Soul Devouring Sword intensified drastically as countless soul-devouring runes lit up across the gigantic blade. The horrifying pressure pressing downward instantly multiplied.","Ray had begun pouring even more of his strength into the Soul Devouring Sword.","The gigantic silver blade descended lower once again.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The seven colored lightning sword in Max’s hands trembled violently under the overwhelming pressure while the surrounding lightning exploded chaotically across the battlefield.","At the same time, the pressure assaulting Max’s soul rose to an even more terrifying level."]},{"number":1665,"title":"Chapter 1665: Dimension of Soul - Unlocked!","paragraphs":["As the pressure emitted by the Soul Devouring Sword continued rising higher and higher, even Max gradually began finding it difficult to withstand it completely.","The gigantic silver blade pressed downward relentlessly while terrifying soul-devouring energy flooded the entire battlefield like an endless storm. The invisible force trying to tear Max’s soul out of his body became increasingly overwhelming with every passing second.","Even his sea of consciousness trembled violently under that horrifying pressure.","The seven colored lightning sword within Max’s grasp shook continuously as crackling lightning exploded wildly around him. Veins bulged across his arms while the power of the Three Divine Veins surged frantically through his body. At the same time, all 5000 Draconic Essences roared violently inside him as golden draconic energy erupted endlessly outward.","Yet despite all of that power—","Max was still gradually being suppressed.","The gigantic Soul Devouring Sword descended lower inch by inch while the ground beneath Max’s feet shattered repeatedly under the overwhelming pressure.","Ray noticed this immediately.","The madness within his eyes intensified further.","\"Hahaha!\" Ray laughed arrogantly as he poured even more strength into the Soul Devouring Sword. \"That’s right! Struggle all you want! In the end, you still cannot resist the Soul Devouring Sword!\"","Boom!!!","The gigantic silver blade released another terrifying wave of soul pressure.","The surrounding participants retreated even farther away while their expressions became increasingly pale. Some weaker geniuses even felt blood leaking from the corners of their mouths after being affected by the horrifying soul aura spreading throughout the battlefield.","At that moment, Max’s expression had already become extremely serious.","He understood very clearly that continuing like this would eventually lead to his defeat.","Then suddenly—","A familiar mechanical voice echoed inside his mind.","[Congratulations Host.]","[The Dimension of Soul has successfully been unlocked.]","[You have gained authority over the Dimension of Soul.]","The instant Max saw those notifications, the seriousness within his eyes disappeared completely.","Then slowly—","A smile appeared across his face.","That smile immediately caused Ray to frown.","However, before anyone could understand what Max was planning to do—","Max suddenly withdrew all of his defenses entirely.","The seven colored lightning sword instantly dispersed into countless sparks of lightning.","The terrifying aura erupting from the Three Divine Veins gradually faded.","Even the overwhelming draconic energy released from the 5000 Draconic Essences began calming down.","Seeing this scene, the surrounding participants widened their eyes in disbelief.","Jonathan’s expression changed sharply.","Julie looked completely stunned.","Even Ray himself was momentarily caught off guard before a crazed grin spread across his face.","\"Hahaha!\" Ray burst into wild laughter. \"So you finally gave up!\"","Without Max resisting it anymore, the gigantic Soul Devouring Sword descended completely.","Boom!!!","The enormous silver blade slammed directly onto Max.","Terrifying soul-devouring energy exploded outward instantly as dazzling silver light engulfed the entire battlefield completely. The horrifying soul aura surged violently in every direction while the surrounding space distorted repeatedly from the overwhelming pressure.","At that moment, countless participants instinctively believed the battle had already ended.","After all, nobody believed someone could survive being struck directly by the Soul Devouring Sword.","However—","A few moments later—","The silver light slowly began fading away.","Then the expressions of everyone present froze completely.","Max was still standing there.","The gigantic Soul Devouring Sword was pressing directly against his shoulder with terrifying force while endless soul-devouring energy continuously surged into his body.","Yet—","Nothing happened.","Max’s soul had not been devoured.","His body had not collapsed.","In fact, Max simply stood there calmly as though the terrifying sword pressing against him possessed no threat whatsoever.","The horrifying soul energy continuously entered his body, yet it vanished completely without causing any damage, almost like rivers flowing into an endless abyss.","Silence instantly descended across the battlefield.","Every participant stared blankly at Max with expressions filled with disbelief and confusion. Their minds could no longer comprehend the scene unfolding before them.","Jonathan’s pupils contracted violently.","Julie’s lips parted slightly in shock.","Even the nearby geniuses who had been retreating earlier now stood frozen in place.","Nobody could understand what they were seeing.","The Soul Devouring Sword was one of the six treasured swords of the Sword God Palace.","It was a terrifying weapon specifically designed to devour souls.","Yet now—","Its soul-devouring power had completely failed against Max.","Ray’s laughter disappeared instantly.","The crazed smile on his face froze completely while disbelief slowly spread across his expression.","His eyes widened more and more as he stared at Max like he had just witnessed something impossible.","\"That...\" Ray muttered unconsciously as his grip around the Soul Devouring Sword trembled faintly. \"How is this possible?\"","\"Since you brought such a good weapon here...\" Max said calmly while looking at the gigantic Soul Devouring Sword pressing against his shoulder. \"Then let me have it.\"","The moment those words fell, Max slowly raised his right hand and touched the enormous silver blade directly.","Then—","The gigantic Soul Devouring Sword suddenly disappeared.","It vanished so abruptly that everyone present froze completely.","The terrifying soul-devouring pressure flooding the battlefield disappeared instantly along with it. The overwhelming silver light faded rapidly while the horrifying aura that had made countless geniuses tremble moments ago vanished without leaving behind even the slightest trace.","Silence descended across the eighth layer once again.","Ray’s eyes widened so much that they almost seemed ready to burst out of their sockets.","\"What?!\" Ray shouted in disbelief.","His face twisted completely as panic and shock exploded within his eyes.","The Soul Devouring Sword was one of the six treasured swords of the Sword God Palace. It was an incomparably precious soul weapon personally entrusted to him for this mission.","Yet now—","It had simply disappeared.","\"What did you do to the Soul Devouring Sword?!\" Ray roared furiously while staring at Max like a madman.","Max merely smiled faintly.","\"It belongs to me now,\" Max replied calmly.","The moment his voice fell, seven colored lightning erupted violently around his body once again.","Crackling divine lightning exploded across the battlefield while a dazzling seven colored lightning sword condensed instantly within Max’s grasp.","The surrounding participants immediately felt their hearts tremble.","Because the moment Max summoned the lightning sword again, the aura around him changed completely.","The relaxed expression from earlier disappeared entirely.","What replaced it instead was cold killing intent.","Then Max slowly raised the seven colored lightning sword toward Ray.","\"Now...\" Max said softly while looking directly into Ray’s terrified eyes. \"It’s your turn to die.\""]},{"number":1666,"title":"Chapter 1666: A new Sword for Max!","paragraphs":["The instant those words entered Ray’s ears, fear exploded inside his heart for the very first time.","\"No!\" Ray shouted frantically.","Boom!!!","Terrifying sharpness erupted from his body once again as he desperately tried to mobilize the power of his Pseudo Cosmic Path. Scarlet spear energy exploded wildly around him while he attempted to launch another attack.","However—","He was too late.","Before Ray could even fully gather his strength, Max’s figure suddenly disappeared from where he originally stood.","Ray’s pupils contracted violently.","Then, in the next instant—","Max appeared directly beside him.","So fast that Ray could not even react properly.","The seven colored lightning surrounding Max’s body illuminated the battlefield brilliantly while terrifying sword intent surged into the heavens.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art,\" Max muttered softly.","At the same time, traces of the half-formed Emotion Severing Cosmic Path fused directly into the sword strike.","The atmosphere around the blade changed instantly.","A terrifying severing aura erupted from the seven colored lightning sword while emotionless sword intent spread outward like an unstoppable tide. It felt as though the sword strike itself had become capable of severing everything in existence.","Ray’s eyes widened completely.","Before he could even defend himself—","Slash!!!","A dazzling sword light flashed across the battlefield.","For a brief moment, everything became silent.","Then Ray’s body froze completely.","The scarlet spear energy surrounding him dispersed instantly while the expression on his face stiffened forever in disbelief and terror.","A thin bloody line slowly appeared across the center of his body.","Then—","His body split apart completely.","Blood exploded into the air as Ray was sliced cleanly into two halves by Max’s sword strike.","The surrounding participants immediately felt chills spread throughout their entire bodies after witnessing that horrifying scene.","Ray Willer—","One of the greatest geniuses present within the Soul Sealing Painting—","Had been killed instantly.","At the same time, countless fragments of light erupted from Ray’s severed body as the rules of the Soul Sealing Painting activated.","Because his soul had not truly been destroyed, Ray’s consciousness was immediately expelled from the Soul Sealing Painting itself.","In the next instant, Ray’s shattered figure disappeared completely from the battlefield.","He had been eliminated.","Max had intentionally chosen not to kill Ray using the Soul Devouring Sword that now rested within his Dimension of Soul.","Although he now possessed complete control over that terrifying weapon, Max understood very clearly what the consequences would be if he truly used it to devour Ray’s soul in front of so many witnesses.","The Soul Devouring Sword was one of the six treasured swords of the Sword God Palace. If Ray’s soul had truly been destroyed here, the force behind him would undoubtedly investigate the matter thoroughly afterward.","At that point, the situation would become troublesome even for Max and for the Black Dragon Clan.","Because of that, Max deliberately chose a different method.","He merely eliminated Ray from the Soul Sealing Painting instead of truly killing him.","However—","That did not mean Max intended to let Ray continue living peacefully afterward.","The moment Max learned that Ray had already joined hands with the Sword God Palace to target him, Max had silently decided Ray’s fate long ago.","Someone who carried such intense killing intent toward him while also possessing terrifying talent and background was not someone Max could afford to leave alive indefinitely.","Especially not after today’s battle.","After this confrontation, Ray’s hatred toward him would only deepen further.","Max naturally understood this clearly.","Which meant there was only one possible outcome waiting for Ray in the future.","Death.","A faintly wicked smile slowly appeared across Max’s face as countless thoughts flashed through his mind silently.","\"I could not kill you in front of so many people today,\" Max thought inwardly while looking at the place where Ray had disappeared moments ago. \"But once we leave the Soul Sealing Painting...\"","The smile on Max’s face deepened slightly.","\"You had better hide well.\"","Max slowly raised his hand.","Then, in the next instant, the Soul Devouring Sword appeared within his grasp once again.","The pure white blade radiated faint silver light while strange soul fluctuations continuously spread from the sword itself. Even after Ray’s elimination, the weapon still emitted an unsettling aura capable of making ordinary geniuses feel instinctive fear deep within their souls.","Max casually waved the sword through the air several times while carefully sensing the terrifying power hidden within it.","Then a faint smile appeared across his face.","\"This really is a good sword,\" Max muttered softly.","The moment he placed the Soul Devouring Sword inside the Dimension of Soul earlier, everything had changed completely.","Within the Dimension of Soul, Max possessed absolute authority over soul-related powers and objects. Because of that overwhelming authority, the ownership connection between Ray and the Soul Devouring Sword had been forcefully severed.","Now, the sword belonged entirely to Max.","Naturally, such a thing should have been impossible under normal circumstances.","The Sword God Palace had long ago engraved an extremely powerful ownership rune upon the Soul Devouring Sword. That rune existed specifically to prevent others from stealing or using the weapon freely.","As long as the rune remained intact, nobody besides Ray should have been capable of controlling the Soul Devouring Sword.","Even if someone managed to snatch the sword away physically, the weapon would still recognize only Ray as its true owner.","However—","For Max, such restrictions no longer mattered.","Inside the Dimension of Soul, the authority he possessed over soul-related laws and connections was simply too overwhelming. The ownership rune left behind by the Sword God Palace had been completely suppressed and erased the moment the sword entered that dimension.","Max slowly examined the silver-white blade once more as thoughtful light flickered through his eyes.","\"The Sword God Palace really seems to possess quite an impressive collection of swords,\" Max muttered with a faint smile.","The first example was naturally the Dragonheart Sword.","Although the sword had once belonged to the legendary Sword Sovereign, the Sword God Palace’s obsession with retrieving it from him had always felt somewhat unusual to Max.","The lengths they were willing to go merely to reclaim that weapon were simply too excessive.","Because of that, Max had gradually developed a suspicion deep within his heart.","Perhaps—","Even the Dragonheart Sword originally belonged to the Sword God Palace as well."]},{"number":1667,"title":"Chapter 1667: Top Rank!","paragraphs":["After putting away the Soul Devouring Sword, Max slowly lifted his gaze and looked toward the remaining participants gathered around the platform.","At that moment, the entire battlefield had already fallen into complete silence.","Nobody spoke.","Nobody moved recklessly.","The scene of Ray’s defeat still lingered vividly within everyone’s minds. From the moment Ray revealed the terrifying power of the Pseudo Cosmic Path until he unleashed the horrifying Soul Devouring Sword, everyone had believed Max would eventually be forced into despair.","Yet in the end—","Ray had still been defeated completely.","Not only had Max survived the Soul Devouring Sword, he had even taken the weapon away directly before eliminating Ray afterward.","That result had shaken everyone deeply.","Especially after witnessing the terrifying physical strength, monstrous regeneration, overwhelming swordsmanship, and incomprehensible soul abilities Max possessed, the remaining participants no longer viewed him as someone within the same level as themselves.","Many of them now looked at Max with genuine fear hidden within their eyes.","Max naturally noticed all of this clearly.","Then, while holding the seven colored lightning sword casually in his hand, he spoke calmly.","\"If you do not want to be eliminated,\" Max said while glancing across the platform slowly, \"then you should leave now.\"","Although his voice was calm, nobody dared ignore those words.","The surrounding participants immediately exchanged uneasy looks with one another.","Nobody stepped forward.","Nobody challenged him.","After all, even Ray Willer, who possessed traces of a Pseudo Cosmic Path and had even used the terrifying Soul Devouring Sword, had still ended up defeated by Max.","If even someone like Ray could not contend against him, then what qualifications did the rest of them possess to fight Max directly?","That thought alone caused many people to lose the courage to remain on the platform.","Very quickly, figures began retreating one after another.","Some left silently.","Others looked toward Max with complicated expressions before turning around and departing from the platform entirely.","Nobody wished to gamble their survival against a monster like him.","Meanwhile, Jonathan remained standing where he was for a few moments longer.","His eyes stayed fixed upon Max while countless thoughts flashed through his mind silently.","Then eventually, a faint smile appeared on Jonathan’s face.","\"You truly are terrifying,\" Jonathan admitted honestly.","There was no hostility in his voice.","Only seriousness.","Then Jonathan slowly turned around before speaking one final sentence.","\"I will see you again later, Max.\"","The moment those words fell, Jonathan’s figure disappeared from the platform.","Julie glanced toward Max once more after Jonathan left.","Her beautiful eyes still carried traces of shock from everything she had witnessed today.","However, she said nothing.","A moment later, Julie also departed alongside Jonathan, leaving the platform completely.","Soon afterward, the once crowded battlefield became almost entirely empty.","\"Nice,\" Max muttered softly while looking toward the cave behind the platform. \"Let’s record all the treasures here before moving forward.\"","After finishing his battle against Ray, Max no longer wasted any time.","He directly entered the cave hidden behind the platform while faint seven colored lightning still flickered around his body. The interior of the cave was filled with numerous treasures radiating powerful fluctuations. Some emitted dense soul aura while others contained astonishing elemental energy.","Max calmly walked toward the center of the cave before placing his name onto the treasure record formation left behind by the Soul Sealing Painting.","The moment his spiritual aura entered the formation, the ownership record for all treasures within the cave instantly changed to his name.","After finishing everything there, Max immediately left the platform and headed toward the remaining areas of the eighth layer.","From that moment onward, almost nobody dared challenge him anymore.","Every participant who saw Max approaching instinctively chose to retreat voluntarily. Some people even abandoned platforms immediately after sensing his aura from afar.","The battle against Ray had already completely established Max’s dominance throughout the tower.","As a result, Max moved through the eighth layer almost unhindered.","Platform after platform.","Cave after cave.","Max continuously recorded every treasure he encountered beneath his name before quickly proceeding deeper into the tower.","Eventually, he arrived at the ninth layer.","The pressure within the ninth layer was far more terrifying than before. The soul suppression filling the surrounding environment had already reached an astonishing level, causing even ordinary peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses to struggle merely standing there.","However, Max remained completely unaffected.","With the support of the Dimension of Soul and his overwhelming physical strength, the terrifying suppression inside the ninth layer no longer posed much threat to him.","Because of that, Max once again began recording treasures rapidly.","However, despite possessing enough strength to monopolize everything within the tower, Max did not take every single platform for himself.","He deliberately left several valuable platforms untouched.","Some were left for Jonathan.","Some were left for Julie.","Others were left for the remaining capable geniuses still climbing the tower.","Max naturally understood that completely monopolizing every opportunity would only create unnecessary hostility from everyone present.","More importantly, he simply did not need everything.","After recording the final treasure at the peak of the ninth layer, Max slowly raised his head and looked toward the vast surroundings beneath him.","Then, after confirming there was nothing else worth staying for, Max finally turned around and left the tower completely.","At the same time, outside the tower, the enormous ranking screen floating above the battlefield suddenly flickered brightly.","The moment Ray Willer had been eliminated earlier, half of his accumulated killing points had automatically transferred directly to Max according to the rules of the Soul Sealing Painting.","Because of that—","Max’s ranking instantly soared to the very top.","Soon, the updated ranking list appeared clearly before everyone.","Max Morgan — 18,940 KP","Jonathan Myres — 13,220 KP","Julie Ravencrest — 12,870 KP","Marcus Vale — 10,430 KP","Serena Ashbourne — 9,980 KP","Darius Holt — 9,110 KP","Ethan Blackwell — 8,760 KP","Alicia Moonfall — 8,340 KP","Leon Draven — 7,950 KP","Victor Kane — 7,510 Kp","The moment the ranking list updated, countless participants inside and outside the Soul Sealing Painting immediately erupted into uproar.","Because Max Morgan’s name now stood firmly at the very top."]},{"number":1668,"title":"Chapter 1668: End of the Third Trial!","paragraphs":["Soon, Max arrived at a vast open area where several other participants had already gathered.","The moment he appeared, many people instinctively turned toward him.","However, compared to the beginning of the trial, the atmosphere now felt completely different.","Earlier, when the Soul Sealing Painting first opened, hundreds of geniuses had entered this world together. Everywhere one looked, powerful participants could be seen fighting for treasures, hunting monsters, and competing against one another.","But now—","The number of remaining participants had dropped drastically.","The once crowded trial world had become strangely quiet.","Max calmly swept his gaze across the surroundings while his Dimensional Sovereign Body spread outward silently.","In the next instant, he accurately perceived the number of people still remaining alive inside the Soul Sealing Painting.","\"There are only around twenty participants left here,\" Max muttered softly.","A thoughtful expression appeared across his face afterward.","\"I suppose this trial is about to end.\"","Max still clearly remembered the rules Elder Cael had announced before the trial began. The Soul Sealing Painting would officially close once the total number of remaining participants dropped below fifty.","At the moment, there were only around twenty people gathered here.","As for the others, Max knew several participants were still inside the Tower of Treasure searching for opportunities.","However, even after counting those individuals, the total number remaining inside the Soul Sealing Painting should no longer exceed fifty by much.","Because of that, Max understood very clearly that it was probably only a matter of minutes before the trial officially concluded.","Then suddenly, another thought surfaced within his mind.","\"That reminds me...\" Max muttered while narrowing his eyes slightly in thought.","\"There is only one internal trial ground called the Tower of Treasure inside this Soul Sealing Painting.\"","The more Max thought about it, the more certain he became.","If even this preparatory trial possessed a special inheritance zone like the Tower of Treasure, then the real Cosmic Ascension Conference would undoubtedly be far more grand and terrifying.","After all, the Cosmic Ascension Conference was held within the Eternal Hourglass itself.","That place gathered geniuses from countless worlds, star domains, and major forces.","The number of participants entering the Cosmic Ascension Conference would likely reach an absolutely terrifying level.","Possibly even trillions.","Because of that, it would naturally be impossible for everyone to compete inside only one area.","Which meant—","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, there should be hundreds or perhaps even thousands of similar internal trial grounds scattered throughout the conference world.","The moment he realized this, excitement gradually appeared within Max’s eyes.","If every one of those internal trials contained treasures and opportunities comparable to the Tower of Treasure, then the Cosmic Ascension Conference would truly become a heaven-defying land of fortune.","\"With the treasures I gathered from the Tower of Treasure...\" Max muttered softly while a faint smile slowly appeared across his face, \"I should be able to break through to the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm.\"","At the same time, another thought surfaced in his mind.","\"And after that, I should finally be able to open the fourth Divine Vein of the Seven Divine Veins...\"","\"The Vein of Speed.\"","Just thinking about it caused anticipation to rise within Max’s heart.","The Vein of Strength had already granted him terrifying physical might.","The Vein of Origin had strengthened his foundations tremendously.","The Vein of Vitality had given him astonishing regenerative power.","Because of that, Max naturally understood how terrifying the Vein of Speed would likely become once it awakened completely.","And that was not his only gain from this trial.","Max’s smile deepened slightly.","\"I also obtained an extremely powerful sword art that I still have not fully mastered yet,\" he murmured thoughtfully.","The Saint Origin Sword Art still possessed enormous untapped potential.","Especially after combining it with traces of the half-formed Emotion Severing Cosmic Path, Max could already vaguely sense how terrifying that sword art might eventually become in the future.","On top of that, this battle had also allowed him to personally witness the power of a Pseudo Cosmic Path.","That experience alone was incredibly valuable.","After all, directly experiencing such power firsthand was far more beneficial than merely hearing stories about it from others.","Eventually, Max let out a faint chuckle.","\"I suppose this trip to the Violet Star Palace was truly worth it.\"","Just as Max was quietly thinking about everything he had gained from this trial, a familiar mechanical voice suddenly echoed throughout the entire Soul Sealing Painting.","At the same time, countless glowing notifications appeared before every remaining participant.","[Total remaining participants have been reduced to fifty.]","[Conditions for completion of the third trial have been fulfilled.]","[The third trial of the Soul Sealing Painting has officially concluded.]","The moment those notifications appeared, the expressions of the surrounding participants changed immediately.","Then, before anyone could react further, the surrounding world suddenly began trembling faintly.","A mysterious spatial force descended upon the entire Soul Sealing Painting.","Max instantly felt the connection between his soul and this world gradually weakening.","At the same time, nearby participants began disappearing one after another.","Some vanished while still standing silently in place.","Others revealed relieved expressions before their bodies gradually dissolved into particles of light.","The entire area became increasingly empty within only a few moments.","The remaining geniuses also vanished rapidly under the power of the Soul Sealing Painting.","Clearly, everyone was now being forcefully returned to their original bodies outside.","Max calmly observed everything around him while faint spatial ripples gradually surrounded his own body as well.","The surrounding scenery began turning blurry little by little.","Even the enormous sky above the Soul Sealing Painting gradually distorted as though the entire world itself was fading away.","Then another notification appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Calculating final rankings...]","[Calculating rewards...]","[Preparing participant transfer...]","A faint smile appeared across Max’s face after seeing those notifications.","This trial had brought him enormous gains.","Not only had he obtained treasures capable of helping him reach the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm, he had also unlocked the Dimension of Soul, obtained the Soul Devouring Sword, witnessed a Pseudo Cosmic Path firsthand, and further strengthened his understanding of the Saint Origin Sword Art.","Compared to those rewards, even his first-place ranking felt secondary.","Soon afterward, the spatial force surrounding Max intensified completely.","Countless particles of light emerged around his body as his figure gradually began fading away from the Soul Sealing Painting.","Then—","Max disappeared completely."]},{"number":1669,"title":"Chapter 1669: End of Smelting Trial!","paragraphs":["Appearing outside the Soul Sealing Painting once again, Max immediately felt a brief sense of discomfort spread throughout his body.","It felt as though his soul and physical body had momentarily fallen out of synchronization after remaining separated for such a long period of time inside the Soul Sealing Painting world.","However, that strange sensation disappeared almost instantly.","Max quickly regained full control over his body as his consciousness stabilized completely.","At the same time, countless other participants also began opening their eyes one after another throughout the massive square of the Violet Star Palace.","Some people revealed exhausted expressions.","Others still appeared shaken from the brutal battles inside the Soul Sealing Painting.","A few participants even looked relieved merely to have survived until the end.","Meanwhile, high above the square, the enormous Soul Sealing Painting floating in the sky gradually dimmed before slowly returning to its previous calm state.","Then Elder Cael stepped forward once again.","The old man swept his gaze across the countless gathered disciples and elders before speaking with a calm yet authoritative voice that echoed throughout the entire square.","\"The third trial has officially concluded.\"","The moment those words fell, the entire crowd immediately became noisy once again.","After all, the third trial had undoubtedly been the most brutal and intense trial so far. Countless geniuses had been eliminated throughout the process, while the battles that occurred inside the Tower of Treasure had shaken nearly everyone watching from outside.","Especially the confrontation between Max and Ray Willer.","That battle alone had already become the center of discussion among countless disciples and elders present.","At that moment, Elder Cael slowly raised his hand.","The noisy crowd gradually quieted down afterward.","Then Elder Cael continued speaking.","\"Next...\" he said calmly, \"look toward the ranking screen.\"","The moment his voice fell, the enormous screen floating above the square suddenly flickered brightly.","Soon afterward, a massive ranking list appeared before everyone’s eyes.","The moment the rankings became visible, countless gazes instantly focused upon the very top.","Then—","The expressions of numerous elders changed immediately.","Max Morgan — 18,940 Points","Jonathan Myres — 13,220 Points","Julie Ravencrest — 12,870 Points","Marcus Vale — 10,430 Points","Serena Ashbourne — 9,980 Points","Darius Holt — 9,110 Points","Ethan Blackwell — 8,760 Points","Alicia Moonfall — 8,340 Points","Leon Draven — 7,950 Points","Victor Kane — 7,510 Points","Silence spread briefly across the square.","Then the entire place erupted into uproar.","\"What?!\"","\"Max Morgan again?!\"","\"He actually took first place in the third trial too?!\"","Many disciples revealed expressions filled with disbelief while numerous elders stared at the rankings with shocked expressions.","This was already the third trial.","And yet—","Max had once again stood at the very top.","Earlier, many people had still believed his first-place performance in the previous two trials might have been due to luck, hidden opportunities, or favorable circumstances.","But now, after the third trial ended with Max taking first place yet again, those doubts gradually began disappearing.","Because this result could no longer be explained away so easily.","The third trial was the harshest and most dangerous trial among all three.","It tested survival ability, combat strength, adaptability, comprehension, and even one’s courage in fighting against other geniuses.","Yet despite all of that—","Max still dominated the rankings completely.","Many elders exchanged serious glances with one another afterward.","Even some hidden experts observing from afar revealed thoughtful expressions.","Meanwhile, within the crowd, the expressions of the Violet Star Palace disciples became increasingly complicated.","Because everyone now understood one terrifying truth.","A true monster had appeared in this Smelting Trial.","After the uproar caused by the ranking list gradually settled down, Elder Cael once again stepped forward slowly.","The old man stood high above the square while his calm gaze swept across the countless gathered geniuses from the various third-rate forces. For a brief moment, his eyes lingered upon several outstanding participants, especially Max, Jonathan, and Julie, before he finally began speaking once more.","\"Now that the results of the third trial have been announced,\" Elder Cael said calmly, his voice echoing clearly throughout the entire square, \"the Smelting Trial has officially come to an end.\"","The moment those words fell, many disciples revealed complicated expressions.","Some looked excited after gaining tremendous opportunities during the trials.","Others appeared disappointed because they failed to obtain satisfactory results.","However, regardless of their emotions, everyone understood one thing clearly.","This Smelting Trial had been extraordinarily important for all of them.","Not only had it provided them with valuable treasures and opportunities, it had also allowed them to personally witness the terrifying strength possessed by the geniuses of other forces.","Especially after seeing monsters like Max and Ray Willer, many participants finally realized just how vast the outside world truly was.","Meanwhile, Elder Cael continued speaking.","\"The true purpose of this Smelting Trial was never merely competition,\" he said slowly. \"It was created to prepare all of you for the coming Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment the words \"Cosmic Ascension Conference\" were mentioned, the expressions of countless geniuses immediately became serious.","Even the surrounding elders revealed solemn looks.","After all, compared to the Smelting Trial, the Cosmic Ascension Conference was the true grand stage of the younger generation.","That was where geniuses from countless worlds and powerful forces would gather together.","Compared to those monstrous talents, the participants present here were still only geniuses among third-rate forces.","\"There are only three months remaining before the Cosmic Ascension Conference officially begins,\" Elder Cael continued calmly. \"I hope all of you will use this remaining time wisely.\"","His gaze gradually sharpened slightly afterward.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference is filled with countless dangers, opportunities, and monstrous geniuses beyond your imagination. Whether you rise or fall there will ultimately depend upon your own abilities.\"","Then, for the first time since the trials began, a faint smile appeared on Elder Cael’s aged face.","\"Still,\" he said slowly, \"I sincerely wish all of you the very best.\"","\"I hope that among the geniuses gathered here today, some of you will one day shine brilliantly throughout the Divine Realm itself.\"","The surrounding disciples immediately became excited after hearing those words.","Even some elders nodded lightly in agreement.","Soon afterward, Elder Cael lightly waved his hand before speaking once more.","\"Finally...\" he said, \"before everyone departs from the Violet Star Palace, a small banquet will be held tomorrow evening.\"","The atmosphere within the square instantly relaxed slightly afterward.","\"A banquet?\" many disciples muttered excitedly.","Elder Cael smiled faintly.","\"You have all worked hard throughout these trials,\" he continued. \"Take this opportunity to relax, exchange experiences, and enjoy yourselves before this gathering officially comes to an end.\"","The surrounding disciples immediately became much more lively after hearing that announcement.","Some people began discussing the banquet excitedly with their companions.","Others discussed the results of the Smelting Trial once again.","Meanwhile, many gazes still continued drifting toward Max from time to time.","After all, regardless of the banquet or the end of the trials, everyone understood one thing clearly.","The greatest topic of this entire Smelting Trial—","Was undoubtedly Max Morgan."]},{"number":1670,"title":"Chapter 1670: Jonathan’s Plea for Help!","paragraphs":["With Elder Cael’s final announcement, the tense atmosphere lingering throughout the square gradually began fading away.","The Smelting Trial had finally ended.","Soon afterward, the countless gathered disciples and elders slowly began dispersing in different directions. Various third-rate forces regrouped together while discussions about the trials echoed endlessly throughout the Violet Star Palace.","Some disciples excitedly discussed the treasures they obtained.","Others spoke about the brutal battles inside the Soul Sealing Painting.","However, the topic mentioned most frequently by nearly everyone remained the same.","Max Morgan.","Many elders looked toward him with complicated expressions while younger geniuses either admired him, feared him, or envied him deeply.","Meanwhile, Max calmly walked through the dispersing crowd before eventually arriving beside Isabella and Lucia.","The moment Isabella saw him approaching safely, the tension within her expression visibly relaxed.","\"You are finally back,\" Isabella said softly while looking at him carefully. \"Do you know how terrifying your battle with Ray looked from outside?\"","Even now, traces of lingering shock could still be seen within her beautiful eyes.","Lucia immediately nodded in agreement afterward. Even though they weren’t present at the platform where the battle between Ray and Max took place, they weren’t far from it. They could see and heard the battle from the nearby platforms at the 8th layer.","\"That Soul Devouring Sword was horrifying,\" Lucia admitted honestly. \"For a moment, even I thought something might happen to you.\"","Max simply smiled faintly after hearing their words.","\"Unfortunately for Ray,\" Max replied calmly, \"things did not go according to his plans.\"","Lucia immediately rolled her eyes slightly.","\"You say that so casually,\" she muttered. \"But you nearly scared everyone half to death.\"","Even Isabella revealed a helpless smile afterward.","Clearly, despite Max acting calm now, the battle earlier had genuinely shocked many people.","Then suddenly—","\"Max.\"","A calm voice sounded from nearby.","The three of them immediately turned toward the source of the voice.","Jonathan slowly walked toward them.","His expression remained calm as usual, but his eyes carried obvious seriousness while looking at Max.","The surrounding disciples instinctively became quieter after noticing Jonathan approaching.","After all, Jonathan was still one of the most famous geniuses present within the Smelting Trial.","And after the third trial rankings, everyone clearly understood that Jonathan and Max were now considered two of the strongest younger generation geniuses among the gathered third-rate forces.","Jonathan eventually stopped several steps away from Max.","Then he spoke directly.","\"I would like to speak with you privately for a moment,\" Jonathan said calmly.","Lucia immediately narrowed her eyes slightly while Isabella became somewhat thoughtful.","However, Max himself did not appear surprised.","\"What is it about?\" Max asked calmly.","Jonathan remained silent briefly before replying.","\"It concerns the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","Hearing those words immediately caused Max’s interest to rise slightly.","Jonathan then continued.","\"Julie is also involved in this discussion.\"","At the mention of Julie’s name, Max became even more thoughtful.","Clearly, this was not some casual conversation.","After a few moments of silence, Max finally nodded lightly.","\"Alright,\" Max agreed calmly. \"Where do you want to meet?\"","A faint smile appeared on Jonathan’s face afterward.","\"There is a quiet pavilion near the eastern side of the Violet Star Palace,\" Jonathan replied. \"Julie is already waiting there.\"","Then Jonathan looked directly into Max’s eyes.","\"There are some things we believe you should know before the Cosmic Ascension Conference begins.\"","Max stared at Jonathan briefly before eventually smiling faintly.","\"Interesting,\" he muttered softly.","Then he nodded once more.","\"Lead the way.\"","Following Jonathan through the quiet pathways of the Violet Star Palace, Max soon arrived at a secluded area far away from the noisy gathering square.","The surroundings here were much calmer.","Beautiful spirit trees swayed gently beneath the evening breeze while faint spiritual mist drifted across the pathways. Small streams of clear water flowed peacefully nearby, creating a tranquil atmosphere completely different from the tense environment of the Smelting Trial earlier.","At the center of the area stood an elegant pavilion built beside a calm spirit lake.","Julie was already waiting there.","She sat quietly near the edge of the pavilion while staring toward the surface of the lake thoughtfully. The faint moonlight reflecting across the water illuminated her expression softly, yet despite the peaceful surroundings, the atmosphere around her felt strangely heavy.","The moment Max and Jonathan stepped into the pavilion, Julie slowly raised her gaze toward them.","However—","The instant Max entered the pavilion, his eyes narrowed slightly.","Because he immediately sensed something wrong.","The atmosphere here was far too tense.","Neither Jonathan nor Julie appeared relaxed in the slightest. Their expressions carried obvious seriousness, and even the spiritual energy fluctuations around them felt faintly unstable.","This was not the atmosphere of people casually discussing the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body silently spread outward for a brief moment before retracting once again.","Then his expression became calm.","At that moment, Max already understood something clearly.","Jonathan had not called him here merely to discuss matters related to the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","There was something else.","And whatever it was, it seemed important enough for both Jonathan and Julie to personally wait for him here.","Because of that, Max no longer wasted time.","He directly walked into the pavilion before stopping in front of the two of them calmly.","Then he spoke immediately.","\"You did not call me here to talk about the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment those words fell, Jonathan and Julie’s expressions changed slightly.","Max’s eyes calmly swept across both of them before he continued speaking.","\"So stop wasting time.\"","His voice remained completely calm.","\"What is it that you actually want?\"","Jonathan remained silent for several moments after hearing Max’s question. Clearly, whatever he wanted to say next was not easy for him to bring up. Even Julie’s expression became visibly heavier as she quietly lowered her gaze for a brief moment.","Eventually, Jonathan took a deep breath before finally speaking.","\"We need your help.\"","The seriousness in his voice immediately caused Max to frown slightly. After everything that happened during the Smelting Trial, Max knew very clearly that people like Jonathan would not casually seek help from others unless the situation was genuinely important.","\"What kind of help?\" Max asked calmly."]},{"number":1671,"title":"Chapter 1671: Ten Thousand Poison Body!","paragraphs":["Jonathan exchanged a glance with Julie first before speaking again.","\"Have you ever heard of a physique called the Ten Thousand Poison Body?\"","The moment those words entered his ears, Max’s expression changed slightly. Naturally, he had heard of it before.","Back when he was still within the Black Dragon Clan, Max had spent enormous amounts of time reading through ancient records and books related to physiques, bloodlines, cultivation constitutions, and forbidden powers.","Because of that, he possessed at least some understanding regarding the Ten Thousand Poison Body.","\"I have heard of it. It is considered one of the most terrifying cursed physiques recorded in the ancient eras. If I remember correctly, the Ten Thousand Poison Body is not a physique people are born with naturally through ordinary bloodline inheritance. Instead, it is something far stranger and far more dangerous.\"","Max continued.","\"It is said that individuals possessing the Ten Thousand Poison Body are cursed by fate itself. The exact origins of the physique remain unclear because even the oldest surviving records regarding it are incomplete. However, one thing has always remained consistent throughout every historical account. The Ten Thousand Poison Body is extremely deadly.\"","As Max spoke those words, even the atmosphere inside the pavilion gradually became heavier.","\"The body of someone possessing this physique naturally generates terrifying poison energy from birth. That poison is not ordinary toxin. It is a highly evolved poisonous force capable of corroding flesh, spiritual energy, bloodlines, organs, and eventually even the soul itself. The truly horrifying aspect of the Ten Thousand Poison Body is that the poison does not merely affect outsiders. It affects the owner as well.\"","Jonathan’s expression darkened noticeably while Julie’s fingers unconsciously tightened slightly.","\"From the moment someone with the Ten Thousand Poison Body is born, their body continuously produces stronger and stronger poison energy over time. At first, the symptoms may remain manageable. However, as the years pass, the poison gradually begins consuming the user from within. Their internal organs weaken first, then their blood, then their meridians, and eventually even their spiritual energy itself becomes poisonous.\"","Max’s expression gradually became more solemn as he continued.","\"In the later stages, even remaining close to someone possessing a fully awakened Ten Thousand Poison Body can become dangerous because their mere presence can spread poison unconsciously into the surrounding environment. Plants wither around them. Spirit beasts die near them. Even powerful cultivators can gradually become infected after prolonged exposure.\"","The silence inside the pavilion grew increasingly heavy.","\"The cruelest part is that the stronger the owner becomes, the stronger the poison becomes as well. That is why the Ten Thousand Poison Body is considered a cursed physique instead of a heaven-defying physique despite its terrifying potential. Although the physique grants overwhelming poisonous power capable of making even powerful cultivators fear them, the owner themselves is also slowly dying the entire time.\"","Max slowly narrowed his eyes afterward.","\"In most historical records, people possessing the Ten Thousand Poison Body rarely live long lives. Many die young. Others lose their sanity from the constant pain and poison corrosion. In some cases, the poison eventually completely loses control and devours both the owner and everyone around them.\"","The moment Max finished speaking, his gaze slowly shifted toward Julie.","The tension on her face already told him more than enough.","Her expression was unusually strained while a faint sense of exhaustion could be seen hidden deep within her eyes. Even the spiritual aura around her felt slightly unstable now that Max paid closer attention to it.","At that moment, Max immediately understood the situation.","\"Is she...?\" Max asked quietly while looking toward Jonathan.","Jonathan slowly nodded.","\"Yes,\" he replied heavily. \"Julie possesses the Ten Thousand Poison Body.\"","The atmosphere inside the pavilion instantly became even heavier.","\"Right now, we are only able to suppress the poison temporarily using several special treasures,\" Jonathan continued. \"Those treasures prevent the poison from leaking out of her body and affecting the surroundings, but this is only a temporary solution.\"","Jonathan’s fists tightened slightly afterward.","\"The poison inside her body is still growing stronger with time. It is already slowly destroying her from within. Unless we completely remove the poison one day, she will eventually die.\"","Julie remained silent throughout the entire conversation, but the slight lowering of her gaze already revealed enough.","Jonathan let out a slow breath before continuing again.","\"There is only one treasure known to possess the ability to completely erase the poison inside someone with the Ten Thousand Poison Body.\"","\"The Poison Erosion Fruit.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Jonathan’s expression became increasingly solemn afterward.","\"However, the Poison Erosion Fruit is unbelievably rare. Some ancient records even claim it has already gone extinct entirely. Finding one is nearly impossible.\"","Then Jonathan looked directly at Max.","\"But according to my sources, the Poison Erosion Fruit still exists.\"","A faint hope appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"And the only force currently known to possibly possess it...\"","Jonathan paused briefly before finishing his sentence.","\"Is the War God Palace.\"","Then he continued quietly.","\"I heard that you have some connection with the War God Palace.\"","\"That is why we need your help.\"","Max fell silent after hearing Jonathan’s explanation.","The pavilion became unusually quiet afterward.","His gaze slowly shifted toward Julie once again while countless thoughts flashed through his mind silently. Now that he knew about the Ten Thousand Poison Body, many things about her suddenly began making sense to him.","The faint instability within her aura.","The unusual tension she constantly carried.","Even the subtle traces of suppression treasures hidden around her body.","Everything finally connected together.","Meanwhile, Julie remained silent beneath Max’s gaze, though the pressure surrounding the conversation had clearly become heavier for her.","Several moments passed before Max finally looked back toward Jonathan.","Then he spoke calmly.","\"I can help her.\"","The moment those words fell, both Jonathan and Julie’s expressions changed immediately.","However, before either of them could speak, Max continued.","\"But I have two conditions.\"","His voice remained calm, yet serious.","\"And both of those conditions must be agreed to first.\"","Jonathan immediately stepped forward slightly without even hesitating.","\"What are the conditions?\" he asked hurriedly.","At that moment, Jonathan no longer cared about anything else.","As long as there was even a possibility of curing Julie’s Ten Thousand Poison Body, he was willing to accept almost any price."]},{"number":1672,"title":"Chapter 1672: Two Conditions!","paragraphs":["Max looked directly at Jonathan before speaking calmly.","\"My first condition is simple,\" he said. \"I want a chance to kill Ray Willer.\"","The atmosphere inside the pavilion instantly became heavier.","\"I do not care how you arrange it,\" Max continued while his eyes gradually turned colder. \"But I want an opportunity to deal with him personally.\"","Jonathan’s expression immediately became solemn after hearing those words.","Naturally, he understood why Max wanted Ray dead.","After everything that happened during the Smelting Trial, especially Ray’s attempt to truly kill Max using the Soul Devouring Sword, hatred between the two sides had already become irreconcilable.","However, Jonathan still did not immediately respond.","Because Ray Willer was not an ordinary genius.","He possessed deep ties with the Sword God Palace, and his status there was extremely high.","Helping Max kill someone like Ray would undoubtedly bring enormous trouble afterward.","Still—","Jonathan did not reject the condition.","Seeing Jonathan remain silent instead of objecting outright, Max calmly continued.","\"My second condition,\" Max said slowly, \"is that both of you must join a secret force I am currently building.\"","Jonathan frowned deeply this time.","\"A secret force?\" he repeated while narrowing his eyes slightly. \"What kind of force?\"","Max remained silent briefly before leaning slightly closer toward Jonathan.","Then he whispered something quietly into his ear.","\"An organization created to kill elves.\"","The moment those words entered Jonathan’s ears, his expression changed drastically.","\"What?!\" Jonathan blurted out in shock while staring at Max in disbelief.","Clearly, he had never expected something like this.","The Elf Race was one of the most ancient and powerful races within the Divine Realm. Their foundations were terrifyingly deep, and countless major powers avoided provoking them unnecessarily.","Yet Max was openly speaking about creating a force specifically aimed against them.","Even Julie’s calm expression changed slightly after hearing this.","However, Max himself remained completely calm.","\"There is no need for you to panic so much,\" Max said quietly. \"I am not foolish enough to challenge the Elf Race recklessly.\"","His expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"I would never make a move against them until I am absolutely certain we possess enough strength to confront them directly.\"","Max’s gaze slowly sharpened.","\"And I certainly would not drag my own people toward meaningless deaths.\"","Jonathan remained silent after hearing those words.","At that moment, he could clearly sense something unusual hidden behind Max’s hatred toward the Elf Race.","This was not simple hostility.","It felt personal.","Very personal.","Then Max looked directly into Jonathan’s eyes once again.","\"If you agree to these two conditions,\" Max said calmly, \"then I can help Julie.\"","Jonathan’s expression tightened slightly.","However, before he could speak, Max continued.","\"And what I have in mind is not merely removing the poison inside her body.\"","The moment those words fell, both Jonathan and Julie’s eyes immediately changed.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"What I can offer her...\" he said quietly, \"is something even better.\"","Silence immediately filled the pavilion.","Then Max finally finished speaking.","\"So think carefully before making your choice, Jonathan.\"","Jonathan fell silent after hearing Max’s conditions.","The pavilion became heavy with tension as he lowered his gaze and began thinking deeply.","Neither condition was simple.","The first meant helping Max create an opportunity to kill Ray Willer, someone closely connected to the Sword God Palace. The second meant joining a secret force aimed at the Elf Race, a terrifying race whose power and foundation were far beyond ordinary forces.","No matter which condition he chose to consider, both carried enormous danger.","For a long while, Jonathan said nothing.","Then his gaze slowly shifted toward Julie.","Julie remained quiet, but the faint weakness hidden in her expression and the exhaustion buried deep within her eyes made Jonathan’s heart tighten.","In the end, nothing mattered more than saving her.","Jonathan slowly clenched his fists.","Then he turned back toward Max.","His jaw tightened, and his voice came out through gritted teeth.","\"Fine.\"","He stared directly into Max’s eyes.","\"I accept both conditions.\"","\"You made the correct choice,\" Max said with a faint smile appearing across his face.","Then, under Jonathan and Julie’s surprised gazes, Max slowly raised his hand and took out a strange fruit.","The fruit radiated chaotic energy fluctuations while crimson and golden flame patterns flickered faintly across its surface. The moment it appeared, the surrounding spiritual energy inside the pavilion immediately became restless.","Jonathan’s eyes narrowed slightly after sensing the extraordinary aura emitted by the fruit.","Meanwhile, Max calmly handed it toward him.","\"This is an extremely rare treasure known as a Chaos Fruit,\" Max explained slowly. \"It possesses very miraculous properties. Normally, after consuming it, a person has a high chance of awakening a flame-element Divine Body.\"","Jonathan’s expression immediately changed after hearing those words.","Even Julie looked shocked now.","Divine Bodies were incredibly rare existences. Countless geniuses throughout the Divine Realm would never obtain such an opportunity even after searching their entire lives.","Yet Max was casually taking out a treasure capable of creating one.","However, Max continued speaking calmly.","\"But Julie’s situation is different.\"","His gaze shifted toward Julie afterward.","\"Because she already possesses the Ten Thousand Poison Body, there is a very high possibility that the effects of the Chaos Fruit will mutate after entering her body.\"","A thoughtful expression appeared across Max’s face as he continued explaining.","\"There are two possible outcomes.\"","\"The first possibility is that the Ten Thousand Poison Body itself undergoes an evolution and transforms into an even stronger physique.\"","\"The second possibility is that the Chaos Fruit awakens a completely new Divine Body within her, but because of the poison already fused deeply into her body, the newly awakened physique will likely become a flame-poison type Divine Body instead of an ordinary flame Divine Body.\"","The pavilion gradually fell silent after hearing his explanation.","Jonathan’s breathing had already become slightly heavier.","Meanwhile, Max calmly continued.","\"Regardless of which outcome occurs, the result will still benefit her greatly.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared on his face afterward.","\"Because once the poison becomes fully integrated into her physique instead of remaining a destructive force inside her body, she will no longer need to fear it destroying her from within.\"","Max looked directly toward Julie.","\"In fact,\" he said calmly, \"the poison that once threatened to kill her may eventually become her greatest source of strength instead.\""]},{"number":1673,"title":"Chapter 1673: Their Choice!","paragraphs":["Jonathan slowly reached forward and accepted the Chaos Fruit from Max’s hand.","The moment the fruit entered his grasp, he immediately felt an astonishing wave of energy flowing from within it. Chaotic flame energy continuously circulated across the surface of the fruit while faint crimson-golden patterns flickered like living flames.","Even so—","A trace of hesitation still appeared within Jonathan’s eyes.","He lowered his gaze toward the Chaos Fruit while countless thoughts surfaced within his mind.","What Max had just described sounded far too unbelievable.","A treasure capable of granting someone a Divine Body?","Such a thing should not even exist.","Within the Divine Realm, Divine Bodies were regarded as heaven-defying physiques possessed only by monstrous geniuses blessed by fate itself. Some inherited them through bloodlines while others awakened them through miraculous opportunities beyond imagination.","But a fruit capable of directly granting a Divine Body?","Jonathan had never once heard of such a thing before.","And with his status and background, his knowledge far surpassed that of ordinary geniuses.","If treasures like this truly existed openly within the Divine Realm, there was no way he would not have heard at least rumors regarding them before.","Yet—","He could not recall a single thing related to fruits capable of creating Divine Bodies.","That alone caused deep uncertainty to rise within his heart.","Jonathan’s expression gradually became more conflicted afterward.","Because Julie’s condition was already extremely dangerous.","The Ten Thousand Poison Body was not something that could be treated carelessly. One wrong decision could completely destabilize the poison inside her body and worsen her condition even further.","And that was exactly what Jonathan feared most.","He did not want to gamble recklessly with Julie’s life using something he did not fully understand.","Even if Max had sounded confident earlier, Jonathan still found it difficult to completely trust such an unbelievable treasure immediately.","Meanwhile, Julie quietly observed Jonathan from the side.","She could naturally understand what he was worried about.","After all, even she herself found Max’s explanation difficult to believe completely.","The pavilion gradually became silent once again as Jonathan continued staring at the Chaos Fruit within his hand, clearly hesitating over whether he should truly let Julie consume it or not.","Max quietly observed the hesitation and uncertainty on Jonathan and Julie’s faces and immediately understood what they were worried about.","After all, everything he had just told them sounded far too unbelievable.","A fruit capable of awakening a Divine Body was something that would shake the entire Divine Realm if news of it spread. It was only natural for them to hesitate before trusting something they had never even heard about before.","However, Max did not attempt to persuade them further.","Instead, he simply spoke calmly.","\"I already gave you a path,\" Max said while looking at the two of them. \"Now the choice is yours whether you want to walk that path or not.\"","Neither Jonathan nor Julie responded immediately.","The atmosphere inside the pavilion remained heavy as Jonathan continued holding the Chaos Fruit silently in his hand.","Seeing this, Max slowly turned around.","Then, before leaving, he spoke once more.","\"The banquet will be held tomorrow,\" Max said calmly. \"I can wait until then.\"","His voice remained steady and unhurried.","\"I hope that by the time we meet again, the two of you will have already made your decision.\"","With those final words, Max no longer stayed inside the pavilion.","He calmly walked away while the faint moonlight reflected softly across the spirit lake behind him.","Meanwhile, Jonathan and Julie remained standing silently within the pavilion, both lost deeply within their own thoughts while staring at the Chaos Fruit in Jonathan’s hand.","As for Max, he soon left the quiet area entirely and headed back toward the mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan.","On the way back toward the Black Dragon Clan’s mansion, Max continued thinking about Jonathan and Julie’s situation.","The more he thought about it, the more tragic their circumstances seemed.","One carried a cursed physique that slowly poisoned her from the inside while the other desperately searched everywhere for even the slightest chance to save her.","In truth, neither of them had many options left anymore.","Max quietly let out a faint sigh.","\"I just hope they make the right choice,\" he muttered softly.","As an outsider, there was only so much he could do for them. In the end, whether they trusted him or not would ultimately depend entirely upon their own decision.","Soon afterward, Max finally arrived back at the mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan.","However, the moment he entered the courtyard, two familiar figures immediately appeared before him.","Lucia crossed her arms while narrowing her eyes suspiciously at him.","\"Where exactly did you go?\" she asked directly.","Beside her, Isabella also looked toward Max curiously.","Seeing their expressions, Max merely smiled faintly.","\"That,\" he replied casually, \"is a secret.\"","Then he looked at Lucia helplessly before adding, \"Besides, you already saw me leaving together with Jonathan earlier, so why bother asking me now?\"","Lucia immediately rolled her eyes after hearing that answer.","Clearly, she was not satisfied with his response at all.","However, before either of them could continue questioning him, Max calmly spoke again.","\"Anyway,\" he said, \"please inform Master that I will not be attending tomorrow’s banquet.\"","Both Isabella and Lucia looked slightly surprised after hearing that.","\"I will be busy training,\" Max added calmly.","After saying that, Max no longer stayed outside.","He directly walked past the two of them and headed toward his room inside the mansion.","Soon, after entering his room, Max immediately noticed a storage ring placed neatly on the table nearby.","A faint smile instantly appeared across his face.","Clearly, these were the rewards distributed after the Smelting Trial ended.","Without wasting time, Max picked up the storage ring and inspected its contents.","The moment his consciousness entered the ring, his eyes brightened immediately.","Inside were enormous amounts of cultivation resources, rare treasures, divine crystals, and numerous valuable materials obtained both from the Smelting Trial rewards and the treasures he personally recorded inside the Tower of Treasure.","Seeing such a massive collection of resources gathered together, even Max could not help revealing a satisfied smile.","\"Nice,\" Max muttered softly.","\"With this much treasure, I should finally be able to enter the peak of the Law Awakening Realm.\"","At the same time, anticipation gradually appeared within his eyes.","\"And after that...\"","A faint draconic aura unconsciously flickered around his body.","\"I can finally open the fourth Divine Vein of the Seven Divine Veins.\"","\"The Vein of Speed.\""]},{"number":1674,"title":"Chapter 1674: Practicing Saint Origin Sword Art","paragraphs":["Max did not immediately use the enormous amount of resources he had just obtained to raise his cultivation to the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","Neither did he rush to unlock the fourth Divine Vein, the Vein of Speed.","Although both breakthroughs were extremely tempting, Max still forcibly restrained himself.","Because at this moment, there was something he considered even more important.","The Saint Origin Sword Art.","After entering the Dimension of Time, Max devoted all of his focus entirely toward comprehending and practicing the sword art left behind by the Sword Saint.","The more he practiced it, the more Max realized how terrifying and profound this sword art truly was.","Every movement.","Every slash.","Every fluctuation of sword intent hidden within the technique seemed to contain layers upon layers of deeper mysteries.","At first glance, the Saint Origin Sword Art appeared straightforward and overbearing, yet the more Max tried to master it, the more he felt as though he had merely touched the surface of an endless ocean.","This realization only made Max even more serious.","After all, this was not some ordinary sword technique.","It was the personal sword art created by the Sword Saint himself.","A legendary existence whose name alone was enough to shake countless worlds.","Because of that, Max became completely immersed within the Saint Origin Sword Art.","Inside the endless flow of time within the Dimension of Time, Max continuously practiced the sword art again and again without pause.","At times, he practiced ordinary slashes.","At other times, he attempted to fuse the Emotion Severing Cosmic Path into the sword art once more.","Slowly, Max began noticing things he had previously overlooked.","The Saint Origin Sword Art was not simply about destructive power.","It carried a strange sense of purity and sharpness capable of severing everything in existence.","The deeper Max comprehended it, the more terrifying the sword art gradually became.","Because of this, Max spent the entire night after the Smelting Trial completely immersed within the Dimension of Time practicing continuously.","He ignored rest entirely.","He ignored cultivation advancement.","Even the temptation of unlocking the Vein of Speed was temporarily pushed aside.","Nothing mattered more to him right now than fully understanding the Saint Origin Sword Art.","It was not until the following morning that Max finally left the Dimension of Time.","And even then, it was not because he wanted to stop practicing.","In truth, Max still wished to continue comprehending the sword art further.","However, someone had arrived outside his room earlier and informed him that Jonathan wished to speak with him again.","Because of that, Max had no choice but to temporarily leave the Dimension of Time and leave the mansion as well.","Not long afterward, Max arrived at the same pavilion where Jonathan had brought him the previous day.","The quiet spirit lake still reflected the soft morning light while the surrounding breeze carried a calm and peaceful atmosphere.","However, the moment Max stepped into the pavilion, he immediately noticed something completely different about Jonathan and Julie.","Yesterday, both of them had been surrounded by gloom, tension, and helplessness.","But today—","Those emotions were completely gone.","Bright smiles could clearly be seen on both of their faces while even the atmosphere around them felt noticeably lighter than before.","Especially Julie.","The previous instability hidden within her aura had vanished almost entirely. Instead, faint crimson poison flames occasionally flickered subtly around her body before disappearing once again under her complete control.","Seeing this scene, Max instantly understood the outcome.","They had chosen to trust him.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"It seems the two of you are in quite a good mood today,\" Max said calmly as he walked into the pavilion.","The moment Jonathan saw him, the usually composed young man immediately stood up.","Then, to Max’s surprise, Jonathan directly looked at him with an expression filled with genuine gratitude.","\"It worked,\" Jonathan said while smiling brightly. \"The Chaos Fruit truly worked!\"","Even now, traces of disbelief could still be seen within his eyes as though he still found the entire situation unreal.","Julie also looked toward Max with gratitude visible within her gaze.","Jonathan quickly continued speaking afterward.","\"After Julie consumed the Chaos Fruit last night, the poison inside her body immediately began reacting violently with the flame energy contained within the fruit.\"","\"At first, we thought something had gone wrong because the poison fluctuations became extremely unstable.\"","Jonathan let out a breath before continuing.","\"But then her Ten Thousand Poison Body suddenly began mutating.\"","The excitement within his voice became increasingly obvious.","\"The poison physique and the flame energy from the Chaos Fruit fused together completely and eventually created an entirely new Divine Body.\"","Jonathan’s eyes brightened noticeably afterward.","\"The Ten Thousand Poison Flame Body.\"","The moment those words were spoken, even the surrounding energy inside the pavilion seemed to fluctuate faintly.","Meanwhile, Julie slowly raised her hand.","In the next instant, crimson poisonous flames silently appeared above her palm.","The flames looked extremely dangerous, yet they remained completely stable beneath her control.","Not even the slightest trace of poison leaked outward anymore.","Seeing this, Jonathan’s expression became even more emotional.","\"You have no idea how unbelievable this is,\" he said while looking toward Max. \"Before this, Julie constantly needed treasures to suppress the poison inside her body. Even then, controlling the poison was incredibly difficult.\"","\"But now...\"","Jonathan looked toward Julie again before smiling.","\"She can control the poison as naturally as controlling her own energy.\"","\"The poison no longer harms her body anymore. Instead, it has completely fused with her new Divine Body.\"","At that moment, even Julie herself looked slightly emotional.","For the first time in many years, she no longer needed to fear the poison inside her own body and just like Max had said yesterday, it had now become her strongest weapon.","\"Good.\" Max was truly happy for them. He then asked about his deal. \"What about my two conditions?\""]},{"number":1675,"title":"Chapter 1675: Poisoned Ray!","paragraphs":["After hearing Max’s words, Jonathan slowly straightened his posture.","The hesitation and uncertainty from yesterday had completely disappeared from his expression. What replaced it now was determination.","\"Since Julie has already been cured,\" Jonathan said seriously while looking directly at Max, \"it is only right that we fulfill our side of the agreement as well.\"","Then he continued without hesitation.","\"Max, we are prepared to join your secret force.\"","A faint smile appeared across Max’s face after hearing that.","At the same time, Jonathan’s expression gradually turned colder.","\"As for your first condition...\" Jonathan said quietly, \"come with us.\"","His eyes narrowed faintly afterward.","\"Everything has already been arranged.\"","The moment those words fell, both Jonathan and Julie turned around and began walking deeper into the pavilion area.","Max calmly followed behind them while silently observing the increasingly secluded surroundings.","The deeper they went, the quieter the atmosphere became.","Soon, Jonathan led Max toward a hidden passage concealed beneath the pavilion itself.","After entering the underground area, the surroundings immediately became dark and cold.","There were no artificial lights illuminating the underground pathways. Instead, old burning torches lined the stone walls on both sides, causing flickering flames to cast long shadows throughout the tunnels.","The entire place carried an ancient and gloomy atmosphere.","It resembled some sort of forgotten underground ruin hidden beneath the Violet Star Palace.","\"What exactly is this place?\" Max asked curiously while looking around the dim underground tunnels.","Julie answered calmly while continuing forward.","\"This is a hidden location beneath the Violet Star Palace,\" she explained. \"A very long time ago, this area was used as a prison.\"","Her voice became slightly colder afterward.","\"Those who committed crimes severe enough to warrant execution were imprisoned here.\"","Max’s eyes flickered slightly.","\"Later, after countless years passed, the location was abandoned and gradually forgotten by most people inside the Violet Star Palace.\"","Max slowly nodded after hearing that explanation.","The deeper they traveled into the underground tunnels, the more the place genuinely resembled an old prison.","Cold stone walls.","Narrow passageways.","Heavy metal doors.","The atmosphere itself carried traces of despair and suffering left behind from the past.","Eventually, after passing through several underground corridors, the three of them arrived before a dark cave-like chamber.","The moment Max stepped closer, he immediately sensed violent fluctuations coming from inside.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","Inside the cave, a young man was frantically punching the stone walls repeatedly.","The entire chamber shook faintly under the force of his attacks.","Then suddenly, after hearing footsteps approaching, the young man abruptly turned around.","The moment his eyes landed on Jonathan, Julie, and Max, his expression twisted violently.","\"Jonathan! Julie!\" Ray roared furiously.","However, unlike his arrogant appearance during the Smelting Trial, Ray now looked completely miserable.","His voice sounded hoarse and weak.","His hair was disheveled.","The color within his eyes had dimmed noticeably.","Even his skin had turned faintly purple.","At a single glance, anyone could tell something was terribly wrong with his condition.","\"I feel weak throughout my entire body!\" Ray shouted while staggering slightly. \"Even the world around me keeps spinning!\"","His furious gaze locked directly onto Jonathan.","\"What exactly did you put inside the drink you gave me?!\"","The moment those words fell, Max immediately understood the situation.","Ray had been poisoned.","\"Did the two of you poison him using one of your poisons, Julie?\" Max asked while calmly observing Ray’s miserable condition.","At that moment, Ray no longer resembled the arrogant genius from the Smelting Trial at all.","His entire body looked weak and unstable while traces of purple poison continuously spread beneath his skin. Even the spiritual energy fluctuations around him had become chaotic and disordered.","Jonathan nodded slowly after hearing Max’s question.","\"Yes,\" he admitted without hiding anything.","Then he let out a helpless breath before continuing.","\"We originally did not know how to deal with him.\"","Jonathan’s expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"Ray is slightly stronger than either of us individually. Though we can handle him if two of us can take actions together but that would create too much chaos.\"","Julie also spoke quietly at that moment.","\"And if he escaped,\" she said calmly, \"everything would become troublesome afterward.\"","After all, Ray was not an ordinary genius.","Not only was he powerful himself, but he also possessed the backing of the Sword God Palace. Once someone like him became alert and cautious, dealing with him secretly would become extremely difficult.","Because of that, Jonathan and Julie could not afford to fail.","Jonathan continued speaking afterward.","\"So in the end, we decided to take a risk.\"","His gaze slowly shifted toward Julie.","\"After Julie awakened the Ten Thousand Poison Flame Body last night, her control over poison improved tremendously.\"","Jonathan’s expression still carried traces of disbelief while speaking about it.","\"The difference was unbelievable. Before this, even Julie herself struggled to completely control the poison within her body. But after awakening the new Divine Body, she became capable of manipulating poison with astonishing precision.\"","Julie calmly nodded afterward.","\"Because of that,\" she explained softly, \"we decided to test one of my new poisons on Ray.\"","A faint coldness flashed within her eyes.","\"We invited him earlier under the excuse of discussing matters related to the Smelting Trial and the coming banquet.\"","Jonathan smiled faintly afterward.","\"Fortunately, he never suspected us.\"","\"Ray drank the poisoned wine without noticing anything unusual.\"","Jonathan then looked toward Ray once again.","\"And apparently...\"","A faint smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"It worked far better than we expected.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face after hearing Jonathan and Julie’s explanation.","\"You two handled this quite well,\" Max said calmly while looking toward the miserable Ray standing inside the chamber.","Then Max’s gaze slowly shifted back toward Jonathan and Julie.","\"Now,\" he continued with a faintly amused smile, \"would the two of you mind leaving us alone for a while?\"","His eyes briefly moved toward Ray afterward.","\"I would like to spend some personal time with him.\"","Jonathan and Julie immediately understood what Max meant.","Neither of them said anything further.","Instead, they simply exchanged a brief glance before shrugging lightly and turning around to leave the underground chamber together.","However, the moment Ray realized they were truly walking away, panic and fury instantly exploded across his face.","\"Jonathan! Julie!\" Ray roared loudly.","His voice echoed throughout the underground chamber while his already disheveled appearance became even more frantic.","At that moment, Ray finally understood what was happening.","He had been completely betrayed.","The people he trusted enough to drink with had secretly poisoned him and handed him directly over to Max.","The realization caused his eyes to turn bloodshot instantly.","\"I trusted the two of you!\" Ray shouted furiously while staggering forward weakly. \"And this is how you repay me?!\"","The hatred and disbelief within his voice became increasingly intense.","\"You actually sold me out to Max!\"","Ray’s face twisted violently with rage afterward.","\"How dare you do this to me?!\"","Then, as though suddenly remembering his own background, Ray immediately began roaring threateningly.","\"Once the Sword God Palace learns about this, both of you are dead!\"","Terrifying hatred filled his eyes completely.","\"The Sword God Palace will never forgive this betrayal!\""]},{"number":1676,"title":"Chapter 1676: Taking Care of Ray!","paragraphs":["After Jonathan and Julie completely left the underground chamber, silence gradually returned once again.","Only Max and Ray remained inside the dark prison-like cave now.","The flickering torch flames hanging along the stone walls cast long moving shadows throughout the chamber while Ray continued breathing heavily from the poison spreading inside his body.","His condition had clearly worsened compared to earlier. Purple poison veins spread visibly beneath his skin while his spiritual aura fluctuated chaotically without stability.","Meanwhile, Max calmly walked forward step by step until he finally stopped directly in front of Ray.","Then he spoke quietly.","\"Before you die, there is something I want to know.\"","Ray slowly raised his head after hearing those words.","Hatred and killing intent immediately filled his bloodshot eyes the moment he looked at Max.","\"Who exactly from the Sword God Palace ordered you to kill me?\" Max asked calmly.","The moment those words entered Ray’s ears, his expression changed slightly.","Although the change was brief, Max still noticed it clearly.","However, that hesitation quickly disappeared and was replaced by a cold sneer afterward.","\"You think I would tell you something like that?\" Ray laughed hoarsely while glaring at Max hatefully.","Even in his miserable state, arrogance still remained deeply rooted within him.","\"You really have no idea what kind of existence the Sword God Palace truly is,\" Ray continued coldly.","His face gradually twisted more and more while hatred filled his voice.","\"If I die here, the Sword God Palace will never let you go.\"","\"The people standing behind me are existences far beyond your imagination.\"","Ray continued threatening Max repeatedly while relying entirely upon the reputation and power of the Sword God Palace.","\"The moment they discover what happened to me, your fate will become worse than death.\"","\"You actually think someone like you can oppose the Sword God Palace?\"","Ray suddenly burst into crazed laughter.","\"You are nothing in front of them!\"","However, throughout the entire exchange, Max’s expression remained completely calm.","He simply observed Ray quietly while pondering silently in his mind.","Since Ray refused to reveal the truth willingly, Max could only speculate himself.","Deep down, Max already possessed a strong suspicion regarding the identity of the person behind all this.","Mira.","The daughter of the Sword God Palace.","From the beginning, she had shown obvious hostility toward him, especially after the matter involving the Dragonheart Sword and what had happened between them in Orion.","Everything pointed toward her.","However—","Another possibility suddenly surfaced within Max’s mind.","Could there perhaps be someone else involved as well?","Someone else within the Sword God Palace who also wanted him dead?","That thought caused Max’s eyes to narrow slightly.","Then slowly, a faint smile appeared across his face.","\"If you refuse to answer,\" Max said calmly, \"then I will simply find the answer myself.\"","Before Ray could properly understand what Max meant, Max suddenly raised his right hand and directly placed it upon Ray’s head.","The moment Max touched him, Ray’s expression changed drastically.","An overwhelming sense of danger exploded within his heart instantly.","\"What are you doing?!\" Ray shouted instinctively.","However, before he could react further—","Boom!!!","A terrifying wave of soul force erupted violently from Max’s body.","The entire underground chamber trembled faintly while strange soul fluctuations spread throughout the surroundings. Even the torch flames along the walls flickered chaotically beneath the pressure.","Then suddenly—","Ray screamed.","\"AAAAAAHHHHHH!!!\"","An incomparably painful scream echoed throughout the underground prison as a translucent figure was forcefully dragged out from within Ray’s body.","It was his soul.","Ray’s soul struggled frantically while emitting terrified screams, but it was completely unable to resist the overwhelming authority of the Dimension of Soul.","At that moment, Max’s eyes glowed faintly while terrifying soul laws silently activated around him.","The next instant, Ray’s soul was directly pulled into the Dimension of Soul.","Inside that mysterious dimension, everything immediately changed.","The moment Ray’s soul entered the Dimension of Soul, it became completely suppressed by the laws governing that place. Invisible soul chains instantly wrapped around it while terrifying refining power descended from every direction.","Ray’s soul struggled desperately.","He screamed.","He begged.","However, nothing could stop the refining process.","Soon afterward, the Dimension of Soul began breaking Ray’s soul apart gradually and refining it into pure soul force.","At the same time, Max immediately felt enormous amounts of refined soul energy flowing directly into his sea of consciousness.","His soul force began increasing rapidly.","The strength of his soul became noticeably more powerful while pure soul energy continuously nourished every corner of his consciousness.","However, that was not the only thing Max obtained.","As Ray’s soul continued being refined completely, countless memories suddenly flooded directly into Max’s mind.","Scenes began flashing rapidly one after another.","Conversations.","Orders.","Hatred.","Plans.","Killing intent.","Max silently watched through all of Ray’s memories while searching for the answer he wanted.","Then eventually—","He saw her.","Mira.","The daughter of the Sword God Palace.","Inside Ray’s memories, Max clearly witnessed Mira personally instructing Ray to kill him during the Smelting Trial. The hatred within her eyes while speaking about Max was unmistakable.","The moment Max saw those memories, a cold smile slowly appeared across his face.","\"So it truly was you,\" Max muttered quietly.","Knowing that the person behind everything was indeed Mira, Max did not feel particularly surprised.","From the very beginning, he had already suspected her involvement. After witnessing the memories extracted from Ray’s soul, that suspicion had merely been confirmed completely.","Because of that, Max no longer wasted any further thought on the matter.","Instead, his gaze slowly shifted toward Ray’s lifeless body lying on the cold stone floor.","Then—","Black flames suddenly erupted from Max’s hand.","The dark flames radiated terrifying devouring energy as they instantly engulfed Ray’s corpse completely. The moment the flames touched the body, Ray’s flesh, blood, bones, and even remaining spiritual energy began rapidly disintegrating.","Within only a few moments, Ray’s body was completely devoured into nothingness.","At the same time, a dense stream of energy immediately surged back into Max’s body through the black flames."]},{"number":1677,"title":"Chapter 1677: Julie’s Plan","paragraphs":["Max calmly closed his eyes briefly while sensing the enormous amount of energy flowing throughout his meridians.","That energy was extremely pure.","After devouring Ray completely, Max could clearly feel his cultivation drawing even closer toward another breakthrough.","Several moments later, the flow of energy gradually stabilized.","Only after the final traces of Ray’s body turned into dust did the devouring process completely end.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"With this,\" he muttered softly, \"I am truly very close to reaching the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm.\"","Then Max calmly turned around and walked out of the underground chamber.","Soon afterward, he arrived back outside the prison area where Jonathan and Julie were already waiting for him silently.","The moment Jonathan saw Max emerge alone, he immediately understood the outcome.","\"You dealt with him?\" Jonathan asked quietly.","Max nodded calmly.","\"He is gone.\"","Jonathan simply nodded after hearing that.","There was neither pity nor hesitation within his expression.","After everything Ray had attempted to do during the Smelting Trial, Jonathan no longer cared what happened to him anymore.","Meanwhile, Julie also remained completely silent.","Then Jonathan looked toward Max once again before asking seriously, \"Now that we have agreed to join your secret force, how exactly are we supposed to contact you or the others afterward?\"","\"We cannot exactly move openly together without attracting attention.\"","Hearing that, Max remained thoughtful for a brief moment before speaking calmly.","\"Extend your hand.\"","Jonathan looked slightly confused after hearing those words.","However, he still trusted Max enough by now not to question him further.","Soon afterward, Jonathan slowly extended his right hand toward Max.","The next instant, Max activated the Dimensional Sovereign Body silently.","Invisible dimensional power instantly gathered around his fingertips while strange spatial fluctuations spread faintly through the surroundings.","Then Max placed his finger lightly against Jonathan’s palm.","A moment later, a mysterious rune slowly began forming upon Jonathan’s hand.","The rune radiated faint silver-blue light while tiny dimensional patterns continuously shifted within it like living space laws.","After several seconds, the rune completely stabilized.","Only then did Max withdraw his hand calmly.","Jonathan immediately lowered his gaze toward the strange rune now engraved upon his palm.","His eyes filled with curiosity instantly.","\"What exactly is this?\" he asked while carefully observing the rune.","Max calmly explained afterward.","\"This rune is an access point connected to a secret domain.\"","Jonathan and Julie’s expressions changed slightly after hearing that.","\"That secret domain,\" Max continued calmly, \"is where the headquarters of my force currently exists.\"","Then Max looked directly toward both of them.","\"If you wish to enter that place, simply imbue the rune with your Divine Essence.\"","\"The rune will automatically create a portal leading directly into the secret domain.\"","Jonathan’s eyes narrowed slightly while sensing the astonishing dimensional fluctuations hidden within the rune.","Clearly, this was no ordinary spatial technique.","Meanwhile, Max continued speaking.","\"Come tonight.\"","His gaze gradually became serious afterward.","\"At midnight, while everyone’s attention is focused upon the banquet.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across his face.","\"That will be your first time entering the secret domain.\"","\"How many members does your secret force currently have?\" Julie asked curiously after hearing Max’s explanation about the secret domain.","The moment she asked that question, Max’s expression immediately became slightly awkward.","He coughed lightly before answering honestly.","\"At the moment...\" Max said while smiling helplessly, \"you two are the only people I have personally recruited.\"","Jonathan and Julie both stared at him silently afterward.","Max continued explaining calmly.","\"There is also a friend of mine managing certain matters inside the secret domain itself. So if we count everyone together, the entire force currently has only three members.\"","Julie immediately frowned slightly after hearing that.","\"Only three?\" she repeated while looking at Max strangely.","However, only a moment later, a thoughtful light suddenly flashed through her eyes.","\"Actually...\" Julie said slowly while smiling faintly, \"I might already have a way to increase those numbers rapidly.\"","Max’s interest immediately rose slightly.","\"And how exactly do you plan to do that?\" he asked curiously.","Julie calmly answered afterward.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Max immediately became thoughtful.","Meanwhile, Julie continued speaking confidently.","\"Right now, although your name has already spread somewhat throughout the Divine Realm because of the Sovereign Sword, most people still do not truly understand how terrifying your strength and potential actually are.\"","Her eyes gradually brightened slightly afterward.","\"But the Cosmic Ascension Conference is different.\"","\"That place gathers geniuses from countless forces and worlds. If you can display overwhelming talent there and truly make a name for yourself during the conference, then many people will naturally become interested in following you.\"","Julie smiled faintly afterward.","\"At that point, countless geniuses would willingly join a force created by someone like you.\"","Max slowly nodded after hearing her explanation.","\"That actually sounds like a very good plan,\" he admitted honestly.","However, shortly afterward, his expression gradually became more serious.","\"There is still one major problem though.\"","Jonathan and Julie both looked toward him curiously.","\"I have no reliable way to determine who can truly be trusted,\" Max explained calmly.","His eyes narrowed slightly afterward.","\"I invited the two of you because I know neither of you would betray me.\"","\"But random people are different.\"","\"If I begin recruiting large numbers of geniuses later, there is no guarantee some of them will not secretly carry their own motives.\"","At that moment, Julie suddenly laughed softly.","\"You really do not need to worry too much about that issue,\" she said calmly.","A faintly dangerous smile slowly appeared across her face afterward.","\"With my poison abilities, I can place a hidden deadly poison mark on every person who joins the force.\"","Jonathan’s expression changed slightly after hearing that.","Meanwhile, Julie calmly continued.","\"The poison would remain dormant normally, so it would not affect them at all.\"","\"However, the moment someone attempts betrayal...\"","A faint crimson poisonous flame flickered briefly within Julie’s eyes.","\"The poison would immediately activate and kill them.\""]},{"number":1678,"title":"Chapter 1678: A Talk with Isabella!","paragraphs":["Max’s eyes immediately brightened slightly afterward.","\"Haha, that is actually a very good idea,\" he admitted while nodding.","Although such a method sounded somewhat ruthless, Max still understood its necessity clearly.","A secret organization like theirs absolutely could not afford betrayal from within.","Fear was sometimes the most effective method of maintaining loyalty.","Especially during the early stages while their foundations remained weak.","The more Max thought about it, the more he felt Julie’s suggestion was extremely useful.","Then suddenly, another idea surfaced within his mind.","The Dimension of Soul.","With the authority he possessed over souls now, Max realized he could potentially create something similar himself.","If future members willingly allowed it, he could directly place a soul mark upon them through the Dimension of Soul.","That soul mark could remain dormant normally without affecting the target at all.","However—","The moment someone attempted betrayal, the soul mark could instantly activate.","At that point, their soul would collapse directly from within.","And once the soul shattered—","Death would become inevitable.","\"Alright,\" Max said while looking toward Julie with a faint smile appearing across his face. \"We will proceed according to your plan.\"","A thoughtful light gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"If things truly unfold the way you described, then the Cosmic Ascension Conference might become the perfect opportunity to expand our force rapidly.\"","After all, the Cosmic Ascension Conference gathered countless monstrous geniuses from across the Divine Realm. If he could truly display overwhelming talent there and make his name resound throughout the younger generation, then attracting talented individuals afterward would naturally become much easier.","Max slowly nodded to himself.","\"In that case,\" he continued calmly, \"I will do everything possible to stand out during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The confidence within his voice was extremely obvious.","Then Max looked toward both Jonathan and Julie once again.","\"Make sure the two of you arrive at the secret domain tonight at midnight,\" he said seriously. \"I will be waiting there personally.\"","Jonathan immediately nodded.","Julie also agreed calmly afterward.","With everything already settled between them, there was no reason to continue remaining inside the underground area any longer.","Soon afterward, Max turned around and began walking away from the hidden prison tunnels.","Meanwhile, Jonathan and Julie silently watched his departing figure thoughtfully.","As for Max himself, he quickly left the underground prison area completely and headed back toward the mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan.","After leaving the underground prison area, Max soon returned to the mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan.","The atmosphere throughout the mansion was noticeably lively because many disciples were still discussing the results of the Smelting Trial and preparing for the banquet that would be held later that night.","However, Max paid little attention to those conversations.","The moment he entered the courtyard, his gaze immediately found Lucia and Isabella speaking together nearby.","\"Isabella,\" Max called out calmly. \"Come meet me alone in my room for a moment.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Lucia immediately narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","\"Alone?\" she repeated while looking between the two of them carefully.","A strange expression gradually appeared across her face afterward.","Meanwhile, Isabella herself looked slightly confused as well.","However, before Lucia could begin questioning him further, Max calmly added, \"There are some important matters we need to discuss.\"","Lucia stared at him silently for several moments afterward.","Clearly, her curiosity had already been completely aroused.","Still, after a brief pause, she eventually let out a helpless sigh.","\"Forget it,\" Lucia muttered while waving her hand dismissively. \"I still have some matters to deal with anyway.\"","Even though she remained suspicious, she ultimately chose not to interfere further.","Soon afterward, Lucia left the courtyard while Isabella quietly followed Max toward his room inside the mansion.","After entering the room, Isabella immediately looked toward Max curiously.","\"What happened?\" she asked directly.","Max did not waste time afterward.","\"I recruited two more members into the force,\" he explained calmly.","Isabella’s eyes immediately brightened slightly after hearing that.","\"Jonathan and Julie?\" she asked almost instantly.","Max smiled faintly afterward.","\"You guessed correctly.\"","Then his expression gradually became more serious.","\"They will officially enter the secret domain tonight at midnight.\"","A thoughtful look appeared across Isabella’s face after hearing that.","Then she nodded lightly.","\"That timing should work perfectly,\" Isabella replied calmly. \"I already finished constructing a basic conference room inside the secret domain earlier.\"","Hearing that immediately caused Max to smile slightly.","\"Good,\" he said while nodding.","Then suddenly, Max extended his hand toward Isabella.","\"Now,\" he continued calmly, \"extend your hand for a moment.\"","Isabella blinked in confusion after hearing that.","Clearly, she did not understand what Max intended to do.","However, trusting him completely by now, she still slowly extended her hand toward him without questioning further.","The next instant, Max activated the Dimensional Sovereign Body silently.","Invisible dimensional power immediately gathered around his fingertips while faint spatial ripples spread throughout the room.","Then Max lightly touched Isabella’s palm.","A moment later, a mysterious silver-blue rune slowly began forming upon her hand.","The rune radiated faint dimensional fluctuations while intricate spatial patterns continuously shifted within it like flowing space laws.","Several seconds later, the rune completely stabilized.","Only then did Max withdraw his hand calmly.","Meanwhile, Isabella immediately lowered her gaze toward the strange rune now engraved upon her palm.","Her beautiful eyes instantly filled with curiosity.","\"What exactly is this?\" she asked while carefully inspecting the rune.","Max calmly explained afterward.","\"This is a dimensional passage rune.\"","His gaze gradually became serious.","\"The rune acts as an access point connected directly to the Dimension of Genesis.\"","Isabella’s eyes widened slightly after hearing that.","Then Max continued explaining calmly.","\"If you channel your Divine Essence into the rune, it will automatically open a portal leading directly into the secret domain.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face afterward.","\"In other words...\"","\"You can now freely enter the Dimension of Genesis whenever necessary.\"","After hearing Max’s explanation, Isabella lowered her gaze toward the dimensional rune on her palm once again.","Faint silver-blue light continued flowing quietly through the intricate patterns engraved upon her skin while subtle spatial fluctuations spread from it continuously.","The more she sensed the rune carefully, the more astonished she became.","Because she could clearly feel that the rune was genuinely connected to another independent space entirely.","This was far beyond ordinary spatial transportation methods.","Eventually, Isabella slowly nodded.","\"This will be extremely useful,\" she said honestly while a faint smile appeared across her face.","Her eyes gradually brightened slightly afterward.","\"With this rune, communication and movement between members of the force will become far easier and much safer. Even if we are scattered across different places in the future, we can still gather inside the secret domain whenever necessary.\"","A thoughtful expression appeared on her face afterward.","\"And more importantly,\" Isabella continued calmly, \"nobody outside the force would even know such a hidden domain exists.\"","The more she thought about it, the more valuable the Dimension of Genesis seemed.","A completely hidden independent world capable of serving as headquarters for their growing organization was something many major forces throughout the Divine Realm would desperately desire.","Meanwhile, Max simply smiled faintly after hearing her words.","Clearly, Isabella had immediately understood just how important the Dimension of Genesis would become for them in the future."]},{"number":1679,"title":"Chapter 1679: Night of the Banquet!","paragraphs":["It was already midnight, and the entire Violet Star Palace had transformed into a magnificent sea of lights.","Every palace building, courtyard, bridge, and pavilion throughout the enormous sect grounds had been decorated beautifully for the banquet. Countless spirit lanterns floated through the sky like glowing stars while streams of colorful spiritual light illuminated the night from every direction.","The atmosphere throughout the Violet Star Palace was lively and celebratory.","Music echoed continuously across the palace grounds while disciples and elders from the various third-rate forces gathered together in large numbers. Some discussed the Smelting Trial enthusiastically while others exchanged cultivation experiences and formed new connections before the coming Cosmic Ascension Conference.","The banquet itself was grand.","Long tables filled with rare spiritual foods, wines, and precious fruits stretched across the main banquet area while beautiful spirit dancers performed beneath the glowing lights.","Everywhere one looked, laughter and conversation filled the surroundings.","However, despite the lively atmosphere, one topic remained at the center of nearly every discussion.","Max Morgan.","Many younger geniuses continued speaking about his overwhelming performance during the Smelting Trial, especially his battle against Ray Willer and the shocking display of strength he revealed inside the Tower of Treasure.","Meanwhile, Max himself had only briefly attended the banquet.","Outwardly, he maintained enough appearances to avoid attracting suspicion by disappearing entirely. He calmly exchanged a few conversations with several elders and disciples before quietly leaving the banquet grounds afterward.","Very few people noticed his departure amidst the enormous gathering.","Soon afterward, Max returned directly to the mansion assigned to the Black Dragon Clan.","The moment he entered his room, the calm expression on his face gradually became more serious.","Then, his figure disappeared completely from the room and entered the Dimension of Genesis.","After entering the Dimension of Genesis, Max did not immediately head toward the meeting hall Isabella had prepared earlier.","Instead, he first went to meet Alice and Lenavira.","The peaceful atmosphere inside the Dimension of Genesis felt completely different from the lively banquet outside the Violet Star Palace. The surrounding land was calm and quiet while dense spiritual energy flowed naturally throughout the entire dimension.","Soon, Max arrived at the area where Alice and Lenavira were currently staying.","The moment Alice noticed him approaching, her eyes immediately brightened.","\"You finally came back,\" she said while quickly walking toward him. \"Do you know how boring it gets staying here sometimes?\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira simply smiled faintly from the side while looking toward Max calmly.","Max chuckled lightly after hearing Alice complain.","\"The Smelting Trial only ended recently,\" he replied helplessly. \"Naturally, I had many things to deal with outside first.\"","Alice immediately crossed her arms afterward.","\"Still,\" she muttered, \"you disappear for long periods every single time.\"","Max only smiled slightly before changing the topic.","\"Actually,\" he said calmly, \"once we return to the Black Dragon Clan, the two of you will get to meet several interesting people.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Alice immediately became curious.","\"Interesting people?\" she repeated quickly.","Even Lenavira’s gaze shifted toward Max with slight interest afterward.","Max nodded lightly.","\"They are indeed very interesting people.\"","However, despite saying that much, Max did not reveal anything else afterward.","The interesting people were of course his spirit Lily and the little dragon Vormir. Max hadn’t got the time to introduce Alice and Lenavira to Lily and Vormir because of the Smelting Trial but now that this trial had ended, Max felt that it was time they finally meet each other.","Alice immediately narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","\"Who exactly are they?\" she asked quickly.","Max merely smiled calmly.","\"That,\" he replied casually, \"is still a secret for now.\"","Alice instantly became dissatisfied after hearing that answer.","\"A secret again?\" she complained immediately. \"Why do you keep making everything sound mysterious lately?\"","Then she quickly stepped closer toward Max while continuing to question him endlessly.","\"Are they strong?\"","\"Are they from the Violet Star Palace?\"","\"Are they geniuses from the Smelting Trial?\"","\"Are there many of them?\"","However, no matter how many questions Alice asked continuously, Max never directly answered any of them.","Instead, he simply smiled faintly every single time.","\"You will find out soon enough,\" he replied calmly.","Alice immediately pouted in frustration afterward.","\"You are doing this on purpose,\" she muttered unhappily.","Meanwhile, Lenavira quietly watched the exchange between the two with amusement visible within her eyes.","Clearly, she already understood that Max deliberately intended to keep the matter hidden for now.","Eventually, after speaking with the two of them for some time longer, Max finally turned toward the direction of the meeting hall Isabella had prepared earlier.","Tonight—","The first true gathering of his secret force was about to begin.","\"Alright,\" Max said while lightly patting both Alice and Lenavira on the head. \"I still have some important matters to deal with first, so I will see the two of you later.\"","Alice immediately looked slightly dissatisfied again.","\"You always say that,\" she muttered quietly.","Meanwhile, Lenavira simply smiled gently afterward.","\"That is fine,\" she said calmly. \"Dinner is almost ready anyway. Once you finish your work, come eat with us.\"","The moment those words entered his ears, a genuinely warm smile slowly appeared across Max’s face.","\"That sounds perfect,\" he replied while nodding lightly. \"I should be back within a few hours.\"","As he spoke those words, a faint sense of warmth quietly rose within Max’s heart.","Ever since Alice and Lenavira had arrived inside the Dimension of Genesis, the atmosphere here had gradually begun changing little by little. What was once merely an empty independent world had slowly started feeling more alive.","And although Max remained extremely busy most of the time with cultivation, battles, and endless responsibilities, he still tried his best to spend time with them whenever possible.","In fact, after returning to the Dimension of Genesis repeatedly over time, Max had gradually developed a habit.","Whenever he was free, he would eat dinner together with Alice, Lenavira, and Isabella.","Sometimes they simply talked casually.","Sometimes Alice complained endlessly about how boring cultivation was.","Other times Isabella discussed matters related to the secret domain while Lenavira quietly listened nearby.","They were simple moments.","Yet strangely—","Max found himself valuing those moments more and more.","Because despite all the dangers surrounding him constantly, those peaceful dinners inside the Dimension of Genesis made the place genuinely begin feeling like home.","Even if he could not remain beside them all the time, Max still tried his best not to completely neglect them.","At the very least, whenever he returned to the Dimension of Genesis, he wanted to spend some time together with them normally.","Meanwhile, after hearing Max agree to return for dinner later, Lenavira’s smile deepened slightly.","\"We will wait for you then,\" she said softly.","Max nodded one final time afterward before finally turning around and heading toward the meeting hall prepared by Isabella deeper within the Dimension of Genesis.","By the time Max arrived at the meeting hall inside the Dimension of Genesis, Isabella, Jonathan, and Julie were already waiting there.","The meeting hall itself was surprisingly refined despite being created recently. A large circular table stood at the center of the room while faint silver lights illuminated the surroundings softly. Intricate dimensional patterns could be seen engraved across portions of the walls, causing the entire hall to carry a mysterious atmosphere.","The moment Max entered, the attention of everyone inside immediately shifted toward him.","A faint smile appeared across Max’s face afterward.","Then he slowly walked toward the center of the hall before looking directly at Jonathan and Julie.","\"First of all,\" Max said calmly, \"welcome to the Crown.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Jonathan and Julie’s expressions changed slightly.","Clearly, this was the first time they had heard the actual name of the secret force."]},{"number":1680,"title":"Chapter 1680: First Meeting of Crown!","paragraphs":["\"The Crown?\" Jonathan repeated thoughtfully.","Max nodded lightly.","\"That is the name of this organization.\"","His voice remained calm, yet the atmosphere inside the hall gradually became more serious afterward.","Then Max gestured toward Isabella standing nearby.","\"This is Isabella,\" he introduced calmly. \"She currently handles many matters related to the secret domain itself.\"","The moment Jonathan and Julie looked toward her, Isabella calmly nodded toward the two of them.","\"It is good to finally meet both of you properly,\" Isabella said with a faint smile.","Jonathan also nodded politely afterward.","Likewise, Julie greeted Isabella calmly as well.","After the brief introductions were finished, the atmosphere inside the hall quickly became much more serious.","Max did not waste unnecessary time afterward.","He directly walked toward the large table at the center of the hall before speaking calmly.","\"Now that everyone is here,\" Max said slowly, \"it is time to discuss the true purpose behind the Crown.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the expressions of Jonathan and Julie gradually became solemn once again.","Meanwhile, Max’s gaze slowly swept across everyone present.","Then he continued quietly.","\"The purpose of this organization is simple.\"","A faint coldness gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"The Crown exists to stand against the Elf Race.\"","Silence instantly filled the meeting hall.","Neither Jonathan nor Julie spoke immediately after hearing those words again.","After all, even now, the idea of directly opposing the Elf Race still sounded unbelievable.","However, unlike earlier, neither of them questioned Max anymore.","Meanwhile, Max himself did not explain further. He did not mention why he possessed hostility toward the elves. He did not explain what kind of connection existed between him and the Elf Race.","Nor did he reveal the true depth of the hatred hidden within his heart.","Those matters remained buried completely within him for now.","Instead, Max simply continued calmly.","\"The Crown will continue growing stronger quietly from the shadows. We will gather resources, we will grow in number and once....\"","A faintly terrifying pressure unconsciously spread from Max’s body.","\"We are strong enough, we will declare war on the Elf Race.\"","Max looked toward the three of them calmly before continuing further.","\"Even though the eventual enemy of the Crown is the Elf Race, none of you need to worry too much about that right now because I have no intention of provoking them recklessly while we are still weak. The current Crown does not even possess the qualifications to stand openly before a race like the elves yet, and I would never drag all of you into a meaningless death. Until we possess enough strength, everything we do will remain hidden in the shadows.\"","The atmosphere inside the meeting hall gradually became more serious afterward.","\"We will quietly continue building our foundations,\" Max continued while his gaze swept across everyone present. \"We will gather resources, connections, influence, and talented people while expanding slowly from the shadows. I will only move against the Elf Race once I am absolutely certain that we possess enough strength to face them directly.\"","Jonathan and Julie silently nodded after hearing those words.","Then Max leaned slightly against the table before continuing calmly.","\"For now, the most important thing for the Crown is growth. If possible, I want all of you to quietly recommend this organization to people you genuinely trust. However, do not recruit random geniuses carelessly. I only want talented people who are capable of keeping secrets and who would never betray us.\"","Jonathan slowly folded his arms while thinking deeply for several moments.","\"That should not be impossible,\" he said thoughtfully. \"I still know several people I trust completely. However, we will need to be extremely cautious because one wrong person could expose everything before the Crown is ready.\"","Julie also nodded lightly afterward.","\"I know a few suitable people as well,\" she said calmly. \"Most of them already possess dissatisfaction toward the current balance of power within the Divine Realm, so convincing them might not be too difficult. Still, I agree that secrecy must remain our highest priority for now.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face after hearing their responses.","\"Good,\" he replied calmly. \"Then from today onward, all of you should begin quietly laying the foundation for the Crown. We may only have a few members right now, but one day this organization will become powerful enough that even the major forces of the Divine Realm cannot ignore us.\"","Max continued discussing several additional matters with them after that.","The four of them talked about how future communication inside the Crown would work, how carefully they needed to handle recruitment, and how they should avoid drawing unnecessary attention toward themselves before the Cosmic Ascension Conference began.","The atmosphere inside the meeting hall gradually became much more relaxed compared to earlier.","Eventually, after nearly everything that needed to be discussed had already been settled, the first official meeting of the Crown finally came to an end.","Jonathan and Julie soon prepared to leave the Dimension of Genesis and return back to the Violet Star Palace before anyone noticed their absence for too long.","However, just as the two of them were about to leave the meeting hall, Max suddenly spoke once again.","\"One more thing.\"","Jonathan and Julie both stopped before turning back toward him curiously.","Max calmly looked toward the dimensional passage runes engraved upon their hands before speaking.","\"You are free to enter the Dimension of Genesis whenever you want,\" he said calmly. \"There are no restrictions placed upon either of you.\"","The moment those words entered their ears, both Jonathan and Julie looked slightly surprised.","Meanwhile, Max continued explaining further.","\"This place is now the headquarters of the Crown, but it is also a safe place for all members of the organization. Whether you need a place to hide, cultivate peacefully, or discuss important matters privately, you may freely come here anytime.\"","A faint smile appeared across his face afterward.","\"You do not need my permission every single time.\"","Jonathan slowly looked around the meeting hall once more after hearing that.","Even now, he still found the existence of this secret independent dimension unbelievable.","A hidden world completely isolated from the outside.","The value of something like this was immeasurable.","Meanwhile, Julie lightly touched the dimensional rune on her palm while speaking softly.","\"This really is an incredible place.\"","Max simply smiled faintly afterward.","\"In the future,\" he replied calmly, \"the Crown will continue growing here.\"","Jonathan eventually nodded seriously afterward.","\"Understood,\" he said calmly. \"We will make good use of it.\"","Julie also nodded lightly before the two of them finally activated the dimensional passage runes on their palms.","Soon afterward, dimensional portals silently opened before them.","The next moment, Jonathan and Julie stepped through the portals and disappeared from the meeting hall completely, leaving only Max and Isabella behind inside the Dimension of Genesis once again."]},{"number":1681,"title":"Chapter 1681: A Peaceful Dinner","paragraphs":["After Jonathan and Julie left the Dimension of Genesis, the meeting hall gradually became quiet once again.","Only Max and Isabella remained there now.","The faint silver lights illuminating the hall reflected softly across the large circular table while the surrounding dimensional patterns continued glowing quietly in the background.","For a while, the two of them continued discussing several remaining matters related to the Crown.","They spoke about possible future recruits, how the organization should remain hidden during its early stages, and how the Dimension of Genesis would gradually need to expand if the number of members continued increasing later.","Isabella also briefly reported several things she had already arranged inside the secret domain, including the construction of temporary living areas and additional meeting spaces for future use.","Max listened carefully to everything before eventually nodding in satisfaction.","\"You handled things very well,\" he said calmly.","A faint smile appeared across Isabella’s face afterward.","\"Someone has to manage things properly while you keep disappearing everywhere,\" she replied lightly.","Max chuckled softly after hearing that.","Eventually, after discussing a few more matters, Max slowly stood up from his seat.","\"That should be enough for tonight,\" he said calmly afterward.","Then his gaze shifted toward Isabella.","\"You should go rest as well.\"","Isabella nodded lightly after hearing that.","Clearly, even she had spent most of the day busy handling various matters both inside and outside the Dimension of Genesis.","Soon afterward, she also stood up from her seat.","\"Alright,\" Isabella replied calmly. \"Then I will leave the remaining matters to you.\"","Max nodded lightly in response.","The next moment, Isabella activated the dimensional rune on her hand before calmly leaving the meeting hall as well, leaving Max alone inside the quiet headquarters of the Crown.","\"Mother... Father...\"","Max quietly muttered those words to himself after Isabella left the meeting hall as well.","The calm expression on his face gradually became heavier afterward while countless thoughts silently surfaced within his mind.","Now that the Crown had finally begun taking shape and more people were slowly gathering around him, Max could already feel himself gradually moving closer toward the path he truly wanted to walk.","A path toward strength.","Toward revenge.","And toward eventually finding the truth behind everything connected to his parents.","\"It will not be much longer before I come for the two of you,\" Max whispered softly.","After remaining silent for several moments longer, Max finally turned around and quietly left the meeting hall as well.","Soon afterward, he returned toward the living area inside the Dimension of Genesis where Alice and Lenavira had been waiting earlier.","The moment Max arrived there, he immediately smelled the fragrance of food filling the surroundings.","Warm spiritual lights illuminated the small dining area softly while several dishes filled with spirit beast meat, spiritual vegetables, and fragrant soup had already been prepared neatly across the table.","Meanwhile, Alice immediately noticed him approaching.","\"You finally came back,\" she said while looking at him suspiciously. \"At this point I was starting to think you forgot about dinner entirely.\"","Max chuckled lightly afterward before taking a seat nearby.","\"I told you earlier that I would return,\" he replied calmly.","Lenavira smiled gently from the side while placing another dish onto the table.","\"At least you still remembered in the end,\" she said softly.","The atmosphere around the table gradually became warm and peaceful afterward.","Unlike the tense discussions inside the meeting hall earlier, the dinner felt completely relaxing.","Alice continuously talked about random things while complaining occasionally about how boring staying inside the Dimension of Genesis could become sometimes.","Meanwhile, Lenavira quietly listened most of the time while occasionally smiling at Alice’s endless chatter.","As for Max—","He simply enjoyed the peaceful atmosphere silently.","For a brief period, he no longer needed to think about the Sword God Palace, the Crown, the Cosmic Ascension Conference, or the countless dangers waiting for him outside.","Instead, he simply ate dinner together with them quietly like an ordinary person.","Eventually, after the dinner finally ended and some more casual conversation passed between them, Max slowly stood up from his seat.","\"I should leave now,\" he said calmly afterward.","Alice immediately looked slightly dissatisfied again.","\"You are leaving already?\" she asked.","Max nodded lightly.","\"I need to prepare for the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","Lenavira smiled softly afterward.","\"Then be careful.\"","Max nodded once more before lightly patting Alice’s head again.","\"I will return soon.\"","Soon afterward, Max activated the Dimensional Sovereign Body once again.","A dimensional portal silently opened before him.","Then, after one final glance toward Alice and Lenavira, Max stepped through the portal and quietly left the Dimension of Genesis.","The next moment, Max appeared once again inside the training chamber connected to the room assigned to him within the mansion where the Black Dragon Clan members were staying temporarily.","The quiet chamber was illuminated softly by spiritual lamps placed around the walls while dense spiritual energy naturally flowed throughout the room.","After returning from the Dimension of Genesis, the atmosphere around Max gradually became much calmer.","He slowly walked toward the center of the training chamber before sitting down cross-legged quietly.","At the same time, countless thoughts surfaced within his mind once again.","\"Tomorrow morning...\" Max muttered softly to himself, \"we will finally leave the Violet Star Palace and return to the Verdant Sky Star Realm.\"","A faint thoughtful expression appeared across his face afterward.","This trip to the Violet Star Palace had brought him enormous gains far beyond his expectations.","Not only had his cultivation and strength improved tremendously, he had also obtained the Saint Origin Sword Art, unlocked the Dimension of Soul, recruited the first true members of the Crown, and gained countless treasures from the Tower of Treasure.","Most importantly—","He had finally begun laying the foundations for his future plans.","However, despite all those gains, Max knew very clearly that his current strength was still far from enough.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference was only three months away.","And compared to the monstrous geniuses who would gather there from throughout the Divine Realm, his current cultivation was still too weak.","Because of that, Max no longer intended to waste any remaining time.","A sharp light gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"Since there are still several hours remaining before dawn,\" Max muttered quietly, \"I might as well use this opportunity properly.\"","The enormous amount of treasures and resources obtained from the Smelting Trial still remained inside his storage ring untouched.","Originally, Max had delayed using them because he focused entirely upon comprehending the Saint Origin Sword Art first.","But now—","It was finally time.","A faint draconic aura slowly began rising around Max’s body while dense Divine Essence fluctuations spread throughout the training chamber.","\"I should finally be able to reach the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm tonight,\" Max said softly.","The moment those words fell, Max immediately took out large quantities of cultivation resources from his storage ring.","Divine crystals.","Divine stones.","Ancient medicinal herbs.","Rare spiritual fruits.","Numerous treasures rapidly appeared around him one after another, filling the entire training chamber with astonishing spiritual fluctuations."]},{"number":1682,"title":"Chapter 1682 - 10th level of Law Awakening Realm!","paragraphs":["Then Max slowly closed his eyes.","The next instant—","He began cultivating.","The moment Max began cultivating, the entire training chamber immediately trembled faintly beneath the pressure erupting from his body.","Dense Divine Essence fluctuations spread throughout the surroundings while enormous quantities of spiritual energy gathered rapidly toward him from every direction.","Meanwhile, the countless treasures placed around him continuously radiated astonishing energy.","However, Max did not absorb those resources normally.","Instead—","Black flames suddenly erupted around his body.","The dark flames burned silently while radiating terrifying devouring power capable of swallowing everything around them. The moment the flames touched the cultivation resources nearby, the treasures immediately began disintegrating rapidly.","Divine crystals shattered one after another.","Rare medicinal herbs withered instantly.","Divine stones dissolved into pure energy.","Every resource refined by the black flames was immediately transformed into incredibly pure energy before being devoured directly into Max’s body.","Boom!","The energy fluctuations within the training chamber intensified violently afterward.","Max calmly sat at the center of the chamber while continuously devouring the treasures surrounding him at an astonishing speed.","At the same time, his cultivation aura began rising steadily.","The ninth level of the Law Awakening Realm gradually approached its limits more and more.","However, Max did not stop.","More black flames spread outward.","More treasures disappeared into pure energy.","The amount of resources consumed by Max was honestly terrifying.","Ordinary geniuses would likely require months or even years to fully refine such an enormous amount of cultivation treasures safely.","Yet under the terrifying devouring ability of the black flames, Max absorbed everything forcefully with overwhelming speed.","As time slowly passed, the aura surrounding Max became increasingly frightening.","Dense seven colored lightning gradually crackled around his body while draconic pressure continuously spread outward from within him.","At the same time, the three already awakened Divine Veins inside his body began glowing brilliantly.","The Vein of Origin.","The Vein of Vitality.","The Vein of Strength.","All three Divine Veins resonated together while enormous amounts of energy surged through his meridians continuously.","Soon afterward—","Crack.","A faint breaking sound suddenly echoed deep within Max’s body.","The next instant, Max’s eyes snapped open sharply.","Boom!!!","An incomparably powerful aura exploded outward from his body instantly.","The entire training chamber shook violently while terrifying waves of Divine Essence spread across the surroundings like a storm.","Seven colored lightning erupted wildly around Max while dense draconic aura filled the room completely.","At that moment—","Max had finally broken through.","The tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face while feeling the overwhelming power surging throughout his body.","Compared to before, his Divine Essence had become far denser and far more powerful.","Even his physical body had strengthened noticeably once again after absorbing such enormous amounts of refined energy.","Meanwhile, the remaining traces of black flames gradually disappeared around him.","The countless cultivation resources originally filling the room had almost completely vanished now.","Everything had been devoured entirely.","Max slowly clenched his fist afterward.","Boom!","The surrounding air exploded instantly from the sheer force alone.","Feeling the terrifying strength flowing through his body now, a sharp light gradually appeared within Max’s eyes.","\"The tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm...\" he muttered softly.","Then a faint smile slowly spread across his face.","\"Now...\"","His gaze gradually sharpened afterward.","\"It is finally time to open the fourth Divine Vein.\"","After successfully reaching the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm, Max still did not stop cultivating.","Instead, the determination within his eyes only intensified further.","The next goal waiting before him was the fourth Divine Vein of the Seven Divine Veins.","The Vein of Speed.","Without wasting any time, Max immediately waved his hand once again.","The next moment, enormous quantities of body cultivation treasures appeared throughout the training chamber one after another. Ancient beast blood sealed within crystal containers floated into the air while rare body tempering herbs, spirit fruits, essence crystals, and countless other treasures radiating dense physical energy filled the surroundings completely.","The spiritual fluctuations released by those treasures alone were already astonishing.","Ordinary cultivators would likely need years to carefully absorb such a massive amount of body cultivation resources safely.","However, Max never intended to absorb them slowly.","Boom!!!","Terrifying black flames erupted around his body once again.","The devouring flames spread rapidly throughout the chamber while instantly engulfing every body cultivation treasure nearby. The moment those flames touched the resources, violent physical energy exploded outward like a raging flood.","Ancient beast blood vaporized instantly into dense crimson energy.","Spirit fruits dissolved into pure body refining essence.","Even the extremely hard essence crystals shattered continuously beneath the terrifying power of the black flames.","Soon afterward, all that violent physical energy surged directly into Max’s body.","The pressure released from the energy was honestly horrifying.","Normally, attempting to absorb such violent body cultivation energy recklessly would instantly destroy a cultivator from within. Flesh would rupture. Meridians would collapse. Bones would shatter beneath the unbearable pressure.","Yet Max remained completely unmoved.","Dense draconic aura erupted throughout his body instantly while golden-black dragon scales gradually appeared across portions of his skin.","At the same time, the power of five thousand Draconic Essences awakened completely inside him.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Terrifying draconic energy surged throughout every corner of Max’s body while the violent body cultivation energy continuously slammed against his flesh, bones, and meridians.","However, unlike ordinary cultivators, Max’s physical body had already become unimaginably durable.","The Dragon Scales Transformation.","The five thousand Draconic Essences.","The continuous strengthening from the previous three Divine Veins.","All of it had already transformed Max’s body into something monstrous.","Because of that, although the violent energy flooding through him remained extremely dangerous, his body forcefully endured everything without collapsing.","His muscles trembled violently beneath the pressure.","His meridians glowed brilliantly while enormous amounts of energy surged through them continuously.","Yet despite all of that, his body never once showed signs of breaking apart.","Instead, it endured everything overwhelmingly.","Meanwhile, the three previously awakened Divine Veins inside Max’s body began resonating violently.","The Vein of Origin released dense foundational power throughout his body.","The Vein of Vitality continuously repaired and strengthened him simultaneously.","The Vein of Strength caused terrifying physical force to erupt from within him endlessly.","As all three Divine Veins resonated together, the hidden fourth pathway buried deep within Max’s body finally began reacting.","The Vein of Speed.","The moment Max sensed that hidden Divine Vein beginning to awaken, his eyes sharpened instantly.","More black flames erupted around him afterward while even more body cultivation treasures disappeared rapidly into pure energy.","The pressure inside the training chamber rose to an astonishing level.","The surrounding walls even began cracking faintly beneath the terrifying aura leaking from Max’s body.","At the same time, the hidden fourth Divine Vein gradually became brighter and brighter.","Then suddenly—","Boom!!!","A terrifying shockwave exploded outward from Max’s body instantly.","Silver-golden light erupted violently throughout his meridians while the hidden fourth Divine Vein finally burst open completely.","At that moment, Max suddenly felt his entire body becoming strangely lighter.","The flow of Divine Essence inside his body accelerated tremendously.","Even the movement of the surrounding spiritual energy appeared slower inside his perception.","Most importantly—","An astonishing sense of speed erupted throughout every corner of his body.","The Vein of Speed had finally awakened completely."]},{"number":1683,"title":"Chapter 1683: Leaving the Violet Star Palace!","paragraphs":["After successfully awakening the Vein of Speed, Max did not immediately stop cultivating.","Instead, he quickly realized something important.","Although the Vein of Speed had already opened completely, he still lacked proper control over the overwhelming speed now flowing through his body.","Every movement felt unnaturally light.","Every circulation of Divine Essence moved several times faster than before.","Even his perception of the surrounding world had changed drastically.","Because of that, Max understood very clearly that if he wanted to fully utilize the true power of the Vein of Speed in battle, he first needed to become completely accustomed to it.","Without hesitation, Max immediately entered the Dimension of Time once again.","The moment he stepped into the endless training world, seven colored lightning erupted around his body while terrifying speed fluctuations spread throughout the surroundings.","Then Max began training.","At first, he merely attempted simple movements.","However, the results shocked even him slightly.","The moment Max took a single step forward, his figure instantly disappeared from his original location.","Boom!!!","Violent shockwaves exploded throughout the Dimension of Time while Max suddenly appeared hundreds of meters away almost instantly.","Even he himself nearly lost control over his own movement speed.","\"So fast...\" Max muttered while narrowing his eyes slightly.","The Vein of Speed was far more terrifying than he initially expected.","Not only did it drastically increase his movement speed, it also enhanced the circulation speed of his Divine Essence, reaction speed, attack speed, and even his overall perception ability.","Because of this, Max spent enormous amounts of time inside the Dimension of Time continuously practicing.","Again and again—","He repeated movements endlessly.","Sometimes he trained pure movement speed.","Other times he fused the Vein of Speed with his seven colored lightning movement techniques.","Occasionally, he even combined it with the Saint Origin Sword Art.","The results became increasingly terrifying.","At times, Max moved so quickly that dozens of afterimages filled the Dimension of Time simultaneously.","At other moments, his sword strikes became so fast that even the surrounding space split apart before the attack itself could fully be seen.","The more Max adapted to the Vein of Speed, the more terrifying his combat ability gradually became.","Most importantly—","Unlike ordinary cultivators, Max’s monstrous physical body allowed him to withstand such terrifying movement speed without collapsing.","Because of the five thousand Draconic Essences and Dragon Scales Transformation, his body remained durable enough to endure the overwhelming pressure generated by the Vein of Speed.","Otherwise, ordinary cultivators would likely tear apart their own muscles and meridians merely trying to move at such terrifying velocity.","Time passed continuously inside the Dimension of Time.","Eventually, after practicing for an unknown amount of time, Max finally managed to gain much better control over the Vein of Speed.","His movements gradually became smoother.","More precise.","More terrifying.","Then suddenly—","A voice echoed from outside the his room.","\"Max, everyone is preparing to leave the Violet Star Palace.\"","The moment he heard those words, Max slowly stopped training.","The violent speed aura surrounding him gradually calmed afterward while the countless afterimages filling the Dimension of Time slowly disappeared one by one.","Then Max let out a slow breath.","\"It is finally time to return,\" he muttered softly.","Soon afterward, Max left the Dimension of Time completely.","By the time he opened his eyes again, he had already returned to the training chamber inside the mansion.","Outside—","The members of the Black Dragon Clan were already preparing to depart from the Violet Star Palace and head back toward the Verdant Sky Star Realm.","Max soon met up with Lucia and Isabella after leaving the training chamber.","At that moment, many members of the Black Dragon Clan and other third rate forces were already preparing to depart from the Violet Star Palace. Numerous disciples and elders moved throughout the palace grounds while various star shuttles belonging to different forces floated high in the air nearby.","The Smelting Trial had officially ended.","And now—","Everyone was finally returning back to their respective realms and factions.","As Max walked together with Lucia and Isabella toward the departure area, Lucia suddenly looked toward him curiously.","\"So,\" she asked while folding her arms lightly, \"how was your experience here?\"","A faint smile immediately appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"It was quite worthwhile,\" he replied honestly. \"The Smelting Trial gave me much better rewards than I originally expected.\"","Then his eyes flashed slightly afterward.","\"The three trials helped me gain a lot of things, and they also allowed my cultivation to finally reach the peak of the Law Awakening Realm.\"","The moment those words entered Lucia and Isabella’s ears, both of their expressions changed slightly.","\"You reached the peak already?\" Lucia asked with obvious surprise.","Even Isabella looked genuinely shocked afterward.","After all, Max’s cultivation speed was honestly becoming increasingly terrifying.","Max simply smiled faintly afterward without explaining further.","Naturally, he did not mention anything regarding the Vein of Speed or the terrifying gains he obtained from the Tower of Treasure.","Meanwhile, as the three of them continued walking, they eventually arrived before the enormous star shuttle belonging to the Black Dragon Clan.","The massive vessel floated majestically above the ground while ancient runes glowed brightly across its dark exterior. Dense star energy continuously circulated around the shuttle while powerful spiritual fluctuations spread outward from it endlessly.","This was the same star shuttle they originally used to travel toward the Violet Sky Star Realm.","At that moment, several elders of the Black Dragon Clan were already standing nearby while organizing the disciples preparing to board.","The moment Max and the others arrived, one of the elders immediately spoke loudly.","\"Everyone, board the star shuttle immediately. We will soon depart from the Violet Sky Star Realm.\"","Soon afterward, disciples from the Black Dragon Clan began entering the enormous vessel one after another.","Meanwhile, just as Max prepared to board as well, his eyes suddenly shifted toward the distance.","There—","Jonathan and Julie could be seen standing quietly far away near another palace platform.","Clearly, the two of them had specifically come there to see him off before his departure.","However, neither Jonathan nor Julie approached directly.","Because with so many people present around the departure area, openly interacting too closely with Max now would only attract unnecessary attention.","Instead, the two of them simply stood silently in the distance.","Then Jonathan lightly nodded toward Max.","Julie also revealed a faint smile afterward.","It was a simple farewell.","Yet all three of them understood clearly that this would not be their final meeting.","Meanwhile, Max also smiled faintly afterward before raising his hand slightly toward the two of them.","A silent goodbye.","Jonathan and Julie quietly watched him afterward while Max finally turned around and entered the enormous star shuttle together with Lucia and Isabella.","Soon afterward—","Boom!!!","The massive star shuttle slowly rose into the sky.","Ancient runes across its surface erupted brilliantly while dense star energy gathered around the vessel continuously.","Then, under the gazes of countless people below, the enormous shuttle accelerated rapidly upward.","Within only a few moments, it pierced through the clouds above the Violet Star Palace completely.","Soon afterward, the gigantic vessel transformed into a streak of light shooting through the endless starry sky before finally disappearing into the distant stars altogether."]},{"number":1684,"title":"Chapter 1684: Useless Skills in the Divine Realm!","paragraphs":["The return journey from the Violet Sky Star Realm did not take very long.","Inside the enormous star shuttle, most disciples spent the majority of the trip either cultivating silently or discussing everything that happened during the Smelting Trial.","The atmosphere throughout the vessel remained completely different compared to when they first departed toward the Violet Star Palace.","At that time, everyone had been filled with anticipation and curiosity regarding the Smelting Trial.","But now—","The confidence and mentality of many disciples had changed completely.","After personally witnessing countless geniuses, terrifying battles, and overwhelming talents during the trials, nearly everyone had finally realized how vast the Divine Realm truly was.","Especially after seeing monsters like Max and Ray Willer, many disciples understood very clearly that their current strength was still far from enough.","Because of that, the atmosphere inside the shuttle became unusually focused.","Many disciples were already eager to begin secluded cultivation the moment they returned.","Meanwhile, Max mostly remained inside his room quietly throughout the journey.","Although he occasionally spoke briefly with Lucia and Isabella, most of his time was spent continuing to familiarize himself with the Vein of Speed and stabilizing his recent breakthroughs.","Eventually, after traveling through the endless stars for some time, the enormous star shuttle finally returned once again to the Verdant Sky Star Realm.","Soon afterward, the massive Black Dragon Palace gradually appeared within everyone’s sight.","The moment the disciples saw the enormous palace standing majestically atop the mountains once again, many people immediately revealed emotional expressions.","After all, despite the dangers and opportunities of the Smelting Trial, returning back home still brought a sense of relief.","Boom!!!","The gigantic star shuttle slowly descended before the Black Dragon Palace while countless disciples and elders below looked upward toward it.","Soon afterward, the shuttle finally landed completely.","The moment the disciples stepped outside once again, the elders of the Black Dragon Clan quickly gathered around to question them regarding the Smelting Trial and its results.","However, despite the excitement surrounding the return, almost every disciple shared the same thought now.","Cultivation.","After all, nearly everyone who survived the Smelting Trial had obtained enormous gains.","Some obtained treasures.","Others gained cultivation resources.","A few comprehended stronger concepts through battle.","Meanwhile, individuals like Max had gained opportunities so great that even ordinary geniuses could hardly imagine them.","Because of this, after returning to the Black Dragon Palace, nearly all participating disciples immediately entered seclusion one after another.","No one wanted to waste even a single moment.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference was only three months away now.","And everyone understood very clearly that those three months would likely determine their future standing within the younger generation of the Divine Realm.","Because of that, the entire Black Dragon Palace gradually entered a strange atmosphere afterward.","The disciples who participated in the Smelting Trial almost completely disappeared from public view as they entered closed-door cultivation continuously.","Some secluded themselves to break through their cultivation realms.","Others focused upon mastering new techniques and treasures.","Everyone desperately tried to digest the opportunities they obtained during the Smelting Trial before the Cosmic Ascension Conference finally began three months later.","Max naturally planned to enter seclusion as well after returning to the Black Dragon Palace.","After all, although he had already broken through to the tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm and awakened the Vein of Speed, there were still countless things he needed to stabilize and comprehend further before the Cosmic Ascension Conference began.","However, before he could properly begin secluded cultivation, he suddenly received a summons from Lady Virelia.","Knowing it was his master calling for him, Max naturally did not delay.","Soon afterward, he arrived before Lady Virelia’s office located deep within the Black Dragon Palace.","After entering the room, Max immediately saw Lady Virelia seated calmly behind a large desk while several ancient scrolls floated quietly around the room.","The atmosphere inside the office felt peaceful yet dignified.","The moment Lady Virelia noticed him entering, she lightly nodded toward him.","\"Sit down,\" she said calmly.","Max nodded respectfully afterward before taking a seat directly across from her.","For several moments, Lady Virelia simply observed him silently.","The more she looked at Max now, the more satisfied she became.","His performance during the Smelting Trial had honestly exceeded even her own expectations greatly.","Eventually, she finally spoke.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference will begin in three months,\" Lady Virelia said calmly while looking directly toward Max. \"How confident are you in entering the top one thousand?\"","The moment those words entered his ears, Max almost laughed inwardly.","Top one thousand?","In truth, his own goal had long since surpassed something like that.","Max was aiming for the very peak of the Cosmic Ascension Conference itself.","The top ten.","However, despite those thoughts, Max still remained calm outwardly.","Because he understood very clearly why Lady Virelia viewed things this way.","After all, she still did not know his true strength completely.","To someone like her, merely entering the top one thousand among the countless monstrous geniuses participating in the Cosmic Ascension Conference would already be an astonishing achievement beyond imagination.","Because of that, Max naturally did not blame her for underestimating him.","Instead, he simply smiled faintly afterward.","\"I should not have any problems entering the top one thousand,\" Max replied calmly. \"Master does not need to worry too much about me.\"","Lady Virelia slowly nodded after hearing that response.","Clearly, she was already quite satisfied with his confidence.","Then suddenly, as though recalling something important, her expression became thoughtful afterward.","\"Max,\" she said slowly, \"back in the mortal realm where you came from, were there things called skills?\"","Max’s eyes flickered slightly after hearing that question.","Then he nodded lightly.","\"Yes,\" he replied honestly. \"There were many skills in the mortal world.\"","A faint nostalgic expression appeared within his eyes briefly afterward.","\"However, after ascending to the Divine Realm, most of those skills became practically useless.\"","Lady Virelia nodded calmly after hearing that.","\"That is normal,\" she explained slowly.","\"The so-called skills used in mortal worlds are ultimately powered through mana.\"","Her gaze gradually became more serious afterward.","\"And mana itself is a power system belonging to the mortal realms.\"","\"Because of that, after ascending into the Divine Realm, the strength produced by ordinary skills becomes extremely weak.\"","Max quietly listened while Lady Virelia continued explaining.","\"The biggest issue is that skills are fundamentally designed to operate through mana pathways and mana laws. Even if someone ascends and begins cultivating Divine Essence afterward, the skills themselves still instinctively consume mana instead.\"","Lady Virelia lightly tapped the desk while continuing.","\"And although Divine Essence technically contains traces of mana within it, that tiny amount is insignificant compared to true Divine Essence.\"","\"That is why attempting to use ordinary mortal realm skills inside the Divine Realm becomes nearly pointless.\"","\"No matter how much Divine Essence you possess, the skill itself will still prioritize consuming the mana hidden inside the Divine Essence rather than the Divine Essence directly.\"","Max slowly nodded afterward.","That explanation immediately made many things clearer for him.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia continued calmly.","\"However...\"","A faint thoughtful expression appeared across her face.","\"That does not mean the Divine Realm lacks alternatives.\"","Max’s eyes immediately sharpened slightly after hearing that.","Lady Virelia slowly leaned back in her chair before continuing.","\"In the Divine Realm, there exists something far superior to ordinary mortal skills.\"","\"Abilities specifically designed to operate through Divine Essence itself.\"","Her voice gradually became heavier afterward.","\"However, unlike the common skills found throughout mortal worlds, these abilities are extremely rare.\"","\"Not every force in the Divine Realm possesses them.\"","\"In fact, many weaker forces may never even encounter one throughout their entire existence.\""]},{"number":1685,"title":"Chapter 1685: Divine Ability","paragraphs":["After hearing Lady Virelia’s explanation, Max gradually fell into deep thought.","Everything she said immediately caused many things to make sense in his mind.","Back in the mortal world, skills had once been considered extremely important.","However, after ascending into the Divine Realm, Max quickly noticed that almost nobody here relied upon ordinary skills anymore. Instead, cultivators focused almost entirely upon cultivation arts, concepts, laws, bloodlines, physiques, and various inheritances.","At first, Max assumed this was simply because Divine Realm cultivators considered ordinary skills too weak.","But now, after hearing Lady Virelia’s explanation regarding mana and Divine Essence, he finally understood the true reason behind it.","The foundation of ordinary skills themselves simply could not properly support Divine Essence.","Because of that, their strength naturally became insignificant after ascension.","Meanwhile, Max slowly raised his head afterward before asking curiously,","\"What exactly are these alternatives called?\"","The moment those words were spoken, Lady Virelia’s expression gradually became more serious.","Then she slowly answered,","\"They are called Divine Abilities.\"","The instant Max heard those two words, his eyes suddenly flickered sharply.","Divine Ability.","The name immediately triggered a memory deep within his mind.","Almost instantly, Max recalled the special Divine Ability he had previously obtained from the Chaos Fruit growing upon the flame branch of his Chaos Tree.","Back then, after refining the Chaos Fruit, he had directly awakened a genuine Divine Ability connected to flames.","At that time, Max still did not fully understand the true significance of that power.","However now—","After hearing Lady Virelia explain everything regarding skills and Divine Abilities, Max finally realized just how extraordinary that ability actually was.","Unlike ordinary skills powered through mana, Divine Abilities were powers specifically created to utilize Divine Essence directly.","In other words—","The Divine Ability he obtained from the Chaos Fruit was a true Divine Realm level power.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia naturally did not know what Max was thinking internally.","She simply continued speaking calmly afterward.","\"Divine Abilities are incredibly precious throughout the Divine Realm. Most of them are inherited through bloodlines, ancient inheritances, special physiques, or extremely rare heavenly treasures.\"","Her gaze slowly focused upon Max afterward.","\"And the strength of a Divine Ability is usually far beyond ordinary skills.\"","Max silently listened while inwardly becoming increasingly thoughtful.","At that moment, he finally began realizing that the Chaos Tree inside him might be even more terrifying than he originally imagined.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia continued speaking calmly while Max silently listened.","\"Divine Abilities themselves are also divided into different ranks,\" she explained slowly. \"The Divine Realm categorizes them from Tier One to Tier Five.\"","Her expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"The higher the tier, the more terrifying the Divine Ability becomes.\"","\"A Tier One Divine Ability might only grant some basic enhancement or special effect.\"","\"However, once you reach the higher tiers, the abilities become increasingly monstrous.\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes narrowed faintly afterward.","\"Some high-tier Divine Abilities are powerful enough to distort natural laws themselves.\"","\"Others can destroy worlds, erase souls, manipulate dimensions, or overturn the heavens entirely.\"","The atmosphere inside the room gradually became heavier as she spoke.","\"Even among the major powers of the Divine Realm, high-tier Divine Abilities are considered priceless treasures.\"","Then, after remaining silent briefly, Lady Virelia suddenly waved her hand.","The next moment, a fist-sized golden stone appeared above her palm.","The stone radiated ancient golden light while strange divine runes continuously flowed across its surface. Dense Divine Essence fluctuations spread from it endlessly while even the surrounding space distorted faintly around the stone itself.","The moment Max saw it, his eyes immediately sharpened slightly.","\"This...\" Max muttered softly.","Lady Virelia slowly looked toward the golden stone before speaking quietly.","\"This is a Divine Ability Core Stone.\"","Her voice carried traces of nostalgia afterward.","\"Inside this stone, a complete Divine Ability has been sealed.\"","The atmosphere inside the office immediately became solemn.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia calmly continued.","\"I obtained this Divine Ability Core Stone many years ago through sheer luck.\"","Her eyes remained fixed upon the stone while countless emotions flickered within them briefly.","\"Since then, I have kept it with me all this time.\"","A faint bitter smile slowly appeared across her face afterward.","\"However, despite possessing it for so many years, I could never fully decide whether I should absorb the Divine Ability for myself or preserve it for a future genius within the Black Dragon Clan.\"","Lady Virelia slowly raised her gaze toward Max afterward.","\"Until I met you.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Max became slightly stunned.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia calmly extended the golden stone toward him.","\"I have already made my decision.\"","Her gaze carried complete seriousness now.","\"Take this Divine Ability Core Stone.\"","Max’s expression immediately changed slightly afterward.","However, before he could speak, Lady Virelia continued firmly,","\"Among the younger generation of the Black Dragon Clan, nobody possesses greater talent or potential than you.\"","\"If this Divine Ability remains hidden with me any longer, it would simply be wasted.\"","The golden light emitted by the stone reflected across the room continuously while dense Divine Essence fluctuations spread outward.","Then Lady Virelia spoke the final words calmly.","\"Absorb the Divine Ability inside this stone and make it your own.\"","Max slowly reached out his hand and accepted the golden stone from Lady Virelia.","The moment the Divine Ability Core Stone entered his palm, his expression immediately changed slightly.","An incomparably mysterious feeling instantly spread throughout his entire body.","The golden stone felt strangely alive.","Dense Divine Essence fluctuations continuously flowed from within it while countless ancient runes flickered faintly across its surface like living symbols. Merely holding the stone caused Max to feel an ancient and profound aura surrounding it completely.","At the same time, a strange instinctive feeling suddenly surfaced within Max’s mind.","Crush it.","The moment that thought appeared, Max immediately understood.","The method of inheriting the Divine Ability sealed within the stone was extremely simple.","He simply needed to destroy the Divine Ability Core Stone itself.","Without wasting any time afterward, Max slowly tightened his grip around the golden stone.","Then—","Crack.","The Divine Ability Core Stone shattered instantly within his hand.","The moment the stone broke apart, a dazzling golden light suddenly erupted throughout the entire office.","Boom!!!","A terrifying wave of Divine Essence fluctuations spread outward while the shattered fragments of the stone instantly transformed into a massive beam of golden light.","Before Max could even properly react, the golden beam shot directly toward him and entered straight into his forehead.","The next instant—","Max’s entire consciousness trembled violently.","Countless streams of information suddenly exploded throughout his mind like a raging flood.","Ancient symbols.","Mysterious laws.","Complex Divine Essence circulation pathways.","All of them continuously poured into Max’s consciousness one after another at astonishing speed.","At the same time, Max immediately felt a completely new power gradually forming deep within his body.","It was fundamentally different from cultivation arts or ordinary techniques.","This power felt far more mysterious.","Far more profound.","And far more terrifying."]},{"number":1686,"title":"Chapter 1686: Star Fist!","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Lady Virelia silently watched everything from nearby without interrupting him.","Clearly, the inheritance process had already begun successfully.","Inside Max’s mind, the enormous amount of information gradually began organizing itself automatically.","Soon afterward, several ancient golden words slowly appeared clearly within his consciousness.","[Tier 3 Divine Ability: Star Fist]","The moment Max saw those words, his pupils contracted sharply.","Then, more information rapidly surfaced afterward.","Star Fist.","A Divine Ability capable of condensing the power of stars directly into one’s fists.","The stronger the user’s Divine Essence and physical body became, the more terrifying the destructive power of the Star Fist would grow.","At higher mastery levels, every punch could contain the weight and explosive force of collapsing stars themselves.","The information flooding through Max’s mind continued increasing afterward.","The Divine Ability did not merely strengthen punches normally.","Instead, it transformed the fists themselves into vessels capable of channeling pure stellar destruction.","The moment Star Fist was activated, Divine Essence would condense into miniature star-like cores inside the fists before exploding outward upon impact with terrifying destructive force.","The more Max understood the Divine Ability, the more shocked he became internally.","Because this Divine Ability—","Was perfectly compatible with his terrifying physical body.","Especially now that he possessed five thousand Draconic Essences, the Vein of Strength, and the newly awakened Vein of Speed.","If those powers were combined together with the Star Fist—","Even Max himself could already vaguely imagine how horrifying the result would become.","Meanwhile, after the inheritance process gradually stabilized, the dazzling golden light surrounding Max slowly disappeared.","The enormous amount of information flooding through his mind also gradually calmed afterward while the newly inherited Divine Ability settled deep within his consciousness completely.","Only then did Max slowly open his eyes once again.","The moment he opened them, a faint golden light briefly flashed through his pupils before disappearing completely.","Lady Virelia, who had been quietly observing everything from nearby, immediately looked toward him afterward.","\"What Divine Ability did you obtain?\" she asked calmly, although curiosity was clearly visible within her eyes.","After all, even she herself had never known what exact Divine Ability was sealed inside that Core Stone all these years.","Max slowly stood up afterward before answering honestly.","\"It is called Tier 3 Divine Ability called Star Fist.\"","The moment those words entered her ears, Lady Virelia’s expression immediately changed slightly.","\"Star Fist?\" she repeated softly.","Then, after briefly sensing the aura surrounding Max now, she suddenly let out a slow breath of relief.","A faint smile gradually appeared across her face afterward.","\"It seems I truly made the correct choice by giving that Divine Ability Core Stone to you,\" she said calmly.","Max looked slightly curious after hearing that.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia slowly shook her head lightly before continuing.","\"Star Fist is clearly a Divine Ability designed specifically for close combat physical fighters.\"","Her gaze slowly swept across Max’s body afterward.","\"The stronger the physical body, the more terrifying the Divine Ability becomes.\"","Then she sighed softly afterward.","\"If I had absorbed that Divine Ability for myself years ago, it would likely have been wasted completely.\"","A faint helpless smile appeared across her face.","\"After all, I was never a close combat cultivator.\"","\"My fighting style has always focused more upon long-range Divine Essence techniques and battlefield control.\"","Lady Virelia then looked directly toward Max once again.","\"But you are different.\"","Her eyes gradually brightened slightly afterward.","\"With your monstrous physical body, and the terrifying close combat abilities you already possess...\"","A faint look of anticipation appeared within her eyes.","\"The Star Fist Divine Ability will become far more terrifying in your hands than it ever could have in mine.\"","Hearing that, even Max himself slowly nodded internally.","He could already vaguely feel it as well.","The Star Fist Divine Ability truly suited him perfectly.","After sensing the terrifying potential hidden within the Star Fist Divine Ability, Max slowly raised his head toward Lady Virelia once again.","Genuine gratitude could clearly be seen within his eyes now.","\"Thank you, Master,\" Max said seriously. \"This Divine Ability is far too valuable.\"","He understood very clearly just how precious something like a Divine Ability truly was within the Divine Realm.","Even major powers treated such things as priceless inheritances.","Yet Lady Virelia had willingly handed the Divine Ability Core Stone over to him without hesitation.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia simply waved her hand lightly afterward.","\"There is no need to thank me for something like this,\" she replied calmly.","A faint smile gradually appeared across her face afterward.","\"If a treasure is simply left unused forever, then it has no meaning.\"","Her gaze slowly focused upon Max once again.","\"And compared to me, you clearly possess far greater potential.\"","Then her expression gradually became thoughtful afterward.","\"Besides...\"","A strange light flashed briefly within her eyes.","\"There is actually a possibility that you may obtain even more Divine Abilities during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment those words entered his ears, Max’s expression immediately changed completely.","\"What?\" Max asked instinctively.","Even he could not completely hide the shock within his voice this time.","After all, based on everything Lady Virelia explained earlier, Divine Abilities were supposed to be extremely rare treasures throughout the Divine Realm.","Yet now—","She was saying he might actually obtain more of them during the Cosmic Ascension Conference?","Meanwhile, seeing Max’s reaction, Lady Virelia smiled faintly afterward.","\"It is not impossible,\" she explained calmly.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference is far more extraordinary than you currently imagine.\"","Her eyes gradually became deeper afterward.","\"That place gathers not only countless monstrous geniuses but also unimaginable inheritances, opportunities, treasures, and ancient legacies left behind by terrifying existences from countless eras.\"","Lady Virelia slowly leaned back in her chair while continuing.","\"Throughout history, there have been people who obtained Divine Abilities during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","\"Some inherited them from ancient ruins.\"","\"Others awakened them through inheritances.\"","\"And a few lucky monsters directly obtained Divine Ability Core Stones themselves.\"","The more Max listened, the more serious his expression gradually became.","At that moment, he finally began realizing once again just how enormous and terrifying the Cosmic Ascension Conference truly was.","Meanwhile, Lady Virelia calmly looked toward him before speaking once more.","\"That is why the Cosmic Ascension Conference is viewed as the greatest opportunity for the younger generation throughout the Divine Realm.\"","Then a faint smile slowly appeared across her face afterward.","\"And with your talent...\"","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","\"You may very well become one of the greatest beneficiaries there.\""]},{"number":1687,"title":"Chapter 1687: Three Months of More Training!","paragraphs":["After hearing everything regarding the Cosmic Ascension Conference and the possibilities hidden within it, Max’s eyes gradually became brighter and brighter.","At that moment, even his anticipation toward the conference itself increased tremendously.","Divine Abilities.","Ancient inheritances.","Countless monstrous geniuses.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference was clearly far more extraordinary than he initially imagined.","Meanwhile, Max slowly looked toward Lady Virelia once again before speaking seriously,","\"I will do my best during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","A sharp determination gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"And I will not disappoint you, Master.\"","The confidence within his voice was extremely obvious.","After everything he had gained recently, Max’s ambitions toward the Cosmic Ascension Conference had already risen far beyond simply entering the top one thousand.","He wanted to stand at the very peak.","Meanwhile, after hearing his response, Lady Virelia slowly nodded in satisfaction.","A faint smile appeared across her face afterward.","\"Good,\" she replied calmly.","Then her gaze slowly shifted toward Max’s fists briefly before continuing,","\"Since you have already inherited the Star Fist Divine Ability, you should focus properly on mastering it before the Cosmic Ascension Conference begins.\"","Her expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"Divine Abilities are not ordinary techniques. Even if you inherit them successfully, fully mastering them still requires tremendous practice and comprehension.\"","Lady Virelia then added calmly,","\"Especially for a close combat Divine Ability like Star Fist, compatibility with your physical body and battle instincts will matter greatly.\"","A faint meaningful look appeared within her eyes afterward.","\"But considering your monstrous physique, I believe this Divine Ability will suit you perfectly.\"","Max nodded seriously after hearing that.","Naturally, he also understood how important it was to familiarize himself with the Star Fist Divine Ability before the conference began.","The stronger he became beforehand, the greater his chances would be during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Eventually, Lady Virelia lightly waved her hand afterward.","\"Alright,\" she said calmly. \"You may leave now.\"","\"Use the remaining three months wisely.\"","Max slowly stood up afterward before respectfully bowing lightly toward her once again.","Then, without wasting any further time, he turned around and left Lady Virelia’s office completely.","At that moment, only a single thought remained within his mind.","He needed to master the Star Fist Divine Ability before the Cosmic Ascension Conference finally began.","After returning back to his room, Max did not waste even a single moment.","The instant he entered the training chamber once again, he immediately activated the Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Space distorted faintly around him while dense dimensional fluctuations spread throughout the room.","The next moment, Max directly entered the Dimension of Time.","Since there were still three entire months remaining before the Cosmic Ascension Conference officially began, Max naturally had no intention of wasting such precious time.","The moment he entered the endless training world inside the Dimension of Time, the atmosphere around him instantly became incomparably solemn.","Everything afterward revolved around cultivation and training.","Max began spending nearly all of his time inside the Dimension of Time continuously mastering everything he had recently obtained.","The Star Fist Divine Ability.","The Saint Origin Sword Art.","The Vein of Speed.","The newly reached tenth level of the Law Awakening Realm.","And even the power of the Dimension of Soul.","Every single one of those powers required enormous amounts of practice and comprehension before they could truly become part of Max’s combat strength completely.","Because of that, Max practically isolated himself inside the Dimension of Time entirely.","Days passed outside.","Meanwhile, inside the Dimension of Time, far greater amounts of time continuously flowed by.","Boom!!!","Again and again, terrifying shockwaves echoed throughout the endless training world.","Sometimes Max practiced the Star Fist Divine Ability endlessly while condensing terrifying stellar power into his fists. Every punch caused the surrounding space to tremble violently while star-like explosions erupted throughout the Dimension of Time continuously.","Other times, he combined the Vein of Speed with the Saint Origin Sword Art, causing countless afterimages to appear throughout the training grounds while sword light split apart the surrounding world at terrifying speed.","Occasionally, Max also entered deep meditation while comprehending the mysteries of the Dimension of Soul and stabilizing his newly strengthened soul force.","Almost all of his time was spent training relentlessly.","However, despite focusing so heavily upon cultivation, Max still did not completely isolate himself from everyone else.","From time to time, he would temporarily leave the Dimension of Time and head toward the Dimension of Genesis.","There, he would spend some peaceful time together with Alice and Lenavira.","Sometimes they simply ate dinner together quietly.","Other times Alice endlessly complained about how boring cultivation was while Lenavira calmly listened nearby with a faint smile on her face.","Those moments became one of the few peaceful breaks Max allowed himself during those intense months of cultivation.","Meanwhile, Jonathan, Julie, and Isabella also occasionally entered the Dimension of Genesis throughout those three months.","The Crown itself gradually began developing slowly from the shadows.","Jonathan and Julie occasionally reported new information regarding possible future recruits while Isabella continuously expanded and improved the secret domain itself.","Whenever necessary, Max would briefly leave the Dimension of Time to meet with them and discuss matters regarding the Crown.","However, aside from those occasional meetings and brief moments spent together with Alice and Lenavira—","Max spent nearly all remaining time cultivating endlessly inside the Dimension of Time.","The closer the Cosmic Ascension Conference approached, the more terrifying Max’s training gradually became.","Time passed quietly.","Inside the Black Dragon Palace, nearly all disciples who participated in the Smelting Trial remained in closed-door cultivation continuously throughout those three months.","The atmosphere across the entire clan gradually became increasingly tense as the date of the Cosmic Ascension Conference drew closer and closer.","Everyone understood very clearly—","The coming conference would determine the future fate of countless geniuses throughout the Divine Realm.","Meanwhile, during those three months, Max almost completely disappeared from public sight.","Very few people within the Black Dragon Clan actually saw him during that period.","Most only occasionally heard terrifying shockwaves erupting from the training areas assigned to him or sensed frightening soul fluctuations spreading from his residence from time to time.","Inside the Dimension of Time, however—","An enormous amount of time had already passed for Max.","During those months, his strength continuously improved at a terrifying pace."]},{"number":1688,"title":"Chapter 1688: Day of the Cosmic Ascension Conference!","paragraphs":["The Star Fist Divine Ability gradually became increasingly mastered under his relentless training. By the end of those months, every punch Max unleashed carried terrifying stellar force capable of distorting the surrounding space itself.","The Vein of Speed also became completely integrated into his combat style. His movements had become so fast that ordinary cultivators at the same level could no longer properly follow his figure with their eyes.","Meanwhile, his comprehension of the Saint Origin Sword Art deepened continuously as well.","At times, Max remained inside the Dimension of Time for what felt like years entirely focused upon a single sword movement or a single circulation pathway of the Star Fist Divine Ability.","The closer the Cosmic Ascension Conference approached, the more terrifying his aura gradually became.","At the same time, the Crown also slowly continued developing quietly within the shadows.","Jonathan and Julie successfully brought several trustworthy individuals into contact with the organization while Isabella continued expanding the Dimension of Genesis steadily.","Although the Crown remained extremely small compared to the major powers of the Divine Realm, its foundations had finally begun forming properly.","And then—","Before anyone truly realized it—","Three entire months passed by in what felt like the blink of an eye.","Finally—","The day of the Cosmic Ascension Conference arrived.","On that day, the atmosphere throughout the entire Black Dragon Palace completely changed.","Countless disciples and elders gathered together while enormous excitement and tension filled the surroundings completely.","Even the sky above the clan seemed unusually solemn.","Because everyone knew—","The greatest gathering of geniuses within the Divine Realm was finally about to begin.","Max finally left the Dimension of Time after completing another long session of cultivation.","The moment he stepped back into reality, the terrifying aura surrounding him gradually calmed once again. However, compared to three months ago, the current Max felt vastly different.","His Divine Essence had become incomparably denser.","The pressure released unconsciously from his body had also become much heavier.","Most importantly—","His eyes themselves now carried a faint sharpness capable of making ordinary cultivators feel pressure instinctively merely by looking at him.","After stabilizing his aura briefly, Max once again entered the Dimension of Genesis.","Since the Cosmic Ascension Conference was finally about to begin, he wanted to meet Alice and Lenavira one final time before departing.","Soon afterward, Max arrived at the living area inside the Dimension of Genesis where the two of them were staying.","The moment Alice noticed him approaching, her eyes immediately brightened.","\"You finally came out of training again,\" she complained while quickly walking toward him. \"At this point I was starting to think you planned to stay inside the Dimension of Time forever.\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira also smiled gently afterward while looking toward Max quietly.","Compared to before, even the two of them could clearly sense how much stronger Max had become during these three months.","Max chuckled lightly after hearing Alice complain once again.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference is finally starting,\" he replied calmly. \"Naturally, I had to prepare properly.\"","Then a faint smile slowly appeared across his face afterward.","\"Actually, I came here today because I want the two of you to meet several special individuals.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Alice immediately became curious again.","\"Special individuals?\" she repeated quickly.","Even Lenavira looked toward Max with slight interest afterward.","Max nodded lightly.","\"They are people I care for them the most these days.\"","His eyes gradually became more thoughtful afterward.","\"They will become very important to us in the future.\"","Alice immediately narrowed her eyes suspiciously afterward.","\"Are these the same mysterious people you kept refusing to tell us about before?\" she asked quickly.","Max only smiled calmly afterward.","\"You will know soon enough.\"","Alice immediately pouted again after hearing that answer.","\"You really enjoy keeping secrets,\" she muttered unhappily.","Meanwhile, Lenavira quietly smiled from the side while observing the two of them.","Clearly, she already understood that Max intentionally wanted the meeting itself to become a surprise.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"Come with me,\" he said calmly while looking toward Alice and Lenavira.","The two of them immediately became curious after hearing that.","However, before either of them could ask further questions, Max suddenly raised both hands and lightly touched their shoulders.","The next instant—","Space around them distorted violently.","Dense dimensional fluctuations erupted instantly while countless silver-blue runes spread throughout the surroundings.","Then—","The surrounding world disappeared completely.","Alice and Lenavira immediately felt the space around their bodies shifting rapidly as though they were crossing through countless layers of dimensions at once.","Only a brief moment later—","The distortion finally stopped.","And the three of them appeared inside an entirely different world.","The moment Alice and Lenavira opened their eyes fully afterward, both of them became completely stunned.","\"This...\" Alice muttered blankly.","Even Lenavira’s calm expression visibly froze slightly.","Because the world before them looked absolutely magical.","The sky above shimmered with countless streams of colorful spiritual light while enormous floating islands drifted peacefully throughout the heavens one after another.","Some islands were covered in vast forests glowing faintly with spiritual energy.","Others contained waterfalls flowing directly through the sky itself before scattering into glowing mist beneath the floating lands.","Countless spirit birds flew freely throughout the heavens while dense spiritual energy filled every corner of the world so heavily that merely breathing felt refreshing.","Massive spirit trees towered throughout the distant islands while rivers of pure spiritual energy flowed through portions of the world like glowing silver streams.","The entire Dimension of Spirit resembled a divine paradise existing beyond reality itself.","At that moment, even Alice completely forgot how to speak properly for several seconds.","\"This place...\" she muttered while staring around in disbelief. \"What exactly is this place?!\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira’s eyes continuously swept across the floating islands and endless spiritual scenery around them while shock filled her gaze completely.","Even she had never seen a world this beautiful before.","The dense spiritual energy present here alone far surpassed most cultivation holy lands.","Then suddenly, Alice pointed upward excitedly.","\"There are islands floating in the sky!\"","Her voice carried complete astonishment.","\"And look over there! Even the waterfalls are floating!\"","Meanwhile, Max simply smiled faintly while observing their reactions quietly.","Clearly, he already expected them to react this way.","After all, the Dimension of Spirit truly looked like a fantasy world created from dreams itself."]},{"number":1689,"title":"Chapter 1689: Cute Vormir!","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, as Alice and Lenavira were still staring around the magical Dimension of Spirit in complete shock, several figures suddenly began approaching rapidly from the distance.","The first thing Alice noticed was a small black dragon flying proudly through the air.","The little dragon possessed glossy black scales that reflected faint purple light beneath the sky while tiny horns curved slightly upward atop his head. His movements carried obvious arrogance while his tiny chest remained puffed up proudly the entire time.","Behind him floated a small red-haired girl who looked around five years old.","Her crimson hair fluttered gently behind her while her large bright eyes radiated pure innocence and curiosity. The little girl wore a beautiful white dress while dense spiritual energy unconsciously flowed around her body continuously.","At the same time, another spirit floated calmly nearby.","Unlike the red-haired little girl, this spirit appeared older, around ten years old. She possessed long silver-black hair and deep dark eyes while strange devouring aura occasionally flickered around her quietly.","The moment Alice and Lenavira saw the three approaching, both immediately became stunned again.","However—","The instant the red-haired little girl noticed Max, her eyes immediately brightened.","\"Father!\"","The little girl instantly rushed toward Max happily before directly hugging him tightly.","The moment Alice and Lenavira heard that word, both of them froze completely.","\"Father?\" Alice repeated blankly while staring at Max.","Even Lenavira looked genuinely shocked now.","Meanwhile, Max himself coughed awkwardly afterward.","\"Yes... there is a reason for that,\" he muttered helplessly.","However, before he could explain properly, Alice immediately narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","\"A reason?\" she repeated slowly. \"You suddenly have a child now and you are saying there is a reason?\"","Meanwhile, the little red-haired girl tilted her head cutely afterward while hugging Max tightly.","Max immediately sighed afterward before beginning his explanation.","\"Lily is not actually my daughter,\" he said helplessly. \"She is a spirit.\"","Then he lightly patted the little girl’s head while continuing.","\"She was born from my blood and spiritual origin, so she naturally formed a connection with me.\"","Max’s expression became increasingly awkward afterward.","\"That is why she calls me father.\"","Alice and Lenavira slowly blinked afterward while processing that explanation.","Meanwhile, Lily continued clinging happily to Max without caring about the situation at all.","Then suddenly, Max remembered something else.","\"Actually...\" he muttered awkwardly, \"when she was first born, she did not call me father.\"","Alice immediately became curious again.","\"Then what did she call you?\"","Max’s face twitched slightly afterward.","\"She called me mother.\"","The moment those words fell—","Alice instantly burst into laughter.","\"Hahahaha!\"","Even Lenavira, who normally remained calm and graceful, could not stop herself from laughing softly afterward.","The image of Max being called \"mother\" by a little spirit was simply too ridiculous.","Meanwhile, Max himself looked completely helpless.","\"It was not my fault,\" he muttered defensively. \"She had just been born at that time.\"","Meanwhile, Lily tilted her head innocently afterward.","\"Father, who are these two?\" she asked curiously while looking toward Alice and Lenavira.","The moment she asked that, Max casually replied without thinking too much.","\"They are your two future mothers.\"","Silence instantly fell afterward.","Then—","Lily’s eyes immediately brightened completely.","\"Mothers!\"","Before Alice and Lenavira could react properly, Lily instantly rushed toward them happily.","Alice immediately became flustered afterward.","\"W-Wait—!\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira’s face also became slightly red unexpectedly.","However, Lily completely ignored their reactions while hugging both of them happily.","\"Mothers!\" she repeated excitedly once again.","Meanwhile, while all attention completely focused upon Lily, the little black dragon nearby gradually became dissatisfied.","The proud little dragon immediately puffed out his chest proudly afterward before flying directly before Alice and Lenavira.","\"Ahem!\"","He deliberately coughed loudly while spreading his tiny wings arrogantly.","Clearly, he was trying very hard to attract their attention as well.","After all, he considered himself extremely majestic and handsome.","Surely these two women would immediately praise him afterward.","However—","Neither Alice nor Lenavira even looked at him.","Both remained completely focused upon the adorable Lily instead.","\"Awww, she is too cute...\"","Alice muttered while patting Lily’s head happily.","Meanwhile, Lenavira gently smiled while speaking softly to the little spirit as well.","The little black dragon froze completely afterward.","Then his expression instantly darkened.","He immediately flew around them several times dramatically while releasing tiny draconic roars proudly.","Still—","Nobody paid attention to him.","At that moment, the little dragon finally became completely devastated.","\"Big Brother Max!\"","Vormir immediately flew toward Max afterward while shouting angrily.","\"They are ignoring me!\"","His tiny dragon face looked completely aggrieved.","\"I am clearly much cooler than Lily!\"","Meanwhile, Max almost laughed seeing the little dragon’s devastated expression.","However, before he could say anything, Alice casually replied while continuing to play with Lily,","\"You are cute too.\"","The moment those words entered Vormir’s ears, the little black dragon froze again.","Cute?","Not majestic?","Not mighty?","Cute?","At that moment, Vormir looked completely heartbroken.","Meanwhile, the atmosphere throughout the Dimension of Spirit gradually became increasingly lively afterward.","Lily remained completely attached to Alice and Lenavira almost instantly as though she had already known them for years.","The little spirit continuously talked excitedly while holding both of their hands happily.","\"Mother Alice, your hair is really pretty!\"","\"And Mother Lenavira smells really nice too!\"","The innocent words coming from Lily immediately caused both Alice and Lenavira to become slightly embarrassed once again.","Especially every single time Lily called them \"mother.\"","Meanwhile, Alice eventually gave up trying to correct her entirely.","Instead, she simply sighed helplessly while patting Lily’s head affectionately.","\"You really are too adorable,\" Alice muttered while smiling brightly.","Meanwhile, Lenavira’s usually calm expression had also softened greatly.","The gentle way Lily clung to them made it genuinely difficult not to become fond of her almost immediately.","Soon afterward, the three of them gradually began chatting happily together.","Lily excitedly explained countless random things about the Dimension of Spirit while continuously dragging Alice and Lenavira around energetically.","At one moment, she proudly introduced the floating islands.","The next moment, she talked about spirit rivers and magical fruits growing throughout the Dimension of Spirit.","Meanwhile, Alice and Lenavira listened patiently while occasionally laughing at Lily’s endless excitement.","The entire scene felt unusually warm and peaceful.","However—","Not far away—","A certain proud little black dragon sat completely alone atop a floating rock.","Vormir looked utterly devastated.","His tiny dragon wings drooped lifelessly while he stared toward the happily chatting group with a deeply wounded expression.","\"They completely ignored me...\" he muttered heartbrokenly.","At that moment, the proud little dragon genuinely could not understand reality anymore.","Clearly, he was majestic.","Clearly, he was cool.","Clearly, he was a mighty black dragon.","So why—","Why was all attention focused entirely upon Lily instead?","Meanwhile, the conversation between Alice, Lenavira, and Lily only became increasingly lively.","\"Mother Alice, Father is actually really boring when he trains,\" Lily whispered secretly.","Alice immediately laughed afterward.","\"I can already tell.\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira smiled softly while asking Lily more questions about life inside the Dimension of Spirit.","Not a single person remembered Vormir still existed nearby.","The little dragon immediately became even more depressed afterward.","Then finally—","Unable to endure it anymore—","Vormir slowly turned toward Max nearby with an aggrieved expression.","\"Big Brother Max...\" he muttered weakly.","His tiny dragon eyes looked almost ready to cry.","\"They do not appreciate dragons at all.\"","Meanwhile, Max finally could not hold back his laughter anymore after seeing Vormir’s utterly defeated appearance."]},{"number":1690,"title":"Chapter 1690: A Small Gathering!","paragraphs":["A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face while quietly watching the lively scene before him.","Alice and Lenavira had already completely become immersed in playing together with Lily and Mimi.","Meanwhile, Mimi, who normally remained calm and somewhat distant, had also gradually relaxed around the two of them. Although she still spoke far less compared to Lily, even she occasionally revealed faint smiles while talking with Alice and Lenavira.","The peaceful atmosphere throughout the floating islands felt unusually warm.","For a brief moment, Max simply stood there quietly while watching them.","Then eventually, he slowly spoke once again.","\"There is actually something important I should tell the two of you.\"","The moment those words entered their ears, Alice and Lenavira both looked toward him curiously.","Meanwhile, Lily remained sitting happily beside Alice while Mimi quietly floated nearby.","Max calmly continued afterward.","\"I already connected the Dimension of Genesis with the Dimension of Spirit.\"","The moment those words were spoken, both Alice and Lenavira became slightly surprised.","Max then explained further.","\"From now onward, the two of you can freely move between both dimensions whenever you want.\"","His gaze slowly swept across the surroundings afterward.","\"If you become bored staying in one place, you may simply travel to the other dimension freely.\"","A faint smile appeared across his face afterward.","\"There are no restrictions anymore.\"","After hearing that explanation, Alice’s eyes immediately brightened.","\"Really?\" she asked excitedly.","Clearly, she was extremely happy hearing that.","Meanwhile, Lenavira also nodded lightly afterward.","\"That will make things much easier,\" she said softly.","Then Alice suddenly waved her hand dismissively toward Max afterward.","\"Alright, alright,\" she said while shooing him away jokingly. \"Now stop worrying about us so much.\"","Her expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"You should focus properly on the Cosmic Ascension Conference instead.\"","Meanwhile, Lenavira also looked toward him calmly before nodding gently.","\"She is right,\" Lenavira said softly. \"You have already prepared for this conference for a very long time.\"","Her eyes gradually softened afterward.","\"So do not waste your attention worrying about us here.\"","Lily immediately nodded seriously afterward as well.","\"Father must become super strong!\" she declared confidently.","Even Mimi quietly nodded in agreement nearby.","Seeing all of them looking toward him like that, Max could not help but smile faintly once again.","At that moment, the warm atmosphere inside the Dimension of Spirit quietly eased much of the pressure buried deep within his heart before the coming Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Max quietly looked toward the four of them for several moments afterward.","Alice.","Lenavira.","Lily.","Mimi.","And even the still somewhat depressed Vormir sitting nearby.","A faint warmth gradually spread through his heart while watching the peaceful scene before him.","Then eventually, Max slowly nodded.","\"I understand,\" he said calmly.","A sharp yet confident light gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"I will do my best during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","His voice was not loud, yet it carried unquestionable determination.","After all, the Cosmic Ascension Conference was not merely an opportunity for him anymore.","It was the beginning of everything.","The beginning of his rise within the Divine Realm.","The beginning of the Crown’s future.","And the beginning of the path that would eventually lead him toward the Elf Race and the truth regarding his parents.","Meanwhile, after hearing his response, Alice smiled brightly afterward.","\"That is more like it,\" she said proudly.","Lenavira also gently nodded while looking toward him quietly.","Meanwhile, Lily immediately raised her tiny fist excitedly.","\"Father will definitely become the strongest!\" she declared confidently.","Even Mimi softly nodded from the side in agreement.","As for Vormir—","The little black dragon finally regained some of his spirit afterward.","\"Hmph,\" he muttered proudly while lifting his head again. \"Big Brother Max naturally cannot lose to anyone.\"","Hearing that, Max could not help but chuckle lightly.","Then, after one final glance toward everyone, Max slowly turned around.","The next moment, dimensional fluctuations quietly spread around his body.","Before leaving completely, Max spoke one final sentence calmly.","\"Wait for me to return.\"","Soon afterward, his figure gradually disappeared from the Dimension of Spirit altogether, leaving behind the peaceful floating world once again.","Once Max left the Dimension of Spirit, he directly returned back to his residence inside the Black Dragon Palace.","The moment he stepped outside his house, he immediately noticed that the atmosphere throughout the palace had become completely different compared to before.","Almost all disciples of the Black Dragon Palace had already gathered together within the enormous hall outside the residential area.","The expressions on everyone’s faces carried obvious excitement, nervousness, and anticipation.","After all—","Today was finally the day the Cosmic Ascension Conference would officially begin.","Meanwhile, many disciples also quickly noticed Max’s arrival.","The moment they sensed the terrifying aura unconsciously leaking from his body, numerous people immediately revealed solemn expressions.","Clearly, after three months of secluded cultivation, Max had become even more frightening than before.","At the same time, Lucia and Isabella also arrived nearby shortly afterward.","Then suddenly—","A terrifying pressure descended throughout the entire hall.","Boom!!!","The surrounding air trembled faintly while countless disciples instinctively straightened their backs.","The next moment, a tall middle-aged man slowly descended from the sky before everyone.","The man possessed sharp eyes and an imposing aura while terrifying Divine Essence fluctuations surrounded him naturally.","The moment many disciples saw him, their expressions immediately became respectful.","One of the Seven Family Heads of the Black Dragon Clan.","Mathew Grimes.","At that moment, Mathew Grimes calmly swept his gaze across the gathered disciples before speaking slowly.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference is finally beginning.\"","His deep voice echoed clearly throughout the enormous hall.","The expressions of countless disciples immediately became serious afterward.","Meanwhile, Mathew Grimes continued calmly,","\"All of you standing here are the younger generation geniuses selected by the Black Dragon Clan to participate in the greatest gathering within the Divine Realm.\"","His sharp gaze slowly swept across everyone afterward.","\"The conference this time will determine not only your personal future but also the future standing and reputation of our Black Dragon Clan.\"","The atmosphere throughout the hall gradually became increasingly solemn.","Then Mathew Grimes suddenly added something else.","\"Naturally, the clan will not treat your efforts unfairly.\"","The moment those words were spoken, many disciples immediately focused their attention completely upon him.","\"The better your ranking during the Cosmic Ascension Conference, the greater the rewards you will receive afterward from the Black Dragon Clan.\"","A faint pressure gradually spread from his body afterward.","\"If anyone manages to achieve an extraordinary ranking, the clan will reward that person heavily.\"","The moment those words entered everyone’s ears, many disciples immediately became excited.","After all, rewards from one of the Seven Families of the Black Dragon Clan would naturally not be ordinary.","Meanwhile, Max silently listened from the side calmly.","Then Mathew Grimes eventually continued explaining the conference itself.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference will be held inside the Eternal Hourglass.\"","The moment those words were spoken, many disciples immediately became attentive again.","\"Once all participating geniuses throughout the Divine Realm gather within the Eternal Hourglass, the conference itself will officially begin.\"","Then Mathew Grimes calmly looked toward everyone once again.","\"As for what all of you need to do now, it is simple.\"","His voice remained calm yet authoritative."]},{"number":1691,"title":"Chapter 1691: Start of the Cosmic Ascension Conference!","paragraphs":["\"You will head toward your assigned houses of lodging and remain there quietly.\"","\"There is no need for anyone to move around recklessly.\"","\"When the Cosmic Ascension Conference officially begins...\"","A faint mysterious look appeared within his eyes afterward.","\"You will naturally know what to do.\"","After Mathew Grimes finished speaking, the enormous hall gradually became noisy once again.","Clearly, many disciples still looked confused after hearing his explanation regarding the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Remain inside their residences?","And simply wait there?","How exactly were they supposed to participate in the conference like that?","Numerous disciples quietly began discussing among themselves afterward while slowly leaving the hall one after another.","\"I still do not understand this at all,\" one disciple muttered with a frown. \"How are we supposed to participate in the Cosmic Ascension Conference by staying inside our lodgings?\"","Another disciple nearby also nodded helplessly afterward.","\"Exactly. I originally thought we would directly enter the Eternal Hourglass somehow.\"","\"Maybe the Eternal Hourglass itself will summon everyone automatically once the conference begins?\" someone else guessed uncertainly.","\"That should not be impossible,\" another disciple added thoughtfully. \"After all, that treasure is one of the legendary Five Primal Treasures.\"","Meanwhile, several younger disciples looked increasingly nervous the more they talked.","\"I heard trillions of geniuses participate in every Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","\"Forget trillions,\" another disciple muttered bitterly. \"I am more worried about surviving at all after hearing about the monsters participating from the higher realms.\"","\"I just hope I can survive long enough to gain some opportunities.\"","Various similar conversations continuously spread throughout the surroundings as disciples slowly returned toward their assigned residences.","Meanwhile, Max quietly walked away from the hall together with Lucia and Isabella.","The atmosphere around the three of them remained much calmer compared to the noisy discussions nearby.","After walking silently for some time, Max eventually looked toward the two women beside him before speaking calmly,","\"Do your best during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","His expression gradually became more serious afterward.","\"This conference will likely become one of the greatest opportunities we encounter within the Divine Realm.\"","Lucia immediately snorted lightly afterward.","\"You make it sound as though we planned to slack off,\" she replied while folding her arms proudly.","However, despite her confident tone, seriousness could still be seen within her eyes.","Clearly, even she understood how important the Cosmic Ascension Conference truly was.","Meanwhile, Isabella also softly nodded afterward.","\"We understand,\" she replied calmly.","Then her gaze shifted briefly toward Max afterward.","\"You should focus on yourself as well.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across her face afterward.","\"After all, with your personality, I would not be surprised if you end up causing chaos throughout the entire conference.\"","Hearing that, even Lucia immediately laughed lightly afterward.","Meanwhile, Max simply smiled faintly without denying it at all.","At that moment, although none of them fully knew what awaited them inside the Eternal Hourglass—","All three clearly understood one thing.","The moment the Cosmic Ascension Conference officially began—","Everything throughout the Divine Realm would change.","Soon afterward, Max said his goodbyes to Lucia and Isabella before finally returning back to his assigned residence.","At that moment, the entire Black Dragon Palace had already gradually become quiet once again.","Almost every disciple had returned to their lodgings while silently waiting for the Cosmic Ascension Conference to officially begin.","Meanwhile, after entering his room, Max directly sat down cross-legged inside the training chamber before entering meditation quietly.","Dense Divine Essence slowly circulated throughout his body while his mind gradually became completely calm.","Time slowly passed afterward.","One hour.","Then another.","It was not until roughly two hours later—","That something suddenly happened.","Buzz!!!","Without any warning whatsoever, the entire space surrounding Max suddenly trembled violently.","The next instant, a massive beam of golden light descended directly from above.","The dazzling golden light instantly engulfed Max completely before he could even properly react.","At the same time, terrifying spatial fluctuations exploded throughout the surroundings.","Then—","Everything around him disappeared completely.","The training chamber vanished.","The Black Dragon Palace disappeared.","Even the entire Verdant Sky Star Realm itself seemed to fade away instantly.","Only endless golden light remained.","The transportation process lasted only briefly.","Then suddenly—","The golden light surrounding Max finally disappeared.","The moment Max opened his eyes once again afterward, he immediately realized he had already arrived in an entirely different place.","At that moment, he stood outside an enormous ancient castle.","The gigantic castle towered into the heavens like a divine fortress while ancient golden runes covered its massive walls endlessly. Dense ancient aura spread from the castle continuously while countless streams of golden light drifted throughout the sky above it.","Meanwhile, outside the enormous castle existed a vast open area large enough to contain entire cities.","And most importantly—","Max quickly realized he was not alone.","Thousands upon thousands of figures already filled the surroundings completely.","The atmosphere throughout the area felt extremely chaotic.","However, what immediately caught Max’s attention was the races gathered there.","Humans naturally occupied a large portion of the crowd.","But aside from humans—","The demon race clearly possessed the greatest number of participants present there.","Everywhere Max looked, demons could easily be seen throughout the enormous gathering.","Most possessed dark black skin while terrifying demonic aura continuously spread from their bodies naturally. Two horns curved upward from their heads while many demons also possessed strange crimson eyes glowing faintly beneath the ancient golden light surrounding the castle.","Some demons carried gigantic weapons on their backs.","Others simply stood silently while releasing overwhelming pressure.","The sheer number of demon race geniuses gathered there honestly felt astonishing.","\"It really includes geniuses from all over the Divine Realm,\" Max muttered softly while observing the enormous number of demons gathered throughout the surroundings.","At that moment, his gaze slowly swept across the vast crowd once again.","The Divine Realm was simply far too enormous.","Humans alone could never dominate every star realm within such an immeasurable world.","Aside from humanity, the Demon Race and the Elf Race also occupied countless territories and powerful star realms throughout the Divine Realm.","Naturally, since the Cosmic Ascension Conference encompassed the entirety of the Divine Realm itself, it was only normal for geniuses from those races to appear here as well.","Meanwhile, the demonic aura spreading throughout portions of the crowd honestly felt extremely oppressive.","Some demons radiated violent killing intent naturally.","Others stood silently while terrifying pressure distorted the surrounding air faintly around them.","Clearly, none of the individuals gathered here were ordinary.","At the same time, while Max silently observed the surroundings, something suddenly happened.","Buzz!!!","The sky above the enormous castle suddenly trembled violently.","The next moment, countless golden runes appeared throughout the heavens one after another before rapidly gathering together.","Then suddenly—","An enormous timer materialized high above everyone’s heads.","[59 Seconds]","[58 Seconds]","[57 Seconds]","The gigantic golden numbers floated throughout the sky while radiating ancient pressure continuously.","The moment the timer appeared, the atmosphere throughout the entire gathering changed instantly.","Originally, countless conversations and discussions filled the surroundings.","However now—","Almost everyone gradually became silent.","Because every participant immediately understood something.","Once that timer reached zero—","The Cosmic Ascension Conference would truly begin.","At that moment, even the surrounding demons gradually became more serious.","Countless sharp gazes lifted toward the timer floating high in the sky.","Meanwhile, Max himself also narrowed his eyes slightly afterward while silently watching the countdown continue decreasing.","[52 Seconds]","[51 Seconds]","[50 Seconds]","The pressure throughout the surroundings gradually became heavier and heavier.","Excitement.","Nervousness.","Anticipation.","Battle intent.","Countless emotions quietly spread throughout the enormous gathering while everyone waited for the timer to finally reach zero."]},{"number":1692,"title":"Chapter 1692: Complete Chaos!","paragraphs":["The enormous golden timer floating throughout the sky continued decreasing relentlessly.","[10 Seconds]","The atmosphere throughout the entire area became incomparably tense.","Countless geniuses silently stared upward while terrifying auras gradually leaked from their bodies uncontrollably.","[9 Seconds]","Some participants slowly took out their weapons.","Others quietly circulated their Divine Essence already.","[8 Seconds]","The surrounding demons released increasingly violent killing intent while numerous humans also revealed solemn expressions.","Everyone understood very clearly—","The moment the countdown ended, the true Cosmic Ascension Conference would officially begin.","[5 Seconds]","At that moment, the enormous gathering had already become completely silent.","Only the countdown remained visible throughout the heavens.","[4 Seconds]","[3 Seconds]","[2 Seconds]","[1 Second]","Then—","[0]","Boom!!!","The instant the timer reached zero, the entire heavens suddenly exploded with dazzling golden light.","At the same time, an ancient voice echoed throughout the entire world.","[The Cosmic Ascension Conference Has Officially Begun.]","The notification resounded directly within everyone’s minds simultaneously.","And the very next instant—","Chaos erupted.","Boom!!! Boom!!! Boom!!!","Terrifying explosions instantly exploded throughout the enormous gathering area.","Without even a moment of hesitation, countless geniuses directly attacked one another.","Sword light erupted everywhere.","Demonic flames exploded violently across the battlefield.","Gigantic weapons smashed through the ground continuously.","The peaceful gathering area from moments earlier instantly transformed into an absolute war zone.","Many weaker geniuses were caught completely off guard.","Some died before they could even properly react.","Others desperately attempted escaping while terrifying attacks rained throughout the surroundings endlessly.","Meanwhile, the demon race participants became especially violent.","Roars echoed throughout the battlefield while numerous demons charged directly into nearby groups like savage beasts.","Blood immediately began splattering throughout the surroundings.","Screams echoed everywhere.","Some participants formed temporary alliances instantly while others directly betrayed people standing beside them moments earlier.","The entire area became pure chaos.","Literal chaos.","At that moment, nobody cared about rules or morality anymore.","Everyone only had one thought remaining.","Survive.","Max’s eyes immediately sharpened afterward while observing the battlefield erupting around him.","Even he had not expected the Cosmic Ascension Conference to begin this brutally.","There were no explanations.","No introductions.","No peaceful beginning.","The conference simply started with slaughter.","Boom!!!","A gigantic demonic axe suddenly descended nearby and instantly crushed several participants into blood mist.","Meanwhile, another human genius unleashed thousands of sword lights throughout the crowd, directly tearing apart countless nearby enemies.","Everywhere Max looked—","People were killing each other.","The battlefield had completely descended into madness within mere seconds after the conference began.","\"This is only one part of the battlefield inside the Eternal Hourglass...\"","Max muttered softly while observing the absolute chaos erupting throughout the surroundings.","Terrifying explosions continuously echoed throughout the heavens while countless geniuses slaughtered one another without hesitation.","Blood stained the ground everywhere.","Sword lights split apart the sky.","Demonic flames and destructive Divine Essence attacks continuously exploded throughout the battlefield endlessly.","And this—","Was merely one section of the Eternal Hourglass.","At that moment, even Max could not help but feel slightly shocked internally.","Compared to this place, the Soul Sealing Painting honestly looked insignificant.","Meanwhile, just as Max calmly observed the battlefield around him, one of the nearby demons suddenly noticed him.","The demon possessed dark black skin and two thick crimson horns atop his head while violent demonic aura surged around his massive body continuously.","The moment the demon sensed Max’s cultivation at merely the peak of the Law Awakening Realm, his crimson eyes immediately flashed greedily.","Clearly, in his eyes, Max had become easy prey.","\"Hahaha! Die!\"","The demon roared loudly afterward while directly charging toward Max.","Boom!!!","The ground exploded beneath his feet while the gigantic battle axe within his hands radiated terrifying destructive power.","The enormous weapon tore through the air violently before smashing directly downward toward Max’s head.","The pressure released by the attack alone was enough to crush ordinary cultivators completely.","However, Max never moved.","His expression remained completely calm.","Then the instant the gigantic battle axe descended before him, Max suddenly raised one hand casually.","Boom!!!","A terrifying shockwave exploded outward instantly.","The surrounding ground shattered violently while nearby participants looked toward the scene in shock.","Because Max had directly grabbed the gigantic battle axe with his bare hand.","The terrifying demonic weapon stopped completely above his head.","The demon’s expression instantly froze afterward.","\"What?!\"","His crimson eyes widened completely in disbelief.","Clearly, he never imagined that someone would actually stop his full-powered axe strike using nothing but physical strength alone.","Meanwhile, Max slowly raised his head afterward.","A faint cold smile gradually appeared across his face.","\"You are too weak.\"","The next instant, Max directly unleashed a punch toward the demon’s chest.","Boom!!!","The terrifying power of the Star Fist Divine Ability instantly erupted completely.","A faint star-like glow condensed around Max’s fist before exploding outward violently upon impact.","The demon’s body immediately collapsed inward grotesquely.","Then another explosion echoed throughout the battlefield as his entire upper body exploded apart into blood mist instantly.","The gigantic demon died on the spot without even possessing the chance to scream properly.","At the same time, several golden notifications suddenly appeared before Max’s eyes.","[You Have Killed A Demon Race Participant.]","[Killing Points +100]","[Current Killing Points: 100]","The moment those notifications appeared, Max’s eyes narrowed slightly afterward.","\"Killing Points...\" he muttered thoughtfully.","Meanwhile, around him, the slaughter throughout the battlefield only continued becoming increasingly chaotic.","Max quietly looked toward the golden notifications floating before his eyes while slowly falling into thought.","Only one hundred Killing Points.","Clearly, the demon he killed earlier had not defeated many participants before targeting him.","Which meant one thing.","The stronger participants who survived longer and killed more people would naturally accumulate increasingly terrifying amounts of Killing Points over time.","The moment that realization surfaced within Max’s mind, a strange thought immediately appeared afterward.","\"Maybe I should simply let everyone kill each other first...\" Max muttered thoughtfully.","His eyes slowly swept across the chaotic battlefield surrounding him.","\"Once enough Killing Points gather onto certain individuals, I can simply sweep them all afterward.\"","Honestly, that seemed far more efficient than hunting weaker participants one after another himself.","Meanwhile, just as Max continued pondering this idea, a furious roar suddenly echoed from nearby.","\"You bastard! How dare you kill me?!\"","The voice exploded with overwhelming anger."]},{"number":1693,"title":"Chapter 1693: Three Lives!","paragraphs":["Max immediately turned toward the source of the shout afterward.","However, the moment he saw the figure rushing toward him, even he became slightly surprised.","Because the one charging toward him was actually the exact same demon he had just killed moments ago.","The same dark black skin.","The same crimson horns.","Even the gigantic battle axe remained identical.","At that moment, Max’s brows instantly furrowed slightly.","He was certain he had already blown apart the demon’s upper body completely earlier.","The demon should have been eliminated entirely.","Yet now—","He was standing there alive once again.","Meanwhile, the demon himself clearly looked completely enraged now.","\"You lowly human!\" the demon roared furiously while charging toward Max once again. \"I will split your body apart piece by piece!\"","Boom!!!","The gigantic battle axe tore through the air violently while demonic aura exploded outward once more.","However, Max no longer even bothered speaking this time.","The instant the demon approached him, star-like light instantly condensed around Max’s fist once again.","Then—","Boom!!!","Max directly unleashed another Star Fist toward the demon.","The terrifying stellar force exploded outward instantly.","The demon’s body once again exploded apart into blood mist completely without possessing the slightest ability to resist.","At the same time, another notification appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Killing Points +50]","[Current Killing Points: 150]","Seeing this, Max’s eyes narrowed slightly afterward.","Only fifty points this time.","Meanwhile, before Max could continue thinking further, his Dimensional Sovereign Body instinctively activated.","Invisible dimensional perception instantly spread throughout the enormous battlefield and beyond it.","The range of his senses rapidly expanded outward.","Then suddenly—","Max saw something.","Inside the enormous castle standing in the distance, the demon he had just killed moments ago had appeared once again.","Alive.","Completely unharmed.","The moment Max realized this, his expression immediately became thoughtful.","\"So that is how it works...\"","At that moment, everything finally became clear to him.","Participants did not truly die after being killed here.","Instead, they revived again inside the castle afterward.","The battlefield outside merely functioned as a giant slaughter zone where everyone continuously fought and stole Killing Points from one another.","However—","That realization immediately caused another question to appear within Max’s mind.","\"If participants revive after dying...\" Max muttered softly.","\"Then exactly how many times can one revive here?\"","Just as Max continued wondering about the revival rules of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, his eyes suddenly narrowed slightly.","Because unlike earlier, the demon he killed twice did not charge back toward the battlefield immediately after reviving.","Instead, the demon appeared extremely panicked.","The moment he revived inside the castle, he immediately began rushing away from the battlefield area entirely as though terrified of something.","Seeing this, a sharp light instantly flashed through Max’s eyes.","Then without hesitation, Max directly withdrew from the chaotic battlefield and silently followed after the fleeing demon.","With the Vein of Speed and Dimensional Sovereign Body assisting him, Max moved through the surroundings silently without attracting much attention at all.","Meanwhile, the demon continuously looked behind himself nervously while leaving the castle area rapidly.","Clearly, the previous two deaths had already completely shattered his confidence.","However, just as the demon finally believed he had escaped safely—","A figure suddenly appeared directly before him.","The demon’s body instantly froze afterward.","Because standing before him calmly was none other than Max himself.","\"You...\"","The demon’s crimson eyes widened completely in horror.","At that moment, his earlier arrogance had completely disappeared.","Instead, only fear remained.","Meanwhile, Max calmly looked toward him before speaking softly,","\"So you really do revive after dying.\"","The demon instinctively took several steps backward afterward.","\"No... no...\" he muttered panickedly.","Then suddenly, the demon hurriedly shouted,","\"Please do not kill me again!\"","The sudden begging honestly surprised Max slightly.","After all, moments earlier, this same demon had looked eager to split him apart with a battle axe.","Yet now—","He looked completely terrified.","Max calmly looked toward him afterward before asking,","\"And why exactly should I not kill you again?\"","The demon’s expression immediately became even uglier afterward.","Then, after hesitating briefly, he hurriedly explained,","\"All participants in the Cosmic Ascension Conference only possess three lives!\"","The moment those words entered Max’s ears, his eyes immediately sharpened slightly.","Meanwhile, the demon continued speaking rapidly in panic.","\"If someone dies once, they revive inside the castle.\"","\"If they die twice, they revive again.\"","\"But if they die all three times...\"","Fear completely filled the demon’s face afterward.","\"They will be truly eliminated from the Cosmic Ascension Conference forever!\"","The surroundings gradually became silent afterward.","Meanwhile, Max finally understood completely.","So that was the rule.","Every participant possessed only three total lives.","Once all three were exhausted—","Their participation in the Cosmic Ascension Conference would end permanently.","Just at that moment, Max suddenly seemed to think of something.","Then a faint sneer slowly appeared across his face.","\"Who exactly are you trying to fool here?\" Max asked while looking directly toward the demon.","The demon’s expression instantly stiffened afterward.","Meanwhile, Max slowly smiled afterward, although there was not the slightest warmth within that smile.","\"You said everyone only possesses three lives,\" Max continued calmly. \"But unfortunately for you...\"","A faint dangerous light gradually appeared within his eyes.","\"I still have no way of knowing whether that information is actually true or not.\"","The moment those words entered the demon’s ears, his face instantly turned pale.","Meanwhile, Max slowly continued walking toward him.","\"And since I am currently very curious about how the revival system truly works...\"","His smile gradually widened slightly afterward.","\"I suppose I will simply have to test it personally.\"","The demon immediately panicked completely afterward.","\"No! Wait!\"","He instinctively stepped backward repeatedly while fear completely filled his crimson eyes.","\"You already killed me twice! I am not lying!\"","However, Max no longer showed any interest in listening.","\"Sadly for you,\" Max replied calmly, \"you happened to become the perfect test subject.\"","The instant those words fell, the Vein of Speed activated instantly.","Boom!!!","The surrounding ground exploded violently.","Before the demon could even properly react, Max’s figure had already appeared directly before him.","The demon’s pupils contracted completely in horror.","\"So fast—!\"","He did not even finish speaking.","Boom!!!","Max directly unleashed another Star Fist toward the demon’s chest.","Terrifying stellar force exploded outward instantly.","This time, the demon’s entire body exploded apart completely into blood mist before even possessing the slightest chance to resist.","At the same time, another notification appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Killing Points +25]","[Current Killing Points: 175]","Meanwhile, Max’s gaze immediately shifted toward the enormous castle afterward.","Then, under the perception of the Dimensional Sovereign Body—","He saw it clearly.","The demon was once again revived inside the castle."]},{"number":1694,"title":"Chapter 1694: Four Times Killing Means True Death!","paragraphs":["Seeing this, Max finally understood clearly.","\"So that is how it works...\" Max muttered thoughtfully.","\"If everyone possesses three lives here, that means participants can die three separate times before being truly eliminated from the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across his face afterward.","At that moment, Max had finally grasped the true rules governing this battlefield.","Meanwhile, not far away, the revived demon looked completely terrified now.","The moment he revived inside the castle once again, he immediately began rushing toward the outer region desperately, clearly trying to escape from Max entirely.","However—","Boom!!!","Max’s figure suddenly blurred before disappearing instantly.","The next moment, he directly appeared before the fleeing demon once again.","The demon’s body froze completely afterward.","His crimson eyes widened in absolute horror.","\"No...\"","The demon instinctively stepped backward repeatedly while his entire body trembled visibly now.","Clearly, the previous deaths had already completely shattered his courage.","Meanwhile, Max calmly looked toward him silently.","That calm expression only made the demon even more terrified.","\"Please!\" the demon suddenly shouted desperately. \"Do not kill me again!\"","Fear completely filled his face afterward.","\"I was telling the truth! I swear I was not lying to you!\"","The demon’s voice even began trembling slightly now.","\"You already killed me three times! Please spare me just this once!\"","At that moment, the demon no longer possessed even the slightest arrogance from earlier.","He looked completely broken.","Meanwhile, Max simply observed him quietly without the slightest change in expression.","Then eventually, Max slowly spoke.","\"It seems your information was indeed correct.\"","The demon’s expression immediately brightened slightly afterward as though he had finally seen hope.","However, before he could say anything else—","Max’s eyes suddenly turned cold.","\"But unfortunately for you...\"","A faint star-like glow gradually condensed around Max’s fist once again.","\"I already decided to test it completely.\"","The moment those words entered the demon’s ears, absolute panic instantly filled his face.","\"No! Wait! Please!\"","The demon desperately tried turning around to escape.","However, it was already too late.","Boom!!!","The Vein of Speed activated instantly.","Before the demon could even properly move, Max had already appeared directly before him once again.","Then—","Boom!!!","The Star Fist Divine Ability erupted completely.","Terrifying stellar force exploded outward instantly before smashing directly into the demon’s chest.","The demon’s body exploded apart completely into blood mist without leaving behind even the slightest trace.","At the same time, another notification appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Killing Points +10]","[Current Killing Points: 185]","Then—","Silence.","This time, even after several moments passed—","The demon never revived again.","\"For one to truly die in this world...\"","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"They actually need to be killed four times in total.\"","At that moment, Max had finally completely understood the rules governing the battlefield outside the castle.","The first three deaths merely consumed lives.","Only the fourth death resulted in true elimination from the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Meanwhile, as this realization fully settled within his mind, another thought immediately surfaced afterward.","A dangerous thought.","\"This is actually a perfect way to farm Killing Points,\" Max muttered softly.","After all, every time someone was killed, Killing Points could still be earned from them.","Which meant participants could repeatedly hunt the same targets multiple times before eliminating them completely.","The more Max thought about it, the more absurd the rules of the Cosmic Ascension Conference appeared.","However—","If even Max could realize this method so quickly, then naturally other geniuses throughout the Eternal Hourglass would eventually realize it as well.","And once everyone understood this...","The battlefield would likely become even more terrifying than before.","At that moment, Max slowly lifted his gaze toward the enormous castle standing in the distance.","Countless participants continuously revived there before charging back into the battlefield again.","The atmosphere surrounding the castle honestly resembled a giant slaughterhouse.","\"Hehe...\"","Max suddenly laughed softly afterward.","\"This really is quite fun.\"","A sharp dangerous light gradually appeared within his eyes afterward.","Meanwhile, his gaze slowly swept across the enormous castle thoughtfully.","At that moment, Max genuinely began wondering something.","Had someone already started hunting everyone within one castle region repeatedly?","Had some monstrous genius already begun wiping out entire groups of participants to harvest enormous amounts of Killing Points?","The more Max thought about it, the more excited he gradually became.","Because if that truly happened—","Then this Cosmic Ascension Conference would become far more brutal and interesting than he originally imagined.","Max no longer wasted his time afterward.","The moment he finished understanding the rules of this battlefield, the Vein of Speed activated instantly.","Boom!!!","His figure blurred before disappearing from the ground completely.","The next moment, Max directly appeared atop the enormous ancient castle overlooking the battlefield below.","From that height, the entire chaotic region became clearly visible before his eyes.","Countless participants slaughtered one another throughout the battlefield endlessly.","Explosions continuously echoed throughout the surroundings.","Sword lights tore through the heavens.","Demonic aura surged wildly everywhere.","Blood stained enormous portions of the battlefield while revived participants continuously rushed out from the castle repeatedly before diving back into the slaughter once again.","The scene honestly resembled complete madness.","Meanwhile, standing atop the highest point of the castle itself, Max quietly observed everything calmly.","The violent winds high above the battlefield caused his clothes to flutter continuously while countless flashes of destruction reflected within his eyes.","Then eventually—","Max slowly sat down atop the castle casually.","He did not immediately join the chaos again.","Instead, a faint smile gradually appeared across his face.","\"There is no need to rush.\"","At that moment, Max had already made his decision.","Rather than wasting effort fighting countless weak participants repeatedly, it would be far more efficient to simply wait.","Wait until stronger participants gathered enormous amounts of Killing Points.","Wait until weaker geniuses gradually became eliminated one after another.","And then—","Sweep everyone remaining afterward.","Max calmly looked down toward the battlefield below while silently waiting.","Meanwhile, above the battlefield itself, enormous golden numbers could be seen floating throughout the sky.","Those numbers represented the total participants remaining alive within this region of the Eternal Hourglass.","And slowly—","The numbers continuously decreased.","Thousands became hundreds.","Hundreds continued dropping lower and lower as the slaughter intensified increasingly.","Every few moments, participants disappeared permanently after exhausting all four lives completely.","The battlefield only became more brutal over time.","Meanwhile, Max simply remained seated atop the castle silently observing everything like a hunter patiently watching prey weaken each other.","\"I will move once the numbers drop low enough,\" Max muttered softly.","His eyes gradually narrowed afterward.","\"Perhaps once only ten or so participants remain...\""]},{"number":1695,"title":"Chapter 1695: Camouflage Demons!","paragraphs":["Just as Max quietly remained seated atop the enormous castle while calmly observing the endless slaughter unfolding below him.","The battlefield only continued becoming increasingly brutal over time.","Participants continuously killed one another repeatedly while Killing Points shifted from person to person endlessly.","The weaker geniuses gradually began disappearing completely after exhausting all four lives while the stronger individuals continued growing increasingly dangerous.","At the same time, the number of surviving participants steadily decreased.","However, despite appearing relaxed outwardly, Max’s senses had never relaxed even slightly.","The Dimensional Sovereign Body continuously spread invisible perception throughout the surroundings while carefully observing everything nearby.","And eventually—","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","Then he lightly chuckled.","\"How long do you three plan on hiding there?\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the surrounding area immediately became silent once again.","Nothing happened.","No movement appeared anywhere nearby.","However, Max’s expression never changed in the slightest.","Instead, he simply continued looking calmly toward empty space nearby.","Several seconds passed afterward.","Then suddenly—","Buzz!!!","Space distorted faintly nearby.","The next moment, three figures slowly emerged out of nowhere.","All three possessed dark black skin and two demonic horns atop their heads.","Demons.","Terrifying demonic aura continuously leaked from their bodies while dense killing intent filled the surroundings instantly.","Meanwhile, after appearing, the three demons immediately looked toward Max with cold expressions.","Clearly, they never expected someone to notice them hiding there beforehand.","At the same time, Max’s eyes quietly narrowed slightly afterward while carefully observing the three demons.","Unlike the weaker demon he killed earlier, these three were clearly much stronger.","Much more dangerous.","One of the three demons slowly stepped forward afterward.","The demon possessed a massive body covered in dark black muscles while a gigantic crimson saber rested casually upon his shoulder. Dense demonic aura continuously leaked from his body while several scars covered portions of his face, giving him an especially savage appearance.","Meanwhile, the demon calmly looked toward Max before speaking.","\"We saw everything earlier,\" he said with a cold grin. \"The way you dealt with Jong was honestly quite impressive.\"","A faint dangerous light flashed within his crimson eyes afterward.","\"Although that fool was not our friend, he was still a member of the Demon Race.\"","The demon slowly pointed the gigantic saber toward Max afterward.","\"And more importantly...\"","A greedy smile gradually spread across his face.","\"He left quite a few Killing Points on you before dying.\"","The other two demons nearby also released faint killing intent afterward while quietly surrounding Max from different directions.","However, Max himself remained completely calm.","Instead, he simply looked toward the three demons casually before replying,","\"If you wanted to fight, then you should have simply attacked directly.\"","A faint mocking smile slowly appeared across his face afterward.","\"Why bother hiding in the shadows like cowards?\"","The moment those words entered their ears, the surrounding demonic aura instantly became colder.","However, instead of becoming angry, the saber-wielding demon simply laughed.","\"Hahaha...\"","His laughter sounded rough and dangerous.","\"We may be demons, but that does not mean we are idiots.\"","The demon’s crimson eyes narrowed afterward while staring directly toward Max.","\"We already saw how easily you killed Jong repeatedly.\"","The atmosphere around the three demons gradually became increasingly dangerous afterward.","\"A peak Law Awakening Realm cultivator capable of casually slaughtering someone like Jong is obviously not normal.\"","The demon then slowly grinned afterward.","\"So naturally, we decided using a more careful approach would be better.\"","The moment those words fell—","Buzz!!!","The bodies of all three demons suddenly blurred strangely.","Then, before Max could even blink properly, the three demons completely disappeared from sight once again as though they had never existed there at all.","\"Invisibility?\" Max muttered softly while slightly raising his brows.","However, only a moment later, he slowly shook his head.","\"No...\"","A faint smile gradually appeared across his face afterward.","\"This is merely camouflage.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Max suddenly moved his right hand sideways casually.","Bang!!!","A violent explosion instantly erupted nearby.","One of the hidden demons, who had been silently approaching Max from the side while concealed beneath the camouflage ability, was directly blasted away violently before he could even properly react.","The demon’s body smashed across the top of the castle while his camouflage immediately shattered apart completely.","At that moment, shock clearly filled the demon’s crimson eyes.","Meanwhile, before the injured demon could stabilize himself, another demon still hidden beneath the camouflage suddenly attacked from the front.","Boom!!!","A gigantic battle axe tore through the air violently while terrifying demonic aura exploded outward.","The enormous weapon descended directly toward Max’s shoulder with enough force to split apart mountains.","However—","Max never moved.","He simply remained standing there calmly.","Then the battle axe slammed directly onto his shoulder.","Clang!!!","A metallic collision sound echoed throughout the surroundings instantly.","The demon’s expression immediately froze afterward.","Because the terrifying battle axe failed to even leave a scratch upon Max’s skin.","The axe stopped completely against his body as though it had struck an indestructible divine metal wall.","At that moment, the demon’s shocked voice echoed throughout the surroundings.","\"How is this possible?!\"","Meanwhile, Max slowly turned his head toward the demon afterward.","A faint smile appeared across his face.","Then—","Boom!!!","Star-like light instantly condensed around Max’s fist.","The next moment, Max directly unleashed the Star Fist Divine Ability toward the demon standing before him.","Terrifying stellar force exploded outward instantly.","The surrounding space distorted violently from the sheer power released by the punch.","The demon did not even possess the slightest chance to escape.","Boom!!!","His entire body exploded apart instantly into countless golden fragments before disappearing completely from the battlefield.","At that moment, the final remaining demon finally revealed himself completely.","Buzz!!!","The camouflage surrounding his body gradually disappeared while dense demonic aura erupted outward violently.","The gigantic demon slowly stepped forward afterward while the enormous crimson saber resting upon his back radiated terrifying killing intent continuously.","However, unlike earlier, the demon’s expression now looked extremely dark.","Clearly, after witnessing Max casually destroy the other two demons, even he no longer remained calm.","Meanwhile, the demon stared directly toward Max before speaking coldly,","\"You can actually see through our concealment?\"","His crimson eyes narrowed dangerously afterward.","Meanwhile, Max simply looked toward him calmly before replying casually,","\"It is merely a trash camouflage technique.\"","A faint mocking smile gradually appeared across his face afterward.","\"Even if the three of you truly possessed invisibility abilities...\"","His eyes slowly sharpened slightly.","\"I still would have found you easily.\"","The moment those words entered the demon’s ears, terrifying rage instantly exploded from his body.","Boom!!!","Violent demonic aura surged wildly throughout the surroundings while killing intent filled the top of the castle completely.","\"You arrogant human!\"","The demon roared furiously afterward.","The next instant, he directly pulled out the gigantic crimson saber from his back."]},{"number":1696,"title":"Chapter 1696: Killing Points Skyrocketing!","paragraphs":["The moment the weapon appeared fully, terrifying saber pressure instantly descended throughout the surroundings.","Compared to the previous demons, this demon was clearly far stronger.","Much stronger.","Dense crimson demonic flames immediately erupted around the saber while strange demonic runes began glowing throughout its blade continuously.","Then—","The demon suddenly raised the enormous saber high into the sky.","Boom!!!","The surrounding heavens instantly darkened slightly.","Terrifying demonic power rapidly gathered around the gigantic blade while enormous saber intent spread outward endlessly.","Then the demon roared once again.","\"Demonic Saber Art!\"","The gigantic crimson saber directly slashed downward toward Max afterward.","The moment the attack descended, a massive crimson saber phantom instantly tore through the sky itself.","The terrifying pressure released by the attack honestly far surpassed every demon Max fought earlier.","Even the surrounding space distorted violently beneath the overwhelming force of the saber strike.","Meanwhile, seeing the incoming attack, Max merely smiled faintly afterward.","Then slowly—","He clenched his fist once again.","Dense star-like light instantly began condensing around his hand while terrifying physical power surged throughout his body completely.","At the same time, the power of five thousand Draconic Essences erupted within him.","The Vein of Strength activated.","The Star Fist Divine Ability circulated completely.","Then, deep within his mind, Max silently muttered one sentence.","\"Power of One Star.\"","The next instant—","Boom!!!","Max directly punched toward the descending gigantic saber attack.","The moment his fist collided with the enormous crimson saber phantom, terrifying stellar force exploded outward completely.","The gigantic saber attack shattered instantly.","Not weakened.","Not pushed back.","Completely obliterated.","The massive crimson saber phantom exploded apart like fragile glass beneath Max’s fist.","Then the terrifying stellar force continued surging forward without slowing down even slightly.","The demon’s expression instantly transformed into absolute horror.","\"What—?!\"","He did not even finish speaking.","Boom!!!","The remaining force of Max’s punch directly swallowed both the demon and his gigantic crimson saber completely.","The demon’s body exploded apart instantly into countless golden fragments before disappearing entirely from existence.","Meanwhile, after obliterating the saber-wielding demon completely, Max slowly turned his gaze toward the first demon he blasted away earlier.","That demon had only barely managed to survive the previous attack and was currently struggling to stand up properly atop the ruined castle.","However, the moment he saw Max looking toward him, fear instantly filled his crimson eyes.","\"N-No...\"","The demon instinctively stepped backward repeatedly afterward.","Unfortunately for him, Max no longer had any interest in wasting time.","Boom!!!","The Vein of Speed activated instantly.","Before the demon could even react, Max had already appeared directly before him.","Then—","Boom!!!","Another Star Fist erupted outward violently.","The demon’s body exploded apart instantly into countless golden fragments before disappearing completely.","At that moment, silence gradually returned atop the enormous castle once again.","Meanwhile, Max slowly walked toward the edge of the castle afterward before calmly looking down toward the battlefield below.","The chaotic slaughter still continued endlessly.","However, compared to earlier, the number of surviving participants had already drastically decreased.","Max quietly waited there afterward.","Minutes slowly passed.","Then eventually—","The enormous golden numbers floating throughout the sky finally changed once again.","[Remaining Participants: 5]","Seeing this, a faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face.","Only five participants remained alive within this battlefield region now.","At the same time, not far below the castle, the demons Max killed earlier also gradually revived once again before reappearing around the battlefield.","Clearly, they still intended to continue surviving somehow.","Unfortunately—","The moment Max saw them gathering below once again, his eyes gradually turned cold.","\"That should be enough.\"","The next instant—","Boom!!!","Terrifying black flames suddenly erupted throughout Max’s body violently.","The dark flames surged wildly around him while dense destructive aura spread throughout the entire battlefield instantly.","At that moment, everyone below immediately sensed overwhelming danger.","Then slowly—","Max raised one hand high toward the sky.","The next instant, the heavens themselves suddenly darkened.","Boom!!!","Countless black flames gathered throughout the sky rapidly before condensing together into an absolutely gigantic flaming sword.","The sword was enormous beyond imagination.","It towered throughout the heavens itself while black flames burned endlessly around its blade.","Compared to the gigantic castle below—","The flaming sword itself was countless times larger.","The terrifying pressure released by the sword immediately caused the surrounding space to tremble violently.","Meanwhile, below the castle—","The remaining five participants instantly froze completely.","Three humans.","Two demons.","And even the three recently revived demons.","All of them slowly raised their heads afterward.","Then—","Despair instantly appeared across every single one of their faces.","\"What... is that...\"","One of the humans muttered blankly.","Meanwhile, the demons Max killed earlier immediately became completely horrified after recognizing him standing above the castle.","\"N-No...\"","The saber demon’s revived form looked utterly terrified now.","At that moment, beneath the enormous black flaming sword hanging throughout the heavens, everyone felt unbelievably small.","Meanwhile, high above the battlefield, Max calmly looked downward before lowering his hand slowly.","Then—","The gigantic black flaming sword descended.","Boom!!!","The heavens themselves seemed to collapse.","The enormous sword smashed downward toward the battlefield with terrifying destructive force beyond imagination.","Then—","The world exploded.","BOOOOOOMMMMMM!!!!","A catastrophic explosion instantly swallowed the entire battlefield completely.","The gigantic ancient castle exploded apart instantly beneath the terrifying impact.","Countless kilometers of land flattened completely.","The catastrophic explosion continued raging throughout the battlefield endlessly.","Black flames devoured everything in sight while enormous shockwaves spread throughout the flattened land continuously.","The gigantic castle had completely disappeared.","Not even ruins remained behind.","Only a massive destroyed crater stretching across the battlefield could now be seen beneath the burning black flames.","Meanwhile, high above the devastated battlefield, Max calmly stood within the sky while silently observing the destruction below.","At that moment, countless golden notifications suddenly began appearing rapidly before his eyes one after another.","[Killing Points +350]","[Killing Points +420]","[Killing Points +500]","[Killing Points +280]","[Killing Points +610]","[Killing Points +150]","[Killing Points +300]","...","The notifications continued increasing endlessly.","Because the attack earlier had not merely killed the final remaining participants.","It had also completely wiped out the demons he previously killed multiple times after they exhausted their remaining lives entirely.","Soon afterward—","A final notification finally appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Current Killing Points: 28,450]","Seeing the enormous amount of Killing Points he gained instantly, even Max’s eyes slightly brightened afterward.","Then a faint smile gradually spread across his face.","\"Hehe...\"","\"This really is efficient.\"","Meanwhile, Max slowly looked down toward the completely obliterated battlefield afterward while calmly analyzing the situation internally.","\"If the number of surviving participants had still been large...\"","His eyes narrowed slightly afterward.","\"And if many of them still possessed multiple lives remaining...\"","A faint helpless smile appeared across his face.","\"Then using such a large-scale attack would honestly have been somewhat wasteful.\"","After all, the more remaining lives participants possessed, the less effective such a massive extermination attack became.","However now—","Only a handful of participants remained alive before the attack.","And most had already died several times beforehand during the chaotic slaughter.","Which meant Max’s final attack had essentially harvested all remaining Killing Points within this battlefield region completely.","At that moment, while black flames still burned throughout the destroyed land below—","Max quietly stood in the sky with a satisfied expression on his face."]},{"number":1697,"title":"Chapter 1697: Terrifying Rainbow Rabbits!","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, after the catastrophic explosion gradually settled down, the endless black flames slowly began disappearing from the battlefield one after another.","Dust and debris still filled enormous portions of the surroundings while the flattened land stretched endlessly beneath the devastated sky.","The once gigantic castle had completely vanished without leaving behind even the slightest trace.","At that moment, Max calmly floated high above the destroyed battlefield while observing everything below quietly.","Since the battlefield region here had already been completely cleared, Max naturally had no intention of remaining any longer.","After all, the Eternal Hourglass was unimaginably vast.","There were undoubtedly countless other battlefield regions similar to this one scattered throughout the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","And naturally—","There were also countless Killing Points waiting to be harvested elsewhere.","\"Time to move to another area,\" Max muttered softly.","However, just as Max was about to leave the battlefield completely—","His expression suddenly changed slightly.","Because the Dimensional Sovereign Body suddenly sensed a strange fluctuation from the exact location where the gigantic castle had originally stood before being destroyed.","The fluctuation felt extremely unusual.","It was faint.","Yet strangely mysterious.","Max immediately narrowed his eyes afterward.","\"What is that?\"","Curiosity instantly surfaced within his mind.","Without hesitation, Max directly descended from the sky afterward before landing near the center of the destroyed battlefield.","The surrounding ground remained filled with enormous cracks and burning destruction everywhere from the previous attack.","Meanwhile, guided by the Dimensional Sovereign Body, Max slowly walked toward the source of the strange fluctuation.","Soon afterward—","He discovered something unexpected.","A small hidden cave had appeared beneath the destroyed remains of the battlefield.","Clearly, the cave had originally been hidden beneath the castle itself and only became exposed after the entire region was flattened completely.","Seeing this, Max’s curiosity immediately increased further.","Then without hesitation, he directly entered the cave.","The inside of the cave looked surprisingly peaceful compared to the devastated battlefield outside.","Soft rainbow-colored light continuously glowed throughout the surroundings while dense spiritual energy quietly filled the cave completely.","Meanwhile, after walking deeper inside briefly—","Max suddenly stopped.","Because inside the cave—","Several strange rainbow-colored rabbits quietly sat there.","Max quietly looked toward the strange rainbow-colored rabbits gathered inside the cave.","The rabbits honestly looked harmless.","Their fur shimmered with countless rainbow colors beneath the glowing spiritual light surrounding the cave while their tiny eyes looked unusually pure and innocent.","At first glance, they appeared almost cute.","And unfortunately for Max—","That became his very first mistake here.","Meanwhile, just as Max continued observing the rabbits curiously, one of them suddenly moved.","Buzz!!!","Without any warning whatsoever, the rainbow rabbit instantly disappeared from its original position.","The next moment—","It directly appeared before Max.","Teleportation.","The speed of the movement honestly shocked even Max slightly.","At the same time, the small rabbit suddenly swung one of its claws directly toward him.","The claw itself looked tiny and harmless.","However, the moment it attacked, terrifying fluctuations erupted from it instantly.","Fortunately, Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted immediately.","His eyes instantly captured the trajectory of the rabbit’s attack.","Then without hesitation, Max directly responded with a punch of his own.","Bang!!!","A violent collision instantly echoed throughout the cave.","The surrounding ground shattered slightly while terrifying force exploded outward from the impact point.","However—","Max’s expression instantly changed afterward.","Because after colliding with the rabbit’s claw, his body was actually pushed backward several steps.","\"What?!\"","Max genuinely became shocked.","He immediately stabilized himself afterward while staring directly toward the small rainbow rabbit before him.","\"I was actually pushed back by a rabbit?\"","At that moment, even Max found the situation difficult to believe.","After all, his physical strength was absolutely monstrous.","Even without activating the Divine Veins or using the power of the five thousand Draconic Essences, his body alone still ranked among the strongest younger generation geniuses participating in the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Yet now—","Against a small rainbow-colored rabbit—","He had actually been overpowered physically.","This honestly shocked Max greatly.","However, the true horror only arrived moments later.","Just as Max was still processing the absurd strength of the rainbow rabbit, his expression suddenly froze.","Because he suddenly felt something warm rising within his throat.","The next instant—","Cough!","Max directly spat out a mouthful of blood onto the ground.","The bright crimson blood immediately stained portions of the cave floor.","Seeing this, Max’s pupils instantly contracted sharply.","At that moment, genuine horror finally appeared across his face.","\"How did this happen?\"","He immediately looked back toward the rainbow rabbit he clashed with earlier.","Meanwhile, the rabbit simply stood there quietly while looking toward him calmly with its rainbow-colored eyes.","Then suddenly—","A terrifying possibility surfaced within Max’s mind.","\"Did it...\"","His expression gradually became increasingly serious.","\"Did that attack ignore my outer body completely and directly damage my internal organs?\"","Understanding this instantly, Max’s expression immediately became incomparably solemn.","Without hesitation, he directly stepped backward several times while widening the distance between himself and the rainbow-colored rabbits.","At that moment, all traces of carelessness had completely disappeared from his face.","Instead, only caution remained.","Meanwhile, the tens of rainbow rabbits inside the cave quietly stared toward him with their colorful eyes while strange fluctuations continuously spread around their bodies faintly.","\"They can teleport...\"","Max muttered while narrowing his eyes seriously.","\"And their attacks can directly bypass external defenses and strike internal organs instead.\"","The more Max analyzed the earlier clash, the more dangerous these seemingly harmless rabbits appeared.","After all, no matter how terrifying someone’s physical defense was, it would become meaningless if the attack ignored the outer body entirely.","At that moment, even Max felt genuine danger from these creatures.","However—","A faint smile slowly appeared across his face afterward.","\"I suppose the best solution is simply immobilizing them first.\"","The next instant, terrifying spatial fluctuations instantly erupted from Max’s body.","Dense Space Concept rapidly spread throughout the entire cave while countless silver-blue dimensional runes appeared around him one after another.","Then Max calmly raised one hand afterward.","\"Void Genesis Art...\"","The surrounding space immediately began trembling violently.","Then Max’s eyes sharpened completely.","\"Space Freeze.\"","Boom!!!","The full power of Max’s Space Concept exploded outward instantly.","The next moment, the entire surrounding space within nearly a one-kilometer radius completely froze.","Not ordinary freezing.","Space itself became solidified completely.","The air stopped moving.","Spatial fluctuations completely ceased.","Even dimensional movement itself became restricted entirely.","Meanwhile, inside the cave, all the rainbow rabbits instantly froze in place one after another beneath the terrifying power of the Void Genesis Art.","Even their strange teleportation fluctuations stopped completely."]},{"number":1698,"title":"Chapter 1698: A hidden trial?","paragraphs":["Seeing this scene, Max finally smiled lightly afterward.","\"It is fortunate that I finally fully mastered the Void Genesis Art during these past months.\"","His gaze quietly swept across the frozen rabbits afterward.","At that moment, Max genuinely felt somewhat emotional internally.","The Void Genesis Art had originally been given to him long ago by his very first master.","Back then, that same master had even helped him create a separate clone body in order to allow him to pursue the path of time independently.","However, after ascending into the Divine Realm, Max became occupied with countless other powers and inheritances.","The Seven Divine Veins.","His bloodline.","And countless other opportunities.","Because of that, he never truly gave the Void Genesis Art the attention it deserved.","As a result, the art gradually became almost useless compared to his other abilities.","Only during these recent three months of secluded cultivation inside the Dimension of Time did Max finally dedicate himself toward completely comprehending the Void Genesis Art to its highest layer.","And now—","After truly mastering it—","Max finally realized exactly what he had been missing all this time.","The Void Genesis Art was far more terrifying than he originally imagined.","Meanwhile, after completely freezing the surrounding space with the Void Genesis Art, the entire cave became deathly silent.","The rainbow-colored rabbits remained frozen in place completely.","Even their strange teleportation fluctuations had entirely stopped beneath the terrifying suppression of the frozen space.","Seeing this, Max no longer hesitated afterward.","A seven-colored lightning sword instantly condensed within his hand.","Crackle! Crackle! Crackle!","Violent lightning continuously surged around the sword blade while terrifying sharpness spread throughout the cave.","Then Max slowly walked toward the nearest frozen rabbit.","At that moment, despite the rainbow rabbit being immobilized completely, Max still did not underestimate it in the slightest.","After all, he already personally experienced how terrifying these creatures truly were.","Without hesitation, Max directly thrust the lightning sword downward.","Puchi!","The sword pierced directly through the rabbit’s body instantly.","The rainbow-colored rabbit immediately exploded apart into countless fragments of rainbow light before disappearing completely.","At the same time—","Several golden notifications instantly appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Killing Points +5,000]","[Current Killing Points: 33,450]","Seeing this, even Max’s expression changed slightly afterward.","\"Five thousand Killing Points from a single rabbit?\"","At that moment, even he became genuinely surprised.","Clearly, these rainbow rabbits were far more valuable than ordinary participants outside.","Meanwhile, after realizing this, Max’s eyes immediately brightened slightly afterward.","Without wasting any more time, Max directly moved toward the next frozen rabbit.","Puchi!","Another rabbit exploded apart into rainbow fragments instantly.","[Killing Points +5,000]","Then another.","And another.","The entire cave soon became filled with flashing golden notifications continuously as Max slaughtered the immobilized rainbow rabbits one after another effortlessly.","Puchi!","Puchi!","Puchi!","Every rabbit he killed immediately granted enormous amounts of Killing Points.","Meanwhile, the frozen space surrounding the cave remained completely stable beneath the power of the Void Genesis Art, preventing any of the rabbits from escaping through teleportation whatsoever.","Eventually—","After the final rainbow rabbit was killed completely—","A massive final notification suddenly appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Current Killing Points: 110,000]","Seeing the enormous number floating before him, even Max himself became slightly stunned for a brief moment.","Then slowly—","A bright smile gradually spread across his face afterward.","\"One hundred and ten thousand Killing Points...\"","Even after slaughtering countless participants throughout the battlefield earlier, his points had never increased this absurdly fast.","Clearly—","The true opportunities hidden inside the Eternal Hourglass were not merely the battlefield regions outside.","There were treasures and hidden encounters hidden throughout this place as well.","\"The strange energy fluctuations I sensed earlier still have not disappeared...\"","Max muttered softly while narrowing his eyes toward the deeper parts of the cave.","Even after slaughtering all the rainbow-colored rabbits nearby, the mysterious fluctuations remained extremely clear beneath the perception of his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","That immediately meant one thing.","\"There is definitely something else hidden here aside from those rabbits.\"","Understanding this instantly, Max no longer wasted any time afterward.","He directly continued moving deeper into the cave.","The deeper he traveled, the denser the strange spiritual fluctuations became.","At the same time, the surroundings gradually became increasingly beautiful as well.","Rainbow-colored light continuously reflected throughout the cave walls while dense spiritual energy filled the air almost like liquid itself.","Meanwhile, during his journey deeper inside, Max encountered several more rainbow rabbits hidden throughout different parts of the cave.","However, after suffering earlier because of underestimating them, Max naturally no longer acted carelessly.","The instant he sensed the rabbits preparing to attack, terrifying spatial fluctuations immediately erupted outward.","\"Void Genesis Art.\"","\"Space Freeze.\"","Boom!!!","The surrounding space instantly solidified once again.","The rainbow rabbits immediately froze in place before even possessing the chance to teleport.","Then Max casually slaughtered them one after another using his lightning sword.","Compared to earlier, handling them now became vastly easier.","Eventually, after traveling deeper for quite some time, Max finally reached the very end of the cave.","The moment he arrived there, his footsteps slowly stopped.","Because floating silently before him—","Was an enormous tetragonal crystal.","The crystal was gigantic.","At least several dozen meters tall.","Its entire body shimmered with beautiful deep blue light while incomparably pure energy continuously flowed throughout its surface endlessly.","At the same time, the strange mysterious fluctuations Max sensed earlier clearly originated from this crystal itself.","Meanwhile, countless strange runes continuously floated around the crystal while dense spatial energy distorted portions of the surroundings faintly.","The moment Max saw the crystal clearly, even his eyes slightly narrowed afterward.","Because he could immediately feel it.","The energy contained within this giant blue crystal was absolutely extraordinary.","Meanwhile, Max quietly stood before the enormous blue crystal while carefully observing it with narrowed eyes.","Dense mysterious energy continuously flowed throughout the crystal while strange spatial fluctuations distorted the surrounding area faintly.","At the same time, the Dimensional Sovereign Body continuously warned him that this crystal was absolutely extraordinary.","\"This thing...\" Max muttered softly.","The closer he looked at the giant tetragonal crystal, the more ancient and mysterious it appeared.","Countless blue runes slowly circulated throughout its surface while deep inside the crystal itself, faint flashes of starlike light could occasionally be seen flickering endlessly.","At that moment, Max genuinely could not determine exactly what this crystal was.","However, just as he was still observing the giant crystal curiously—","Buzz!!!","The surrounding space suddenly trembled lightly.","The next instant, several enormous golden notifications abruptly appeared before Max’s eyes.","[Hidden Trial Detected.]","[Genesis Trial]","[Requirement To Enter: 500,000 Killing Points]","[Would You Like To Spend 500,000 Killing Points To Begin The Genesis Trial?]","The moment Max saw those notifications, his expression instantly froze slightly.","\"Five hundred thousand Killing Points?\"","Even Max became genuinely shocked afterward.","After all, obtaining one hundred and ten thousand Killing Points already required him to wipe out an entire battlefield region and slaughter dozens of strange rainbow rabbits.","Yet now—","This hidden trial actually required five hundred thousand Killing Points merely to enter.","At that moment, Max immediately understood something.","This so-called Genesis Trial was undoubtedly an unbelievably high-level opportunity hidden within the Eternal Hourglass.","Otherwise, the entrance requirement would never be this absurdly expensive.","Meanwhile, Max slowly looked back toward the giant blue crystal afterward while his eyes gradually became increasingly solemn.","Because now—","He finally understood.","This crystal itself was likely the entrance to the mysterious Genesis Trial."]},{"number":1699,"title":"Chapter 1699: A Peaceful Zone!","paragraphs":["The moment Max saw the requirement displayed before him, he could not help but fall silent.","Five hundred thousand Killing Points.","The number honestly felt absurd.","Even after everything he had gone through since entering the Eternal Hourglass, his current total only stood at one hundred and ten thousand.","That meant he still lacked nearly four hundred thousand Killing Points before he could even qualify to enter the Genesis Trial.","Meanwhile, Max slowly looked back toward the gigantic blue crystal floating quietly before him.","The crystal continued radiating mysterious blue light while ancient runes circulated endlessly across its surface.","Just looking at it made Max feel that the opportunity hidden within was extraordinary.","After all, anything requiring half a million Killing Points merely to enter could not possibly be ordinary.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face afterward.","\"It seems I discovered something incredible.\"","His eyes gradually brightened.","Although he could not enter the Genesis Trial immediately, simply knowing its location was already a tremendous gain.","After all, the crystal was hidden beneath an entire battlefield region and guarded by those strange rainbow rabbits. If he had not accidentally destroyed the castle and investigated the fluctuations afterward, he might never have discovered this place at all.","Meanwhile, Max calmly began calculating his situation.","\"One hundred and ten thousand Killing Points...\"","He muttered thoughtfully.","\"I still need another three hundred and ninety thousand.\"","At that moment, Max naturally had no intention of giving up on the Genesis Trial.","On the contrary—","The enormous requirement only made him more interested.","Because the greater the entry cost, the greater the reward was likely to be.","Eventually, Max nodded to himself.","\"The Genesis Trial is not going anywhere.\"","His gaze slowly swept across the enormous crystal one final time.","\"I can always come back later.\"","At that moment, a clear plan gradually formed within his mind.","The Eternal Hourglass was unimaginably vast.","If one battlefield region could provide tens of thousands of Killing Points and even hide treasures such as the rainbow rabbits, then there were undoubtedly countless other opportunities scattered throughout the conference.","First, he would continue exploring.","He would hunt participants.","Search for hidden opportunities.","Farm as many Killing Points as possible.","And once he accumulated the required five hundred thousand Killing Points—","He would return here and enter the Genesis Trial.","A faint grin appeared across his face afterward.","\"Looks like I need to work a little harder.\"","With that, Max memorized the location of the cave completely using the Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Then he slowly turned around and began walking toward the exit.","The mysterious blue crystal continued floating silently behind him while ancient blue light illuminated the cave endlessly.","Meanwhile, Max’s attention had already shifted toward his next objective.","Gathering enough Killing Points to unlock the Genesis Trial.","A lot of Killing Points.","Only after accumulating five hundred thousand of them could he return and uncover the secrets hidden inside the Genesis Trial.","Soon afterward, Max exited the cave completely.","The next moment, the Vein of Speed activated.","Boom!!!","His figure shot into the sky like a streak of light before disappearing into the horizon.","The Eternal Hourglass was unimaginably vast.","Mountains.","Forests.","Battlefields.","Ancient ruins.","Cities.","Countless landscapes continuously flashed beneath Max as he flew through the world at astonishing speed.","Meanwhile, the Dimensional Sovereign Body continuously remained active while searching the surroundings for areas containing large concentrations of participants.","After all, where there were participants, there would be opportunities.","And where there were opportunities, there would be Killing Points.","It did not take very long before Max finally discovered something.","\"Hm?\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","Far in the distance, he sensed an enormous concentration of life signatures.","Not thousands.","Not tens of thousands.","Hundreds of thousands.","The sheer number immediately attracted Max’s attention.","Without hesitation, he adjusted his direction and flew toward it.","Several minutes later, a gigantic city gradually appeared before him.","The city was absolutely enormous.","Its walls stretched beyond the horizon while countless buildings filled the interior. Ancient towers rose into the sky while enormous roads crossed throughout the city like a massive network.","However—","The moment Max arrived above the city, his expression immediately became strange.","Because the scene before him was completely different from what he expected.","Hundreds of thousands of participants filled the city.","Humans.","Demons.","Elves.","And even members of other races.","The entire city was crowded with geniuses from across the Divine Realm.","Yet—","Nobody was fighting.","Not a single battle could be seen anywhere.","Participants calmly walked through the streets.","Some sat within restaurants.","Others entered various buildings.","Many gathered in groups while discussing things quietly.","The atmosphere honestly felt more like a bustling marketplace than a battle royale.","At that moment, Max genuinely became confused.","He slowly descended onto a rooftop while observing the city below.","\"What is going on here?\"","His brows gradually furrowed.","Earlier, the battlefield outside the castle had resembled absolute hell.","People slaughtered one another without hesitation.","Yet here—","Hundreds of thousands of participants occupied the same city peacefully.","No fighting.","No killing.","No chaos.","The contrast was so extreme that it honestly felt bizarre.","\"How can nobody be fighting in a battle royale?\"","Max muttered softly.","His gaze slowly swept across the city once again.","The more he observed, the stranger the situation appeared.","Because not only were people not fighting—","Many participants actually appeared completely relaxed.","As though they were not even participating in the Cosmic Ascension Conference at all.","At that moment, curiosity instantly filled Max’s mind.","Clearly—","There was something very unusual about this city.","Meanwhile, after observing the city from above for some time, Max finally decided to investigate personally.","After all, merely watching from a distance would not reveal the true reason behind such a strange situation.","The next moment, his figure descended from the rooftop before entering the city directly.","As soon as Max crossed through the city boundaries—","Buzz!!!","A strange fluctuation suddenly swept across his body.","At the same time, several golden notifications immediately appeared before his eyes.","[You Have Entered A Peaceful Zone.]","[All Forms Of Combat Are Strictly Prohibited Within This Region.]","[Participants Are Forbidden From Attacking One Another.]","[Violators Will Be Punished By The Eternal Hourglass.]","The moment Max saw those notifications, everything instantly became clear.","\"So that is the reason.\"","A look of realization appeared across his face afterward.","He finally understood why hundreds of thousands of participants could gather inside this city without trying to kill one another.","It was not because they suddenly became friendly.","Nor was it because they reached some kind of agreement.","Rather—","The Eternal Hourglass itself prohibited fighting inside the city.","And judging from the wording of the notification, the punishment seemed serious enough that nobody was willing to test it."]},{"number":1700,"title":"Chapter 1700: Starfall Haven!","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Max quietly looked around afterward.","Now that he understood the rules, the scene before him immediately made much more sense.","Participants walked through the streets calmly.","Many entered shops and buildings.","Others gathered together to exchange information or rest after fighting outside.","Some wounded participants could even be seen recovering peacefully without worrying about being ambushed.","At that moment, the city suddenly felt completely different from the battlefield regions outside.","Outside the city—","The world was filled with slaughter.","Inside the city—","A strange order existed.","Almost like a temporary sanctuary amidst endless chaos.","Max slowly walked through the streets afterward while observing everything around him carefully.","A faint smile gradually appeared across his face.","\"Interesting.\"","This city clearly possessed a purpose beyond merely providing shelter.","Otherwise, the Eternal Hourglass would never create an entire peaceful zone containing hundreds of thousands of participants.","Which meant one thing.","There were likely opportunities hidden within this city as well.","Meanwhile, after walking through the city for some time, Max realized that simply observing the surroundings would not answer all the questions in his mind.","There were simply too many unusual things about this place. The peaceful zone, the enormous crowds, and the countless shops and buildings all made the city feel far too organized to be a random part of the Eternal Hourglass.","Eventually, Max approached a small group of human participants standing near a large plaza. The moment one of the men saw him, he frowned slightly.","For some reason, Max seemed familiar to him. He felt as though he had seen his face somewhere before, yet no matter how much he thought about it, he could not recall where. Nevertheless, he did not dwell on it for long.","Max directly asked, \"Can you tell me what exactly this city is?\"","The man looked at him with surprise before replying, \"You really do not know? This place is one of the neutral cities scattered throughout the Eternal Hourglass. You can think of it as a giant hub for all participants. As long as you possess enough Killing Points, you can buy almost anything here. Resources, cultivation treasures, rare medicines, powerful weapons, information, maps, inheritances, Divine Ability and even opportunities can all be found within this city. Some people have even obtained legendary treasures here before. Of course, whether you can afford them is another matter entirely.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly as he listened.","The man continued, \"This city is not unique either. There are many neutral regions throughout the Eternal Hourglass, although each one is different. Participants eventually visit them because everyone needs resources or information at some point. Fighting is strictly forbidden here because the Eternal Hourglass itself enforces the rules. That is why you see hundreds of thousands of people walking around peacefully despite this being a battle royale.\"","Max nodded thoughtfully before asking, \"What is this city called?\"","The man smiled faintly and replied, \"This city is called Starfall Haven. It is one of the largest neutral cities in this region of the Eternal Hourglass. Most participants pass through it sooner or later. Looking at you, I would guess you have been spending all your time fighting and hunting Killing Points rather than exploring.\"","Max chuckled lightly after hearing that.","The man was not wrong.","Ever since entering the Eternal Hourglass, Max had done little besides fight, kill, and search for opportunities.","Now, however, it seemed he had finally discovered a completely different side of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","After understanding the purpose of Starfall Haven, Max thanked the man and continued exploring the city on his own.","The more he walked through the bustling streets, the more amazed he became by the scale of the place. Everywhere he looked, participants were buying treasures, exchanging information, or searching for opportunities. Some shops sold rare cultivation resources while others specialized in weapons, armor, maps, pills, and inheritances.","Eventually, Max arrived before an enormous pavilion unlike anything he had seen before.","Above the entrance hung a massive golden sign.","Divine Ability Pavilion","The moment Max read those words, his interest was immediately piqued.","Without hesitation, he entered.","Inside, a massive crystal screen floated in the center of the pavilion. Thousands upon thousands of names continuously scrolled across its surface.","Max walked closer and began browsing through them.","Soon, a list of Divine Abilities appeared before him.","[Tier I Divine Ability - Stone Skin]","Effect: Greatly increases physical defense.","Price: 10,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier I Divine Ability - Swift Wind]","Effect: Increases movement speed.","Price: 12,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier I Divine Ability - Iron Bones]","Effect: Strengthens skeletal structure and durability.","Price: 15,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier II Divine Ability - Blood Burning]","Effect: Temporarily doubles combat strength.","Price: 35,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier II Divine Ability - Thunder Step]","Effect: Allows instantaneous bursts of lightning movement.","Price: 42,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier III Divine Ability - Void Shatter]","Effect: Creates destructive spatial fractures.","Price: 150,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier III Divine Ability - Heavenly Flame Wings]","Effect: Condenses wings of divine flames capable of flight and combat.","Price: 180,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier IV Divine Ability - Starfall Cataclysm]","Effect: Summons falling stars from the heavens.","Price: 750,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier IV Divine Ability - Eternal Phoenix Body]","Effect: Grants terrifying regenerative abilities.","Price: 920,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier V Divine Ability - World Devourer]","Effect: Consume all energy within a designated region.","Price: 5,000,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier V Divine Ability - Heavenly Genesis Hand]","Effect: Create and destroy matter through divine authority.","Price: 8,500,000,000 Killing Points.","[Tier V Divine Ability - Infinite Star Sovereign Physique]","Effect: Transform the body into a vessel of endless stellar power.","Price: 12,000,000,000 Killing Points.","As Max continued scrolling through the endless list, his expression gradually became stranger and stranger.","The Divine Abilities themselves were shocking enough.","However—","The prices were even more absurd.","Ten million Killing Points.","That was merely the entry price for the weakest Tier I Divine Ability.","And the higher-tier abilities quickly climbed into hundreds of millions and even billions of Killing Points.","At that moment, Max suddenly looked at his own Killing Point count.","[Current Killing Points: 110,000]","Silence.","A strange expression immediately appeared on his face.","He had previously thought that one hundred and ten thousand Killing Points was already a considerable amount.","After all, he had slaughtered an entire battlefield, farmed multiple lives from participants, and wiped out dozens of rainbow rabbits just to accumulate that amount.","Yet now—","Looking at the Divine Ability Pavilion’s prices, Max suddenly felt unbelievably poor.","Very poor.","In fact, he was so poor that even the cheapest Divine Ability was nearly one hundred times beyond his reach.","The corner of Max’s mouth twitched slightly.","\"I thought I was rich.\"","He looked once more at the ten-million-Killing-Point price tag of the cheapest Divine Ability.","Then he looked at his own one hundred and ten thousand points.","\"I should have known this isn’t much when the requirement to enter the secret trial was 500k KP.\"","For the first time since entering the Eternal Hourglass, Max genuinely felt as though he possessed almost nothing."]}]);
